  "Large Apiary": "大型養蜂箱",
  "Provides more slots for frames and drones.": "フレームとドローンの追加スロットを提供する",
  "^orange;Basic^reset; Microscope": "^orange;ベーシック^reset;顕微鏡",
  "A basic microscope designed to inspect queen bees. User must be present.": "女王蜂を検査するためのシンプルな顕微鏡。使用者の立ち合いが必要",
  "^orange;Advanced^reset; Microscope": "^orange;アドバンスド^reset;顕微鏡",
  "A basic microscope designed to inspect queen bees. Works automatically.": "女王蜂を検査するためのシンプルな顕微鏡。自動で動作",
  "Bee Flower Head": "ビーフラワーヘッド",
  "The head of a Bee flower. Contains traces of anti-mite poison!": "ビーフラワーの頭部。ダニ除け毒の痕跡を含む！",
  "^red;What do you need now, Jesson?!?!?^reset; Oh. It's not him. Hi. What?": "^red;今度は何の用だ、ジェソン？！？！？^reset; あ、ジェソンじゃないのか。やあ。何？",
  "Are you that newcomer that Saunter said absolutely adores bees? You must be, or else why would you be here, right?": "お前、サウンターが言ってた蜂が大好きな新入りか？そうに違いない、でなきゃなんでここにいるんだ？",
  "No? Allright...you standing there is getting a bit annoying, then. On your bike. Off you go.": "違う？分かった…じゃあそこに突っ立ってるのはちょっと邪魔だな。あっち行って。シッシッ。",
  "No? Allright. ^red;$#@@#%^reset; it I guess. I'm ^green;Kevin^reset;, and I am probably quite a bit smarter than you are.": "違う？分かった。^red;$#@@#%^reset;、仕方ない。俺は^green;ケビン^reset;、お前よりかなり頭がいい",
  "I know this not just because you ^green;look^reset; a little bit stupid, but also because I am a master artisan. Yes, really. A ^cyan;Master Sandwich Maker^reset;. The noblest of professions.": "お前が少し^green;バカっぽく見える^reset;からだけじゃなく、俺がマスター職人だからだ。そう、本当のマスター職人",
  "Few can truly appreciate the fine art of sandwich making. It takes a steady hand, a sharp mind and a keen sense of balance to create true culinary perfection.": "サンドイッチ作りという崇高な芸術を真に理解できる者は少ない。安定した手、鋭い頭脳、そして繊細なバランス感覚が必要だ",
  "Once, I made a sandwich so amazing that my name is forever inscribed in the ^orange;Hall of Sandwiches^reset; on Cygnus Igni IV. Look it up. There's even a ^red;#$@%%$^reset; statue and stuff.": "かつて、俺があまりにも素晴らしいサンドイッチを作ったので、シグナスVにある^orange;サンドイッチの殿堂^reset;に永遠に名前が刻まれた",
  "For the bread? Rye of course. Not just any rye, though. Not that garbage Jesson used to sell down by the market. I mean real Rye. Stuff like Garla always has. Fresh. Succulent.": "パンは？もちろんライ麦だ。ただのライ麦じゃない。ジェソンが市場で売ってたゴミみたいなやつじゃない。本物の",
  "From there, you need to set aside the loaf for a bit. You need to let it wait, anticipate your intentions. So for now, lets move on the the Horkulbeast. Get it fresh. It won't be cheap.": "そこから、パンを少し置いておく必要がある。お前の意図を察知させるんだ。だから今は、",
  "The difference in the meat quality though...that's unmistakeable. You won't ever want to eat another thing again, I promise you that. Once I add the rest of the ingredients...mmmmm.": "肉の品質の違いは…間違いようがない。他のものは二度と食べたくなくなる、約束する",
  "Garlic, you ask? Hell yes there is garlid. As much as we can muster. We want about 4 cloves. Trust me here, any less is criminal. Set a pan out, turn on your burner and add some oil while it warms.": "ニンニクかって？もちろんだ。できる限りたっぷり。4片くらい欲しい。信じろ、それ以下は",
  "We're going to fry the horkulbeast now, at about medium for 3 minutes a side. While it cooks, mash up the garlic and add it in. Then we just need one more thing.": "ホルクルビーストを中火で片面3分ずつ焼く。焼いている間にニンニクを潰して加える",
  "What is it you ask? Why obviously thats love and tenderness! You wanna cook that stuff up for 3 mins per side, flipping only once.": "それは何かって？もちろん愛と優しさだ！片面3分ずつ、返しながら焼くんだ",
  "Just before you're about to take that horkulbeast, egg and garlic medley off the burder be sure to flap your arms like a bird and screech like a norlaac in mating season.": "ホルクルビーストと卵とニンニクのメドレーをバーナーから下ろす直前に、必ず鶏みたいに腕をバタバタさせろ",
  "Kevin knows his stuff. Don't question the genius here: Next I got a nice spoonful of antimatter. I added that to 3 ounces of snarshed soda crackers.": "ケビンは分かってる。この天才を疑うな。次にスプーン一杯の反物質。それを3オンスに加えた",
  "Now I needed to toast that bread. Then it was a simple matter of farlixxing the qualtross-barr barrier using the flesh-engine.": "パンをトーストする必要があった。それからフレッシュ・エンジンを使ってクォルトロス・バー・バリアをファーリックスするだけだった",
  "Then I combined all that crap. The perfect, sapient, singing sandwich. It looked amazing, by the way. Truly astonishing. The screams when devoured...less so.": "そして全部合わせた。完璧で、知性ある、歌うサンドイッチ。見た目も最高だった。本当に驚異的だ",
  "I gave up that noble profession, however. My true interest lay down the path of knowledge and understanding. I even invented the ^cyan;Kill-Pod^reset; in ^red;Strawberry^reset;!": "しかし俺はその高貴な職業を捨てた。俺の真の興味は知識と理解の道にあった。発明までしたぞ",
  "And now I'm here. At least until I no longer am. Thankfully that can't happen without a Quintex Obliterator, and those aren't invented yet. Did I miss anything?": "そして今ここにいる。少なくとも、いなくなるまでは。幸いそれにはクインテックス・オブリタレーターが必要で、あれは",
  "My fellow citizens... Our collective worlds face a threat unlike any we've seen before. Five major Protectorate hubs have been destroyed in the last month!": "市民の皆さん…我々の世界は、かつてない脅威に直面しています。先月だけで5つの主要なプロテクトレート拠点が破壊されました！",
  "The time for action has come. We must join forces now to repel this strange new enemy and stop fighting amongst ourselves over petty nonsense, lest we face unparalleled danger.": "行動の時が来た。この奇妙な新たな敵を撃退するため今こそ力を合わせ、些細なことで争うのをやめなければ、前例のない危機に直面することになる。",
  "If we do not engage immediately we risk total annihilation! We cannot let whatever this...thing...is tear our noble republic apart!": "直ちに交戦しなければ全滅の危機だ！この…ものが…高貴なる共和国を引き裂くのを許すわけにはいかない！",
  "To combat the threat, I suggest a toxin derived from a rare substance known as Protheon. With it we could weaponize our greatest tool...": "脅威に対抗するため、プロシオンという稀少な物質から派生した毒素を提案する。これで我々の最大の道具を兵器化できる…",
  "The ^orange;Matter Manipulator^white;. Properly infused, it could halt the spread of ...": "^orange;マターマニピュレーター^white;。適切に注入すれば、拡散を止められるかもしれない…",
  "Huh? What was that? Security, could you perhaps take a look?": "え？今のは何？警備員、ちょっと見てきてくれないか？",
  "NO! It's HERE! ^orange;Everyone FLEE!^reset;": "いけない！ここに来た！^orange;全員逃げろ！^reset;",
  "You, Agent! Take the Manipulator and run! Get to safety!": "君、エージェント！マニピュレーターを持って逃げろ！安全な場所へ！",
  "50% of Pixels Lost": "ピクセルの50%を失った",
  "Housing Request": "住居申請",
  "Buildingbuildingbuildingbuildingbuildingbuildingbuildingbuildingbuildingbuildingbuildingbuilding. The voices tell me to build, so I build. If I had ^red;my own workshop with access to an Elder Altar^reset; I could build even greater temples.": "建てる建てる建てる建てる建てる建てる建てる建てる建てる建てる建てる建てる。声が建てろと言うので建てる。^red;エルダーの祭壇にアクセスできる自分の工房^reset;があれば、もっと偉大な寺院を建てられるのに。",
  "Atropus: Worlds of Meat": "アトロパス: 肉の世界",
  "Little is known of what have been dubbed 'Atropus' worlds. The reference to atrophy is apt, for the innate strangeness of these celestial bodies cause murmurs of fear in every known species inhabiting the galaxy. Many theorize these fleshy worlds are sapient. Preposterous, but people will always be superstitious. Still, one must give credit where it is due: These places are unsettling.": "「アトロパス」世界と呼ばれるものについてはほとんど知られていない。萎縮への言及は適切で、これらの天体の固有の奇妙さは",
  "The stench can only be tolerated for so long. Eventually the rankness permeates even the most adequate protections. At that point it becomes almost impossible to keep a mask on. Involuntarily, you will eventually try to pry it off, despite knowing the air makes you crazy. The team has dubbed it 'the meat fever' and it is liable to be the death of us if care is not taken.": "悪臭に耐えられるのはここまでだ。やがて腐臭はどんなに適切な防護も浸透する。その時点で",
  "Atropus Research Notes": "アトロパス研究ノート",
  "Taylor was able to sedate me in time to prevent total loss of the digit in question. I regret it, but at the time I was just so hungry...something kept compelling me to eat meat at any cost, immediately. I felt that I had no choice but to obey.": "テイラーが間に合って鎮静剤を打ち、問題の指の完全な喪失を防いでくれた。後悔しているが、あの時はとにかく空腹で…何かがどんな犠牲を払ってでも即座に肉を食べるよう強要し続けた。従うしかないと感じた。",
  "I was not prepared for the bizarre place. Simply breathing the air caused immediate loss of mental acuity, and mild hallucinations began mere seconds after exposure. As time progressed the symptoms increased in severity. Within 30 seconds I was substantially less capable of cohesive thought and at one point attempted to ingest my own finger.": "その奇妙な場所に備えができていなかった。空気を吸うだけで即座に精神の鋭さを失い、軽い幻覚が始まった。",
  "Rumors": "噂",
  "There are rumors that Atropus worlds are not individual entities, but rather, parts of a singular one scattered throughout the cosmos. If this were true, how unimaginably vast would such a being be? What would its purpose be?": "アトロパスの世界は個別の存在ではなく、宇宙中に散らばった一つの存在の部分だという噂がある。もし本当なら、そのような存在はどれほど想像を絶する広大さだろうか？その目的は何か？",
  "Breakthrough!": "大発見！",
  "Unfortunately, we're going to need a lot more samples to prove our theory. I might suggest sending in some ground crews in the near future to see what else we can pull from these seemingly living worlds.": "残念ながら、理論を証明するにはもっと多くのサンプルが必要だ。近い将来、地上クルーを派遣して、この一見生きている世界から他に何が得られるか調査することを提案する。",
  "I am absolutely positive that these samples taken from fifteen separate Atropus worlds share the same DNA sequences in common, Gina. Take a look at the structure here, in diagram A. Note that compared to every sample from group C! Something is strange here and I think we may be on the verge!": "ジーナ、15の別々のアトロパス世界から採取されたこれらのサンプルが同じDNA配列を共有していることは絶対に確実だ。図Aの構造を見てくれ。グループCの全サンプルと比較してみろ！ここには何か奇妙なことがあり、我々は突破口に立っていると思う！",
  "Black Stars": "ブラックスター",
  "...The larger question still remains, however: What are Black Stars? How do they fail to generate any real light and yet maintain orbits and gravity...and allow for life in their sphere of influence? None of it makes any sense and there must be -some- sort of sense to it. And yet...conventional physics cannot adequately explain it. Not even Denshubbs Law of Matter can apply to them in full, a fact that still baffles science to this day.": "…しかしより大きな疑問が残る：ブラックスターとは何か？どうやって実際の光を生成せずに維持しているのか",
  "Travel Log: Penumbra 1": "旅行記: ペナンブラ 1",
  "This shouldn't be too bad; just need a good suit of armor and a nice sidearm. I'll keep my homing device ready in case I must beam up fast.": "そこまでひどくないはず。良い防具とサイドアームがあればいい。素早く転送する必要がある場合に備えてホーミング装置を準備しておこう。",
  "Day 1 - \nI saw a weird planet on my system scanners and decided to explore it. My SAIL did not know what to make of it, and scanning the planet revealed it to be perpetually in semi-darkness due to the composition of its atmosphere, and also that it had a plethora of ore: Titanium, Thorium, Neptunium, and even some minerals that have never been discovered before. If I could get my hands on some of this stuff, I bet I'd be rich! Atmosphere scans show that other than the strange gasses that prevent light from getting through, the air at ground level is actually breathable and of favorable temperature.": "1日目 -\nシステムスキャナーで奇妙な惑星を見つけ探索することにした。SAILもどう解釈すべきか分からず、スキャンでは",
  "Travel Log: Penumbra 2": "旅行記: ペナンブラ 2",
  "Day 2 - \nBeamed down on this strange planet to find myself surrounded by some of the weirdest foilage -- tree-like plant structures that have big round glowing skyblue bulbs on them, small little flowers that glow with light. I also keep hearing distant sounds, rustling of weeds, but I can't see more than a few feet in front of me, even with a flashlight. I think I'm going to start digging down into the ground, maybe board the exit off behind me. I don't want to get pulled into the jungle by some nasty beast or something.": "2日目 -\nこの奇妙な惑星にビームダウンすると、最も奇妙な植生に囲まれていた — 木のような植物構造",
  "Travel Log: Penumbra 3": "旅行記: ペナンブラ 3",
  "This place is fascinating, I'm definitely saving these coordinates to come back here later. I just want a sample of this ore SAIL told me about...": "ここは魅力的だ。後で戻ってくるために座標を保存しておこう。SAILが教えてくれた鉱石のサンプルが欲しいだけなんだ…",
  "Day 3 - \nI found a small natural cave system, and decided to take a rest. The rock found on these planets is unusually hard, and it has this weird property that absorbs light. Even shining my flashlight directly at this rock, I can't see very much of anything around me as the rock appears to eat the light coming out of my flashlight. I lit a campfire in here, after I felt a breeze slipping through the cracks, hopefully I don't choke myself with the smoke. I can see more caves below, I'll explore those in a minute.": "3日目 -\n小さな自然の洞窟系を見つけ、休憩することにした。これらの惑星の岩は異常に硬く、",
  "Travel Log: Penumbra 4": "旅行記: ペナンブラ 4",
  "Day 4 - I found a solid metal of a sort. It remains translucent but glowing, even in darkness. Whether it is metal or crystal, I can't tell. I'm glad it's here though, because I can see some movement in the darkness around me. Little glowing eyes are peering from the shadows...": "4日目 - ある種の固体金属を見つけた。暗闇でも半透明のまま光っている。金属かクリスタルかは判断できない。しかしここにあって嬉しい。周囲の暗闇に動きが見えるからだ。小さな光る目が影から覗いている…",
  "Travel Log: Penumbra 5": "旅行記: ペナンブラ 5",
  "Whatever that stuff was I now I feel sick in the stomach. I already threw up twice. I need to get back out of here...back to the surface. It gets worse by the moment, and unless I get help I fear I may die.": "あの物質が何であれ、今お腹が気持ち悪い。もう2回吐いた。ここから出なければ…地上に戻らないと。一刻一刻悪化しており、助けがなければ死ぬかもしれない。",
  "Day 5 - Yuck. While trying to get away from the sea of transparent metal, I found myself in another cave system, the floor of which oddly did not absorb my light like the rock had before. I probably should have been more careful, but one step on this stuff, and I found myself sliding down a steep incline, and when I landed, I bounced around the room several times and wound up face-first in some of the most disgusting tar-like substance I've ever seen! I managed to somehow crawl out of the junk and back up onto more rock.": "5日目 - うえ。透明な金属の海から逃れようとしている時に、別の洞窟系に入った。床は",
  "Travel Log: Penumbra 6": "旅行記: ペナンブラ 6",
  "Day 6 - \nI found it! Too bad I am so deep in, I'm not sure I could possibly get back out. I found the ore... you can't miss it. It glows with this gentle sky-blue color, lighting entire cave systems up. For some weird reason, the rocks that ate my flashlight beams, don't eat this type of light. I wish I could get a sample of this to a lab... but sadly I don't think I'm going to make it. If anybody finds this... please... take this book back to Earth and give it to my family...\n - M. Hodgins": "6日目 -\n見つけた！こんなに深くまで来てしまい、戻れるか分からないのが残念だ。鉱石を見つけた…見逃しようがない。",
  "The Agarans": "アガラン族",
  "To read this codex, use your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset; and click the Book icon.": "このコデックスを読むには、^orange;パーソナルトリコーダー^reset;を使用してブックアイコンをクリックしてください。",
  "The origin of the Agaran species has long been disputed. There are many factors at play in the ongoing argument, but the largest contributor to their mystery is how they disperse themselves through the cosmos. While the rest of us require ships and technology, Agarans are able to simply ^green;emit a spore cloud^reset; and eventually some will find their way through the atmosphere due to their unusually resilient structure.\n\nEven more unusual is how difficult these spores are to even examine! The structure of these spores is ever-shifting which makes any detailed analysis slow-going. We've been able to come to several conclusions based on the evidence presented thus far however:\n\n- All Agarans are quite fatally affected by any atmosphere lacking nitrogen. Any such place results in their eventual suffocation, and that's if they are able to survive the blistering that accompanies it (both interally and externally).\n- An Agaran is not merely hard to understand - their ability to create sounds relies on swift vibrations that creates a hum-like sound. Our translators are not able to mimic these tonal emissions. This makes the species quite unintelligible.\n- They are linked directly to Florans at the genetic level, despite having a completely re-arranged set of internal organs (and some new organs the purpose of which we can only guess). It is believed that spores affected Florans, and genetically mutated their hosts bodies.\n- The spores emitted from an Agaran are able to track sources of warm moisture (especially blood) from several kilometers away and use wind to reach their target. While not sapient, it is most certainly some sort of behavior previously not displayed by this sort of organism.\n\nThe spores emitted by these creatures can prove ^red;exceptionally^reset; fatal, and any individual killed by these spores will become a host to a parasite within. This parasite will immediately 'hijack' the hosts central nervous system. At this point the Agaran conciousness is born. I advise any explorers that notice a clan of this species to stay clear for this reason. There are tales of entire colonies being decimated in a matter of days by spore clouds.": "アガラン種族の起源は長い間議論されてきた。議論には多くの要因が絡み合っているが、最大の謎は彼らが宇宙中にどのように広がるかということだ。他の種族が船や技術を必要とするのに対して、アガランは単純に^green;胞子を宇宙に放出する",
  "Test Template": "テストテンプレート",
  "^orange;Title^reset;\n\n   We use ^green;text^reset; to convey information.\n\n\n   ^cyan;I am a section header^reset;\n\n   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.": "^orange;タイトル^reset;\n\n 私たちは^green;テキスト^reset;を使って情報を伝えます。\n\n\n  ^cyan;セクションヘッダー^reset;\n\n ヘッダーの下のテキストです。お前の母ちゃんは子犬が嫌いだ。",
