pies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.   And I am text under the header. Your mom hates puppies.": "^orange;タイトル^reset;\n\n   情報を伝えるために^green;テキスト^reset;を使います。\n\n\n   ^cyan;セクションヘッダー^reset;\n\n   ヘッダーの下に入るテキストです。あなたのお母さんは子犬が嫌い。   ヘッダーの下に入るテキストです。あなたのお母さんは子犬が嫌い。   ヘッダーの下に入るテキストです。あなたのお母さんは子犬が嫌い。   そして私は",
  "Gemcrafting": "宝石細工",
  "What are you looking at? I'm not finished yet.": "何を見てる？まだ終わってないぞ",
  "An Amazing Fact": "驚くべき事実",
  "001 ^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : ^yellow;^reset;Core Guide^yellow;^reset;": "001 ^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : ^yellow;^reset;コアガイド^yellow;^reset;",
  "This guide will brief you on what you need to know to play with Frackin' Universe effectively. You need to keep in mind that a lot of the default play of Starbound has been altered by many aspects of the mod. \n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;The Tricorder - Your Best Friend:\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nThis device is the ^cyan;singlemost useful item in your inventory^reset; at any time. It provides access to the ^orange;Research System^reset;, along with numerous other functions accessed via the icons on its screen. It also has the following additional functions:\n\n^green;Right Mouse Button^reset; - Accesses the Quest tracker. This will provide you access to the FU tutorials and a wealth of useful rewards. It's well worth your time.\n\n^green;Shift + Click^reset; - Accesses the Configuration menu. Through this you can customize your Matter Manipulator output, and can even swap your own chosen tools into slots normally occupied by the paintbrush, wire tool, etc. Very handy. Using this, you can make the Tricorder a permanent hotkey item!\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Research? What do you mean, Research?^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nFrackinUniverse now introduces a progression overhaul we've called the ^orange;Research System^reset;. Accessed through your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset;, ^orange;SAIL Computer^reset; or ^orange;Quickbar^reset; , it is the sole means by which you learn new blueprints for crafting. To unlock new blueprints you'll need resources as well as the important currency known as ^green;Research^reset;.\n\nThrough this system, you'll be able to custom-tailor the new unlocks you want and in the order you choose to pursue them.\n\n\nYou gain ^green;Research^reset; at a rate of 1 every second, passively, as long as you are playing. This rate increases by +1 per planet tier. Thus, a Threat 6 planet will provide 7 total passive gain.\n\nYou can also gain ^green;Research^reset; through other means, including:\n^cyan;Laptops and Data Centers^reset;\n^cyan;Fossil Collection^reset;\n^cyan;Microscopes^reset;\n^cyan;Having high Madness^reset;\n^cyan;Certain armor and gear^reset;\n^green;Protheon / 10^reset; (to a maximum of +10)\n\nIn short, play and experiment and you'll get all the research you need. ^red;NOTE: Research gain slows down while you are not exploring. AFK collection to easy-mode progression will not work.^reset;.\n\nIf you have unlocked things that ^red;should^reset; appear at a station but do not seem to: Be sure you have ^orange;upgraded^reset; the station. That still needs to be done to create higher-tier items.\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;What the heck is Protheon^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nA rare currency resource, it will allow you to procure tons of Research by converting it at certain shops or processes. It can affect you in other ways when amassed, however, allowing you to work Madness off at a much faster rate (especially in an Insta-Freud) as well as increase your Research gain rates.\n\nObtaining this Protheon resource will require artifacts and luck.\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Racial Abilities^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\nEach of the various species in the FU universe has different gameplay mechanics. Some are more resistant to fire, while others might have special powers or are really good with swords. This provides players with many new gameplay options.\n\n^yellow;I don't want to play with racial abilities^reset;!\n\nYou can enable and disable racial abilities from within your ^orange;ship SAIL computer^reset;. Simply access it, press the ^green;[ MISC ] ^reset;button and choose to disable the option.\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Special Techs^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\n^orange;Tech Usage Costs^reset;\nCertain techs in FU consume Food instead of Energy, if applicable, to a certain threshold. Past that threshold, they will drain Energy, and in some cases health!\n\n^orange;Directional/Cursor Aim Techs^reset;:\nThese techs are used with ^green;Head Tech Key^reset;, either tapped or held.\n^orange;Directional Aim Techs^reset; are aimed by holding ^green;movement keys^reset; and can fire in 8 different directions! To aim straight up or down hold the ^green;Walk^reset; key.\nIn FU, these techs use Directional Aim: Hunter/Razor/Miner Claw.\n^orange;Cursor Aim Techs^reset; need no fancy keys, and simply fire toward your cursor!\nIn FU, these techs use Cursor Aim: Psychic/Shard Blast, Acid Spit. Additionally, Shard Blast allows a fully randomized spread by holding ^green;Walk^reset;, while Acid Spit will fire a tile destroying glob instead of a caustic missile.\n\n^orange;Tech Scaling^reset;:\nCertain techs scale with your stats! Some are listed here for convenience.\n^orange;Shadowborne^reset;: Scales with Max Energy.\n^orange;Acid Spit^reset;: Scale with Bonus Health. Caustic missile deals DoT damage, tile destroyer deals damage and lasts longer.\n^orange;Miner Claws^reset;: Scales with current Food level.\n^orange;Psychic Blast^reset;: Scales with Max Energy and Defense.\n^orange;Razor^reset;/^orange;Hunter Claws^reset;: Hunting damage that scales with Max Health, Power and current Food level.\n^orange;Elduu'khar Burst^reset;, ^orange;Shard Blast^reset;, ^orange;Dragonfire^reset;: Scale with Max Energy, Defense and current Food level.\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Combat^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nSee FU Guide: Battle\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Mechs^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nMechs are not the same as you're used to in Starbound. They now ^red;require fuel^reset;, and can be refueled with many types. In addition, they have separate Health from their Fuel/Energy bar. The end result is a much more useful vehicle that can extend mining trips and greatly improve survivability in harsh environments.\n\nMechs now ^green;calculate their Mass^reset;. ^cyan;Heavier^reset; mechs are able to ^green;stomp and do massive damage^reset; to the ground as well as having better armor. ^cyan;Light^reset; mechs are ^green;much faster^reset; and have vastly ^green;improved fuel efficiency^reset;.\n\nYour mech can ^green;Sprint^reset; by double-tapping ^cyan;A^reset; or ^cyan;D^reset;.\n\nYour mech can switch to ^green;Flight Mode^reset; by double-tapping ^cyan;W^reset;.\n\nThere are dozens of new types of mech part, including Mech Modules. These act like Augments for your Mech and can allow a great amount of customization. There's a mech part for your playstyle.\n\nRefuel or Re-equip your mech through your ^orange;Personal Tricorder^reset;.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Status Effects^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nFrackinUniverse adds a ^green;great number^reset; of new Status Effects, beneficial and harmful, that can affect characters and monsters alike. Most can be resisted or ignored with the proper equipment.\n\nPart of the experience is learning how to survive in new environments through experimentation and ingenuity, and strategizing your ^orange;Research^reset; around it.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Madness^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nAnother form of currency in FrackinUniverse. It can be gained from many actions (most commonly the bizarre or terrifying) but will also fade away with time. The more ^#e43774;Madness^reset; you possess, the greater the negative effects you experience.\n\nCarrying around terrifying things in your bag can also result in gaining ^#e43774;Madness^reset; over time. Pay attention if SAIL warns you of this.\n\nThere are more than 50 possible effects of ^#e43774;Madness^reset;.\n\n^yellow;How do I lose madness?^reset;\n\nSpending your ^#e43774;Madness^reset; on ^green;Research^reset; in ^orange;Metaphysics^reset;\nShip Counsellor Crewmates\n^orange;Instafreud^reset; machines, when sat in, will rapidly consume madness.\n^green;Protheon / 10^reset; (to a maximum of -10)\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Genes^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nThis currency replaced the ^red;33 separate Gene items^reset; used from 2014-2020. Now, a singular form of ^green;Gene^reset; is used, making tracking your totals much easier and giving you more than 30 less resources to store.\n\n^green;Genes^reset; are used for ^orange;Agriculture^reset; and ^orange;Genetics^reset;.\n\nYou can trade in your current genes for the new currency by simply placing them into a Xeno Lab or Sprouting Table.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;BYOS (Build your own Ship)^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nIn FrackinUniverse, you can create your own ship from the ground up. This system means you no longer need to purchase Ship Upgrades, as any expansion is done by yourself. You'll also need to craft your own engines and will be able to craft special equipment to benefit your ship.\nNote that if you select BYOS mode at character creation, this choice is permanent.\n\nAt Character Creation, you can select ^cyan;Frackin Ship^reset; or ^cyan;Vanilla Ship^reset;. The Frackin Ship is the BYOS option. Once you make this choice, you're given options for starting ship configurations. Once they make this choice, they begin play like usual.\n\nCrew use special rules on these ships:\n\nYou can use ^orange;Crew Deeds^reset;, which follow the same rules as ^orange;Colony Deeds^reset; (Walls, Door, Lights, Bed) ^red;\n\n-or-\n\n^reset; you can opt to use ^orange;Crew Beds^reset; if quick-and-dirty with little planning is more your style.\n\nYou can ^red;not^reset; use both a ^orange;Crew Deed^reset; and ^orange;Crew Bed^reset; together in the same room.\n\nThere is a hard-cap of 12 crew. Mods that increase crew limits likely will not operate properly with BYOS.\n\nBYOS ships have additional options in construction, namely better engines and thrusters that can prove useful in exploration.\n\n\n\n^red;'Help, I have BYOS lag!' ^reset; or  ^yellow;I don't want atmosphere effects on my ship^reset;!\n\nBYOS has an atmosphere mode you can enable and disable from within your ^orange;ship SAIL computer^reset;. Simply access it, press the ^green;[ MISC ] ^reset;button and choose to disable the option.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^cyan;Swimming^reset;\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nSwimming operates differently than you're used to:\n\nSwim : ^yellow;W A S D^reset;\n\nJump Out : ^green;hold ^yellow;W^green; , press ^yellow;Spacebar^reset;.\n\nIt will take you a bit to get used to it, but the end result is a much easier control experience.\n\nNote that not all liquids provide buoyancy like water or other similar fluids. In these liquids, or within gases, physics can behave quite different than expected.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;The Frackin Wiki\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nIf you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here:\n^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset;\n\n^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.": "このガイドはFrackin' Universeを効果的にプレイするために必要な知識を解説します。Modによってスターバウンドのデフォルトのプレイが多くの面で変更されていることを念頭に置いてください。\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;トリコーダー -",
  "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Biomes": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : バイオーム",
  "There are new worlds across the cosmos awaiting exploration. The next few pages will detail some of them. Note that there are many more than listed.\n\nBiomes can appear around different types of stars, and some appear only in specific stars. For example: You will never find an ^orange;Infernus^reset; around a ^white;Gentle Star^reset;.\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Star Types^reset;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nGentle Star\nTemperate\nRadioactive\nFrozen\nFiery\nBinary\nRed\nBlue\nBlack\nDying\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Bog^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nRich in algae, muck, and plant life. They are ripe with rainy weather, and thick swamps. Travel can be difficult, but the surplus algae will be useful.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Rainforest^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nTeeming with plantlife, Rainforests have rich soil, far exceeding the capacity of ordinary dirt. They host a wide array of wildlife, including plenty of bees.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Crystalline^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nA rich source of silicon (thanks to the extraction of Purple Crystal) and ^yellow;Lunari^reset; crystals. Watch out for the crystal rain, though.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Gelatinous^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nGreat for genetic material. Definitely don't try the lettuce, unless you really like flavorless gelatin soup squishing in your mouth. If you need goopy stuff, this is your first stop.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Proto World^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese bizarre planets are not inhospitable, but the natural biological slime there can melt your flesh. Plus the slime storms, ew. And really, really weird plant life. But they are the only place to get the extremely valuable protocite. You'll need it. Also be advised that the atmosphere contains bizarre bacteria that affect unconditioned lifeforms negatively. Use caution when exploring.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Ice Waste^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nIce wastes are absolutely terrifyingly cold. Don't swim in the water or you'll freeze even faster. They do have some unique sorts of ice there, which provide something extra when extracting. Furthermore, valuable Isogen ore is plentiful on them.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Sulphuric^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese are among the harshest environments you'll encounter. Every moment on a sulphur world is lethal. Deadly winds, blowing debris, no oxygen. Lovely. But, they are extremely rich in Sulphur. Not the place for a summer house, though. Yet people keep trying...\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Penumbra^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nPitch black for most of their existence, these rare worlds have some sort of environmental barrier to the sun. A natural sunglasses-effect in the ozone, or something. Whatever the case...dark and spooky.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Wasteland^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nOnce bustling populations lived on these desolate rocks. Now, their ruins stud the surface like discarded refuse. Technology may remain that can be scavenged, and there is no shortage of Spare Parts if you are looking for some.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Irradiated^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese radioactive rocks are curiously abundant in native life. Granted, it's not edible and you still don't want to hang out there too much. You'll find heaps of radioactive resources here, obviously.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Infernus^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nI'd not suggest going here without a lot of protection. Their surfaces are far from hospitable. They are teeming with danger of every sort, but the allure of Pyreite ore is hard to resist.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Frozen Moon^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese frigid moons are quaint, and not altogether threatening. No life walks on their surfaces. On account of the whole no-air thing.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Nitrogen Sea^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nDoesn't this sound like a fun place to swim? Yea, it really isn't. Some handy liquid there, though.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Cybersphere^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nSomeone, at some point, built these impossibly huge constructs in space. How these were ever engineered remains a hotly contested debate among the scientific community.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Primeval Forest^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nHuge trees, lots of wildlife and abundant natural resources make these a wonderful place to visit. Typically not too dangerous, but watch your back anyhow...you never know what lurks in these huge forests. I've heard rumors of titanic reptiles standing 10 or more metres in the air!\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Atropus^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nA violation of all things decent, Atropus planets are both living and dead. They are quite literally composed of flesh, and some even believe them to be sentient. How they are even possible remains unknown but there is no doubt it is unnatural in every sense of tthe word.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Mountainous^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nWhile it is probably fairly obvious by the name, I have been instructed to inform you that these worlds are rather bumpy and mountainy. They are rich in resources, possessing more metal than most biomes (other than Sulphuric) including rare Zerchesium ore.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Tidewater^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nThese oceans are vastly more rocky and unstable than typical water planets. They generally lack tropical islands, but if you love rocky terrain and coral reefs they might be right up your alley. Through Tidewater, explorers have found unusual nodules capable of scientific miracles.\n\n\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\n^green;Lightless^white;\n^blue;------------------------^reset;\nThese unusual worlds are ancient and something prevents any sun from reaching their surfaces. There may be some useful things there, however. Bring lots of lights!\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;The Frackin Wiki\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nIf you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here:\n^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset;\n\n^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.": "宇宙には探索を待つ新しい世界がある。次のページではその一部を詳しく説明します。ここに列挙されているよりもはるかに多くのバイオームが存在することに注意してください。\n\nバイオームはさまざまな種類の恒星の周りに現れ、特定の恒星にのみ現れるものもあります。例えば、^orange;インフェルヌス^reset;",
  "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Stats": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : ステータス",
  "In addition to stats normally present in Starbound, FU adds a host of its own as well. Some may be character stats, some may be weapon stats. Some may be both! They are detailed within this guide for easy access later.\n\n^green;Charisma^white; - When shopping on FU space stations, Charisma helps you to make a profit by influencing ^cyan;Selling and Buying^reset; values. A high charisma means a high income ratio! Note that this only applies on Space Station trades and their related Kiosks for the time being. As a special note, every 33% charisma will allow you to bring an additional crewmember with you in the field. Be warned, penalties to charisma can have the opposite effect!\n\n^green;Stun Chance^white; - With blunt weapons, each hit has a chance to stun enemies. Likewise with successful shieldbashes. This stat influences the chance that this stun will occur. This also can occur with daggers, rapiers, and a few other weapons.\n\n^green;Shieldbash Chance^white; - When blocking with your shield, you have a chance to shieldbash. This stat influences the chances that the bash succeeds.\n\n^green;Shieldbash Push^white; - How far a shieldbash will push an enemy, and how much damage it will inflict when successful.\n\n^green;Projectile Count^white; - Typically only seen as a stat on weapons, it is indicated in most gun tooltips by 3 diagonally aligned bullets. This indicates how many projectiles are fired at once.\n\n^green;Burst Count^white; - Exclusively on weapons. Indicated in the tooltip by a spread of 4 small bullets. These weapons fire a burst of projectiles in sequence.\n\n^green;Tech Bonus^white; - There are various types of Tech Bonus. These will be listed when relevant. Any such bonus will influence techs. For example 'Jump Tech +25%' increase the efficiency of any Jump related techs by that amount.\n\n^green;Weapon Mastery^white; - Occasionally you'll find gear that can grant 'Weapon Mastery' at different levels. Weapon Mastery provides additional benefits to particular weapons.\n\n^green;Crit Chance^white; - The likelihood that you will score a successful critical attack with your weapon. Note that this can be a stat on both you -and- on a weapon. They will combine.\n\n^green;Crit Damage Bonus^white; - The total bonus applied, in percentage, to critical damage strikes.\n\n^green;Leech^white; - A form of healing that is unaffected by normal healing modifiers. This healing is divided over a duration (10 seconds at base); +10% leech means you will heal up to 1% of your health per second for 10 seconds per instance.\n\n^green;Maximum Leech^white; - The maximum amount of healing you can have at a time, from leech. The default is 10%; from all leech instances you will not be able to heal more than 10% of your health per second.\n\n^#e43774;Madness^white; - A measurement of your current sanity. The higher the value, the crazier you are. More than 50 effects can occur from madness, and not all are bad. You can spend Madness in the ^#e43774;Metaphysics Research Tree^reset;.\n\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;The Frackin Wiki\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nIf you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here:\n^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset;\n\n^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.": "スターバウンドに通常存在するステータスに加えて、FUは独自のステータスも多数追加しています。キャラクターステータス、武器ステータス、またはその両方が存在します。後から参照しやすいようにこのガイドで詳しく説明しています。\n\n^green;カリスマ^white; - FUの宇宙ステーションで買い物をする際、カリスマが役立ちます",
  "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : 4": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : 4",
  "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Environments": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : 環境",
  "FrackinUniverse adds a great number of additional status effects, environmental hazards and environmental interactions. These can be both detrimental or beneficial depending on circumstances. This short guide should help to sort them out for you. Click next page to continue.\n\n\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Resistances^reset;:\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\n   Your resistance to effects is a pretty big deal. Bear in mind that the ^cyan;higher your value^reset; in a resistance type, the ^cyan;less you are affected by various debuffs as well as damage of that type^reset;. ^red;Weakness^reset; plays a factor too.\n\n   ^orange;Example^reset; :\n\n   A Floran has ^red;-50% Fire Resistance^reset;. He will take ^red;50% more damage from fire^reset; and will need an ^orange;additional 50% resistance^reset; in order to negate the penalty. That means that if a biome has a 40% resistance requirement for immunity to its effects he will ^orange;actually need 90%^reset;.\n\n   On the other hand, should your race have a ^cyan;bonus against elements^reset; you will need ^orange;less resistance^reset; than the normal amount. A race with ^green;+30% to Fire Resistance^reset; would need ^green;30% less resistance to fire effects in order to gain immunity^reset;. This allows you to have native immunity to minor effects such as desert heat or minor cold.\n\n^cyan;All resistances stack^reset;.\n\n\n   ^blue;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   As a general rule, assume resistance for biome types works as such:\n\n   ^green;20%^reset; (Mild) / ^yellow;40%^reset; (Moderate) / ^orange;60%^reset; (Extreme) / ^red;80%^reset; (Lethal)\n\n   Note that severe storms and other factors can influence the potency of a biomes effect, so on occasion you will have increased requirements while the event transpires.\n\n   Enemies can ^yellow;also have resistance strengths and weaknesses^reset;. Some are utterly immune to particular elements but easily felled by another, so be prepared to experiment.\n\n\n\n   ^blue;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Weather^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Various types of weather exist that can cause you harm. All can be resisted with a relevant protection type. Electrical storms are blocked by electric resistance, poison gas by poison, and so on. Some are less obvious however, such as Aether sickness, which requires specialized immunity from armor or augments.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Tile Breaking^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   If you're falling a bit too fast, some tiles will be unable to bear the strain of your weight. Ice, glass, slime, mud and other materials can break on impact. So, watch your step and take care.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Tile Effects^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Some tiles give buffs or debuffs when stepped on. Many of these will not give indicators, but will affect your movement. Snow, mud, jungle dirt and clay are some examples of this in action. Asphalt increases your ground speed, which is useful in bases. Experiment, and you might find some really useful stuff.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Temperature^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Cold, Heat and Radiation are things from ordinary Starbound, true. But in FU they play a different role. You won't find many Immunity effects on EPP packs. Instead, you'll primarily be using ^cyan;resistances^reset; obtained from them or augments. The higher your resistance in an element, the less it will bother you (or be blocked completely). Resistances stack.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Desert Heat^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Deserts are typically dry and non-humid, and their heat will slowly sap your health and food. From noon till sundown, it will be at its worst. Nights are relatively harmless and cool. Underground is colder. You can resist Deserts with Fire Resistance.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Jungle Heat^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Much like deserts, the heat of a Jungle will gradually drain your health and food, and is less severe at night. Unlike Desert Heat, it will take Physical resistance to counter this effect.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Radiation^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Radiation can be rather hazardous to the unprepared. This nasty effect will drain your health and energy rapidly (your max health/energy, not your current amount). If you reach 0 max health, you will die without warning...so do keep an eye on yourself. You will also starve faster. Wind will make things worse for you. Resistance requires Radioactive Resistance.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Sulphuric^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Sulphuric effects can be nasty, rapidly eating your armor and then doing health damage. Worse, on sulphuric worlds you have storms to contend with that make this effect even more dangerous, acid rain and pools of caustic acid! To resist this effect you'll need ^orange;Physical resistance^reset; or an ^orange;acid immunity^reset; effect.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Proto-Poison^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   This nasty effect is a threat on Proto Worlds. It will slowly sap your maximum health and *will* eventually kill you. Furthermore, it will reduce your critChance and apply damage over time. Seek out ^orange;proto-poison protection^reset; from various gears in your lab stations, ^orange;poison resistance^reset;.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Insanity^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   A constant degradation of your mental state, insanity saps your ability to protect yourself over a sustained period by draining your Protection. Additionally, it gives a mild bit of damage per tick. Your brain will become muddled and you will hallucinate, and go hungry faster. Augments and armor exist to combat this nasty effect, or you could have decent resistance to ^orange;both Shadow and Cosmic^reset; and you'll be okay.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Pressure^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Perhaps the deadliest of all the status effects, extreme pressure will ^red;definitely kill you in seconds^reset; if you do not have protection. Thankfully, it is found in few places (primarily on Gas Ball biomes). ^orange;Do not risk this environment effect without a protective suit^reset;. You *will* die.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Poison^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Fairly self explanatory. You don't want to be poisoned, but some are worse than others. You've got basic poisoned, mercury poison (which is especially nasty), contaminated water, food poisoning and darkwater poison to name a few. ^orange;Poisoned immunity or resistance^reset; will do the trick in avoiding this particular set of hazards. Potent poisons require higher amounts of resistance.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Pus^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   This fluid is absolutely repulsive, and even having the stuff on you causes retching and nausea. To traverse it, you will need some sort of ^orange;physical protection^reset;. This acidic bile is not your friend. I recommend against ingesting it.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Black Tar^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Black tar slows you down ^red;a lot^reset; and makes jumping a decent height nearly impossible. It hampers, but does not directly cause damage. You can block it with various armors or produce.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Gas^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   Gas can be both positive (Helium 3) or negative (Caliginous Gas, Hydrogen etc) to immerse yourself in. Blocking gas is generally straightforward...^orange;wear something that protects from gas^reset;. However, Some are more specialized. ^orange;Caliginous Gas requires Shadow Resistance^reset; and ^orange;Poison Gas is non-functional with high poison resistance^reset;.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Organic Soup^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   One of the few effects that is actually something you *want*. Organic soup will increase your health total as well as remove the effects of hunger (and even fill you up!). Take a bath in it when you can!\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Bio Ooze^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   This fluid will stick to you, make you ill and affect your movement and survival chances while active. Wearing protection is recommended. Most common on Proto Worlds and a few other select biomes. Can be ^orange;blocked or mitigated with Poison Resistance or Immunity^reset;.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Liquid Nitrogen^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   I hear its a bit cold, so stepping in this might just be a crappy idea for fun times. However, you can make it a joyously fun event by simply wearing adequate ^orange;Ice Resistance^reset;.\n\n\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Darkness^reset;\n   ^#555555;-----------------------------------^reset;\n\n   There is darkness capable of permeating your vision centers and turning the world around you into a lightless expanse. Be wary of these effects. Thankfully, it is most common in places that are already dark.\n\n\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\n   Note that there are many other effects you can be affected by in your exploration of the universe. Not all of them can be resisted, and some might be resisted by surprising things. Just stay aware...and stay safe.\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^yellow;The Frackin Wiki\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\nIf you need the help of a Wiki, use our ^cyan;official wiki^reset; here:\n^green;frackinuniverse.miraheze.org^reset;\n\n^red;Do not^reset; use the Fandom wiki. It is horribly outdated.": "FrackinUniverseはステータス効果、環境的危険、環境との相互作用を多数追加しています。状況によって有害にも有益にもなり得ます。この短いガイドが整理の助けになるでしょう。次のページに進んでください。\n\n   ^blue;-------------",
  "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Food and Armor": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : 食料と防具",
  "Use the Enhanced Codex Viewer to read this. Access it in your Tricorder.": "拡張コデックスビューアーで閲覧できます。トリコーダーからアクセスしてください。",
  "FrackinUniverse adds a large amount of armors (and foods) and enhances some older ones, allowing for a greater variety of playstyles. These can be very useful through gameplay and provide exceptionally useful benefits!\n\n^yellow;Set Bonus Inheritance^reset;: As an important note, armors that are used to craft other armors can still be used to complete armor set bonuses for sets that were used in the crafting chain, so partially upgrading your set is still viable.\n\n^orange;Stats^reset; : Vanilla players may notice there are more than they are used to, and even the ones they are used to have different ranges. FU presents a wider variety of armor classes to spice up your play, and does the same with food.\n\nIf you are more interested in damage, pick up Power Armor or Hyper Power Armor to trade defensive stats for offensive ones. Alternatively, pick up Tank or Hyper Tank sets to outlast your enemy. They come in melee OR ranged! Fighting not quite your thing? Pick up an Exploration oriented set, and be at home in your environment! You're guaranteed to locate a set that suits your playstyle somewhere out there!\n\n^orange;Resistances^reset; : Many armors in FU come with inherent resistances. Many biome weather effects will simply stop affecting you once you hit an appropriate amount, and various enemy attacks will do less damage. Nifty, right? It gets better; upgrade your armor, and those resistances will increase!\n\n^orange;Bonuses^reset; : Most are increases to your stats, plenty are conditional.\nAny that say ^green;+value^reset; are typically additive increases. It can be a little confusing, however. As example: if it gives +^green;3^reset;% Crit Chance it increases your crit chance by a flat 3%, but if it says +^green;3^reset;% Energy Regen, that's 3% of your base. The easiest way to remember is to ask yourself...does it have a base of 0? If so, it likely is like Crit Chance! If a bonus says x^green;1.3^reset;, or ^green;More^reset;, that's a multiplier on the value you currently have. Have 1000% Damage somehow? 100% More (or 2x) would make it 2000%! Small note: Regen is usually per second.\n\nOf course, some bonuses have hidden components we couldn't easily include, for tooltip space.\n Additionally, there are some other phrase uses to note. If a set bonus states that it grants immunity to ^green;ALL^reset; of a related effect, that typically means all biome weather ^orange;as well as^reset; specific status effects related to that element. For heat, that includes burning and even lava! For radiation, that includes rad-burn.\nAs a small side-note, some terms or symbols are used loosely. If you see a bonus with x/y, that means the bonuses are different based on how their conditions are met. For weapons, this means how many of that type. If you see something like (Machine) Pistols, that means the bonus applies to Machine Pistols OR Pistols. This is typically done for tooltip space.\n\n^cyan;Mining Sets^reset; :\n Mining laser sets grant a lot more mining laser damage...but that bonus is reduced significantly if you are pairing them with something else. Using a mining laser with a pistol, as example: 2x Mining Laser Damage becomes 1.25x.\n^orange;Colors^reset;: Colors are important in identifying and understanding bonuses. To start with, set bonuses are identified by a ^yellow;^reset;, while a ^green;^reset; is only visible in crafting interfaces to display resistances. If a bonus stat is ^green;GREEN^reset;, that means it is a good thing. ^red;RED^reset; means it is a bad thing. ^cyan;Cyan^reset; is for bonuses that are binary. They typically do not stack with similar effects. This will be especially apparent with various foods...so choose carefully. It is worth noticing that there is ONE exception to the rules regarding colors: Glow. If you see Glow in a color, that is usually the color of the glow effect.\n\n^orange;Special Bonuses^reset; : Some sets have special bonuses that don't really display much information due to lack of space, an unfortunate limitation of the game. Here, some bonuses will be explained.\n\n^cyan;Adaptive Armor^reset;: Multiplies the wearer's total defense based on current health percentage, scaling between the left value at 20% health and the right value at 100% health.\n\n^cyan;Auto-Medic^reset;: More complicated than ordinary regeneration, this effect will restore more health per second at the cost of an equal percentage of energy. It will also decrease energy regen and increase energy regen lock-out multiplicatively at 2x the heal percent.\n\n^cyan;Thorns^reset;: a nova of thorns when hit, ^cyan;Fire Burst^reset; makes a nova of fire instead.\n\n^cyan;Summons Minions^reset;: summons short-lived allies to fight alongside you or distract enemies. These minions scale based on the lowest armor's tier, so upgrading it is essential! Upgrade ALL of the pieces.\n\n^cyan;Life/Energy Shell^reset;: Gain damage absorption (shell) which scales based on a resource (health, energy) to protect your health, comes with a matching overhead bar to indicate its state. Regenerates quickly if you haven't taken damage recently. ^cyan;Shell Immunities^reset; are granted only while the shell holds. The numbers on the effect's label indicate the conversion rate relative to the resource's stats. In order: capacity, regeneration rate, and the delay upon taking damage before it begins regenerating.\n\n^cyan;Life Shell^reset; specific: Regeneration rate is a direct percentage of health per second, lockout is in specified seconds.\n\n^cyan;Energy Shell^reset; specific: Regeneration rate is a percentage of the energy regeneration stat, base vanilla regeneration is 58.5% per second. Special note due to balance: Minimum lockout time of 0.5 seconds, and a maximum regen rate of 50% per second.\n\n^cyan;Gravity Normalization^reset;: Personal gravity too low? Up it goes. Too high? Down instead. Exception: Zero-gravity.\n\n^cyan;Vital Power^reset; and ^cyan;Juggernaut^reset;: these effects are set bonus exclusive, and quite powerful; they grant one stat based on a percent of another. Vital power grants power as life, Juggernaut grants life as power.\n\n^cyan;Undying Resolve^reset;: increases Protection as your life gets lower, up to the stated amount, while ^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset; grants HP Regen instead. If a set grants either, it will grant ^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset; to your pet.\n\n^cyan;Dark Commander^reset;/^cyan;Beast Master^reset;: Increases Damage, Protection, HP and Speed of your pets (both) and crew (Dark Commander) by the listed percent, increases their jump ability by half of that, and regenerates HP at a sixth of that amount per second.\n\n^cyan;Capturenaut^reset;: Increases pet count by 1, plus an additional 1 per 2 tiers (up to +2) of the lowest equipped set piece. Grants an additional +1 if using alongside the back item. This means a fully upgraded set will allow up to 5 additional pets!\n\n^red;Wretchel Toxicity^reset;: Ingesting Wretchel reduces core stats and healing received, and drains health over time. These effects increase in severity the more you consume in a short time frame, as well as while your health is critically low. It will ^red;KILL^reset; you, if you are careless.\n\n^cyan;Charisma^reset;: Your ability to bargain with Traders at space stations. The higher your charisma, the better the deal (and fatter your bank balance!)\n\n\n\n^cyan;Pet/Crew Stat Inheritance^reset;:\nOverall scaling is as follows: HP, directly from your character, rather than just equipped armor. Protection: applied as a multiplier to HP via a specific formula. Damage: directly from character sheet. Health Regen: Inherits as a flat amount, except in special cases (^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset;, effects not covered by FU, etc.). If you have 100 health and 10% HP Regen, it will grant your pet 10 HP per second. If a stat isn't here, a pet most likely does not inherit it.\n^yellow;Special notes^reset;: Be mindful when taking powerful buffs like ^cyan;Glass Cannon^reset;, as it will reduce their health noticeably.": "FrackinUniverseは大量の防具（および食料）を追加し、古い防具の一部を強化することで、プレイスタイルの幅を広げています。これらはゲームプレイを通じて非常に便利で、有用な恩恵をもたらします！\n\n^yellow;セットボーナス継承^reset;：重要な注意点として、使用する防具は",
  "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Battle": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : 戦闘",
  "View in your Tricorder Codex tab in the 'FU' section.": "トリコーダーのコデックスタブにある「FU」セクションから閲覧できます。",
  "^orange;Monster Resistances^reset;\n------------------------\nSome monsters resist, or are completely immune to, certain types of damage.\n\nTo combat these threats you are going to need weapons of ^green;different elemental types^reset; at any given moment. Try to use ^green;at least 2 to 3^reset; of the more than 8 available types so you are ready for any challenge.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\n\n^orange;Weapons and Combat^reset;\n----------------------\nRanged and Melee weapons behave a little differently in FrackinUniverse. The most important changes are listed in this codex.\n\n\n^orange;Crit Chance and Crit Damage^reset;\n---------------------------\nWeapon item tooltips have new icons. The two on the left represent Critical Chance bonus and Critical Damage bonus.\n\n\n^orange;Ammo and Reload Speed^reset;\n---------------------------\nAmmo and Reload speed are represented by the right-side icons.\n\nItems with a '--' representing a value in any of the above stats means it does not apply to them. This is the case with modded weapons, or energy-only (non-ammo) guns, primarily.\n\n\n^orange;Mastery^reset;\n---------------\n\nOccasionally, you'll see Mastery traits applied to equippable gear, or in Racial Bonuses. These imply that you have greater capability in a particular weapon type. Generally speaking, ^yellow;Masteries^reset; simply ^cyan;improve already existing weapon benefits^reset; including Tech bonuses. In an upcoming topic below, you'll see various weapons listed along with the various capabilities each carries with it. These listed benefits will all be improved through ^yellow;Mastery^reset;.\n\nAn example: When wielded individually a Rapier will provide an increase to Crit Chance when timing strikes carefully (to a max of 5). The amount of the bonus applied is higher by the amount listed in your ^yellow;Mastery^reset; stat. At 100% this would mean a maximum Crit Chance bonus of +10.\n\nThe amount of benefit gained can vary from weapon to weapon. In some cases you will get a modifier based directly on your ^yellow;Mastery^reset; trait, while others will reduce that value by half, quarter, eigth or other such fractions.\n\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n\n\n^green;Ranged^reset;\n----------------------------------\n\n^orange;Ammo-Based Weapons^reset;\n------------------\nSome weapons now use ammunition. Don't worry, you won't need to carry resources around with you to refill them. These weapons simply use much, much less energy in exchange for the mobility boost provided by having extra energy! Note that their alt fires will always require energy, regardless of their primary fire.\n\nYou can reload these weapons manually by holding the SHIFT key and clicking the mouse button. Emptying the magazine through shooting will also automatically engage the reload.\n\n^orange;Ammo Mastery^reset;\n------------------\nThis Mastery is quite straightforward: your rating in Ammo Mastery directly correlates to the % reduced from your Reload Time as well as the $ of ammo gained per magazine.\n\n^orange;Pistol^reset;\n------------------\nWith mastery applied, Pistols gain increased Damage, reduced reload time and a higher critical strike chance.\n\n^orange;Machine Pistol^reset;\n------------------\nWith mastery applied, Machine Pistols gain increased Damage, reduced reload time and a higher critical strike chance.\n\n^orange;Arm Cannon^reset;\n------------------\nWith mastery applied, Arm Cannons provide varied benefits based on how they are wielded. Power, Crit Chance, Crit Damage and Protection are all impacted. When using just arm cannons (dual or single) you get less protection benefits but a much higher critical chance. With an armcannon and shield you gain a much better protection bonus in exchange for reduced power.\n\n^orange;Assault Rifle^reset;\n------------------\nAssault rifles benefit from mastery by increasing overall damage output while increasing magazine size and critical damage.\n\n^orange;Sniper Rifle^reset;\n------------------\nWith a mastery in Sniper rifles you gain magazine size and critical chance. This stacks with the usual crit benefits of sniper rifles and allows for a very high crit chance with charge-ups!\n\n^orange;Grenade Launcher^reset;\n----------------------\nWhen wielding grenade launchers with mastery expect to gain increased damage and magazine size while also benefiting from reduced reload time.\n\n^orange;Rocket Launcher^reset;\n----------------------\nObliterating the enemy is easy with mastery in rockets! You'll do a lot more damage, reload faster and have increased magazine size.\n\n^orange;Shotgun^reset;\n----------------------\nThese dangerous weapons, when mastered, profice exceptional crit chance and power along with increased magazine size and reduced reload time.\n\n^orange;Magnorb^reset;\n----------------------\nThese unusual weapons provide increased damage, crit chance, crit damage and energy to masters that wield them.\n\n^orange;Bow^reset;\n----------------------\nBows have a large number of benefits masters can take advantage of. Crit damage and crit chance increase, along with damage. In addition, they can fire bows faster and shoot arrows farther while consuming less energy!\n\n^orange;Whip^reset;\n----------------------\nWhip users get a sizeable increase in crit chance and crit damage while also increasing damage output with this mastered weapon.\n\n\n^blue;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^green;Melee^reset;\n\n^orange;Combos^reset;\n---------------\nEach strike of a combo, whether or not it hits a target, consumes 1% of your energy. If your energy is expended, you will no longer be able to combo and will instead perform frenzied normal attacks.\nBe warned, tactics involving stun-locking enemies are no longer as viable.\n\nMany weapons with combos provide additional bonuses when striking with these combos.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Shield Bash^reset;\n---------------\nBlocking with shields on enemies has a chance to Shield Bash. Certain gear can increase the Shield Bash chances.\n\nShield Bash can damage foes, and send them reeling backwards. When Perfect Blocking, there is a 50% chance to Stun foes that are successfully bashed. When not perfect blocking, be wary: There is a chance -you- will get stunned on a badly timed block.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Hammer^reset;\n---------------\nThe longer you hold the charge of this melee weapon type, the higher your Critical and Stun chance get (to a maximum of ^green;100^reset;%).\n\nA hammer charged above ^green;75^reset;% will inflict a massive bonus eruption capable of stunning and tossing foes around.\n\nOver-Charging the hammer past ^green;100^reset;% will automatically cancel the bonus.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Great Axe^reset;\n---------------\nThe longer you hold the charge of this melee weapon type, the higher your Critical Chance and Critical Damage get (to a maximum of ^green;100^reset;%).\n\nA greataxe charged above ^green;75^reset;% will inflict a massive bonus eruption capable of bleeding and tossing foes around.\n\nOver-Charging the greataxe past ^green;100^reset;% will automatically cancel the bonus.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Axe^reset;\n---------------\nEach consecutive kill made with an axe increases your maximum damage by +^green;1^reset;%, to a maximum of ^green;50^reset;%.\n\nIf your health is reduced below ^red;20^reset;%, this bonus is cancelled.\n\nEach consecutive hit in a row with an axe increases Crit Chance by +^green;3^reset;% (to a maximum of ^green;15^reset;%)\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Dagger^reset;\n---------------\nConsecutive rapid kills temporarily increase damage\n\n+^green;25^reset;% Dodge Tech Efficiency\n\nCombo Strikes increase Protection and Crit Chance with each strike. The protection bonus is greatest on First Strike, and reduces each hit thereafter.\n\n^cyan;Dual-Wield (Melee):^reset; +^green;5^reset;% Movement Speed\n\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Shortsword^reset;\n---------------\n+1 Combo strike (was 2, now 3)\n\nEach combo hit increases your Crit Damage amount\n\n+^green;1^reset;% Crit Chance per Combo Strike\n\nFirst Combo strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage. Second hit does +^green;25^reset;% Crit Damage.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Broadsword^reset;\n---------------\nKills made in rapid succession increase defense for a short time\n\n+^green;1^reset;% Crit Chance per Combo Strike\n\nFirst Combo strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage. Second hit does +^green;25^reset;% Crit Damage.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Scythe^reset;\n---------------\n+^green;1^reset;% Crit Chance per Combo Strike\n\nFirst Combo strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage. Second hit does +^green;25^reset;% Crit Damage.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Longsword^reset;\n---------------\n3rd Combo Strike does +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage\n\n^cyan;Single Longsword^reset;: -^green;30^reset;% Combo Cooldown\n\n^cyan;Longsword + Shield (Dual Wield)^reset;: +^green;4^reset;% Shield Bash, +^green;1^reset; Shield Bash Push Distance, +^green;15^reset;% Healing Tech Efficiency, +^green;25^reset;% Defense Tech Efficiency\n\n^cyan;Longsword + Any Weapon (Dual Wield)^reset;: Defense x^red;0.8^reset;, +^green;5^reset;% Movement Speed\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Rapier^reset;\n---------------\nWhen wielding a rapier, the longer you wait between swings the higher your critical strike chance becomes (to a maximum of 5). Attacking resets this bonus.\n\n^cyan;Single Rapier:^reset; +^green;15^reset;% Crit Damage, +^green;35^reset;% Dodge and Dash Tech Efficiency\n\n^cyan;Rapier + Dagger (Dual Wield):^reset; x^green;1.12^reset; Protection, +^green;15^reset;% Dodge and Dash Tech Efficiency\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Shortspear^reset;\n---------------\n^cyan;Single Shortspear^reset;: +^green;30^reset;% Crit Damage\n\n^cyan;Shortspear + Shield^reset;: +^green;10^reset;% Shield Bash, +^green;2^reset; Shield Push Distance, Shield Regen x^green;1.2^reset;, +^green;50^reset;% Defense Tech Efficiency\n\n^cyan;Shortspear + Shortspear (Dual Wield)^reset;: Defense x^red;0.8^reset;, Bonus Crit Chance x^red;0.5^reset;\n\nShort Spears also count as Hunting weapons.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Spear^reset;\n---------------\nSpears are relatively straightforward. They gain crit chance, higher damage output and an increase in Dash Tech efficiency.\n\nSpears can be held out by holding the fire button to help keep enemies at bay. If using a Lance typed spear you also gain increased damage based on your movement speed while holding it out. It cannot be aimed during this.\n\nSpears also count as Hunting weapons.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Quarterstaff^reset;\n---------------\nEach hit with a combo increases your Defense.\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Mace^reset;\n---------------\nCombo strikes increase Stun Chance by 2% per hit.\n\n^cyan;Single Mace^reset;: +^green;2^reset;% Stun Chance\n\n^cyan;Mace + Shield^reset;: +^green;3^reset;% Shield Bash, +^green;1^reset; Shield Push Distance, Defense x^green;1.1^reset;\n\n^cyan;Mace + Any Weapon (Dual Wield)^reset;: Bonus Crit Chance x^red;0.85^reset;, Bonus Stun Chance x^red;0.5^reset;, +^green;5^reset;% Movement Speed\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Katana^reset;\n---------------\nEach swing grants a Movement Speed bonus of ^green;1 + (combo step / 10)^reset;%\n\nCombo hits increase knockback resistance\n\n^cyan;Single Katana^reset;: +^green;15^reset;% Defense Tech Efficiency\n\n^cyan;Katana + Heavy Melee (Dual Wield)^reset;: Damage x^red;0.8^reset;, Defense x^red;0.9^reset;\n\n^cyan;Katana + Light Melee (Dual Wield)^reset;: Energy x^green;1.15^reset;, +^green;20^reset;% Crit Damage, +^green;25^reset;% Dodge and Dash Tech Efficiency\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Fists^reset;\n---------------\n\nNormal attacks consume ^red;3% energy^reset; per attack. Holding the button will activate this mode.\n\nCombos require timing: Holding or tapping the button too rapidly will use a normal attack.\n\nCombo strikes increase Crit Chance by ^green;1%^reset;, Stun chance by ^green;4%^reset; and Protection +1 per strike. When attacking, they use ^red;1%^reset; energy.\n\nAlt/Finisher is activated with ^cyan;[Shift + Click]^reset;. Outside of a combo this will use ^red;15%^reset; energy. When completing a combo as the last strike, it will consume none.\n\n\n^#555555;--------------------------------------------------^reset;\n^orange;Addendum^reset;\n---------------\nBonus Crit/Stun Chance refer to stats that are not inherent on the weapons themselves, such as from armor or consumables.": "^orange;モンスターの耐性^reset;\n------------------------\n一部のモンスターは特定のダメージタイプに耐性があるか、完全に免疫です。\n\nこれらの脅威に対抗するためには、どんな場面でも^green;異なる属性の武器^reset;が必要です。^green;少なくとも2〜3種類^reset;",
  "^#ffea00;FU Guide^reset; : Generators and You": "^#ffea00;FUガイド^reset; : ジェネレーターの使い方",
  "In Frackin' Universe, there are many generators and power sources to fuel your labs and factories. In this codex, each type of generator, its functionality and its mechanics are described.\n\n\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^pink;A Note on Batteries^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nEight kinds of batteries can be crafted in Frackin' Universe. These store energy and dispense it as needed at any level of power, allowing even a weak generator to fuel a very power-hungry machine, if only slowly.\n\nIt is always beneficial to use a battery in any power setup, no matter how small or how large, and it will help eliminate problems where a generator produces power at a different rate than the machine expects it.\n\n\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^white;Table of Contents^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\n^green;Renewable Power^reset;\n  ^#F9F193;Solar Panels^reset;\n  ^#AA6DFF;Nocturn Panels^reset;\n  ^#BBE5E8;Wind Turbines^reset;\n\n^#FF612F;Fuel-Based Generators^reset;\n  ^#BA893F;Alternator Generators^reset;\n  ^gray;Combustion Generators^reset;\n  ^pink;Neuro-Psionic Generators^reset;\n  ^#8CBEF2;Quantum Reactors^reset;\n  ^#FFC600;Precursor Reactors^reset;\n\n^yellow;Decay-Based Generators^reset;\n  ^red;Hydraulic Dynamos^reset;\n  ^#CEF400;Fission Reactors^reset;\n  ^#B7E3E5;Small Fusion Reactors^reset;\n  ^cyan;Large Fusion Reactors^reset;": "Frackin' Universeには、ラボや工場に電力を供給するための多くの発電機や電源があります。このコーデックスでは、各発電機の種類、機能、仕組みについて説明しています。\n\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^pink;バッテリーについての注意点^reset;\n   ^blue;-----------------------",
  "^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^green;Renewable Power^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nGreen energy. Low-powered, situational, inconsistent but completely free to operate, renewable energy is suitable for low-power setups or where power is needed infrequently enough that it can be left to build up in a battery for later use.\n\nIf intending to explore renewable energy sources it's recommended to craft the Weather Beacon, researched in the initial node of the ^orange;Electronics tree^reset;. It can be used to determine the power output of renewable energy sources placed at that location, to determine the suitability of the planet.\n\n\n^#F9F193;Solar Panels^reset;\n\nSolar panels come in three varieties. The ^#F9F193;Solar Panel^reset;, ^orange;Solar Array^reset; and ^red;Solar Tower^reset;. When placed on a planet, they generate power during the day and when the natural light is bright enough - up to ^#F9F193;4W^reset;, ^orange;10W^reset; and ^red;24W^reset; respectively on a typical planet, such as a Lush world. On some rare planet types, the light can exceed normal levels and produce significantly more power. Artificial light sources cannot power a solar panel, and panels will not function when submerged in liquid.\n\nOn a ship, space station, or in a star-orbiting asteroid belt, there is no day-night cycle and so solar panels will always produce a fixed amount of power - ^#F9F193;3.5W^reset;, ^orange;8.75W^reset; and ^red;21W^reset; respectively. They're a much more reliable source of energy when the sun never sets.\n\n\n^#AA6DFF;Nocturn Panels^reset;\n\nSimilar to solar panels, Nocturn Panels care about the level of light falling upon them. Unlike solar panels, however, Nocturn Panels fear the light and thus produce more energy in a darkened space - up to ^#AA6DFF;10W^reset; in the pitch black. Nocturn Panels are perfectly content underground and do not care whether it is day or night. They're happy to be contained within a lightless box, producing the same level of power eternally, but they do not function when submerged.\n\nNocturn Panels are the product of ^orange;maddened research^reset;, and function anywhere.\n\n\n^#BBE5E8;Wind Turbines^reset;\n\nWind Turbines come in one variety, which can produce up to ^#BBE5E8;12W^reset; in ideal conditions. The amount of power produced depends on how windy the current weather is, and the types of weather available depend on the planet. Some planet types have eternally windy weather and will produce a constant ^#BBE5E8;12W^reset; of power, while some will never produce any power at all, and others will vary. Experimentation and the Weather Beacon will help identify the best planets for wind power.\n\nWind Turbines do not function on ships, space stations, and in asteroid belts.": "^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^green;再生可能エネルギー^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nクリーンエネルギー。低出力で状況依存、不安定ですが完全に無料の再生可能エネルギーは、低電力設備や電力が不定期にしか必要でない場面に適しています",
  "^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^#FF612F;Fuel-Based Generators^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nBad for the environment and good for your factory, fuel-based generators are the backbone of any serious early- to mid-game lab or factory, producing significant power.\n\nAll fuel-based generators work using a Heat system. When fuel is first placed in the generator, or it is turned on, it will consume one fuel item and begin heating up. Its heat level, which reaches maximum productivity after 18-20 seconds, either partially or fully determines the power output of the generator. In some generators the chosen fuel determines only how quickly the generator consumes fuel, and in some the chosen fuel also provides power on top of that generated by its heat.\n\nWhen a fuel-based generator is turned off, by supplying an 'off' signal to its first blue input node, it will finish consuming its current fuel item before ceasing operation to avoid wasting fuel.\n\n\n^#BA893F;Alternator Generators^reset;\n\nThe first generator a player will gain access to. The Alternator Generator can only consume wood and coal, though these materials are abundant on most worlds. The Alternator Generator will only produce ^#BA893F;4W^reset; at full heat (reached after 18s), and so it should be quickly replaced by the ^gray;Combustion Generator^reset; or another power source.\n\nAccepted fuels (burn time):\n----------\nWooden Log (10s), Coal (16s), Golden Wood (20s), Redwood Bark (20s), Penumbral Bark (30s), Alien Weird Wood (40s), Energy Wood (50s), Aen Wood Log (60s)\n\n\n^gray;Combustion Generator^reset;\n\nA serious power source for a growing industrialist, the Combustion Generator accepts the greatest variety of fuels of any generator and can produce a respectable amount of power from both solid and liquid fuels, including wood, erchius and fuel canisters. The Combustion Generator produces ^gray;12W^reset; of power at full heat (reached after 18s).\n\nAccepted fuels (burn time):\n----------\nPaper (1s), Unrefined Wood (2s), Wooden Log (5s), Coal (8s), Hydrogen (9s), Methanol (9s), Liquid Erchius Fuel (10s), Oil (10s), Redwood Bark (10s), Biofuel Canister (10s), Crystal Erchius Fuel (12s), Unrefined Fuel (13s), Refined Fuel (15s), Penumbral Bark (15s), Golden Wood (15s), Erithian Biofuel Canister (15s), Protocite Fuel Canister (20s), Alien Weird Wood (20s), Energy Wood (25s), Erchius Crystal (25s), Aen Wood Log (30s), Crunchy Chick (30s)\n\n\n^pink;Neuro-Psionic Generators^reset;\n\nThe product of ^orange;maddened research^reset;, Neuro-Psionic Generators use neurological power, drawn from stolen brains, to fuel your mad experimentation. Brains are a plentiful resource with the right equipment, and so a budding mad scientist can easily provide for all their power needs if they're not afraid to get their hands dirty. Neuro-Psionic Generators can produce ^pink;60W^reset; of power at full heat (reached after 18s).\n\nAccepted fuels (burn time):\n----------\nInferior Brain (10s), Superior Brain (20s), Artificial Brain (60s), Perfect Brain (60s), Psi-1 Energy (60s), Psi-2 Energy (80s), Psi-3 Energy (100s), Psi-4 Energy (120s), Brain in a Jar (200s), Superior Brain Housing (360s), Artificial Brain Housing (360s), Advanced Brain Housing (520s)\n\n\n^#8CBEF2;Quantum Reactors^reset;\n\nAn incredibly efficient and powerful generator, a single Quantum Reactor is sufficient to power a substantial lab all by itself, and can be trivially powered by infinitely-obtainable fuel sources in the late game. The Quantum Reactor's output depends on its fuel source, and can reach ^#8CBEF2;620W^reset;, of which ^#8CBEF2;20W^reset; is heat built up over 20s of use.\n\nAccepted fuels (power, burn time):\n----------\nBiofuel Canister (60W, 40s), Erithian Biofuel Canister (70W, 50s), Uranium Rod (70W, 50s), Energiflower (80W, 60s), Plutonium Rod (80W, 60s), Helium-3 (90W, 70s), Liquid Protocite (100W, 80s), Neptunium Rod (110W, 90s), Thorium Rod (110W, 90s), Energy Wood (125W, 105s), Enriched Uranium Rod (150W, 130s), Essentia Obscura (170W, 150s), Protocite Fuel Canister (220W, 200s), Enriched Plutonium Rod (240W, 220s), Metallic Hydrogen (275W, 255s), Deuterium Rod (300W, 280s), Tritium Rod (320W, 300s), Solarium Star (470W, 450s), Ultronium Rod (520W, 500s), Liquid Metallic Hydrogen (570W, 550s), Liquid Deuterium (620W, 600s)\n\n\n^#FFC600;Precursor Reactors^reset;\n\nThe most powerful generator in the game bar none, Precursor Reactors create phenomenal amounts of power but cannot be crafted, and are instead found in the abandoned colonies and factories of the extinct Precursors. Unlike other generators, they have an additional requirement - to channel the power sources of the ancients, you must place one Neutronium Rod and one Anti-Neutronium Rod, both products of ^orange;maddened research^reset;, in the designated slots. For your trouble, Precursor Generators can produce up to ^#FFC600;1055W^reset; depending on their fuel source, of which ^#FFC600;95W^reset; is heat, reaching their full output (50%+ heat) after 20s.\n\nAccepted fuels (power, burn time):\n----------\nPoop (135W, 40s), Crunchy Chick (195W, 100s), Essentia Obscura (315W, 220s), Quantum Fluid (515W, 420s), Ultronium Rod (745W, 650s), Dimensional Cell (1055W, 960s)": "^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^#FF612F;燃料系発電機^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\n環境には悪いですが工場には最適な燃料系発電機は、初期から中期にかけての本格的なラボや工場の中心的存在で、大量の電力を生産します。\n\nすべての燃料",
  "^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;Decay-Based Generators^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\nMake sure to dispose of the waste cleanly (or profitably). Decay-based generators output power by gradually and randomly consuming isotopes over time. Uniquely, these generators come with multiple fuel slots, giving them the ability to vary their power output by filling the desired number of slots to adapt to any required workload without changing the fuel type, though each fuel slot may use different fuel if desired.\n\nDecay-based generators will turn off immediately when an 'off' signal is supplied to their first blue input node, and will not waste fuel in doing so.\n\n\n^red;Hydraulic Dynamo^reset;\n\nAn honourable inclusion, the Hydraulic Dynamo is an early-game generator that evaporates water using hot solids and liquids (or liquid nitrogen) in order to generate power. Although very large, it outperforms many other early generators despite being craftable on the first world and fuelled by trivially-obtainable substances such as lava and core fragments. The Hydraulic Dynamo can generate up to ^red;21W^reset; at maximum output, but will not function without water, consuming one for each fuel item used. The Hydraulic Dynamo has three fuel slots.\n\nAccepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time):\n----------\nLava (4W, 10s), Core Fragment (5W, 40s), Liquid Iron (6W, 32s), Volatile Powder (7W, 40s), Scorched Core (7W, 180s), Liquid Nitrogen (6W, 20s)\n\n\n^#CEF400;Fission Reactors^reset;\n\nGood old-fashioned nuclear power, the greenest thing about it is the uranium it consumes. Fission Reactors are an affordable way to create significant amounts of power, reaching up to ^#CEF400;360W^reset; across their four fuel slots. Uniquely, this generator creates Tritium Rods as a by-product of its fission, with a 50% chance for one to be made each time a fuel item is consumed. It will also create Toxic Waste, two if Tritium is created and one otherwise. While active, depending on how long it's been operating and how much power it's generating, the Fission Generator will begin to flood its nearby area with Moderate Radiation, up to 16 tiles away. Walls and other containment will not block this, only distance and Moderate Radiation immunity will help.\n\nAccepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time):\n----------\nTritium Rod (10W, 40s), Deuterium Rod (15W, 50s), Uranium Rod (20W, 90s), Plutonium Rod (30W, 90s), Neptunium Rod (40W, 90s), Thorium Rod (50W, 90s), Enriched Uranium Rod (60W, 120s), Enriched Plutonium Rod (80W, 180s), Solarium Star (80W, 240s), Ultronium Rod (90W, 300s)\n\n\n^#B7E3E5;Small Fusion Reactors^reset;\n\nHarness the power of the stars for your lab, albeit on a very small scale. Fusion Reactors of both kinds fuse light isotopes together, releasing nuclear energy from them to create power. Like the Fission Reactor, Fusion Reactors generate Moderate Radiation the longer and more productively they operate, which cannot be blocked. Small Fusion Reactors have four fuel slots, and can generate ^#B7E3E5;360W^reset; when filling all of them. They must be given coolant to continue operating or will quickly overheat and shut down, releasing a burst of radiation, though water is typically sufficient. Each consumed fuel will create one Toxic Waste, which can be used as coolant in a pinch.\n\nAccepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time):\n----------\nHydrogen (15W, 50s), Tritium Rod (25W, 60s), Helium-3 (45W, 80s), Solarium Star (55W, 150s), Deuterium Rod (60W, 120s), Ultronium Rod (90W, 700s)\n\nAccepted coolants (heat reduction per item)\nToxic Waste (10), Salt Water (30), Water (30), Liquid Nitrogen (80), Cryonic Extract (125)\n\n\n^cyan;Large Fusion Reactors^reset;\n\nOriginally pioneered by the Skath, Large Fusion Reactors are simply better-built, scaled-up versions of Small Fusion Reactors with a greater power output. Filling their four slots, they can generate up to ^cyan;600W^reset;. They generate radiation and produce Toxic Waste as Small Fusion Reactors do.\n\nAccepted fuels (power per fuel slot, average decay time):\n----------\nHydrogen (35W, 50s), Tritium Rod (55W, 60s), Helium-3 (60W, 80s), Solarium Star (105W, 150s), Deuterium Rod (90W, 120s), Liquid Deuterium (90W, 120s), Ultronium Rod (150W, 700s)\n\nAccepted coolants (heat reduction per item)\nSalt Water (20), Water (30), Toxic Waste (40), Liquid Nitrogen (80), Cryonic Extract (125)": "^blue;------------------------^reset;\n   ^yellow;崩壊系発電機^reset;\n   ^blue;------------------------^reset;\n\n廃棄物はきちんと（または有益に）処理してください。崩壊系発電機は、同位体を時間をかけてランダムに徐々に消費することで電力を出力します。独特な点として、これらの発電機は",
  "Fleshweaving Quarterly": "肉織り季刊誌",
  "A colorful magazine loaded with all sorts of wonderful sewing and decorative craft instruction. Every single object is crafted in flesh from other races, which is likely quite upsetting if you are not a Floran. Of note, three separate articles detail removing flesh from a still-living 'donor'.": "あらゆる素敵な裁縫と装飾工芸の指導が詰まったカラフルな雑誌。全てのオブジェクトが他の種族の肉で作られており、フローランでなければかなり動揺するだろう。特筆すべきは、まだ生きている「ドナー」から肉を剥がす方法を詳述する3つの別々の記事だ。",
  "Floran Delicacies": "フローランの珍味",
  "A Floran cook-book. It features a myriad of recipes, all carnivorous in nature. Each recipe section corresponds to a different sentient species. This has resulted in it being banned from the majority of Protectorate space.": "フローランの料理本。肉食性のレシピが無数に載っている。各レシピセクションは異なる知的種族に対応。その結果、プロテクトレート宙域の大部分で禁書となっている。",
  "Origins IV": "起源 IV",
  "The gift of fire was given to the Eld'uu in an age before warmth ever touched this planet.": "炎の贈り物は、温もりがこの惑星に届くよりも前の時代にエルドゥーに与えられた。",
  "For aeons, our people had wandered aimlessly through the dark with only the crystals to guide them, clinging to each other to survive in the harsh landscape.": "長い年月、我が民はクリスタルだけを頼りに暗闇をあてもなく彷徨い、過酷な環境で生き延びるために互いにしがみついていた。",
  "The Lotus took pity on our struggling race, and, descending from a bright light in the sky, she touched the foreheads of two Eld'uu. One male, one female.": "蓮は苦闘する我が種族を哀れみ、空の明るい光から降り立ち、二人のエルドゥーの額に触れた。男一人、女一人。",
  "In her gentle voice, she urged the pair to spread their gift, to restore the cold, unforgiving landscape of our planet.": "優しい声で彼女は二人に贈り物を広めるよう促した。冷たく容赦ない惑星の風景を回復するために。",
  "For a time, peace and prosperity was the order, the Eld'uu had found a way of survival through these two chosen.": "しばらくの間、平和と繁栄が秩序であり、エルドゥーはこの二人の選ばれし者を通じて生存の道を見出していた。",
  "It was not to last.": "それは長くは続かなかった。",
  "A lurid magazine": "扇情的な雑誌",
  "This rather...revealing publication appears to contain humans in various states of undress engaging in mating rituals of just about every imaginable sort. And some that are not all that imaginable. It would seem (at least before the end of Earth) that Humans document their mating acts. And sell it to other humans. Strange.": "あの液体がこの薬剤に何をしたにせよ、残りの全サンプルの破棄を勧告する。危険すぎてさらなる研究のために生かしておけない。同僚スタッフから採取した血液サンプルでのテストを開始する。グレッグの実験的プリオンが何とか広がっているのではないかと懸念している。",
  "^yellow;FU Guide^reset; : Beginner ITN": "^yellow;FUガイド^reset; : ITN入門",
  "Inventory Transference Network (ITN) devices allow you to create an automated, object-based network that can move and sort any item between your inventory, containers, and the open world. ITN objects use Starbound's wiring system to function, a familiarity with wiring is recommended but not required to use the ITN. All ITN objects are found at the Electronics Center (or its upgraded version, the Power Center).": "インベントリ転送ネットワーク（ITN）デバイスを使えば、オブジェクトベースの自動化ネットワークを構築し、インベントリ、コンテナ、オープンワールド間であらゆるアイテムを移動・仕分けすることができます。ITNオブジェクトはStarboundのワイヤリングシステムで動作するため、ワイヤリングの基礎知識があると望ましいですが、必須ではありません。すべてのITNオブジェクトはエレクトロニクスセンター（またはアップグレード版のパワーセンター）で作成できます。",
  "Pay close attention to the item tooltips for the various ITN objects, these will tell you exactly what each of that object's nodes are used for. Also be aware that some item descriptions will change after being placed - examine them both in your inventory and while placed! Also note that while many of these objects have power nodes that can be used to toggle them between active and inactive, none of the ITN objects require power (as created by generators) to function.": "各ITNオブジェクトのアイテムツールチップには特に注目してください。各ノードの用途が詳しく記載されています。また、一部のアイテムは設置後に説明文が変わることがあるため、インベントリ内と設置後の両方で確認しましょう。多くのオブジェクトにはオン/オフを切り替える電源ノードがありますが、ITNオブジェクトはジェネレーターによる電力供給なしで動作します。",
  "The first core component of the ITN is the storage bridge, which is used to provide containers with input & output wiring nodes by way of proxy. Storage bridges look around themselves for the nearest container to connect to (by placement point), but can get confused if you put them right between multiple containers. Make sure your storage bridges are placed as close as possible to the one container you want them linked to, and to leave space between them and other containers.": "ITNの最初の中核コンポーネントはストレージブリッジです。コンテナにプロキシ経由で入出力ワイヤリングノードを提供するために使用します。ストレージブリッジは周囲の最も近いコンテナ（設置ポイント基準）に自動接続しますが、複数のコンテナの間に配置すると混乱が生じることがあります。ストレージブリッジは接続したいコンテナのできるだけ近くに設置し、他のコンテナとの間には十分なスペースを空けてください。",
  "Storage bridges work with more than just ordinary containers. Almost any object which can be interacted with that has item slots can be linked to a storage bridge. This includes some FrackinUniverse crafting stations and a few misc. objects that might already have power nodes (but no input/output nodes). If you find yourself uncertain about which nodes to use, remember that storage bridge nodes always function as ITN input/output nodes.": "ストレージブリッジは通常のコンテナ以外にも対応しています。アイテムスロットを持つインタラクト可能なオブジェクトであれば、ほぼすべてストレージブリッジに接続できます。FrackinUniverseの一部のクラフトステーションや、電源ノードを持つ（ただし入出力ノードを持たない）オブジェクトも含まれます。どのノードを使うべきか分からなくなったら、ストレージブリッジのノードは常にITNの入出力ノードとして機能することを覚えておいてください。",
  "Object Data Sensor: Crafted in the tinkering table. Detects object placement points, to allow for more precise placement of Storage Bridges. Bridges select a single container based on the distance between themselves and object placement points.": "オブジェクトデータセンサー: ティンカリングテーブルで作成できます。オブジェクトの設置ポイントを検出し、ストレージブリッジをより正確に配置できるようにします。ブリッジは自身とオブジェクトの設置ポイント間の距離に基づいて、単一のコンテナを選択します。",
  "Item Transference Devices (ITDs) are additional core components of the ITN system. While ITDs are capable of moving all items by default, you will need special token items to filter for currencies or items the ITD does not recognize. You can place them wherever you want as long as you can keep their wiring straight. Mastery of the ITD will bring mastery over the entire ITN system.": "アイテム転送デバイス（ITD）はITNシステムのもう一つの中核コンポーネントです。ITDはデフォルトですべてのアイテムを移動できますが、通貨やITDが認識しないアイテムをフィルタリングするには特別なトークンアイテムが必要です。ワイヤリングを整理できる限り、どこにでも設置できます。ITDをマスターすれば、ITNシステム全体をマスターしたことになります。",
  "Overflow: ITDs will sound off alarms if you are trying to move too much into a container that does not have space. They will also slow down their processing speed. If you have alarms sounding and periodic lag, you should work on improving flow control.": "オーバーフロー: 空き容量のないコンテナに大量のアイテムを移動しようとすると、ITDはアラームを鳴らします。処理速度も低下します。アラームが鳴り、定期的なラグが発生する場合は、フロー制御の改善に取り組んでください。",
  "Stack Move: To move stacks of specific sizes, place the desired stack size in your filter area. This works well with Even Split and Slot Split, as it will only move stacks there are enough to do so equally. It does not, however, account for amounts in the destination.": "スタック移動: 特定のサイズのスタックを移動するには、フィルターエリアに目的のスタックサイズを配置します。均等分割やスロット分割と組み合わせると、均等に分配できる十分な量がある場合にのみスタックを移動します。ただし、移動先の量は考慮されません。",
  "In order to set up a basic ITN network, connect the red output node for a container's storage bridge to the second blue input node for an ITD, and then connect the ITD's red output node to the blue input node of a second container's storage bridge. Now all items put into the first container will be automatically moved to the second one.": "基本的なITNネットワークをセットアップするには、コンテナのストレージブリッジの赤い出力ノードをITDの2番目の青い入力ノードに接続し、次にITDの赤い出力ノードを2番目のコンテナのストレージブリッジの青い入力ノードに接続します。これで、最初のコンテナに入れたすべてのアイテムが自動的に2番目のコンテナに移動されます。",
  "ITDs can be interacted with to bring up their configuration menu. Input slots indicate what slots in a container the ITD will pull from; output slots designate what inventory slots in a container the ITD will drop items into. You can press the red I button to invert the selected slots, telling the ITD to ignore those specific slots rather than use them specifically. Even splitting and slot splitting dictate whether the ITD sorts items into single stacks or splits items between every indicated output slot. ITDs may not be used as repeaters.": "ITDをインタラクトすると設定メニューが開きます。入力スロットはITDがコンテナから取り出すスロットを指定し、出力スロットはITDがアイテムを入れるインベントリスロットを指定します。赤いIボタンを押すとスロット選択を反転でき、指定したスロットを「使用する」から「無視する」に切り替えられます。均等分割はアイテムを単一スタックに仕分けるか、指定した全出力スロットに分配するかを制御します。ITDはリピーターとして使用できません。",
  "You can place items in the empty item boxes in the top-right corner of an ITD's configuration screen to tell it to pull specific kinds of items and ignore others. You can further specify whether you want the ITD to pull that exact item, or else the same types or categories of that item. Furthermore, you can specify how many to move at a time by placing stacks of the desired quantity. Using the Inverted Logic setting tells the ITD to ignore that specific, type, or category of item.": "ITD設定画面の右上にある空のアイテムボックスにアイテムを配置すると、特定の種類のアイテムだけを取り出し、それ以外を無視するように指示できます。さらに、そのアイテムそのものを対象にするか、同じタイプやカテゴリのアイテムを対象にするかを指定できます。また、目的の数量のスタックを配置することで、一度に移動する量も指定できます。反転ロジック設定を使うと、その特定のアイテム・タイプ・カテゴリを無視するようになります。",
  "Item Types:\n  Hand Tools (Flashlight, rope, picks)\n  Instruments (Violin, xylaphone, assflute)\n  Thrown weapons (Throwing knives, bombs)\n  Augments\n  Collars\n  Dyes": "アイテムタイプ:\n ハンドツール（懐中電灯、ロープ、ピッケル）\n 楽器（バイオリン、シロフォン、尻笛）\n 投擲武器（投げナイフ、爆弾）\n 拡張モジュール\n 首輪\n 染料",
  "Item Categories:\n  Treasure (Valuable & rare items)\n  Materials (Blocks, liquids, platforms)\n  Rails (Including platforms and trams)\n  Books (Including Blueprints)\n  Ingredients (Crafting materials, ores)\n  Objects (Containers, crafting stations, lights & doors)\n  Farm (Most agricultural products)\n  Weapons\n  Armor (Including back items & augments)\n  Unhandled (Anything not in the other categories)": "アイテムカテゴリ:\n 財宝（貴重品・レアアイテム）\n 素材（ブロック、液体、プラットフォーム）\n レール（プラットフォームやトラムを含む）\n 書物（設計図を含む）\n 材料（クラフト素材、鉱石）\n オブジェクト（コンテナ、クラフトステーション、照明、ドア）\n 農業（ほとんどの農産物）\n 武器\n 防具（背中装備・拡張モジュールを含む）\n 未分類（他のカテゴリに含まれないもの）",
  "Once you have a basic ITN setup (described on page 9), you can make a terminal at the electronics/power center. By connecting the output of a container's storage bridge to a terminal's input node, you can see and search through every item stored in that container, and pull them into your inventory - but you cannot send items back through the terminal. A single terminal can be connected to multiple containers this way, letting you view and pull items from multiple containers at once.": "基本的なITNセットアップ（9ページ参照）ができたら、エレクトロニクス/パワーセンターでターミナルを作成できます。コンテナのストレージブリッジの出力をターミナルの入力ノードに接続すれば、そのコンテナ内のすべてのアイテムを確認・検索し、自分のインベントリに取り出すことができます。ただし、ターミナル経由でアイテムを送り返すことはできません。一つのターミナルを複数のコンテナに接続すれば、複数のコンテナのアイテムを同時に閲覧・取り出しできます。",
  "A common, useful storage setup is to have rows of containers and storage bridges all linked to a single terminal (or series of terminals) so you can pull from all of them, with a chest nearby and its storage bridge linked to multiple ITDs that will automatically sort any items you dump into it into specific containers in the network without you having to do anything else.": "よくある便利なストレージ構成として、コンテナとストレージブリッジの列をすべて一つのターミナル（またはターミナル群）に接続し、すべてのコンテナから取り出せるようにする方法があります。近くにチェストを置いてそのストレージブリッジを複数のITDに接続すれば、チェストに投入したアイテムが自動的にネットワーク内の特定のコンテナに仕分けられます。",
  "As you start making more sophisticated ITN setups, you may have trouble getting your wiring across large areas of space without vanishing, or else want to optimize the efficiency of your wiring. Repeaters can serve as wiring waypoints to extend your wiring range, while a single Repeater can be wired to all your containers so that you do not need to wire all of them individually between a dozen different terminals. It is important to note that if repeaters are looped, they will cease function.": "より高度なITNセットアップを構築し始めると、広いエリアにワイヤリングを引き回す際に途中で消えてしまったり、配線の効率を最適化したくなることがあります。リピーターはワイヤリングの中継点として使用でき、接続範囲を拡張できます。また、一つのリピーターにすべてのコンテナを接続すれば、各コンテナを複数のターミナルに個別に接続する必要がなくなります。リピーターをループ接続すると動作しなくなるので注意してください。",
  "Dos & Don'ts:\n\n  Do daisy-chain multiple containers. Use ITDs to draw items out of a container dumped to by another ITD to help automatically compress item stacks where possible and to give you more item-specific storage space.\n\n  Do not try to move large amounts of items into a container which already has many items in it. Do not daisy-chain ITDs. These are sources of lag, and ITD configurations do not stack without a separating container.": "すべきこと・してはいけないこと:\n\n すべきこと: 複数のコンテナをデイジーチェーン接続しましょう。ITDを使って別のITDが投入したコンテナからアイテムを取り出すことで、アイテムスタックの自動圧縮や、アイテム別のストレージスペースの確保が可能です。\n\n してはいけないこと: 既に多くのアイテムが入っているコンテナに大量のアイテムを移動しようとしないでください。ITDをデイジーチェーン接続しないでください。これらはラグの原因となり、間にコンテナを挟まないとITDの設定は重複しません。",
  "Dos & Don'ts:\n\n  Do create branching ITD trees along a string of containers where you feel you need to.\n\n  Do Not create any sort of infinite back-and-forth loop that shifts the same items between the same containers unless you have a very good reason to do so. This can be a substantial source of lag.": "すべきこと・してはいけないこと:\n\n すべきこと: 必要に応じて、コンテナの列に沿って分岐するITDツリーを作成しましょう。\n\n してはいけないこと: 明確な理由がない限り、同じアイテムを同じコンテナ間で無限に往復させるようなループを作らないでください。これは重大なラグの原因となる可能性があります。",
  "The pros of the ITN system are that it allows for extremely powerful, precise, decentralized and fully automated item storage. No more having to prance between dozens of different containers whenever you get back from a loot haul, you can just drop it all in a single chest and have it all sorted exactly where you need it, or else retrieve exactly the materials you need for crafting without having to leave a crafting station.": "ITNシステムの利点は、極めて強力で精密、分散型かつ完全自動化されたアイテム保管が可能なことです。戦利品を持ち帰るたびに何十ものコンテナの間を走り回る必要はもうありません。一つのチェストにすべて放り込めば、必要な場所に正確に仕分けられます。クラフトステーションを離れることなく、必要な素材を正確に取り出すこともできます。",
  "The cons of the ITN system are that that it requires extensive setup and occasionally sophisticated wiring to get working, and requires examples of the items you want it to filter. It can also be a significant source of lag, the process of shifting and reorganizing upwards of a hundred stacks of items between multiple containers at once can be one of the most process-intensive aspects present in Starbound.": "ITNシステムの欠点は、大掛かりなセットアップと時には複雑なワイヤリングが必要であること、そしてフィルタリングしたいアイテムの実物が必要なことです。また、ラグの大きな原因にもなり得ます。複数のコンテナ間で百を超えるスタックのアイテムを一度に移動・整理する処理は、Starboundで最も負荷の高い処理の一つとなることがあります。",
  "Credits:\n\n  Kherae for making all this arcane schlock work.\n  HelloWorld123 for writing the original Network Guide.\n  TP for Steambound Reloaded.\n  Cratesmith for the Vesselbound Container Link Code.\n  Terminal for figuring out how to reverse entropy and for writing this guide.": "クレジット:\n\n Kherae - この難解な仕組み全体の制作\n HelloWorld123 - オリジナルのネットワークガイドの執筆\n TP - Steambound Reloaded\n Cratesmith - Vesselbound Container Link Code\n Terminal - エントロピーの逆転方法の解明とこのガイドの執筆",
  "Troubling News": "不穏なニュース",
  "Just because hes a Hylotl, Dad is flipping out! It's not fair! Dennyx and I love one another! Who cares what species he is??? Dad insists that 'No Munari of mine is going to marry a good-for-nothing Hylotl' but we'll show him! I just paid 20,000 pixels to the Closed Fist to 'take care' of our problem in the traditional manner. Our wedding will proceed as planned, no matter what!": "ハイロトルだからってパパは大騒ぎ！不公平！デニックスと私は愛し合ってるのに！どの種族だろうと何が問題なの？？？パパは",
  "Unusual Adoption": "珍しい養子縁組",
  "I heard some sort of screaming a while ago. It sounded like Squiggles, and she paid no mind to it. Maybe there's more like her out there.": "しばらく前に何かの悲鳴を聞いた。スクイグルズみたいな声で、彼女は気にしなかった。外に彼女のような存在がもっといるのかもしれない。",
  "Squiggles came with us on our ship. SHE IS EATING EVERYTHING. Maple still adores the hell out of the little thing, but damn if we don't get hundreds in property damages from this weird cat eating our ship!": "スクイグルズが船に乗ってきた。全部食べている。メイプルはまだこの小さな生き物を溺愛しているが、この奇妙な猫が船を食べて数百ピクセルの物的損害だ！",
  "I really have a feeling that this isn't a cat.": "これは猫じゃないという気がしてならない。",
  "WE KIDNAPPED AN ALIEN AND MY WIFE CALLED IT A CAT": "エイリアンを誘拐したら妻が猫と呼んだ",
  "Squiggles acts a lot like a cat. She likes to meow and coo when we scratch her on the cheek, and she nips our ankles when she's upset. Also, she is REALLY fat. Maybe she needs to go on a diet. It gets uncomfortable when she sits in my lap.": "スクイグルズは猫のように振る舞う。頬を撫でるとニャーと鳴き、怒ると足首を噛む。あと、本当に太っている。ダイエットが必要かも。膝に座ると居心地が悪い。",
  "I did some Bloogling and as I suspected, this is no cat. Apparently it's a thing called a Radling? They eat everything in sight, and that dense gooey stuff is liquid. Lead. Liquid lead! No wonder she's so heavy! Also, she's apparently a baby. And she'll grow up into... oh god.": "ブログルして調べたところ、案の定これは猫ではない。ラドリングというものらしい？目に入るものは何でも食べ、あのドロドロの密度の高い物質は液体の鉛だ！どうりで重いわけだ！あと、どうやら赤ちゃんらしい。成長すると…ああ。",
  "Today, my buddy Maple and I found a weird, but adorable little cat-thing. I've never seen anything like it, and Maple insists that it's a cat. I mean, it looks a lot like a cat. It's fluffy, it kinda meows, it has four legs, and it has sharp teeth. It's just... really fat, and drools some sort of nasty metal goo. Makes my skin itch. Maple decided to name our new cat ''Squiggles''.": "今日、相棒のメイプルと私は奇妙だが愛らしい猫のような生き物を見つけた。見たことのないもので、メイプルは主張する",
  "Fitting Small Things Into Larger Things": "大きいものに小さいものを入れる方法",
  "A surprisingly informative book devoted entirely to fitting small objects into larger objects. Page length: 280 pages. Publisher: Penguin": "小さな物を大きな物に収める方法だけに捧げられた驚くほど有益な本。ページ数：280ページ。出版社：ペンギン",
  "Ramblings": "とりとめのない話",
  "my associates, connected only with a small university, have little chance of making an impression where matters of a wildly bizarre or highly controversial nature are concerned.": "小さな大学とのみつながりのある私の仲間たちは、極めて奇妙な、あるいは非常に物議を醸す性質の事柄で印象を与える機会がほとんどない。",
  "I am forced into speech because men of science have refused to follow my advice without knowing why. It is altogether against my will that I tell my reasons for opposing this contemplated invasion of the antarctic with its vast fossil-hunt and its wholesale boring and melting of the ancient ice-cap—and I am the more reluctant because my warning may be in vain. Doubt of the real facts, as I must reveal them, is inevitable; yet if I suppressed what will seem extravagant and incredible there would be nothing left.": "科学者たちが理由を知らずに私の助言に従うことを拒否したため、発言を余儀なくされた。全く私の意思に反するが",
  "The hitherto withheld photographs, both ordinary and aerial, will count in my favour; for they are damnably vivid and graphic. Still, they will be doubted because of the great lengths to which clever fakery can be carried. The ink drawings, of course, will be jeered at as obvious impostures; notwithstanding a strangeness of technique which art experts ought to remark and puzzle over.": "これまで非公開だった写真、通常のものと航空写真は、私に有利に働くだろう。恐ろしいほど生々しく写実的だからだ。それでも",
  "In the end I must rely on the judgment and standing of the few scientific leaders who have, on the one hand, sufficient independence of thought to weigh my data on its own hideously convincing merits or in the light of certain primordial and highly baffling myth-cycles; and on the other hand, sufficient influence to deter the exploring world in general from any rash and overambitious programme in the region of those mountains of madness. It is an unfortunate fact that relatively obscure men like myself and": "結局、一方では十分な独立性を持つ少数の科学指導者の判断と立場に頼らざるを得ない。",
  "Ridiculous Groinshakes": "馬鹿げた腰振りダンス",
  "In this 15 part docu-series, we'll be investigating human mating habits in detail. From the most unusually shaped genitals to the bizarre positions, preening and beauty habits, and everything else associated with their unusual mammalian mating rituals.": "この15部構成のドキュメンタリーシリーズでは、人間の交尾習慣を詳しく調査する。最も珍しい形の生殖器から奇妙な体位、身だしなみと美容の習慣、そして彼らの珍しい哺乳類の交尾儀式に関わる全てまで。",
  "There exists a species so strange in its mating habits...so unorthodox...that literally the entire galaxy is curious about it. These creatures will mate nearly anywhere and for effectively no reason at all besides fun or a means to pass the time (in some documented cases). And yet...their gestation? Slow. Their young? Mewling and helpless for quite some time. The species? Human.": "交尾習慣があまりに奇妙で…あまりに非正統的で…文字通り銀河全体が好奇心を持つ種族がいる。",
  "Classified document. 11 - 2 - XX": "機密文書 11 - 2 - XX",
  "myself, escaped with our lives, and only minor injuries. We lost the project and our facility to the Florans that very day.": "私自身は軽傷のみで命からがら逃げ出した。その日、プロジェクトと施設をフローランに奪われた。",
  "This document is only meant to be viewed by U.S.C.M bio-engineering staff of classification level 5 or higher. In the events this document is read by other eyes, it is meant to be destroyed. If you, are reading this, without being of any classification, you are about to uncover some truths.": "この文書はUSCM生体工学スタッフの分類レベル5以上のみが閲覧すべきものである。他者の目に触れた場合、破棄されるべきである。分類なしでこれを読んでいるあなたは、いくつかの真実を明らかにしようとしている。",
  "09 - 4 - XX,05:00 AM\n\nA product case was suggested to the head of the leading science and recreation division of the science outpost, the location of which is disclosed to anyone without a direct invitation to the facility, or with means to contact them otherwise. Dr. V. was asked to conduct advisory roles for the development of project Termite Hill,": "09 - 4 - XX、午前5時\n\n製品ケースがサイエンスアウトポストの主任科学・娯楽部門長に提案された。",
  "for the U.S.C.M. Termite hill is a classified project, but as this is a final report on the matter, I will be honest. We tried to make humans more disposable as before, by making - imperfect - clones. Clones close to humankind but in multiple ways genetically different so those soldiers would not be able to be traced back to us, nor mankind. An elite": "USCM用。ターマイトヒルは機密プロジェクトだが、これは最終報告なので正直に書く。人間を作ろうとした",
  "task force, with no name, no past, no future. Production went well.\n\n\n 22 - 6 - XX\n\nThe production passed its testing phase with flying colors, the clones were brought up from infantile sizes to full-grown produce. Trained in black ops combat, and tested against small villages of hostile alien species. Most of which unknown to the united federation of": "名前も過去も未来もない任務部隊。生産は順調だった。\n\n\n22 - 6 - XX\n\n生産はテスト段階を見事に通過し",
  "space inhabitants. Those that are known are the [REDACTED].\n\n\n13 - 7 - XX\n\nDr. V was disclosed from the project at his request, every involvement is erased and any technology provided reproduced. As such, efficiency in productivity dropped by 22%. But it was a sacrifice we were willing to take. Dr. V never spoke a word about it since.": "宇宙の住人。知られているのは[削除済み]。\n\n\n13 - 7 - XX\n\nV博士は自らの要請によりプロジェクトから開示され、全ての関与は消去され提供された技術は複製された。そのため生産性の効率は22%低下した。しかしそれは我々が受け入れる犠牲だった。V博士はそれ以来一言も語っていない。",
  "08 - 8 - XX\n\nOur badly reproduced machinery have created a heat-signature strong enough to pass through our reinforced walls of the underground base on planet [REDACTED] - A Floran Armada picked up on the signature and invaded, making short work of the unprepared minimal security force, and several of the scientists on the work floor. Only a handful, including": "08 - 8 - XX\n\n我々の粗悪に複製された機械は、地下の強化壁を透過するほど強い熱信号を生み出した",
  "Present Day\n\nWe have seen that several new food items have been universally spread by Floran distributors. Prepared human-like faces, and baby-heads on a stick. The baby heads have an exact match with the scrambled DNA sequence we had given the clones. It is clear what happened to our facility, and its clear what the Floran have turned it into. To this day, no-one has linked it back to humankind, nor the U.S.C.M": "現在\n\nフローランの流通業者によって新しい食品がいくつか普遍的に広まったことが判明した。人間に似た調理済み顔の",
  "A study in Floran Weaponry": "フローラン族の兵器に関する考察",
  "An alarming discovery was recently made while spying in a Floran collective. A row of Floran warriors were lined up, which was normal enough; what wasn't was the weaponry they bared.For one, it was the array of weaponry; several tech levels higher than would be assumed for them.": "フローラン族の集落を偵察中に、憂慮すべき発見がなされた。フローラン戦士たちが一列に整列していたこと自体は珍しくない。しかし彼らが携えていた武器は異常だった。まず、その武器の種類の多さ。技術レベルはフローラン族の想定をはるかに上回っていた。",
  "The second, and more harrowing realization was as such: The weapons were being operated by their POWERFUL THIGHS. One appeared to be an ordinary disc fed machine gun; operated by an accordion pump apparatus. The second was much more intimidating, taking the appearance of a buckshot": "二つ目の、より恐ろしい発見はこうだ。武器はその強靭な太腿で操作されていた。一つはアコーディオン式ポンプ機構で駆動する、ごく普通のディスク給弾式機関銃に見えた。二つ目はさらに威圧的で、散弾の形状をしていた。",
  "shell inflated until with a loud retort scattering the entire payload across a scarecrow target. The most fearsome however, was the cannon. Even if it only shot round shot, it did cut though an entire cornfield as if it was merely the air.": "弾丸は大きな炸裂音とともに膨張し、案山子の標的にペイロード全体をばらまいた。しかし最も恐ろしかったのは大砲だ。丸弾しか発射しないにもかかわらず、トウモロコシ畑全体をまるで空気のように貫通した。",
  "Retreating to my scout ship wasn't going to be a quiet thing for sure, the sound of their weapon tests ringing out, rocking the air, and shaking my very being. Leaving their jungle huts safely out of my sight, it was only upon reaching the clearing where I had parked my shuttle that it now became clear that my choice of parking spot was a dire mistake. My personal shuttle, dented and firmly smashed up by runaway cannonballs,\nseveral of her systems damaged, the orbital engines nearly critically so. As I flee this planet of the damned, projectile warnings ring out from my Bitching Betty unit. But my shuttle is too damaged for anything but the laziest of evasions, I pray aloud that my ship won't be struck; the ablative plating already having been crumpled into a very expensive ball.": "偵察シャトルへの撤退は静かにとはいかなかった。武器テストの轟音が鳴り響き、大気を揺るがし、私の全身を震わせた。ジャングルの集落が視界から消えた頃、シャトルを駐機していた空き地にたどり着いて初めて、駐機場所の選択が致命的な間違いだったことに気づいた。私のシャトルは砲弾の流れ弾でへこみ、完全に叩き潰されていた。\n複数のシステムが損傷し、軌道エンジンはほぼ致命的な状態だった。この忌まわしい惑星から逃げ出す最中、警告装置が飛来物の警報を鳴らし続ける。だがシャトルの損傷はひどく、最も鈍い回避しかできない。撃たれないことをただ祈るしかなかった。アブレーション装甲は既に高価な鉄くずと化していた。",
  "Suddenly, a lurch! A cannonball which had been wedged in the underside of my ship gave to the forces of gravity, freeing some weight. I'll be needing my brown jumpsuit now. I can only hope that CentComm is willing to investigate into this new mad breed of weapon...": "突然、衝撃が走った！ シャトルの底部に挟まっていた砲弾が重力に屈して落下し、重量が軽くなった。茶色のジャンプスーツが必要になりそうだ。この新種の狂気じみた兵器について、中央司令部が調査に乗り出してくれることを祈るばかりだ...",
  "Hylotl Near Extinction?": "ハイロトル絶滅の危機？",
  "Next time fishman whine at you about their numberssss, just lay that on em. Maybe only 10% ssssurvive, but ssstill enough to fight Floran war instead of becoming lunch.": "次に魚人がその数についてしつこく言ったら、これを突きつけろ。生き残るのは10%かもしれないが、昼食になる代わりにフローランの戦争を戦うには十分だ。",
  "Sssso, Floransss gotta ssssecret. Hylotl never wasss in danger. Think about it. What fish do naturally? Lay a lot of eggsssss. Hylotl are fishpeople. Floran not sssure how there ssso many Floran or how more are made, But sssmelly butt fishman? Eggsss out the wazoo.": "そう、フローランにはシュシュシュ秘密がある。ハイロトルは危険ではなかった。考えてみろ。魚は自然に何をする？たくさんの卵を産む。ハイロトルは魚人だ。フローランはフローランがどうやって増えるか知らないが、臭い尻の魚人？卵がうじゃうじゃ。",
  "Your Dad": "お前の親父",
  "From cover to cover, this book appears to be a recounting of the life of your father.": "表紙から裏表紙まで、この本はあなたの父親の人生を綴っているようだ。",
  "About the Hylotl's low numbers...": "ハイロトルの少なさについて…",
  "So, you know how we pivoted so easily to protecting the Hylotl when the Florans started their war? Well, while we did honestly help defend them, they could've easily kept their numbers as high as they are anyways; we were preventing them from exploding in numbers before the Florans came in and started doing so; we're just preventing the plants from being too aggressive in the population control. Think about it for a bit, and it'll make sense. What do fish and frogs do naturally? Lay a lot of eggs. Hylotl are quite similar in that regard. I'm not sure how there's so many Florans or how more are made, But as for the Hylotl? Eggs out the wazoo.": "フローランが戦争を始めた時、我々がどれほど容易にハイロトルの保護に転じたか知っているだろう？正直に助けたが、",
  "Next time they whine at you about their numbers, let 'em have that food for thought. Sure, only 15% of the survivors from our constant raiding might've come out the other side of the Hylotl-Floran wars, which means about 10% of the overall population pulled through, but that was still more than enough to defend themselves (with a little bit of assistance, of course) instead of becoming lunch. If our kind starts breaking the treaty we signed, though, there might actually be a reason for them to worry about underpopulation.": "次にフローランが数について愚痴を言ったら、考えるネタをやれ。確かに我々の征服の生存者の15%しか",
  "Protheon, Mystery Substance": "プロテオン、謎の物質",
  "Nobody in the known galaxy has any clue what it is, or where it comes from. Possessing strange qualities that enable it to affect reality around it seemingly at random, Protheon remains the most sought resource in existence.": "既知の銀河の誰も、それが何でどこから来たのか手がかりがない。周囲の現実を一見ランダムに影響させる奇妙な性質を持ち、プロシオンは存在する最も求められる資源であり続けている。",
  "There is simply no telling what could be accomplished with the substance. I've seen it alter time in minute ways within its sphere of influence. I've seen it affect gravity. I've even seen it repair dead tissue back to living status.": "この物質で何が達成できるか予測のしようがない。影響圏内で微細な時間の変化を見た。重力への影響も見た。死んだ組織を生きた状態に修復するのさえ見た。",
  "What does this mean? Well, my friends, brace yourself: It means that it has touched numerous realities like ours...yet not like ours. And when it crosses those thresholds between worlds, they carry the information and energy from other dimensions along with them.": "これは何を意味するか？友よ、覚悟しろ：我々のような…しかし我々とは異なる多数の現実に触れたということだ。世界間の境界を越える時、他の次元からの情報とエネルギーを一緒に運ぶ。",
  "Of course, you have likely never before even heard of this material. They don't want you to know the truth. I heard it from someone that worked high up in the Ministry of Knowledge: they theorize that the bizarre element is capable of transcending reality as we know it.": "長らく安全を脅かしていたものを。今、彼らの世界は銀河がこれまで見たことのない石の職人技の砦で覆われている。これは種族のルネサンスにつながり、既知の宇宙で最高の職人という評判を得た。もし必要なら",
  "The X'ian Die-Off": "シーの大量死",
  "The most harrowing time for the X'ian people came soon after. According to texts there are accounts that speak of invaders or visitors from 'elsewhere' that interrupted their progress through literal planetary upheaval and forced terraforming. While none of the records name this race speculation is high that it could have been the Anodyne due in part to their description being a close match. This is now, sadly, rumor pulled from antiquated records...at best.": "シィの民にとって最も悲惨な時期はその直後に訪れた。テキストによると侵略者または訪問者について語る記録がある",
  "Roomba Robots": "ルンバロボット",
  "Stabby had a casualty. It stabbed Vinalisj in the heel and he smashed it with his tail out of surprise. Rest in peace, Stabby. We will avenge you. Probably not with knives.": "スタビーに犠牲が出た。ヴィナリスジの踵を刺し、驚いた彼が尻尾で叩き壊した。安らかに眠れ、スタビー。復讐する。たぶんナイフでは無いが。",
  "So as it turns out, despite how we expected, taping a knife to a roomba does not entertain Heshu as much as we thought it would. Instead, he always gets on all fours and hisses whenever 'Stabby' enters the room. It's actually pretty funny.": "予想に反して、ルンバにナイフをテープで貼るのはヘシュを思ったほど楽しませなかった。代わりに、「スタビー」が部屋に入るたびに四つん這いになってシーッと威嚇する。実際かなり面白い。",
  "Reinventing History": "歴史の再発明",
  "We even found prototype blueprints in these texts. This is a huge game changer! Our entire view on these mysterious beings has been flipped upside down. Now a greater question remains... where did they go?": "これらのテキストの中にプロトタイプの設計図まで見つけた。これは大きな転換点だ！この謎の存在に対する見方が完全にひっくり返った。さらなる疑問が残る…彼らはどこへ行ったのか？",
  "Reading through historical documents has revealed an astonishing truth: The Ancients were an artificial race, built from energized stone and often stationed as sentries. We can't be sure who or what made them, but we are one hundred percent certain they did not simply come about from nowhere. No, these stone goliaths were built by hand, designed to replicate themselves and protect their creators.": "歴史文書を読み解くと驚くべき真実が明らかになった：古代種は人工的な種族で、エネルギーを帯びた",
  "Science Journal": "科学ジャーナル",
  "Note to self: Flesh Reapers do not make good pets.": "メモ：フレッシュリーパーは良いペットにならない。",
  "I got **** *** drunk last night and woke up covered in chickens. Who did this.": "昨夜**** ***酔っ払って鶏まみれで目が覚めた。誰がやった。",
  "I apparently covered myself in chickens.": "どうやら自分を鶏で覆ったらしい。",
  "Today I was dared to eat the dirt that that druggie X'i sells. It's just dirt. I didn't get my money's worth.": "今日、あの薬中のシィが売ってる土を食べるよう挑発された。ただの土だ。金の価値はなかった。",
  "Turns out that dirt is a powerful drug to X'i. I have an idea.": "土がシィにとって強力な薬物だと判明。アイデアがある。",
  "The hypothesis: I could get my coworker Atucha extremely drunk to the point of revealing secrets. That's not what happened though. Vinalisj is very angry at me.": "仮説：同僚アトゥチャを泥酔させて秘密を暴露させられる。しかし実際はそうならなかった。ヴィナリスジは私にとても怒っている。",
  "I didn't learn from last time. Atucha offered me some of his lunch. I ate a ****ing rock.": "前回から学ばなかった。アトゥチャが昼食を分けてくれた。****岩を食べてしまった。",
  "Holy Scripture of Arvokk": "アルヴォクの聖典",
  "Some believe they came from elsewhere. Another universe, subspace...whatever. I say nonsense to this. Nonsense! Only the Pure can come from beyond! Precursors are unholy abominations. Enablers of the Ancients. Slayers of Worlds. A pox upon their kind! A pox of our design.": "別の宇宙やサブスペースから来たと信じる者もいる。何でもいい。ナンセンスだと言う。ナンセンス！純粋な者だけが彼方から来れる！先駆者は不聖な忌まわしき存在。古代種の手先。世界の殺戮者。彼らの種族に疫病を！我々が設計した疫病を。",
  "Instead, turn your attention to those who came before, and gaze upon their spendour as they gnash and devour the order of things and give rise to the glorious cadence cast by absolute entropy. True chaos. Smile, and be reborn as they wipe clean your mortal mind. Be laid bare before their might and have all that you were before purged! Let Them change you.": "代わりに、前に来た者たちに目を向け、彼らが物事の秩序を噛み砕き貪り食い、新たなものを生み出す壮麗さを見よ",
  "First, you must gather the artifacts and drive them into the Cazl Tide. There they will grow and become the Devourer. Only then can you birth the Watcher from the stygian blackness beyond time and space. Through him, we will be torn asunder...and the death of the universe will give rise to a new one. Its newborn form, however, is fragile.": "まず、アーティファクトを集めてカズルの潮流に打ち込まなければならない。そこでそれらは成長しデヴァウラーとなる。その時初めて",
  "To protect the Stillborn God, you must call upon the cleansing power of Yaz'guul and drench the bones of Uniadelz'ik in the rendered fat of a Diluvian. Should no Diluvians remain in existence, instead you must locate a place known as Maine, on a planet known as Earth. There you shall find a town known as Innsmouth. Seek the temple. The blood of Dagon is required.": "スティルボーンの神を守るには、ヤズグールの浄化の力を呼び起こし、ウニアデルジクの骨を浸さなければならない",
  "With the blood secured, then you must drink of it under the light of a Reinkarrd moon. Sadly, these occur only within the event horizon of black holes sufficiently aged. Should you locate one, you may proceed to the next step...[well over 2,000 pages remain. The first half of this process ends on page 800. Reading more would be pointless].": "血を確保したら、ラインカード月の光の下で飲まなければならない。残念ながら、これはブラックホールの事象の地平線内でのみ発生する",
  "Hidden Secrets": "隠された秘密",
  "Scattered knowledge makes up the entire base of what we know about the race we refer to as the Precursors. Largely because we have no way to know what they called themselves. No text ever speaks of their species identification. Nothing ever mentions a homeworld, star, system...if they were xenophobes they were exceptionally protective and paranoid ones.": "散在する知識が、先駆者と呼ぶ種族について知っている全ての基盤を構成する。主な理由は彼らの実際の名前を知る方法がないからだ",
  "Fortunately, most scholars aren't me. I came across a ruin...I'll keep the location secret for now. Sasha...you won't believe it! A library. A massive, well-preserved and fully functioning library. The information within is, without a doubt, the most significant archaeological find in the history of the entire cosmos. All I need to do is make it to the meeting on Earth and I can present my findings after the Protectorate emergency summit.": "幸い、ほとんどの学者は私ではない。遺跡を見つけた…場所は今は秘密にしておこう。サーシャ…信じられないよ！",
  "53 More Things to do in Zero Gravity": "無重力でやる53のこと（追加編）",
  "True to its title, it contains 53 fun things to do in Zero Gravity. Interestingly enough, 4 of them involve murder and 2 involve suction cups and laxatives.": "タイトル通り、無重力でできる53の楽しいことが載っている。興味深いことに、4つは殺人を含み、2つは吸盤と下剤を含む。",
  "Annoying Florans": "うっとうしいフローラン",
  "This tome is 4,362 pages, entirely devoted to annoying or pissing off anything Floran. It contains useful tips such as 'salt their houses' and 'ignite their infants'. It was allegedly penned by legendary Hylotl revolutionary (and crazed mad-man) Yikasha Hirochi.": "この書物は4,362ページで、フローランを苛立たせるか怒らせることのみに捧げられている。「家に塩をまけ」「幼体に火をつけろ」などの有用なヒントを含む。伝説のハイロトル革命家（かつ狂った男）ヤカシャ・ヒロチが著したとされる。",
  "^red;The following details infractions allegedly committed against other members of the outpost by one Myulthor 'Kevin' Sanchatak^white; :": "^red;以下は、ミュルソール「ケビン」サンチャタクなる人物が基地の他のメンバーに対して犯したとされる違反行為の詳細である^white; :",
  "Jun 1 - This individual broke into my private office, stole all of my grapes, and rather than eat them constructed an elaborate 'art piece' of me. Peeing on a beehive. He then filled the room with bees, so that when I opened the door I got swarmed and stung 755 times.": "6月1日 - この人物が私の個人オフィスに侵入し、ブドウをすべて盗んだ。食べるのではなく、ブドウで私が蜂の巣に小便をかけている精巧な「芸術作品」を作った。さらに部屋を蜂で満たし、私がドアを開けた途端に群がられて755回刺された。",
  "Jun 2 - Against all better judgement I allowed Kevin to borrow my bunsen burner. When asked to return it, he brought back a small stack of ash and announced that you can burn a bunsen burner with another bunsen burner if you allow it to burn long enough.": "6月2日 - 良識に反してケビンにバンゼンバーナーを貸した。返却を求めたところ、小さな灰の山を持ってきて、「バンゼンバーナーは別のバンゼンバーナーで十分長く燃やせば焼けるんだ」と言い放った。",
  "Jun 3 - My lab notes went missing. Weeks of work. When asking around, several others saw Kevin take them from my desk. I found them later, folded up and being used to prop up a wobbly table.": "6月3日 - 実験ノートが消えた。数週間分の研究成果だ。聞き込みをすると、複数の人間がケビンが私のデスクから持ち去るのを目撃していた。後日発見されたが、折りたたまれてガタつくテーブルの脚の下敷きにされていた。",
  "Jun 12 - Kevin got back from vacation today. Is it a coincidence that my lunch was swapped with a bucket of mooshi urine on the same day?": "6月12日 - ケビンが今日休暇から戻った。私のランチがムーシの尿が入ったバケツにすり替えられていたのは偶然だろうか？",
  "Jun 13 - Kevin is forbidden from using the coffee machine, it took me 2 hours to clean the mess it made. I don't care where he got all that blood, it's just unsanitary and I won't stand for it.": "6月13日 - ケビンはコーヒーマシンの使用を禁止された。掃除に2時間もかかった。あの血をどこから手に入れたかは知らないが、不衛生極まりないので許容できない。",
  "Jun 14 - A reminder that the Coffee Machine in the kitchen is to be used EXCLUSIVELY for brewing coffee. Any other substance should not be used under any circumstances, so please do not put any of these in the machine: Fruit (of any kind), Vegetables (of any kind), Meat, Florans,  Pixels, Aether, Mercury, Blood.": "6月14日 - キッチンのコーヒーマシンはコーヒーを淹れるためだけに使用することを再度通達する。いかなる状況においても、以下のものをマシンに入れてはならない：果物（あらゆる種類）、野菜（あらゆる種類）、肉、フローラン族、ピクセル、エーテル、水銀、血液。",
  "Jun 15 - All of the toilet paper rolls appear to have been replaced with sandpaper. All of them. Even the backups. I can hear Kevin giggling.": "6月15日 - トイレットペーパーがすべて紙やすりに交換されていた。すべて。予備も含めて。ケビンのクスクス笑う声が聞こえる。",
  "Jun 19 - Why the hell is all of the hydrochloric acid gone and replaced with vodka?!?!": "6月19日 - なぜ塩酸が全部なくなってウォッカに置き換えられているんだ？！？！",
  "Jun 22 - That son of a bitch swapped the natural gas and hydrogen tanks. I don't think he realizes how dangerous that could have been.": "6月22日 - あのクソ野郎が天然ガスと水素のタンクを入れ替えやがった。どれだけ危険だったか分かっているのか。",
  "Jun 25 - Despite his clear genius, when asked on where he completed his education Kevin merely slapped me on the ass and told me to be a good servant and get him a coffee. He then proceeded to follow me around for the rest of the day making 'wide-load' truck-beeping sounds every time I moved.": "6月25日 - その明らかな天才性にもかかわらず、ケビンに教育をどこで修了したか尋ねたところ、私の尻を叩いて「いい召使いだな、コーヒーを持ってこい」と言い放った。その後、一日中私の後をついて回り、私が動くたびに「幅広車両注意」のトラック警告音を鳴らし続けた。",
  "Jul 1 - No matter how much evidence we provide, Kevin is unwilling to accept that the universe contains more than one odor. He insists it is all simply varition of the same scent. To prove it, he keeps randomly farting at our stations. I really hate this idiot. I honestly want him dead.": "7月1日 - どれだけ証拠を示しても、ケビンは宇宙には一つの匂いしか存在しないと認めようとしない。すべては同じ香りの変形に過ぎないと言い張る。それを証明するために、各自の作業台で唐突にオナラをし続けている。本当にこのバカが嫌いだ。正直、死んでほしい。",
  "Jul 8 - Once again, every last sample in the lab gene storage has been removed and in their place are test tubes with googly-eyes glued to them.": "7月8日 - またしても、研究室の遺伝子保管庫のサンプルが全て取り除かれ、代わりに目玉シールが貼られた試験管が置かれていた。",
  "June 9 - Kevin has broken into Dr. Lesley's computer. Kevin found out many people keep notes of him. Kevin is popular. This pleases Kevin.": "6月9日 - ケビンがレズリー博士のコンピュータに侵入した。多くの人が彼についてメモを残していることを知った。ケビンは人気者だ。ケビンはこれに満足している。",
  "Jul 7 - Twice this week the backup generator fuel was siphoned and completely replaced with Essentia Obscura, causing station-wide hallucinations. Where this fluid was even *obtained* is a question in and of itself.": "7月7日 - 今週2回、非常用発電機の燃料が抜き取られ、エッセンシア・オブスクラに完全に入れ替えられていた。基地全体で幻覚症状が発生した。そもそもこの液体をどこで*入手*したのかという疑問が残る。",
  "Jul 17 - Ten days of glorious prank-free nonsense...and then I open up my Plasmic Fluid sample fridge and inside...no samples. There is a note, however, that thanks me for donating to the Juice Salvation Society.": "7月17日 - 10日間のイタズラなしの素晴らしい日々...そして血漿サンプル冷蔵庫を開けたら...サンプルがない。代わりに、「ジュース救済協会への寄付に感謝します」と書かれたメモがあった。",
  "Jul 18 - Woke up to my eyelids glued together. Thanks, Kevin.": "7月18日 - まぶたを接着剤でくっつけられた状態で目覚めた。ありがとう、ケビン。",
  "Jul 21 - I cannot even begin to imagine how long it took Kevin to construct this statue of Kluex composed entirely of severed Poptop penises. If it weren't so horrific and appalling, I might actually be impressed. I'm less than pleased that he chose to do it on the long weekend, as it has been festering in the lobby for four days.": "7月21日 - ケビンが切断されたポップトップの陰茎だけで構成されたクルエックスの像を制作するのに、いったいどれだけの時間を費やしたのか想像もつかない。もしこれほど恐ろしく不快でなければ、感心すらしたかもしれない。連休中にやったため、ロビーで4日間放置されて腐っていたのは特に不愉快だった。",
  "Jul 25 - Some one drown him! Please! I can't fathom how he considers it humorous but once again he has traded my prosthetic leg to a Gnome in exchange for a Gnome-sized jar of peanut butter. I'm not sure how he even *does* it. It's biometrically locked to my torso!": "7月25日 - 誰か溺死させてくれ！ 頼む！ どうして面白いと思えるのか理解不能だが、またしてもケビンは私の義足をノームに渡して、ノームサイズのピーナッツバターの瓶と交換してきた。いったいどうやっているのか分からない。あれは私の胴体に生体認証でロックされているのに！",
  "Aug 4 - Someone put ixo eggs in the air system. There are now about 900 ixolings rampaging in the kitchen. To 'calm them down' Kevin then added four pounds of Rage Powder. Four. Pounds. Where did he get that much of a class-A narcotic?!?!": "8月4日 - 誰かがイクソの卵を空調システムに入れた。現在約900匹のイクソの幼体がキッチンで暴れ回っている。「落ち着かせるため」にケビンがレイジパウダーを4ポンド投入した。4ポンドだ。そんな大量のクラスA麻薬をどこで手に入れたんだ？！？！",
  "Aug 8 - Another 'fat guy' joke from Kevin. He's recorded sounds of a tuba playing. Whenever I move, he presses play. This has been ongoing since Jul 16th, and I can't take it anymore.": "8月8日 - またしてもケビンの「デブいじり」ジョーク。チューバの演奏音を録音していた。私が動くたびに再生ボタンを押す。これは7月16日から続いており、もう限界だ。",
  "Aug 12 - I really can't figure out how it is comical to replace someone's hair products with watered down sulphuric acid. My skin may be immune, but now I'm bald and look like the ass of a newborn.": "8月12日 - 誰かのヘアケア製品を薄めた硫酸に入れ替えることのどこが面白いのか、本当に理解できない。私の皮膚は免疫があったが、今や禿げ頭で新生児の尻のような見た目になってしまった。",
  "Aug 22 - I think he's finally toned it down...Nothing since the 12th.": "8月22日 - ようやくおとなしくなったようだ...12日以来何もない。",
  "Aug 23 - Damnit. I spoke too soon. He apparently replaced all of the ostrich eggs in the enclosure with raptor eggs. They hatched, and ate the babies. When we got angry, he explained 'the eggs were lonely. I gave them friends.'": "8月23日 - ちくしょう。早とちりだった。どうやらケビンは飼育場のダチョウの卵をすべてラプトルの卵にすり替えていた。孵化した幼体がヒナを食べてしまった。怒ると、彼は「卵が寂しそうだったから。友達を連れてきたんだ」と説明した。",
  "Aug 26 - Kevin won't let anyone near the raptors. He has dressed them all in tiny little ballerina tutus and refers to them as his 'students'.": "8月26日 - ケビンは誰もラプトルに近づけさせない。全匹に小さなバレリーナのチュチュを着せ、「生徒たち」と呼んでいる。",
  "Oct 12 - I'm impressed. In a short period of time, Kevin has trained the raptors to perform a simple ballet routine. Unfortunately, he calls it 'dance of the death claws', and had them perform it...in the now-repopulated ostrich enclosure.": "10月12日 - 感心せざるを得ない。短期間で、ケビンはラプトルたちに簡単なバレエの演目を仕込んだ。残念ながら、それを「死の爪の踊り」と名付け、補充されたばかりのダチョウの飼育場で披露させた。",
  "Oct 13 - We've decided to dismantle the ostrich enclosure. We've invited some bee-science folk to come and fill the space. It made sense, on account of the *thousands of bees* he put in my office in June still roaming around.": "10月13日 - ダチョウの飼育場を解体することにした。蜂の研究者たちを招いてスペースを埋めることにした。6月に彼が私のオフィスに放った*数千匹の蜂*がまだうろついていたので、理にかなった判断だった。",
  "Oct 15 - I attempted to prank Kevin. I apparently suck. Not only did it fail, he found it, dismantled it and placed it in my room. I am now the proud owner of a giant bucket of Poptop feces spilled on my floor.": "10月15日 - ケビンにイタズラを仕掛けてみた。見事に失敗した。それどころか、彼は見つけて解体し、私の部屋に設置した。おかげで床にぶちまけられた巨大なバケツ一杯のポップトップの糞の誇り高き所有者となった。",
  "Oct 20 - I cannot believe that just happened. Kevin weaponized a shark by using a capture ball on a timer attached to a complicated mechanism. I was eating lunch, and a *great white shark* appears directly above my table, eats my lunch, and then enters a portal on the table and dissapears. I really hate Kevin.": "10月20日 - 信じられない出来事が起きた。ケビンがタイマー付きキャプチャーボールと複雑な機構を使ってサメを兵器化した。昼食を食べていたら、テーブルの真上に*ホオジロザメ*が出現し、私のランチを食べ、テーブル上のポータルに入って消えた。本当にケビンが嫌いだ。",
  "Oct 25 - Bandits attacked. Kevin used weaponized shark to kill them. Feeling less hateful.": "10月25日 - 盗賊が襲撃してきた。ケビンが兵器化したサメで撃退した。少し嫌悪感が薄れた。",
  "Oct 26 - Kevin has used self-same weaponized shark device to instead create Bunny-things that won't stop making adorable sounds. We can't hurt them, because they just burrow into pocket dimensions or something...and then pop back out and annoy. This is not going to be fun.": "10月26日 - ケビンが同じサメ兵器装置を使い、今度は可愛らしい音を出し続けるウサギのような生物を生成した。殺そうにも、奴らはポケット次元か何かに潜り込んでは戻ってきて邪魔をする。これは楽しくなりそうにない。",
  "Oct 27 - The Bunny-thing in my office is especially annoying. I think Kevin has genetically modified them, as mine cannot stop swearing. It literally does nothing but call me a litany of racist remarks, gives me the finger, and pops back into its...hole thing.": "10月27日 - 私のオフィスのウサギもどきが特にうっとうしい。ケビンが遺伝子改造したらしく、こいつは罵詈雑言を吐き続けることしかできない。文字通り、人種差別的な暴言を吐き散らし、中指を立て、穴のようなところに戻っていくだけだ。",
  "Oct 29 - Three days is enough. I left my office, and had the life support system withdraw all air from the unit. It took six minutes and fifty-three seconds but the bunny-thing died in panic. I am pleased.": "10月29日 - 3日で十分だ。オフィスを出て、生命維持システムに室内の空気をすべて抜かせた。6分53秒かかったが、ウサギもどきはパニック状態で死んだ。満足だ。",
  "Oct 31 - Whatever 'Halloween' was on Earth, I am more than certain it does not involve repeated attacks with a limp zucchini while shouting 'Excelsior!'. Kevin, however, disagrees with this and insists his knowledge of Earth ways is unmatched. Our human members are not incredibly pleased about this since Kevin has never even *been* to Earth.": "10月31日 - 地球の「ハロウィン」とやらが何であれ、ぐにゃぐにゃのズッキーニで繰り返し叩きながら「エクセルシオール！」と叫ぶ行事ではないと確信している。しかしケビンはそれに異議を唱え、自分の地球文化に関する知識は比類がないと主張している。ケビンは地球に行ったことすら*ない*ので、人間のメンバーたちはあまり喜んでいない。",
  "Dec 25 - Well, he waited a while...probably because he was training the raptors again. They have now mastered the art of targeted defecation, and are utilizing this new skill as much as possible. To ensure 'maximum dance power' Kevin has set them to roam free in the nearby woods. They like to aim their shots through the windows when we open them.": "12月25日 - しばらくおとなしかったが...おそらくラプトルの訓練をしていたのだろう。奴らは今や標的排泄の技術を習得し、この新たなスキルを存分に活用している。「最大ダンスパワー」を確保するため、ケビンはラプトルたちを近くの森に放し飼いにした。窓を開けると、そこを狙って射撃してくるのが好きらしい。",
  "Jan 3 - I've been getting reports of missing lab equipment and consumables, mostly CO2 canisters. I've decided to increase storage security.": "1月3日 - 研究機器や消耗品の紛失報告が相次いでいる。主にCO2カニスターだ。保管庫のセキュリティを強化することにした。",
  "Jan 5 - An explosion on the lower levels led to us finding Kevin launching wooden logs at a steel blade from what appears to be a CO2 cannon, constructed from fridge spare parts and duct tape. Later I also found out he was building an altar in my personal storage room decorated with photographs of my Uncle Steve. I have no idea how he got the pictures. Several piles of shaved wood sat in one corner, and a huge statue of my Uncle riding an angry Bullfrog made from split logs, decorated the other.": "1月5日 - 下層階での爆発をきっかけに、ケビンが冷蔵庫の部品とダクトテープで作ったCO2砲から木の丸太を鉄の刃に向けて発射しているのが発見された。後に私の私物保管室で、スティーブおじさんの写真で飾られた祭壇を建設していたことも判明した。写真の入手経路は不明。隅に削り木の山が積まれ、反対側には割り木で作った、怒ったブルフロッグに跨るスティーブおじさんの巨大な像が飾られていた。",
  "Jan 9 - Kevin was caught stealing large amounts of concentrated sulfuric acid, nitric acid and toluene. After an inspection of his room, a large box of nails was found, with the words 'Death to Equestria' scribbled on the side with crayons.": "1月9日 - ケビンが大量の濃硫酸、硝酸、トルエンを盗んでいるところを捕まった。部屋を検査したところ、大きな箱いっぱいの釘が見つかり、側面にクレヨンで「エクエストリアに死を」と走り書きされていた。",
  "Jan 15 - Kevin has declared this week 'Vuvuzela Appreciation Week' in honor of a now nearly extinct Earth...instrument...if you can call it that. Within about 11 seconds, we wanted to murder him. We are now on hour seven. I have purchased a new rifle from the Ansible network.": "1月15日 - ケビンが今週を、絶滅寸前の地球の...楽器の「ブブゼラ感謝週間」と宣言した。楽器と呼べればの話だが。約11秒で殺意が芽生えた。現在7時間目。アンシブルネットワークで新しいライフルを購入した。",
  "Jan 24 - We received a shipment of about 400 000 of these vuvuzelas from the Ansible network. We also received a 15% discount card off our next big-scale purchase. Kevin was later found fuelling a bonfire with them and grilling mice over it.": "1月24日 - アンシブルネットワークから約40万本のブブゼラが届いた。次回大量購入の15%割引カードも付いていた。ケビンは後にブブゼラを燃やした焚き火でネズミを焼いているところを発見された。",
  "Jan 30 - Kevin made a shrine for a bigger more primitive apex-like animal the humans had on earth, called 'haramber' or something. He kept making off with several of the stocked bananas. This only means we need to change the password on the food storage...again.": "1月30日 - ケビンが地球にいた、より大きく原始的なエイペックスに似た動物のための祠を作った。「ハランバー」とかいう名前だったか。備蓄のバナナを何度も持ち出していた。食料保管庫のパスワードをまた変更しなければならない。",
  "Feb 2 - Someone switched all of the Smarties with Skittles.": "2月2日 - 誰かがスマーティーズをすべてスキットルズにすり替えた。",
  "Feb 8 - After Kevin somehow got his hands on an ancient audiotrack of the old Earth music known as 'Darude; sandstorm', we weren't bothered at first. When he wouldn't let that damn song get a rest for several hours, even at night, we had to do something. We scheduled a trip to the most nearby desert biome with dangerous sandstorms tomorrow. Lets see if Kevin ever plays that Gods-forsaken song again after being sandblasted for an hour or two. We'll say it's a picnic.": "2月8日 - ケビンがどうにかして「Darude; sandstorm」という古い地球の音楽の音源を入手した後、最初は気にしなかった。夜中も含めて何時間もその曲を止めようとしなかったため、何とかしなければならなかった。明日、最寄りの危険な砂嵐がある砂漠バイオームへの遠足を計画した。1、2時間砂嵐に吹かれた後でもあの忌々しい曲を流す気になるか見てやろう。ピクニックだと言うつもりだ。",
  "Feb 9 - Yep. He kept playing the song. Louder. He then composed a version completely in reverse, played only with vomit sounds and a strange repeated word: 'Yolo'.": "2月9日 - 案の定。彼はその曲を流し続けた。さらに大音量で。そして完全に逆再生したバージョンを作曲し、嘔吐音と「ヨロ」という奇妙な繰り返しの言葉だけで演奏した。",
  "Feb 10 - I found a deep-fried mooshi scrotum on my desk today along with a side of ice cream and a Happy Birthday card. My birthday was nine months ago. He is also aware that I have an allergic reaction to Mooshi.": "2月10日 - 今日、机の上にムーシの揚げた陰嚢がアイスクリーム添えで置かれていた。誕生日おめでとうカードも。私の誕生日は9ヶ月前だ。彼は私がムーシにアレルギーがあることも知っている。",
  "Feb 15 - We had to make clear to Kevin that 'surprise-feeding' us Glitch food, doesn't make us do 'the robot' any faster but instead gives us horrible indigestion and potentially lethal food poisoning. He insists that our version of science is akin to (and I quote) 'making love to a dead sea lion in the air while on fire'. I am now attempting to picture exactly what this act would look like.": "2月15日 - グリッチフードを「サプライズ給食」しても、「ロボットダンス」が早くなるわけではなく、ひどい消化不良と致命的になりかねない食中毒を引き起こすだけだとケビンに明確に伝えなければならなかった。彼は我々の科学は（引用すると）「空中で燃えながら死んだアシカと愛を交わすようなもの」だと主張している。今、それが正確にはどんな行為なのか想像しようとしている。",
  "Feb 18 - Norbert finally snapped. He pushed Kevin off the roof after luring him upstairs for 'ninja practice', a thing which no Kevin can resist. We had assumed at long last that we had freed ourselves from his tyrannical pranking. We were sorely mistaken. It turns out he has gene-linked his mind to this facility. Any attempt at murder results in a clone being immediately spawned using his most recent brainscan. He claims 'the station made him do it'. He also apparently 'invented the question mark'.": "2月18日 - ノーバートがついにキレた。「忍者の練習」で屋上に誘い出し、ケビンを突き落とした。忍者に抵抗できるケビンはいない。ようやく奴の暴君的イタズラから解放されたと思ったが、大きな間違いだった。ケビンは自分の意識をこの施設に遺伝子リンクしていたのだ。殺害を試みると、最新のブレインスキャンから即座にクローンが生成される。「ステーションに命じられた」と主張している。また「クエスチョンマークを発明した」とも。",
  "Feb 21 - Kevin kept persistently saying that 'the bird is the word' today. This made the meeting of the engineering staff awkward, seeing as he just burst in. And Axiena, the fuel-expert of us, who is an Avian was there. Now, being a 'bird' wouldn't be so bad to ignore kevin's 'quirks' but she's also a mute. Being reminded that she couldn't 'be the word' at all (having no vocal capability since birth) was rather rude. Preparing a cake congratulating her on her muteness was worse.": "2月21日 - ケビンが今日一日中「バード・イズ・ザ・ワード」と言い続けた。エンジニアリングスタッフの会議に突然乱入してきたので気まずかった。燃料専門家のアヴィアン族のアクシエナもそこにいた。「鳥」であること自体はケビンの「癖」を無視できなくもないが、彼女は生まれつきの唖者だ。生まれてから声を出す能力がないことを「言葉になれない」と暗に指摘されるのはかなり失礼だ。彼女の唖を祝うケーキを用意したのはさらにひどかった。",
  "Feb 24 - Kevin came back from a research expedition. He brought somebody named 'Greg' with him. Please kill me.": "2月24日 - ケビンが調査遠征から戻ってきた。「グレッグ」という名前の誰かを連れてきた。殺してくれ。",
  "Feb 25 - Kevin has been missing for several days. Nobody knows where he is. Also, somebody has been eating my cheesecake. I'll ask the cooks to bring it to my office.": "2月25日 - ケビンが数日間行方不明だ。誰も居場所を知らない。それと、誰かが私のチーズケーキを食べている。コックに私のオフィスに届けるよう頼もう。",
  "Feb 27 - I'm sure somebody is breaking into my personal office to do nothing else but eat my cheesecake. Sounds like something Kevin would do, but he's nowhere to be seen.": "2月27日 - 誰かが私の個人オフィスに侵入して、チーズケーキだけ食べていると確信している。ケビンがやりそうなことだが、彼の姿はどこにもない。",
  "Mar 1 - After routine inspection everything has been accounted for, except the prototype phase shift module Dr. Nilson has been working on. I have a very bad feeling about this.": "3月1日 - 定期点検の結果、ニルソン博士が開発中の試作位相転移モジュール以外はすべて確認された。嫌な予感がする。",
  "Mar 2 - I found a note on my desk. 'You talk about cheesecake while you sleep. You also snore. Love, Kevin.'. I think I need to undergo psychiatric reevaluation.": "3月2日 - 机にメモがあった。「お前は寝言でチーズケーキの話をしている。あと、いびきもうるさい。愛を込めて、ケビン」。精神科の再評価を受ける必要があると思う。",
  "Mar 4 - Kevin refused to work with any of the Glitch this week. Kept yelling that he couldn't bare the thought of thinking with those 'console peasants'. Which was odd, as the Glitch in that group aren't even near any console-panels.": "3月4日 - ケビンが今週グリッチ族との作業を全面拒否した。あの「家庭用ゲーム機の平民ども」と考えることすら耐えられないと叫び続けた。そのグループのグリッチ族はコンソールパネルの近くにすらいなかったので、妙な話だった。",
  "Mar 8 - Kevin assaulted several crewmembers by throwing a capture capsule in their face after yelling at the top of his lungs - and I quote - 'Our eyes have met, we must battle!'. We still have no idea when, or how he managed to catch an adult Fleshreaper.": "3月8日 - ケビンが大声で「目が合った、バトルだ！」と叫んだ後、数名のクルーの顔にキャプチャーカプセルを投げつけた。成体のフレッシュリーパーをいつ、どうやって捕獲したのか、いまだに分からない。",
  "Mar 12 - He won't stop saying 'Eureka! I've done it!' and is running around like a maniac.": "3月12日 - 「エウレカ！ やったぞ！」と言い続けて狂ったように走り回っている。",
  "Mar 20 - He is still doing the Eureka thing.": "3月20日 - まだエウレカをやっている。",
  "Mar 28 - Well, he's finally showed us what his Eureka moment is. Apparently, he has single-handedly discovered how to make hamsters able to self-replicate instantly via application of sunlight. Why he thinks this is a pleasing result, that's another story entirely. He set them loose from his rather cramped lab into the goddamned *greenhouse*!": "3月28日 - ようやくエウレカの成果を見せてくれた。どうやら、日光を当てるだけでハムスターを即座に自己複製させる方法を独力で発見したらしい。なぜこれが喜ばしい成果だと思うのかは別の話だ。かなり手狭になった研究室からハムスターを*温室*に放し飼いにした！",
  "Mar 29 - He shared the reason of why he made this hamster fiasco happen; It was purely so that he could make a star system completely composed of hamsters. A ham-star, he said.": "3月29日 - このハムスター騒動を起こした理由を明かした。完全にハムスターで構成された星系を作るためだけだった。ハム・スター（ハムスター）だと言った。",
  "April 1 - Nothing to report.": "4月1日 - 報告事項なし。",
  "April 2 - Kevin got air of our fossil restoration project, and wanted to join in. We gave him a Trilobite to clean off, and he did a good job at it (surprisingly). Unfortunately, we made the mistake of letting him choose the next fossil he wanted to prepare for showcasing on the exposition on the lower decks. We had to pry private Holix's grandmother - who came to visit - out of Kevin's hands.": "4月2日 - ケビンが化石修復プロジェクトの話を聞きつけ、参加を希望した。三葉虫のクリーニングを任せたところ、意外にも立派にやり遂げた。残念なことに、次に展示する化石を自分で選ばせるという過ちを犯した。見学に来たホリックス一等兵のおばあちゃんをケビンの手から引き離さなければならなかった。",
  "April 9 - Kevin was urinating on one of the visiting Kirhos delegates, and got mad when we attempted to stop him. He claims that the man was stung by invisible jellyfish and he was merely attempting to help him ease his pain.": "4月9日 - ケビンが訪問中のキルホスの代表団の一人に放尿しているところを発見された。止めようとすると怒り出し、その男は透明なクラゲに刺されたのであり、痛みを和らげようとしただけだと主張した。",
  "April 12 - I found Kevin in the break room today, rolling around on stolen cheese. We made eye contact. He seemed ashamed. He then moved over, and motioned that I should join him and explained by merely stating 'it's Tuesday'.": "4月12日 - 今日、休憩室でケビンが盗んだチーズの上を転がり回っているのを発見した。目が合った。彼は恥ずかしそうだった。それから横に寄って、私も加わるよう手招きし、「火曜日だから」とだけ説明した。",
  "April 13 - Dereck was excited that Kevin had made him lunch today. When I explained the stolen cheese...he seemed somewhat less excited about his 'delicious cheese sandwich'": "4月13日 - デレックはケビンが昼食を作ってくれたことに喜んでいた。盗まれたチーズのことを説明すると...「美味しいチーズサンドイッチ」への興奮がいくらか冷めたようだった。",
  "April 15 - Today it was like Kevin only just ever discovered what water did with paper. And he wouldn't shut up about how wonderfully soggy it felt.": "4月15日 - 今日のケビンは、まるで水が紙にどう作用するかを初めて発見したかのようだった。びしょびしょの感触がいかに素晴らしいか、延々と語り続けた。",
  "April 18 - Kevin has wandered around for three days, screaming at the top of his lungs. When asked to stop, he tells us that 'my caps lock key is broken' and then gives us the finger.": "4月18日 - ケビンが3日間、大声で叫びながら歩き回っている。やめるよう頼むと、「Caps Lockキーが壊れている」と言って中指を立てた。",
  "April 19 - Today Kevin celebrated nudity day. This makes the total of 'times we didn't want to see Kevin nude' to 322.": "4月19日 - 今日、ケビンはヌーディストデーを祝った。これで「ケビンの裸を見たくなかった回数」が通算322回となった。",
  "April 25 - The medical bay was full of honey bees today. Kevin said he could help, and provided a briefcase. It held a rather large amount of yet more agitated bees.": "4月25日 - 今日、医療室がミツバチだらけになった。ケビンが手伝うと言い、ブリーフケースを差し出した。中にはさらに大量の、もっと興奮した蜂が入っていた。",
  "April 26 - He now calls himself Dr.Bees. Non-stop. As if that wasn't annoying, he just burst into my office and said 'What's this? an office woefully unpopulated by bees? This briefcase full of BEES should take care of that!' and poured them into my office.": "4月26日 - 彼は今や自分をDr.ビーズと名乗っている。ひっきりなしに。それだけでも迷惑なのに、私のオフィスに飛び込んできて「何だこれは？ 嘆かわしいほど蜂が不足したオフィスか？ この蜂入りブリーフケースで解決だ！」と言って蜂をオフィスにぶちまけた。",
  "April 30 - Kevin came to the kitchen with a meal of cooked human hands, and fried faces today. Despite the morbid thoughts we had, and the salivating Floran crewmembers, we had to ask where he gotten these horrid recipes. He merely said he had an Alpaca friend somewhere, who was a hat enthusiast by the name of Carl.": "4月30日 - ケビンが調理した人間の手と揚げた顔をキッチンに持ってきた。不吉な想像とよだれを垂らすフローランのクルーを前にしつつ、どこでこんな恐ろしいレシピを入手したのか聞かなければならなかった。彼はただ、どこかにいるカールという名の帽子マニアのアルパカの友人がいると言っただけだった。",
  "May 2 - Our weapons research team had to ban Kevin from their wing, after he managed to destroy a data bank with a modified electric toothbrush.": "5月2日 - 武器研究チームがケビンを立入禁止にせざるを得なかった。改造した電動歯ブラシでデータバンクを破壊した後のことだ。",
  "May 15 - He's stopped being a douche for a bit now. I'm actually a little concerned. Ever since his friend MacReady left for the Wastes he's been acting a little odd...": "5月15日 - しばらくバカなことをやめている。正直少し心配だ。友人のマクレディがウェイストランドに出発してから、少し様子がおかしい...",
  "May 20 - Well, seems he is back to normal. I awoke today with Kevin sitting on the edge of my bed, petting my feet and talking to them as if they were puppies. When I woke up, he told me I wasn't invited and I should leave , but leave the feet.": "5月20日 - どうやら通常運転に戻ったようだ。今日目覚めると、ケビンがベッドの端に座り、私の足を撫でながら子犬に話しかけるように語りかけていた。起きると、「お前は招かれていない、出て行け。ただし足は置いていけ」と言われた。",
  "May 28 - Every single piece of art in the station has been replaced with a picture of Kevin and the words 'Lip Gloss' in bold underneath. No one has any clue what the hell this is about.": "5月28日 - ステーション内のすべての美術品が、ケビンの写真とその下に太字で「リップグロス」と書かれた画像に差し替えられていた。これがいったい何の意味なのか、誰にも見当がつかない。",
  "May 30 - Every single object in the station, floors included, is coated in lip gloss. I have no idea how this was accomplished. We were only gone 8 hours! Cleaning it is next to impossible. What an asshole.": "5月30日 - ステーション内のすべてのオブジェクトが、床を含めてリップグロスでコーティングされている。どうやってこれを成し遂げたのか分からない。我々はたった8時間留守にしただけだ！ 掃除はほぼ不可能だ。なんて奴だ。",
  "Aug 31 - Nothing from Kevin for a whole month. Then, suddenly we all get thrown out of the outpost by some strange force. Apparently Kevin found a way to alter space-time by dropping liquids on painted dirt.": "8月31日 - ケビンからまるまる1ヶ月何もなかった。そして突然、全員が謎の力で基地から放り出された。どうやらケビンが、塗料を塗った土に液体を垂らすことで時空を改変する方法を発見したらしい。",
  "Sep 1 - Kevin invited a friend over with a particularly limited set of vocabulary. Since this time, 6 staff members can do nothing but speak the exact same dialect.": "9月1日 - ケビンが語彙が著しく限られた友人を招待した。それ以来、6名のスタッフがまったく同じ方言しか話せなくなっている。",
  "Sep 2 - Greg. Gregga greg?": "9月2日 - グレッグ。グレッガ グレッグ？",
  "Sep 5 - Kevin had baked cookies today and was handing them out. We didn't pay much attention to it at the time, although we should have. He came from the genetics lab with those. It wasn't clear to us until the cookies showed sentience by pleading not to eat them, and talking about their cardboard-related ideas for several minutes. We incinerated most of them, though one of them is kept around, for research purposes.": "9月5日 - ケビンが今日クッキーを焼いて配っていた。その時はあまり気にしなかったが、注意すべきだった。あのクッキーは遺伝学研究室から持ってきたものだった。クッキーが知性を示し、食べないでくれと懇願し、段ボールに関するアイデアを数分間語り始めるまで、我々は気づかなかった。大半を焼却処分したが、一枚は研究目的で保管している。",
  "Sep 7 - We were awakened by terrible screams today. When we investigated, we found Kevin in a state of utter horror. When pressed for further information he merely gestured vaguely towards the kitchen. Inside the kitchen we found an open can. Inside the can we found a smaller version of Kevin, gesturing to a micro-sized version of the kitchen, inside of which was a tiny can, containing another tinier Kevin...and so on. We have no idea how this was done.": "9月7日 - 今日、恐ろしい叫び声で目が覚めた。調べてみると、ケビンが完全に恐怖に怯えていた。詳細を聞くと、ただキッチンの方を漠然と指差すだけだった。キッチンには開いた缶があった。缶の中には小さいケビンがいて、ミニチュアサイズのキッチンの方を指差していた。そのキッチンの中にも小さな缶があり、さらに小さなケビンが入っていた...延々と。どうやってこれが成し遂げられたのか見当もつかない。",
  "Sep 9 - The entire food supply has been replaced with odd, lumpy, red waffles that have an unusually meat-like aroma and a bizarre reddish-brown color with flecks of black not unlike rotting meat. I don't think I want to know. Kevin insists they are cherry flavor.": "9月9日 - 食料備蓄がすべて奇妙なでこぼこした赤いワッフルに置き換えられていた。異様に肉のような匂いがし、腐った肉を思わせる黒い斑点のある奇妙な赤茶色をしている。知りたくもない。ケビンはチェリー味だと主張している。",
  "Sep 12 - Kevin was chasing scientists around with an agitated Lilodon today, humming a tune with increasing intensity. Often suggesting we should get a bigger boat. In related news, our boats are all missing.": "9月12日 - ケビンが興奮したリロドンを持って科学者たちを追いかけ回し、どんどん激しくなるメロディーをハミングしていた。しきりに「もっと大きい船が必要だ」と提案していた。関連して、我々の船はすべて行方不明だ。",
  "Sep 13 - A loud buzzing sound is driving us all crazy. It's coming from Kevin's room. I am positive he's doing the bee thing again.": "9月13日 - 大きなブンブンという音が全員を狂わせている。ケビンの部屋から聞こえてくる。また蜂をやっているに違いない。",
  "Sep 14 - The bee sound has stopped, and a rather large shipment of milk was delivered today. Exactly 2972 cartons, to be exact. I have no idea why.": "9月14日 - 蜂の音が止み、かなり大量の牛乳が届いた。正確には2972パック。なぜだかまったく分からない。",
  "Sep 19 - The cartons of milk have been relabelled 'Sour Milk and Bees'. Every food item in everyone's private stores has been swapped with this. Our food, on the other hand, has been elaborately stitched into dresses.": "9月19日 - 牛乳パックのラベルが全て「酸っぱい牛乳とハチ」に貼り替えられていた。全員の私物の食料が全てこれに置き換わっている。一方、我々の食料はというと、手の込んだドレスに縫い込まれていた",
  "Sep 8 - Kevin figured out time travel. Screw you guys!": "9月8日 - ケビンがタイムトラベルを実現した。くたばれお前ら！",
  "Sep 9 - Today there were several rib-shattering injuries reported to staff. Upon further investigation I discovered that Vinalisj had a sign taped to his back. It read 'FREE RIDES $0.25'. People decided to go along with Kevin's pranks for a day and it appears that there have been multiple people jumping on the director's tail and promptly being flung into the nearest wall or desk.": "9月9日 - 今日、肋骨を砕くような怪我の報告が複数あった。調査したところ、ヴィナリシュの背中に看板がテープで貼り付けられているのを発見した。そこには「乗り放題 0.25ドル」と書かれていた。みんなケビンのイタズラに一日だけ乗ることにしたらしく、複数の人間が所長の尻尾に飛び乗り、即座に最寄りの壁や机に投げ飛ばされるという事態が発生していた",
  "Sep 10 - The directors' office door has been crudely painted like a skull-mounted stone crypt door, and his nameplate replaced with a poster saying 'This is the Vinal boss'. The only way in appears to be by opening Steve's storage locker and obtaining a key that weighs approximately 4 tons. Upon touching the key a very loud voice informs you that you have obtained the boss key, and plays a catchy 4-note tune. Any attempt to move is impossible unless you remove the key from the storage. Nobody is strong enough to do so.": "9月10日 - 所長のオフィスのドアが、頭蓋骨を模した石の地下墓所の扉のように雑に塗装され、名札が「ここはヴァイナルボスの部屋」というポスターに差し替えられていた。入る唯一の方法はスティーブの収納ロッカーを開けて約4トンの鍵を手に入れることらしい。鍵に触れると非常に大きな声で「ボスの鍵を手に入れた！」と告げられ、キャッチーな4音のメロディが流れる。鍵を収納から取り除かない限り移動は不可能だ。そしてそれができるほど力の強い者は誰もいない",
  "Oct 2 - Xiticix, our security officer, has been in a huff all day. Kevin has been randomly jumping out from behind various office furniture and spraying him with bug spray. Upon being asked to stop, Kevin merely answers with KILLS BUGS DEAD and hides behind the planter in the lobby where we can plainly see him.": "10月2日 - 警備主任のシティシクスが一日中不機嫌だった。ケビンがオフィスの家具の陰からランダムに飛び出しては殺虫スプレーを浴びせていたのだ。やめるよう言われると、ケビンはただ「害虫は確実に駆除！」と答え、ロビーの植木鉢の後ろに隠れた。我々からは丸見えなのだが",
  "Oct 4 - The assault on Xiticix continues. Kevin has stolen every single piece of his clothing, and replaced them with numerous decorative cod-pieces. Xiticix is annoyed for several reasons. Firstly, his species does not possess mammalian genitals to facilitate such fashion accessories, and two, Kevin is also an insect and *knows* this is the case. When pressed, Kevin insists that wearing the cod-pieces will help him *grow* them.": "10月4日 - シティシクスへの攻撃は続いている。ケビンは彼の衣服を一着残らず盗み出し、大量の装飾的なコッドピースに差し替えた。シティシクスが怒っている理由は複数ある。第一に、彼の種族はそのようなファッションアクセサリーを必要とする哺乳類の生殖器を持っていないこと。第二に、ケビン自身も昆虫であり、そのことを*知っている*ということだ。問い詰めると、ケビンはコッドピースを着ければ生殖器が*生えてくる*と主張した",
  "Oct 9 - Interestingly, Kevin was not lying. Xiticix has grown a mammalian set of genitals. He is dismayed by this fact. Kevin insists he will be 'happier this way because now he can fly if it spins fast enough'": "10月9日 - 興味深いことに、ケビンは嘘をついていなかった。シティシクスに哺乳類の生殖器が生えたのだ。彼はこの事実に愕然としている。ケビンは「こうなった方が幸せだよ、十分速く回転させれば空も飛べるし」と主張している",
  "Oct 10 - Vinalisj has seen the situation with Xiticix and is now screaming constantly. I didn't know that a creature as large as him could make such a high-pitched, piercing shriek.": "10月10日 - ヴィナリシュがシティシクスの状況を目撃し、ずっと叫び続けている。あれほど大きな生物があんな甲高い、耳をつんざくような悲鳴を上げられるとは知らなかった",
  "Oct 12 - While the cause is not clear, somehow Kevin has managed to convert every living thing in the outpost, myself included, into a moldable lump of putty. It is frustratingly difficult to write this log.": "10月12日 - 原因は不明だが、ケビンはどうにかして基地内の全生物を——私を含めて——こねくり回せるパテの塊に変えてしまった。この記録を書くのが恐ろしく難しい",
  "Oct 14 - 'Someone' placed a pleasure doll dressed as my mother in the staff room. While this was initially humorous, samples have shown that the doll contains traces of my familial DNA. Any attempt to touch or relocate the doll results in it speaking directly to the offender in my mother's voice and seductively asking them to make her a sandwich using rather graphic terminology.": "10月14日 -「誰か」が私の母そっくりの服を着た快楽人形を休憩室に置いた。最初は笑い話だったが、検体分析の結果、人形には私の家族のDNA痕跡が含まれていることが判明した。人形に触れたり移動させようとすると、人形は触った相手に私の母の声で直接語りかけ、かなりきわどい言い回しでサンドイッチを作ってくれと色っぽく頼んでくる",
  "Oct 16 - Steve killed himself. His suicide note simply read 'I hate you, Kevin'. Steve was especially vexed when he resurrected in Kevin's 'replication' terminal. Apparently, Kevin has gene-linked more than himself. How is he getting our samples!?!?! Why can none of us *escape his damnable pranks*?!?!?": "10月16日 - スティーブが自殺した。遺書にはただ「お前が憎い、ケビン」とだけ書かれていた。スティーブはケビンの「複製」端末で蘇生した時、特に激怒していた。どうやらケビンは自分以外の者も遺伝子リンクしていたらしい。どうやって我々のサンプルを手に入れているんだ！？なぜ誰も*あの忌々しいイタズラ*から逃れられないんだ！？",
  "Oct 31-1 - Kevin has claimed to have planned out a 'Halloween' party for later in the day. I am loathe to see what sort of shenanigans he has planned this year, as last year was far from pleasant. He's had various party supplies brought into the lab (where does he even get these things in such quantities?) and several ^red;tons^white; worth of pumpkins. He's barricaded me out of my office, claiming to be the 'Pumpkin King'.": "10月31日-1 - ケビンが今日の夕方に「ハロウィン」パーティーを企画したと言い出した。去年は全く楽しくなかったので、今年はどんな馬鹿騒ぎを計画しているのか見るのが恐ろしい。彼は様々なパーティー用品を研究室に持ち込み（一体どこからあんな大量のものを調達してくるんだ？）、数^red;トン^white;分のカボチャも用意した。私のオフィスをバリケードで封鎖し、自分が「パンプキンキング」だと名乗っている",
  "Oct 31-2 - Kevin has taken the liberty of applying what I am hoping is fake blood to the walls of the lab. If it's real blood, that brings up the question of not only how he obtained such large quantities, but also from where. I'm thinking I should take an impromptu vacation just to avoid Kevin's schemes.": "10月31日-2 - ケビンが研究室の壁に、偽物であることを祈るが、血を塗りたくっていた。本物の血だとすれば、どうやってあれほど大量に入手したのか、そしてどこから手に入れたのかという疑問が生じる。ケビンの企みを避けるため、急遽休暇を取るべきだと思い始めている",
  "Oct 31-3 - I must admit, Kevin has a rather detailed zombie costume. Despite what it is depicting being rather graphic, the attention to detail is absolutely flawless. If he weren't so insufferable, I would actually give him the compliment in person.": "10月31日-3 - 認めざるを得ないが、ケビンのゾンビコスチュームはかなり精巧だ。描写しているものはかなりグロテスクだが、細部へのこだわりは完璧と言っていい。あれほど鬱陶しい奴でなければ、直接褒めてやるのだが",
  "Oct 31-4 - I take back any compliments I've given Kevin. That was not him in a zombie costume but a ^red;real^white; zombie. About ten scientists have been bitten and subsequently converted into undead monstrosities. I'm going to kill Kevin. Right after I kill these zombies. Now where did I leave my revolver?": "10月31日-4 - ケビンへの褒め言葉は全て撤回する。あれはゾンビコスチュームを着たケビンではなく、^red;本物の^white;ゾンビだった。約10人の科学者が噛まれ、次々とアンデッドの化け物に変わっている。ケビンを殺してやる。このゾンビどもを片付けたらすぐにだ。リボルバーはどこに置いたっけ？",
  "^red;-- ERROR: BUFFER OVERFLOW --\n\nA longer codex page is needed to view this entry!\n^#666666;(Use the High-Fidelity Codex to view this page)": "^red;-- エラー: バッファオーバーフロー --\n\nこのエントリを表示するには、より長いコーデックスページが必要です！\n^#666666;（このページを表示するにはハイフィデリティ・コーデックスを使用してください）",
  "^red;The following details infractions allegedly committed against other members of the outpost by one Myulthor 'Kevin' Sanchatak :^reset;\n\n\n^#EDB347;Jun 1^#FFFFFF; - This individual broke into my private office, stole all of my grapes, and rather than eat them constructed an elaborate 'art piece' of me. Peeing on a beehive. He then filled the room with bees, so that when I opened the door I got swarmed and stung 755 times.\n\n^#EDB347;Jun 2^#FFFFFF; - Against all better judgement I allowed Kevin to borrow my bunsen burner. When asked to return it, he brought back a small stack of ash and announced that you can burn a bunsen burner with another bunsen burner if you allow it to burn long enough.\n\n^#EDB347;Jun 3^#FFFFFF; - My lab notes went missing. Weeks of work. When asking around, several others saw Kevin take them from my desk. I found them later, folded up and being used to prop up a wobbly table.\n\n^#EDB347;Jun 12^#FFFFFF; - Kevin got back from vacation today. Is it a coincidence that my lunch was swapped with a bucket of mooshi urine on the same day?\n\n^#EDB347;Jun 13^#FFFFFF; - Kevin is forbidden from using the coffee machine, it took me 2 hours to clean the mess it made. I don't care where he got all that blood, it's just unsanitary and I won't stand for it.\n\n^#EDB347;Jun 14^#FFFFFF; - A reminder that the Coffee Machine in the kitchen is to be used EXCLUSIVELY for brewing coffee. Any other substance should not be used under any circumstances, so please do not put any of these in the machine: Fruit (of any kind), Vegetables (of any kind), Meat, Florans,  Pixels, Aether, Mercury, Blood.\n\n^#EDB347;Jun 15^#FFFFFF; - All of the toilet paper rolls appear to have been replaced with sandpaper. All of them. Even the backups. I can hear Kevin giggling.\n\n^#EDB347;Jun 19^#FFFFFF; - Why the hell is all of the hydrochloric acid gone and replaced with vodka?!?!\n\n^#EDB347;Jun 22^#FFFFFF; - That son of a bitch swapped the natural gas and hydrogen tanks. I don't think he realizes how dangerous that could have been.\n\n^#EDB347;Jun 25^#FFFFFF; - Despite his clear genius, when asked on where he completed his education Kevin merely slapped me on the ass and told me to be a good servant and get him a coffee. He then proceeded to follow me around for the rest of the day making 'wide-load' truck-beeping sounds every time I moved.": "^red;以下は、前哨基地の他のメンバーに対してMyulthor「ケヴィン」Sanchatakが犯したとされる違反行為の詳細です：^reset;\n\n^#EDB347;6月1日^#FFFFFF; - この人物は私の個人的なオフィスに侵入し、ブドウをすべて盗み、食べるのではなく「芸術作品」を作り上げました",
  "^#EDB347;Jul 1^#FFFFFF; - No matter how much evidence we provide, Kevin is unwilling to accept that the universe contains more than one odor. He insists it is all simply varition of the same scent. To prove it, he keeps randomly farting at our stations. I really hate this idiot. I honestly want him dead.\n\n^#EDB347;Jul 8^#FFFFFF; - Once again, every last sample in the lab gene storage has been removed and in their place are test tubes with googly-eyes glued to them.\n\n^#EDB347;Jul 9^#FFFFFF; - Kevin has broken into Dr. Lesley's computer. Kevin found out many people keep notes of him. Kevin is popular. This pleases Kevin.\n\n^#EDB347;Jul 7^#FFFFFF; - Twice this week the backup generator fuel was siphoned and completely replaced with Essentia Obscura, causing station-wide hallucinations. Where this fluid was even *obtained* is a question in and of itself.\n\n^#EDB347;Jul 17^#FFFFFF; - Ten days of glorious prank-free nonsense...and then I open up my Plasmic Fluid sample fridge and inside...no samples. There is a note, however, that thanks me for donating to the Juice Salvation Society.\n\n^#EDB347;Jul 18^#FFFFFF; - Woke up to my eyelids glued together. Thanks, Kevin.\n\n^#EDB347;Jul 21^#FFFFFF; - I cannot even begin to imagine how long it took Kevin to construct this statue of Kluex composed entirely of severed Poptop penises. If it weren't so horrific and appalling, I might actually be impressed. I'm less than pleased that he chose to do it on the long weekend, as it has been festering in the lobby for four days.\n\n^#EDB347;Jul 25^#FFFFFF; - Some one drown him! Please! I can't fathom how he considers it humorous but once again he has traded my prosthetic leg to a Gnome in exchange for a Gnome-sized jar of peanut butter. I'm not sure how he even *does* it. It's biometrically locked to my torso!": "^#EDB347;7月1日^#FFFFFF; - どれだけ証拠を提示しても、ケヴィンは宇宙に複数の匂いが存在することを認めません。すべては同じ香りの変種にすぎないと主張します。それを証明するために、ステーションで突然おならをし続けています。このバカが本当に嫌いです。正直なところ、彼には",
  "^#EDB347;Aug 4^#FFFFFF; - Someone put ixo eggs in the air system. There are now about 900 ixolings rampaging in the kitchen. To 'calm them down' Kevin then added four pounds of Rage Powder. Four. Pounds. Where did he get that much of a class-A narcotic?!?!\n\n^#EDB347;Aug 8^#FFFFFF; - Another 'fat guy' joke from Kevin. He's recorded sounds of a tuba playing. Whenever I move, he presses play. This has been ongoing since Jul 16th, and I can't take it anymore.\n\n^#EDB347;Aug 12^#FFFFFF; - I really can't figure out how it is comical to replace someone's hair products with watered down sulphuric acid. My skin may be immune, but now I'm bald and look like the ass of a newborn.\n\n^#EDB347;Aug 22^#FFFFFF; - I think he's finally toned it down...Nothing since the 12th.\n\n^#EDB347;Aug 23^#FFFFFF; - Damnit. I spoke too soon. He apparently replaced all of the ostrich eggs in the enclosure with raptor eggs. They hatched, and ate the babies. When we got angry, he explained 'the eggs were lonely. I gave them friends.'\n\n^#EDB347;Aug 26^#FFFFFF; - Kevin won't let anyone near the raptors. He has dressed them all in tiny little ballerina tutus and refers to them as his 'students'.": "^#EDB347;8月4日^#FFFFFF; - 誰かが空気系統にイクソの卵を入れた。今、キッチンでは約900匹のイクソリングが暴れ回っている。「落ち着かせるため」にケヴィンはレイジパウダーを4ポンド追加した。4ポンドも。どこでそれほどのクラスA麻薬を手に入れたのか？！\n\n^#EDB347;8月8日^#FFFFFF; - また「デブ男",
  "^#EDB347;Oct 12^#FFFFFF; - I'm impressed. In a short period of time, Kevin has trained the raptors to perform a simple ballet routine. Unfortunately, he calls it 'dance of the death claws', and had them perform it...in the now-repopulated ostrich enclosure.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 13^#FFFFFF; - We've decided to dismantle the ostrich enclosure. We've invited some bee-science folk to come and fill the space. It made sense, on account of the *thousands of bees* he put in my office in June still roaming around.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 15^#FFFFFF; - I attempted to prank Kevin. I apparently suck. Not only did it fail, he found it, dismantled it and placed it in my room. I am now the proud owner of a giant bucket of Poptop feces spilled on my floor.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 20^#FFFFFF; - I cannot believe that just happened. Kevin weaponized a shark by using a capture ball on a timer attached to a complicated mechanism. I was eating lunch, and a *great white shark* appears directly above my table, eats my lunch, and then enters a portal on the table and dissapears. I really hate Kevin.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 25^#FFFFFF; - Bandits attacked. Kevin used weaponized shark to kill them. Feeling less hateful.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 26^#FFFFFF; - Kevin has used self-same weaponized shark device to instead create Bunny-things that won't stop making adorable sounds. We can't hurt them, because they just burrow into pocket dimensions or something...and then pop back out and annoy. This is not going to be fun.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 27^#FFFFFF; - The Bunny-thing in my office is especially annoying. I think Kevin has genetically modified them, as mine cannot stop swearing. It literally does nothing but call me a litany of racist remarks, gives me the finger, and pops back into its...hole thing.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 29^#FFFFFF; - Three days is enough. I left my office, and had the life support system withdraw all air from the unit. It took six minutes and fifty-three seconds but the bunny-thing died in panic. I am pleased.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 31^#FFFFFF; - Whatever 'Halloween' was on Earth, I am more than certain it does not involve repeated attacks with a limp zucchini while shouting 'Excelsior!'. Kevin, however, disagrees with this and insists his knowledge of Earth ways is unmatched. Our human members are not incredibly pleased about this since Kevin has never even *been* to Earth.": "^#EDB347;10月12日^#FFFFFF; - 感心した。短期間でケヴィンはラプターに簡単なバレエを仕込んだ。残念ながら彼はそれを「デスクロウのダンス」と呼び、再び住民が戻ったダチョウの囲いの中で披露させた。\n\n^#EDB347;10月13日^#FFFFFF; - 我々は決断した",
  "^#EDB347;Dec 25^#FFFFFF; - Well, he waited a while...probably because he was training the raptors again. They have now mastered the art of targeted defecation, and are utilizing this new skill as much as possible. To ensure 'maximum dance power' Kevin has set them to roam free in the nearby woods. They like to aim their shots through the windows when we open them.": "^#EDB347;12月25日^#FFFFFF; - やっと待ちに待った…おそらくラプターの再訓練をしていたのだろう。今やラプターたちは狙い定めた排泄の技術を習得し、可能な限りそのスキルを活用している。「最大のダンスパワー」を確保するため、ケヴィンは彼らを近くの森に放し飼いにした",
  "^#EDB347;Jan 3^#FFFFFF; - I've been getting reports of missing lab equipment and consumables, mostly CO2 canisters. I've decided to increase storage security.\n\n^#EDB347;Jan 5^#FFFFFF; - An explosion on the lower levels led to us finding Kevin launching wooden logs at a steel blade from what appears to be a CO2 cannon, constructed from fridge spare parts and duct tape. Later I also found out he was building an altar in my personal storage room decorated with photographs of my Uncle Steve. I have no idea how he got the pictures. Several piles of shaved wood sat in one corner, and a huge statue of my Uncle riding an angry Bullfrog made from split logs, decorated the other.\n\n^#EDB347;Jan 9^#FFFFFF; - Kevin was caught stealing large amounts of concentrated sulfuric acid, nitric acid and toluene. After an inspection of his room, a large box of nails was found, with the words 'Death to Equestria' scribbled on the side with crayons.\n\n^#EDB347;Jan 15^#FFFFFF; - Kevin has declared this week 'Vuvuzela Appreciation Week' in honor of a now nearly extinct Earth...instrument...if you can call it that. Within about 11 seconds, we wanted to murder him. We are now on hour seven. I have purchased a new rifle from the Ansible network.\n\n^#EDB347;Jan 24^#FFFFFF; - We received a shipment of about 400 000 of these vuvuzelas from the Ansible network. We also received a 15% discount card off our next big-scale purchase. Kevin was later found fuelling a bonfire with them and grilling mice over it.\n\n^#EDB347;Jan 30^#FFFFFF; - Kevin made a shrine for a bigger more primitive apex-like animal the humans had on earth, called 'haramber' or something. He kept making off with several of the stocked bananas. This only means we need to change the password on the food storage...again.": "^#EDB347;1月3日^#FFFFFF; - ラボ用機器や消耗品（主にCO2缶）の紛失報告が入っている。倉庫のセキュリティを強化することにした。\n\n^#EDB347;1月5日^#FFFFFF; - 下層での爆発をきっかけに、ケヴィンが木製の丸太を鋼鉄の刃に向けて何らかの装置から発射していることが発覚した",
  "^#EDB347;Feb 2^#FFFFFF; - Someone switched all of the Smarties with Skittles.\n\n^#EDB347;Feb 8^#FFFFFF; - After Kevin somehow got his hands on an ancient audiotrack of the old Earth music known as 'Darude; sandstorm', we weren't bothered at first. When he wouldn't let that damn song get a rest for several hours, even at night, we had to do something. We scheduled a trip to the most nearby desert biome with dangerous sandstorms tomorrow. Lets see if Kevin ever plays that Gods-forsaken song again after being sandblasted for an hour or two. We'll say it's a picnic.\n\n^#EDB347;Feb 9^#FFFFFF; - Yep. He kept playing the song. Louder. He then composed a version completely in reverse, played only with vomit sounds and a strange repeated word: 'Yolo'.\n\n^#EDB347;Feb 10^#FFFFFF; - I found a deep-fried mooshi scrotum on my desk today along with a side of ice cream and a Happy Birthday card. My birthday was nine months ago. He is also aware that I have an allergic reaction to Mooshi.\n\n^#EDB347;Feb 15^#FFFFFF; - We had to make clear to Kevin that 'surprise-feeding' us Glitch food, doesn't make us do 'the robot' any faster but instead gives us horrible indigestion and potentially lethal food poisoning. He insists that our version of science is akin to (and I quote) 'making love to a dead sea lion in the air while on fire'. I am now attempting to picture exactly what this act would look like.\n\n^#EDB347;Feb 18^#FFFFFF; - Norbert finally snapped. He pushed Kevin off the roof after luring him upstairs for 'ninja practice', a thing which no Kevin can resist. We had assumed at long last that we had freed ourselves from his tyrannical pranking. We were sorely mistaken. It turns out he has gene-linked his mind to this facility. Any attempt at murder results in a clone being immediately spawned using his most recent brainscan. He claims 'the station made him do it'. He also apparently 'invented the question mark'.\n\n^#EDB347;Feb 21^#FFFFFF; - Kevin kept persistently saying that 'the bird is the word' today. This made the meeting of the engineering staff awkward, seeing as he just burst in. And Axiena, the fuel-expert of us, who is an Avian was there. Now, being a 'bird' wouldn't be so bad to ignore kevin's 'quirks' but she's also a mute. Being reminded that she couldn't 'be the word' at all (having no vocal capability since birth) was rather rude. Preparing a cake congratulating her on her muteness was worse.\n\n^#EDB347;Feb 24^#FFFFFF; - Kevin came back from a research expedition. He brought somebody named 'Greg' with him. Please kill me.\n\n^#EDB347;Feb 25^#FFFFFF; - Kevin has been missing for several days. Nobody knows where he is. Also, somebody has been eating my cheesecake. I'll ask the cooks to bring it to my office.\n\n^#EDB347;Feb 27^#FFFFFF; - I'm sure somebody is breaking into my personal office to do nothing else but eat my cheesecake. Sounds like something Kevin would do, but he's nowhere to be seen.": "^#EDB347;2月2日^#FFFFFF; - 誰かがスマーティーズをすべてスキトルズにすり替えた。\n\n^#EDB347;2月8日^#FFFFFF; - ケヴィンが何らかの方法で「Darude; Sandstorm」として知られる古い地球の音楽の古い音源を入手した後、最初は気にしなかった。しかし何日もその曲を休ませない",
  "^#EDB347;Mar 1^#FFFFFF; - After routine inspection everything has been accounted for, except the prototype phase shift module Dr. Nilson has been working on. I have a very bad feeling about this.\n\n^#EDB347;Mar 2^#FFFFFF; - I found a note on my desk. 'You talk about cheesecake while you sleep. You also snore. Love, Kevin.'. I think I need to undergo psychiatric reevaluation.\n\n^#EDB347;Mar 4^#FFFFFF; - Kevin refused to work with any of the Glitch this week. Kept yelling that he couldn't bare the thought of thinking with those 'console peasants'. Which was odd, as the Glitch in that group aren't even near any console-panels.\n\n^#EDB347;Mar 8^#FFFFFF; - Kevin assaulted several crewmembers by throwing a capture capsule in their face after yelling at the top of his lungs - and I quote - 'Our eyes have met, we must battle!'. We still have no idea when, or how he managed to catch an adult Fleshreaper.\n\n^#EDB347;Mar 12^#FFFFFF; - He won't stop saying 'Eureka! I've done it!' and is running around like a maniac.\n\n^#EDB347;Mar 20^#FFFFFF; - He is still doing the Eureka thing.\n\n^#EDB347;Mar 28^#FFFFFF; - Well, he's finally showed us what his Eureka moment is. Apparently, he has single-handedly discovered how to make hamsters able to self-replicate instantly via application of sunlight. Why he thinks this is a pleasing result, that's another story entirely. He set them loose from his rather cramped lab into the goddamned *greenhouse*!\n\n^#EDB347;Mar 29^#FFFFFF; - He shared the reason of why he made this hamster fiasco happen; It was purely so that he could make a star system completely composed of hamsters. A ham-star, he said.": "^#EDB347;3月1日^#FFFFFF; - 定期検査の結果、ニルソン博士が開発中だった試作位相シフトモジュール以外はすべて正常。非常に嫌な予感がする。\n\n^#EDB347;3月2日^#FFFFFF; - 机の上にメモが置いてあった。「あなたは寝言でチーズケーキの話をしています。あなたも",
  "^#EDB347;April 1^#FFFFFF; - Nothing to report.\n\n^#EDB347;April 2^#FFFFFF; - Kevin got air of our fossil restoration project, and wanted to join in. We gave him a Trilobite to clean off, and he did a good job at it (surprisingly). Unfortunately, we made the mistake of letting him choose the next fossil he wanted to prepare for showcasing on the exposition on the lower decks. We had to pry private Holix's grandmother - who came to visit - out of Kevin's hands.\n\n^#EDB347;April 9^#FFFFFF; - Kevin was urinating on one of the visiting Kirhos delegates, and got mad when we attempted to stop him. He claims that the man was stung by invisible jellyfish and he was merely attempting to help him ease his pain.\n\n^#EDB347;April 12^#FFFFFF; - I found Kevin in the break room today, rolling around on stolen cheese. We made eye contact. He seemed ashamed. He then moved over, and motioned that I should join him and explained by merely stating 'it's Tuesday'.\n\n^#EDB347;April 13^#FFFFFF; - Dereck was excited that Kevin had made him lunch today. When I explained the stolen cheese...he seemed somewhat less excited about his 'delicious cheese sandwich'\n\n^#EDB347;April 15^#FFFFFF; - Today it was like Kevin only just ever discovered what water did with paper. And he wouldn't shut up about how wonderfully soggy it felt.\n\n^#EDB347;April 18^#FFFFFF; - Kevin has wandered around for three days, screaming at the top of his lungs. When asked to stop, he tells us that 'my caps lock key is broken' and then gives us the finger.\n\n^#EDB347;April 19^#FFFFFF; - Today Kevin celebrated nudity day. This makes the total of 'times we didn't want to see Kevin nude' to 322.\n\n^#EDB347;April 25^#FFFFFF; - The medical bay was full of honey bees today. Kevin said he could help, and provided a briefcase. It held a rather large amount of yet more agitated bees.\n\n^#EDB347;April 26^#FFFFFF; - He now calls himself Dr.Bees. Non-stop. As if that wasn't annoying, he just burst into my office and said 'What's this? an office woefully unpopulated by bees? This briefcase full of BEES should take care of that!' and poured them into my office.\n\n^#EDB347;April 30^#FFFFFF; - Kevin came to the kitchen with a meal of cooked human hands, and fried faces today. Despite the morbid thoughts we had, and the salivating Floran crewmembers, we had to ask where he gotten these horrid recipes. He merely said he had an Alpaca friend somewhere, who was a hat enthusiast by the name of Carl.": "^#EDB347;4月1日^#FFFFFF; - 特記事項なし。\n\n^#EDB347;4月2日^#FFFFFF; - ケヴィンが化石復元プロジェクトを耳にして参加したがった。三葉虫を渡したところ（驚くべきことに）上手くやり遂げた。残念ながら、次の化石を選ばせてしまったのが間違いだった",
  "^#EDB347;May 2^#FFFFFF; - Our weapons research team had to ban Kevin from their wing, after he managed to destroy a data bank with a modified electric toothbrush.\n\n^#EDB347;May 15^#FFFFFF; - He's stopped being a douche for a bit now. I'm actually a little concerned. Ever since his friend MacReady left for the Wastes he's been acting a little odd...\n\n^#EDB347;May 20^#FFFFFF; - Well, seems he is back to normal. I awoke today with Kevin sitting on the edge of my bed, petting my feet and talking to them as if they were puppies. When I woke up, he told me I wasn't invited and I should leave , but leave the feet.\n\n^#EDB347;May 28^#FFFFFF; - Every single piece of art in the station has been replaced with a picture of Kevin and the words 'Lip Gloss' in bold underneath. No one has any clue what the hell this is about.\n\n^#EDB347;May 30^#FFFFFF; - Every single object in the station, floors included, is coated in lip gloss. I have no idea how this was accomplished. We were only gone 8 hours! Cleaning it is next to impossible. What an asshole.": "^#EDB347;5月2日^#FFFFFF; - 武器研究チームは改造した電動歯ブラシでデータバンクを破壊した後、ケヴィンを部門から追い出さなければならなかった。\n\n^#EDB347;5月15日^#FFFFFF; - しばらくの間、嫌がらせをやめている。少し心配だ。友人のマクレディが去って以来",
  "^#EDB347;Sep 1^#FFFFFF; - Kevin invited a friend over with a particularly limited set of vocabulary. Since this time, 6 staff members can do nothing but speak the exact same dialect.\n\n^#EDB347;Sep 2^#FFFFFF; - Greg. Gregga greg?\n\n^#EDB347;Sep 5^#FFFFFF; - Kevin had baked cookies today and was handing them out. We didn't pay much attention to it at the time, although we should have. He came from the genetics lab with those. It wasn't clear to us until the cookies showed sentience by pleading not to eat them, and talking about their cardboard-related ideas for several minutes. We incinerated most of them, though one of them is kept around, for research purposes.\n\n^#EDB347;Sep 7^#FFFFFF; - We were awakened by terrible screams today. When we investigated, we found Kevin in a state of utter horror. When pressed for further information he merely gestured vaguely towards the kitchen. Inside the kitchen we found an open can. Inside the can we found a smaller version of Kevin, gesturing to a micro-sized version of the kitchen, inside of which was a tiny can, containing another tinier Kevin...and so on. We have no idea how this was done.\n\n^#EDB347;Sep 9^#FFFFFF; - The entire food supply has been replaced with odd, lumpy, red waffles that have an unusually meat-like aroma and a bizarre reddish-brown color with flecks of black not unlike rotting meat. I don't think I want to know. Kevin insists they are cherry flavor.\n\n^#EDB347;Sep 12^#FFFFFF; - Kevin was chasing scientists around with an agitated Lilodon today, humming a tune with increasing intensity. Often suggesting we should get a bigger boat. In related news, our boats are all missing.\n\n^#EDB347;Sep 13^#FFFFFF; - A loud buzzing sound is driving us all crazy. It's coming from Kevin's room. I am positive he's doing the bee thing again.\n\n^#EDB347;Sep 14^#FFFFFF; - The bee sound has stopped, and a rather large shipment of milk was delivered today. Exactly 2972 cartons, to be exact. I have no idea why.\n\n^#EDB347;Sep 19^#FFFFFF; - The cartons of milk have been relabelled 'Sour Milk and Bees'. Every food item in everyone's private stores has been swapped with this. Our food, on the other hand, has been elaborately stitched into dresses.\n\n^#EDB347;Sep 8^#FFFFFF; - Kevin figured out time travel. Screw you guys!\n\n^#EDB347;Sep 9^#FFFFFF; - Today there were several rib-shattering injuries reported to staff. Upon further investigation I discovered that Vinalisj had a sign taped to his back. It read 'FREE RIDES $0.25'. People decided to go along with Kevin's pranks for a day and it appears that there have been multiple people jumping on the director's tail and promptly being flung into the nearest wall or desk.\n\n^#EDB347;Sep 10^#FFFFFF; - The directors' office door has been crudely painted like a skull-mounted stone crypt door, and his nameplate replaced with a poster saying 'This is the Vinal boss'. The only way in appears to be by opening Steve's storage locker and obtaining a key that weighs approximately 4 tons. Upon touching the key a very loud voice informs you that you have obtained the boss key, and plays a catchy 4-note tune. Any attempt to move is impossible unless you remove the key from the storage. Nobody is strong enough to do so.": "^#EDB347;9月1日^#FFFFFF; - ケヴィンが語彙の非常に限られた友人を招待した。それ以来、6人のスタッフメンバーが全員まったく同じ方言しか話せなくなった。\n\n^#EDB347;9月2日^#FFFFFF; - グレッグ。グレッグが グレッグ？\n\n^#EDB347;9月5日^#FFFFFF; - ケヴィンが今日クッキーを焼いて配り始めた",
  "^#EDB347;Oct 2^#FFFFFF; - Xiticix, our security officer, has been in a huff all day. Kevin has been randomly jumping out from behind various office furniture and spraying him with bug spray. Upon being asked to stop, Kevin merely answers with KILLS BUGS DEAD and hides behind the planter in the lobby where we can plainly see him.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 4^#FFFFFF; - The assault on Xiticix continues. Kevin has stolen every single piece of his clothing, and replaced them with numerous decorative cod-pieces. Xiticix is annoyed for several reasons. Firstly, his species does not possess mammalian genitals to facilitate such fashion accessories, and two, Kevin is also an insect and *knows* this is the case. When pressed, Kevin insists that wearing the cod-pieces will help him *grow* them.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 9^#FFFFFF; - Interestingly, Kevin was not lying. Xiticix has grown a mammalian set of genitals. He is dismayed by this fact. Kevin insists he will be 'happier this way because now he can fly if it spins fast enough'\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 10^#FFFFFF; - Vinalisj has seen the situation with Xiticix and is now screaming constantly. I didn't know that a creature as large as him could make such a high-pitched, piercing shriek.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 12^#FFFFFF; - While the cause is not clear, somehow Kevin has managed to convert every living thing in the outpost, myself included, into a moldable lump of putty. It is frustratingly difficult to write this log.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 14^#FFFFFF; - 'Someone' placed a pleasure doll dressed as my mother in the staff room. While this was initially humorous, samples have shown that the doll contains traces of my familial DNA. Any attempt to touch or relocate the doll results in it speaking directly to the offender in my mother's voice and seductively asking them to make her a sandwich using rather graphic terminology.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 16^#FFFFFF; - Steve killed himself. His suicide note simply read 'I hate you, Kevin'. Steve was especially vexed when he resurrected in Kevin's 'replication' terminal. Apparently, Kevin has gene-linked more than himself. How is he getting our samples!?!?! Why can none of us *escape his damnable pranks*?!?!?\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 31-1^#FFFFFF; - Kevin has claimed to have planned out a 'Halloween' party for later in the day. I am loathe to see what sort of shenanigans he has planned this year, as last year was far from pleasant. He's had various party supplies brought into the lab (where does he even get these things in such quantities?) and several ^red;tons^white; worth of pumpkins. He's barricaded me out of my office, claiming to be the 'Pumpkin King'.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 31-2^#FFFFFF; - Kevin has taken the liberty of applying what I am hoping is fake blood to the walls of the lab. If it's real blood, that brings up the question of not only how he obtained such large quantities, but also from where. I'm thinking I should take an impromptu vacation just to avoid Kevin's schemes.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 31-3^#FFFFFF; - I must admit, Kevin has a rather detailed zombie costume. Despite what it is depicting being rather graphic, the attention to detail is absolutely flawless. If he weren't so insufferable, I would actually give him the compliment in person.\n\n^#EDB347;Oct 31-4^#FFFFFF; - I take back any compliments I've given Kevin. That was not him in a zombie costume but a ^red;real^white; zombie. About ten scientists have been bitten and subsequently converted into undead monstrosities. I'm going to kill Kevin. Right after I kill these zombies. Now where did I leave my revolver?": "^#EDB347;10月2日^#FFFFFF; - セキュリティ担当のシティシックスは一日中機嫌が悪かった。ケヴィンが様々なオフィス家具の陰から突然飛び出して虫除けスプレーを吹きかけているのだ。やめるよう求めると、ケヴィンはただ「KILLS BUGS DEAD」と答えてロビーのプランターの陰に隠れた",
  "^#EDB347;Nov 16^#FFFFFF; - Today we had a new visitor, and by \"new\" I mean \"we have never seen this species up until today\". He says his species is \"Spirit Guardian\", or just \"Spirit\" for short. He was quite popular with the bio-science team, given that his species has biological males and females, yet they do not have the organs necessary for procreation. He explained that they are instead created by a giant tree called the \"Spirit Tree\".\n\nThis information was very interesting to our team members, so they asked him to return to the outpost tomorrow for some testing. I bring this up in the infraction log because I couldn't help but to notice Kevin frequently walking in front of the doorway to our meeting room during our initial encounter with the Spirit. It was kind of giving me a bad vibe. I'll have to ask him what's on his mind.\n\n^#EDB347;Nov 17^#FFFFFF; - Turns out that Kevin was simply interested in participating in the tests we had planned for today. We had planned to take a genetic sample, take measurements of his body proportions and mass, and get other various physiological attributes. The usual stuff.\n\nEverything went smoothly, and dare I say that Kevin was actually *pretty helpful* in getting this thing done. Not only that, but our visitor became quite comfortable with him. I was thinking on actually thanking him for his good work, but before I could, Kevin left the lab because he had to \"go to the bathroom\". Not that big a deal, we were in the conclusion process anyway, so we were able to finish the work without him. Turns out, Kevin was just waiting behind the doorway with an airhorn. When the Spirit left the room, Kevin blew the horn. The Spirit got scared so badly that when he kicked off of the wall to propel himself away, he ended up putting a good size dent into the sheet metal. I think the sound of him kicking the wall startled people more than the airhorn did, now that I consider it.": "^#EDB347;11月16日^#FFFFFF; - 今日、新しい来客があった。「新しい」とは「今日まで見たことのない種族」という意味だ。彼は自分の種族を「スピリットガーディアン」または略して「スピリット」と名乗った。彼の種族には生物学的な男性と女性がいることから、バイオサイエンスチームに非常に人気だった",
  "Day 3 - I wonder if the beings at this outpost realize that my catlike antics and simplemindedness are a facade? If they knew what I was, they might ask me to leave. Not like any of them could make me...": "3日目 - この前哨地の住人たちは、私の猫のような振る舞いと単純さが偽装だと気づいているだろうか？正体を知れば出て行くよう頼むかもしれない。誰も強制できないが…",
  "Day 45 - Kevin came in and asked how I managed to fit in my shell if I was so fat. So much for his earlier politeness...I told him 'Suck it in, fatty bug.' He seemed pleased at the answer for some reason...": "45日目 - ケビンが来て、そんなに太っているのにどうやって殻に収まるのか聞いた。前の丁寧さはどこへ…「引っ込めろ、デブ虫」と言ったら、なぜか嬉しそうだった…",
  "Day 26 - Kevin has been missing a week. Not unheard of, but usually he leaves something to keep people busy. This time he's just...absent.": "26日目 - ケビンが1週間行方不明。珍しくはないが、普段は人々を忙しくさせる何かを残す。今回はただ…不在だ。",
  "Day 25 - Kevin's a quick study. Learned how to reactivate the stasis systems and used them to store poptops. Oddly amusing, up until he let them out in the dining room. The florans went ^gray;hungry^reset; tonight.": "25日目 - ケビンは覚えが早い。ステイシスシステムの再起動方法を習得し、ポップトップの保存に使った。食堂に放つまでは妙に面白かった。今夜フローランたちは^gray;空腹のまま^reset;だった。",
  "Day 18 - Should have guessed Kevin had an ulterior motive. I had to correct the blueprint, his design was ^gray;unstable^reset;. Found one of his bodies exploded in one of the vents, mixed with his Atom Smasher. He didn't seem too upset by it.": "18日目 - ケビンに裏の動機があったと気づくべきだった。設計図を修正しなければならなかった。彼の設計は^gray;不安定^reset;だった。通気口で彼の体の一つがアトムスマッシャーと混ざって爆発しているのを発見。彼はあまり動揺していなかった。",
  "Day 19 - Apparently, a week is two days. That damn squeaker is back and keeps trying to sell me their garbage. No, I do not want to buy a used fur throw! Did manage to reverse-engineer the ^gray;orange^reset; Kevin gave me. Some 'dare' that was.": "19日目 - どうやら1週間は2日らしい。あのチューチュー野郎が戻ってきてガラクタを売ろうとする。中古の毛皮は買いたくない！ケビンがくれた^gray;オレンジ^reset;のリバースエンジニアリングには成功した。「挑戦」ってそういうことか。",
  "Day 1 at the outpost - I don't keep track of days. But the first day I was aware was...interesting. I was asleep, then I was awake. A star, sentient. These little creatures laugh when I ask about it, despite the existence of the Novakid. 'Do stars think?'": "前哨地1日目 - 日数は数えない。しかし意識を持った最初の日は…興味深かった。眠っていて、目覚めた。知性を持つ星。ノヴァキッドの存在にもかかわらず、小さな生き物たちはそれを聞くと笑う。「星は考えるのか？」",
  "Day 2 - I realized the concept of ^gray;time^reset; is something smaller beings are obsessed with. They measure it, quantify it, yet far too often lose track of its passing and all too often they fade before my core pulses once. Still getting used to that.": "2日目 - ^gray;時間^reset;という概念は小さな存在たちが執着するものだと気づいた。測り、定量化するが、あまりにも頻繁にその経過を見失い、私のコアが一度脈動する前に消えてしまう。まだ慣れない。",
  "Day 39 - We managed to get a working prototype, though Kevin kept trying to ^gray;feed me^reset; the materials we were working with. Kept having to remind him we needed them for the generator. A pity, they would have fed me for a few centuries at minimum.": "39日目 - 実用的なプロトタイプを完成させたが、ケビンは作業用の素材を^gray;私に食べさせ^reset;ようとし続けた。発電機に必要だと何度も言い聞かせた。残念、少なくとも数世紀分の食糧になったのに。",
  "Day 14 - Another prank...a ^gray;briefcase full of bees^reset;. Kevin didn't seem amused when I returned them, mixed into cartons of orange juice. Claimed I was infringing on a patent. I thought his was sour milk and bees? According to the poorly guarded infraction log it was, anyway.": "14日目 - また悪戯…^gray;蜂でいっぱいのブリーフケース^reset;。オレンジジュースのパックに混ぜて返したらケビンは面白くなさそうだった。特許侵害だと主張。彼のは酸っぱい牛乳と蜂じゃなかった？管理の甘い違反記録によればそうだったが。",
  "Day 1 (Again) - Decided to start over the day counter. Saw new visitors today. Well, one wasn't new. Apparently, I needed to tell my past self that 'Kevin is stuck again'. Turns out, he was stuck partway in the ceiling. Maybe I shouldn't share that new recipe with just anyone.": "1日目（再び）- 日数カウンターをリセットすることにした。今日新しい来訪者を見た。一人は新しくなかった。過去の自分に「ケビンがまた挟まった」と伝える必要があったらしい。天井に途中まで挟まっていた。あの新レシピは誰にでも教えるべきではないのかも。",
  "Day 34 - Bubblegum. Why did it have to be bubblegum? At least he knew better than to drop any on me...but almost everyone else in the Science Outpost is stuck to the ceiling. Squeaker got stuck in an outhouse, though. Either Kevin got annoyed, or someone is reading my journal again.": "34日目 - バブルガム。なぜバブルガムなのか？少なくとも私には落とさなかったが…サイエンスアウトポストのほぼ全員が天井にくっついている。スクイーカーは屋外トイレに挟まった。ケビンが苛ついたか、誰かが日記を読んでいるか。",
  "Little beings supposedly keep journals to record things. Right? Okay. This is mine. I'm Khe, a blue supergiant star pretending to be an insane cat-person. Dear reader: If you share this with anyone without my permission you will find out what it's like to be entombed in a vat of ^gray;molten^reset; metal.": "小さな存在は物事を記録するために日記をつけるらしい。そうだろう？分かった。これは私のだ。私はケー、狂った猫人のフリをしている青色超巨星。読者へ：許可なく誰かに見せたら^gray;溶けた^reset;金属の桶に埋められる気分を味わうことになる。",
  "Day 11 - The one called 'Kevin' amuses me. He studies sciences far beyond what any of these other scientists do, but wastes much of his potential on entertaining himself with foolish pranks. He attempted one such prank on me. A ^gray;box full of wolves^reset; as a 'welcome gift'. They were scrawny and didn't taste good.": "グリーンフィンガーの部族的役割はトライブマスターとは異なるようだが、例外的なフローランは両方を兼ねることもある。グリーンフィンガーは非常に賢く技術的に熟練した呪術師のようで、互いに文通する証拠さえ見たことがある。部族の使者のように機能している。",
  "Day 28 - Several days of work later, we managed to rework the ^gray;precursor stasis system^reset; into a limited form of time travel. Kevin is testing it, but he can't seem to go further than his most recent respawn. He did, however, promise to keep my secret if we could work on something together. Wouldn't say what.": "彼らは吹雪のような条件のため、キャンプの外、我々の視界のはるか先にいた。ドリルの問題を解決しようと外にいた時、ささやき声が始まった。必死にその源を探したが見つからなかった。本当に正気を失いかけていると思ったが、動きに気づいた。",
  "Day 35 - A week after our last project, Kevin brought in papers detailing an idea he'd had; ^gray;cheating spacetime to re-use certain devices continually^reset;. I suggested simple duplication, and he just patted my head and said 'silly kitty, tricks are for kids'.": "35日目 - 前回のプロジェクトの1週間後、ケビンが^gray;時空を騙して特定のデバイスを継続的に再利用する^reset;というアイデアの書類を持ってきた。単純な複製を提案したら、頭を撫でて「おバカな子猫ちゃん、トリックは子供向け」と言った。",
  "Day 17 - Kevin brought me a gift...a surprisingly good one, this time. An entire pallet of gold bars. An hour later one of the humans barged in demanding they be returned. Offered them a piece I'd sculped into a crude poptop penis and said 'Kevin give shiny!' That prompted them to walk out of the room while yelling obscenities.": "17日目 - ケビンが贈り物を持ってきた…今回は驚くほど良いもの。金の延べ棒のパレット丸ごと。1時間後に人間が返せと怒鳴り込んできた。粗雑なポップトップの男性器に彫った一片を差し出して「ケビンがくれたキラキラ！」と言ったら、罵倒しながら部屋を出ていった。",
  "Day 23 - So it would appear Kevin knows what I am. He came in with a small scale solar system, entirely made of densinium, but had replaced the sun at the center with an obsidian sculpture of me. He then bombarded me with questions, asking what I knew of various eldritch or precursor beings and whether I had ever eaten people, among other things. He was...oddly polite, except that last question. Does he think I'll eat someone?": "23日目 - どうやらケビンは私の正体を知っているようだ。デンシニウムで完全に作られた小型太陽系模型を持ってきたが、",
  "Day 24 - Found out why Kevin was so polite when asking questions. I caught him trying to make written copies on sections of human skin. Gave him a choice: get more technical knowledge of certain ^gray;precursor^reset; machines, or publish the recordings and watch as his replication terminal gets swallowed whole. He chose the precursor tech.": "24日目 - ケビンがあんなに丁寧に質問していた理由が分かった。人間の皮膚の部分に手書きのコピーを作ろうとしているのを捕まえた。",
  "Day 41 - Seems Kevin outdid himself. Everyone, himself included, had their gravity reversed. I had to remove the ^gray;precursor gravitic node^reset; he had placed in one of our generators. Didn't enjoy faking a physics field tech, but the others believed the response of 'Want pretty ball!' so I didn't have to explain anything. They just blamed Kevin.": "41日目 - ケビンはやりすぎたようだ。本人を含む全員の重力が反転した。^gray;先駆者の重力ノード^reset;を取り外さなければならなかった",
  "Day 61? Or is it 71? - Decided to try brewing today, since that drunk barkeep seems to love booze. Got distracted and forgot Kevin was coming by. Naturally, he wanted to 'contribute'...and proceeded to dump ^gray;phase matter^reset; and a few other things into my distilled ^gray;soulleaf^reset;. I told him not to drink it, so naturally he did the opposite. Now he's ^gray;walking through people^reset; and shouting 'Boo!'. Hilarious. Calling it Soulleaf Spritz.": "61日目？71日目？- 今日は醸造を試そうと思った。あの酔っぱらいバーテンダーは酒が大好きだから。気を取られてケビンを忘れていた",
  "Day 3 - New person from yesterday arrived again. Kevin sent them for oranges. Decided to follow them. Maybe they'll toss a few snacks in their extraction equipment? Mmm...^gray;ancient gold coins and avolite crystals^reset;, with a bottle of something special, maybe? Kevin left some ^gray;weird seeds^reset; for me to try growing. Definitely weren't ^gray;orange tree^reset; seeds.": "3日目 - 昨日の新人がまた来た。ケビンがオレンジを取りに行かせた。ついて行くことにした。おやつを投げてくれるかも",
  "Day 17 - Along comes Kevin waving about his hands, then \"Suck it in, fat kitty\" he said...and threw a ^gray;neutron bomb^reset; at me. Nice snack. Then he asked me if I wanted to see a magic trick. Couldn't resist...said yes. What was the trick? He fired an ^gray;Atom Smasher^reset; at that annoying Fenerox in the market, ^gray;without seemingly having one^reset;. Gave me the ^gray;blueprint^reset; and said \"For Science!\" Also, he set the noisemaker's respawn delay to a week.": "17日目 - ケビンが手をバタバタさせながらやって来て、「引っ込めろ、デブ子猫」と言い…^gray;中性子爆弾^reset;を投げつけた",
  "Day 27 - He made a copy of ^gray;my gun^reset;...and the damn thing spews ^gray;gregisms^reset; like it's a birthday party. He also claims he mass-produced ^gray;cheap knockoffs^reset; to distract the 'peasants', but ^gray;I worry^reset; that they might end up back here. We don't need another ^gray;Greg infestation^reset;, even if ^gray;he^reset; claims he made failsafes against it.": "27日目 - 彼は^gray;私の銃^reset;のコピーを作った…しかもその銃は誕生日パーティーのように^gray;グレッグ語^reset;を吐き出す。彼はまた",
  "Day 35 - No bubblegum for me, instead he brought the outpost's entire supply of gold, in molten form, and dropped it on me while I was napping under the bridge. Then proceeded to warn everyone of the 'dangerous moat monster' for the rest of the day, while I was enjoying the warmth. I think only he is laughing this time, though.": "35日目 - バブルガムはなし、代わりに前哨地の金の全在庫を溶かした形で持ってきて、橋の下で昼寝している私に落とした。そして一日中「危険な堀の怪物」を皆に警告していた。暖かさを楽しんでいたのに。今回は彼だけが笑っていると思う。",
  "Care and Feeding of Tapeworms": "サナダムシの飼育と餌やり",
  "This is potentially the most disturbing book you've read in some time. It details how best to care and feed a tapeworm you are afflicted by in order to maximize its growth for use in viral and bacteriological studies. It makes a case for utilizing these horrifying parasites for benign...and non-benign...purposes.": "おそらくしばらくの間で最も不穏な本だ。感染したサナダムシの成長を最大化するための最善の飼育法を詳述している。ウイルスおよび細菌学的研究に使用するため。これらの恐ろしい寄生虫を良性…および非良性…の目的に利用する理由を説いている。",
  "The Vakrishaw War Vol371": "ヴァクリショウ戦争 第371巻",
  "An extremely long and drawn out accounting of an ancient war fought by two long-forgotten races. It appears that this entire war was based solely on the misappropriation of four muffins and a pound of baking flour. This somehow takes 11,456 pages to accomplish.": "忘れ去られた2つの種族による古代戦争の極めて長く引き延ばされた記録。この戦争全体がマフィン4つとベーキング粉1ポンドの横領だけに基づいていたようだ。なぜか11,456ページもかかっている。",
  "Pixels - 100000": "ピクセル - 100000",
  "The expiry date for this coupon appears to be the week before your Protectorate graduation ceremony.": "このクーポンの有効期限はプロテクトレート卒業式の前の週のようだ。",
  "This coupon entitles the holder - yes, you! - to a life-changing experience. Come on down to Antonio's Bargain Pizzeria, just a short walk from the Protectorate Academy, and enjoy the fabulous value of 3 grande pizzas for the price of two and a half! Don't wait, drop by today!": "このクーポンの所持者 — そう、あなた！ — に人生を変える体験を提供する。プロテクトレートアカデミーから徒歩すぐのアントニオの格安ピザ屋にお越しあれ。3枚のグランデピザが2枚半の価格！待たずに今日立ち寄ろう！",
  "Bee Genomes": "ミツバチのゲノム",
  "Use the Enhanced Codex Viewer in your Tricorder to view this codex.": "このコーデックスを閲覧するにはトリコーダーの拡張コーデックスビューアーを使用してください",
  "^orange;Genomes^reset;\n\nA string composed of numbers and characters similar to hexidecimal, but going up to Z instead of F (0-35 instead of 0-15 | 0-1295 instead of 0-255 with two characters)\n\nA genome is composed of (number of stats * 2) characters, where every two characters store the value of a stat. Each such pair is called a gene. The way a stat is translated from stat to string varies, but here's the general idea:\n\nValue * 100 -> char (0 = 00, 12.95 = ZZ, 2 = 5J)\n\nHere is an example set of stats and their genome:\n\nBase Production: 3, Drone Toughness: 1, Drone Breed Rate: 1, Queen Breed Rate: 5, Queen Lifespan: 3, Mutation Chance: 1 (out of 100)\n\nFinal Genome: 030101050301HZ\n\n\n\n^orange;Stats^reset;\n\n-Subtype: A bee's strain within its given breed. These typically have different production output or behaviors.\n-Base Production: Resource production at 100% hive efficiency, excluding other modifiers.\n-Drone Toughness: How well do the drones resist anything that tries to kills them: different queen, lack of queen, rivalry fights, etc.\n-Drone Breed Rate: Base drone breeding rate.\n-Queen Breed Rate: Base queen breeding rate.\n-Queen Lifespan: How many bee production ticks before the queen dies (up to 1295).\n-Mutation Chance: Chance for a drastic mutation to occur. Jumps by (math.floor(100/1295*100*n)*0.01) each increment. (As example: '00': 0 | '01': 0.07 | 'HZ': 49.96 | 'ZZ': 100)\n-Work Time: Some bees are diurnal, some are nocturnal, some are both.": "^orange;ゲノム^reset;\n\n数字と16進数に似た文字列だが、FではなくZまで続く（0〜35ではなく0〜1295、0〜255ではなく0〜15）\n\nゲノムは（ステータス数 * 2）文字で構成され、2文字ごとに1つのステータスの値を格納します",
  "Bee Details": "ミツバチの詳細",
  "^orange;Working With Bees^reset;\n\n\nTo newcomers interested in beekeeping as a hobby or career, welcome! This rewarding lifestyle is not one walked lightly. Becoming successful in the trade requires more than just tossing some bees in a box and walking away! You have many things to keep in mind when beekeeping. I'll try to cover the major points here, so you can get to work on what really matters!\n\n\n\n^red;Note^reset;\n\n\nBees will not produce or mate on your ship. Space stations, however, will work fine.\n\n\n\n^orange;Species^reset;\n\n\nEvery species of bee has its own benefits and pitfalls that can help or hinder the beekeeper, with the end result being a highly profitable business if the keeper is savvy and keeps an eye on the well-being of his charges. To make the most out of bees, though, you'll need to be willing to experiment.\n\nMixing and matching species by mating a queen to a different sort of drone can substantially improve the potency of the offspring of that queen. Some bees prefer certain environments, times of day and locations. Others detest other families of bees, which means you might need to take care what you are breeding in your apiaries. Just keep that in mind.\n\n^orange;Bee Needs^reset;\n\n\nThere are several things that are necessary for any bee hive to nest and produce goods. The first and most obvious is an apiary for them to inhabit. Build yourself one of these to start with (I'd recommend a larger size one as soon as you are able!). Once you've set up the apiary, the next (and most important) step is to find some bees. Wander the wilds of the universe and keep an eye out. When you see insects, pull out a trusty bug net and start capturing them. If you get lucky, you'll find yourself a Queen or a Drone! You'll need both a Queen and a Drone to get an apiary running!\n\nNext, you'll need flowers. Bees are pollinators, which means they will seek out and gather pollen from plants before moving onward and spreading that pollen to other plants. More plants (flowers are a common favorite for most bees) means more production for your hives. Some types of flowers and plants are more appealing to certain breeds of bees than to others. This means some trial and error might be required to get the absolute most out of any bee type. Most are not incredibly picky, so any flower or plant will generally do if you don't know their favorites.\n\nOnce you've got the apiary, Queen, Drone and Flowers there is one more key piece of gear required. Frames are quite useful, acting as a platform for bees to live on and build their hive around and on. We, as beekeepers, are able to produce various types of frames through creative application of resources. Great frames can impact your bee quality quite heavily, especially when it comes time to breed them and enhance their genetic capability! Be sure to investigate the many potential types of frames available, and match them up with your hives needs and weaknesses to maximize production!\n\nFinally, the location and time of day can make a huge impact on a hive. Some bees loathe certain environments (or can be outright killed by them!) while they thrive in others. It's your duty as a keeper to learn which environments will result in your apiaries thriving. Some bees are active only during the day (Diurnal), some are active only at night (Nocturnal). A select few are able to operate at any time.\n\nThe final thing to keep in mind is rivals: Some bees will hunt particular subspecies down and kill them in a fierce rivalry. These bees will never thrive when nearby another hive containing their rivals. They'll just kill each other off.\n\n\n\n^orange;Microscopes^reset;\n\n\nChecking in a microscope can identify the subspecies of any bee, allowing you to gain knowledge of the bees stats to help in breeding and selection processes. Each tier of microscope performs slightly better than the previous tier. The greatest available type is the Electron Microscope.\n\n\n\n^orange;Bee Breeding and Production^reset;\n\n\nPlace your Queen in the first slot of the apiary. That's where she goes. The Drone goes in the second slot. Note that in a large apiary, you'll have two slots for drones. This allows you to put in two *different* drones, adding genetic variation towards the queens mate selection process. The other slot on the left side is for your frame (two, if using a large apiary). Once these slots are full, so long as the bees living there have their needs met, they will begin production. When those needs are not met, your bees will be incapable of mating. So, if you have added all that should be required and nothing is happening, it's time to check what might be up.\n\nThe first thing to check is if other bee types produce in the exact same situation. If honey bees work fine and orchid bees do not, then it could either be the time of day, or the biome, or nearby rivals that stop your 'broken' bees from thriving. Once the needs are met, your bees will start producing resources! This will happen gradually, over time, whether or not you are present. If you are off-world, the apiary will 'simulate' the work your bees would have done while away and apply it upon your return. This is both a benefit and a penalty, however, as it also applies the same data to queen age, which can kill a hive if not paying attention. Queens have a limited lifespan, and will die at the end of that time. When a queen dies, the drones have approximately 60 seconds of safety after which point they will begin to slowly die without her there to guide them. This leads to the inevitable collapse of the entire hive. Thus, the importance of breeding becomes clear.\n\n\n\nTo breed bees you will need: A queen, a drone, an apiary and patience. There are some peculiarities to keep in mind when breeding: If a brand new queen and drone are placed in an empty apiary with a frame, the queen will only mate with the FIRST drone added into the apiary. This is a selective breeding process. Once she has mated with the drone, she will then begin to produce her own stock of drones that will become her brood. The old drone(s) will be killed, being of now inferior stock. This new stock of drones will mimic the queens genome identically, producing constantly. Occasionally, a queen will birth a Young Queen. These are your goldmine, as it were. Scan the young queens in a microscope, and keep your best stock for breeding. The rest, sell at the Bee Refuge for easy profit.\n\nEach new generation of bees has a chance to mutate into a superior breed. The chance to mutate is influenced by their species, biome, frames and luck. When a mutation occurs, the benefit is a random bonus to at least one stat. This bonus is usually significant. Through selective breeding, you can guide your bees into a highly mutative form capable of passing on to new generations. With careful planning, that could lead to enormous profits.": "^orange;ミツバチとの生活^reset;\n\n養蜂に興味を持つ新参者の皆さん、ようこそ！この報われる生活は軽々しく歩めるものではありません。この業界で成功するには、単にハチを箱に放り込んで去るだけでは不十分です！念頭に置くべき多くのことがあります",
  "The Benefits of Aquaculture": "養殖の利点",
  "Aquaculture seems to be the wave of the future. By modifying traditional Hylotl agricultural practices, we have been able to increase nutrient paste output by approximately 200%. Needless to say, this has interesting ramifications for Apex society as a whole.": "養殖は未来の潮流のようだ。伝統的なハイロトルの農業慣行を修正することで、栄養ペーストの生産量を約200%増加できた。言うまでもなく、これはエイペックス社会全体にとって興味深い影響がある。",
  "Our only regret is that we have yet to produce a banana variant that will tolerate submersion in brine, but Delta Team appears to be onto some promising results. In the meantime, we suggest increasing allotments of 'I can't believe it's not banana!' banana flavouring to mollify citizens.": "唯一の後悔は塩水への浸漬に耐えるバナナの変種をまだ作れていないことだが、デルタチームが有望な結果を得ているようだ。当面、市民を宥めるため「信じられない！バナナじゃないなんて！」バナナフレーバーの配給量を増やすことを提案する。",
  "Fish, corals and vegetation work together to produce a superb closed ecosystem with minimal waste and outside inputs. Space is saved, even when one considers standard hydroponic setups. We are confident that in two years' time, ration books will be a thing of the past, breaking the greatest hold the resistance has on the populace.": "魚、サンゴ、植生が協力して最小限の廃棄物と外部投入で素晴らしい閉鎖生態系を生み出す。標準的な水耕栽培を考慮してもスペースが節約される。2年以内に配給簿は過去のものとなり、レジスタンスが大衆に持つ最大の支配力を打ち破ると確信している。",
  "20% Cooler": "20%クール",
  "The thought reassignment evaluations proceed apace. I note with satisfaction that the shark tank method was considerably improved by the addition of lasers to the predator's heads.": "思想再割り当て評価は順調に進んでいる。捕食者の頭部にレーザーを追加したことでサメ水槽法がかなり改善されたことを満足をもって記す。",
  "While absolutely useless as more than laser pointers, the waterproof lasers increased the margin of intimidation on most subjects by at least 50%. The sharks themselves might also have become 20% cooler.": "レーザーポインター以上の用途は全くないが、防水レーザーはほとんどの対象への威嚇効果を少なくとも50%向上させた。サメ自体も20%クールになったかもしれない。",
  "The only reason we are not recommending the immediate implementation of such measures in all population centers is the space requirement that comes with constructing the appropriate facilities. Upkeep is surprisingly low.": "全ての人口中心地でのこれらの措置の即時実施を推奨しない唯一の理由は、適切な施設の建設に伴うスペース要件だ。維持費は驚くほど低い。",
  "I Can't Believe It's Not Banana!": "バナナじゃないなんて信じられない！",
  "This marks a sounding success as the subject was a three-time winner of the cooking game show, 'Big Ape's Kitchen'. As of our latest formulation, less than 0.1% of subjects were able to discern the substitute.": "対象者は料理ゲーム番組「ビッグエイプのキッチン」の3度の優勝者だったので、これは大きな成功だ。最新の配合では、代替品を見分けられた対象者は0.1%未満。",
  "Soon, it may be possible to replace up to 70% of bananas consumed by all Apex with 'I can't believe it's not banana!' coralcreep-derived paste, lowering costs and easing rationing procedures.": "近いうちに、全エイペックスが消費するバナナの最大70%を「信じられない！バナナじゃないなんて！」コーラルクリープ由来ペーストで置き換え、コスト削減と配給手続きの緩和が可能になるかもしれない。",
  "In taste test #398, the subject was unable to distinguish between the taste of real banana (for a value of real, anyway) and that of 'I can't believe it's not banana!' banana-flavoured substitute. In fact, when presented with evidence to the contrary, she flatly refused to believe it.": "味覚テスト#398で、被験者は本物のバナナ（まあ「本物」の定義によるが）と「信じられない！バナナじゃないなんて！」バナナ風味代替品の味を区別できなかった。実際、反証を提示されても彼女は断固として信じなかった。",
  "Ishj'ik Tel-tagn": "イシュイク・テルターグン",
  "Passage": "通路",
  "Foul liquids, toxic.\nChained and helpless.\nOne, the lock pick.\nBe patient, and judge each in turn.\nAwait the Old Ones decision.": "邪悪な液体、有毒。\n鎖に繋がれ無力。\n一つ、鍵開け。\n忍耐し、順番に判断せよ。\n古き者の決定を待て。",
  "Varok Hashtur": "ヴァロク・ハシュトゥール",
  "The Dweller In Darkness": "闇に住む者",
  "...for the True Believer will need no eyes,\n  Remove them for He whom Sees,\nPassage is barred for those with sight;\n  In Darkness you must dwell.": "…真の信者に目は不要\n 見る者のために取り除け\n視力ある者に通路は閉ざされる\n 暗闇に住まねばならぬ。",
  "The Testimony of Abd-al Hazrad": "アブドゥル・ハズラドの証言",
  "This is the testimony of all that I have seen, and all that I have learned, in those years that I have possessed the Three Seals of MASSHU. I have seen One Thousand and One moons, and surely this is enough for the span of a mans life, though it is said the Prophets lived much longer. I am weak, and ill, and bear great tired- ness and exhaustion, and a sigh": "これはMASSHUの三つの印を所有していた年月に見た全て、学んだ全ての証言である。",
  "hangs in my breast like a dark lantern, I am old.  The wolves carry their name in their midnight speeches, and that quiet, subtle Voice is summoning me from afar. And a voice much closer will shout into my ear with unholy impatience. The weight of my soul will decide its final resting place. Before the time, I must put down here all that I can concerning the horrors that stalk Without,": "暗いランタンのように胸にぶら下がり、私は老いた。狼は真夜中の演説でその名を運び、あの静かで微妙な",
  "and which lie in wait at the door of every man, for this is the ancient arcana that has been handed down of old, but which has been forgotten by all but a few men, the worshippers of the Ancient Ones (may their names be blotted out!).  And if I do not finish this task, take what is here and discover the rest, for time is short and mankind does not know or understand the evil that awaits it, from every": "全ての人間の扉の前で待ち伏せする古代の秘伝で、古くから伝えられてきたが、",
  "side, from every open Gate, from every broken barrier, from every mindless acolyte at the altars of madness. For this is the Book of the Dead, the Book of the Black Earth, that I have writ down at the peril of my life, exactly as I received it, on the planes of IGIGI, the cruel celestial spirits from beyond the Wanderers of the Wastes.   Let all who read this book be warned thereby that the habitation": "全ての開いた門から、全ての壊れた障壁から、狂気の祭壇に仕える全ての無心の信者から。これは狂気の書であり",
  "of men are seen and surveyed by that Ancient Race of gods and demons from a time before time, and that they seek revenge for that forgotten battle that took place somewhere in the Cosmos and rent the Worlds in the days before the creation of Man, when the Elder Gods walked the Spaces, the race of MARDUK, as he is known to the Chaldeans, and of ENKI our master, the Lord of Magicians.   Know, then, that I have trod": "時の前の時代からの古の神と悪魔の種族によって人間の世界は見られ調べられ、彼らは復讐を求めている",
  "all the Zones of the Gods, and also the places of Azonei, and have descended into the foul places of Death and Eternal Thirst, which may be reached through the Gate of GANZIR, which was built in UR in the days before Babylonian was.   Know, too, that I have spoken with all manner of spirit and daemon, whose names are no longer known in the societies of Man, or were never known. And the seals of these are writ herein ; yet": "神々の全ての領域、またアゾネイの場所も、そして死と永遠の渇きの邪悪な場所にも降りた",
  "others I must take with me when I leave you. ANU have mercy on my soul!   I have seen the Unknown Lands, that no map has ever charted. I have lived in the deserts and the wastelands, and spoken with demons and the souls of slaughtered men, and of women who have died in childbirth, victims of the she-fiend LAMMASHTA. I have traveled beneath the Seas, in search of the Palace of Our Master, and found the stone monuments of": "去る時に持って行かなければならない他の者たち。ANUよ私の魂に慈悲を！未知の地を見た、どの地図にも描かれたことのない",
  "vanquished civilizations, and deciphered the writings of some of these; while still others remain mysteries to any man who lives. And these civilizations were destroyed because of the knowledge contained in this book. I have traveled among the stars, and trembled before the gods. I have at last found the formula by which I passed the gate of ARZIR, and passed into the forbidden realms of the foul IGIGI. I have raised demons, and": "征服された文明の文字を解読した。まだ生きる者には謎のままのものもある。",
  "the dead. I have summoned the ghosts of my ancestors to real and visible appearance on the tops of temples built to reach the stars, and built to touch the nethermost cavities of HADES. I have wrestled with the Black Magician, AZAG-THOTH, in vain, and fled to the Earth by calling upon INANNA and her brother MARDUK, Lord of the double-headed AXE. I have raised armies against the Lands of the East, by summoning the hordes of fiends I have": "死者の。祖先の亡霊を、星に届くよう建てられた寺院の頂上に、現実の目に見える姿で召喚した",
  "made subject unto me, and so doing found NGAA, the god of the heathens, who breathes flame and roars like a thousand thunders. I have found fear. <There are hundreds more pages, and the deeper into the tome you get, the more insane it sounds. Yet there is something about it that unsettles you, especially given where this book was found.>": "私に服従させ、そしてNGAAを見つけた。異教徒の神で、炎を吐き千の雷のように轟く。私は見つけた",
  "Perfect Balance": "完璧なバランス",
  "Some moons will fall,\n  answering the Call.\nBalance their mass;\n  by twos shalt thou pass.": "月が落ちる\n 呼びかけに応えて。\n質量を均衡させよ\n 二つずつ通るべし。",
  "The Narmic Equation": "ナルミック方程式",
  "weapon to use there, also indecipherable by your current understanding of physics.>": "そこで使う武器も、あなたの現在の物理学の理解では解読不能。>",
  "Let it be known that there is no space for us after our end. All that we are, all that we could ever be, belongs to THEM. Prowling about in the spaces between, indifferent to all our petty squabbles. Their nature is the very essence of chaos. They will return one day, and devour the cosmos. Watch the places where all light fades. Watch them well.": "我々の終わりの後に空間はないことを知れ。我々の全て、我々がなりえた全ては彼らのものだ。暗闇を徘徊し、",
  "<There are dozens of pages in this volume, all strange math and bizarre calculations using a numbering scheme completely alien to you. They at first seem like incoherent blabbering until the formula starts to resolve itself almost before your eyes. It appears to give a location in coordinates that match no known sector of space and a blueprint for a": "<この巻には数十ページあり、全てあなたには完全に異質な数え方を使った奇妙な数学と奇妙な計算だ。彼らは",
  "Invocation of Hashtur": "ハシュトゥールの祈祷",
  "First, you must carve the flesh from the bones of the sacrifice; be careful, for any tearing of the skin will result in severe repercussions.": "まず、生贄の骨から肉を切り出さなければならない。皮膚を破ると深刻な反動があるので注意せよ。",
  "Now, you must stitch the flesh into your own, starting at the toes and working up. Only once the full suit is complete may you begin the Black Chant.": "次に、つま先から上に向かって肉を自分の体に縫い付けなければならない。完全なスーツが完成して初めて黒の詠唱を始めることができる。",
  "Next, place the artifact in the center and begin the chant and the dance. His power guides you, should you be true to the call. Should the sacrifice struggle, end that struggle for the time has come. You shall be cleansed.": "次に、アーティファクトを中央に置き、詠唱と舞いを始めよ。召命に忠実ならば彼の力が導く。生贄が抵抗するなら、その時が来たのだから抵抗を終わらせよ。汝は浄化される。",
  "Portals": "ポータル",
  "<diagrams of unknown creatures, star-charts and math in ancient dialects appears to describe a way between universes from one particular location.>": "<未知の生物の図表、星図、古代方言の数学が、特定の場所から宇宙間を移動する方法を記述しているようだ。>",
  "Xallosh Feer": "ザロシュ・フィーア",
  "To invoke the hive-mind representing chaos.\n    Invoking the feeling of chaos.\n    With out order.\n    The Nezperdian hive-mind of chaos. Zalgo.\n    He who Waits Behind The Wall.": "混沌を司る集合精神を喚起せよ\n 混沌の感覚を呼び起こせ\n 秩序なき世界\n ネズパーディアンの混沌の集合精神 ザルゴ\n 壁の向こうで待つ者",
  "Liber Ivonis": "リベル・イヴォニス",
  "<over 200 pages of ranting like this...none of which makes any sense to you.>": "<このような暴言が200ページ以上…あなたには何一つ理解できない。>",
  "...and therein find the migration patterns of Callishk-Nyarrath and bring upon them the doom that they wrought on others. And so it was that They were cast out into the black beyond cursed forever to wander the spaces between until an arbiter of sufficient strength is capable of casting off the locks that hold the shifting spaces that form the mass of Them.": "…そしてカリシュク＝ニャラスの移動パターンを見つけ、彼らが他者にもたらした破滅を彼らに降り注がせよ。そしてそれは",
  "Proper Cult Wear - Torso": "正式な教団服 - 胴体",
  "No self-respecting cultist is without his robe. To make your upper garment, you must place seven Nocxium Bars, a Rune Wand and an Elder Fragment upon the altar and recite the incantation of Horvalaatsh.": "自尊心のあるカルト教徒なら法衣は必須。上衣を作るには祭壇にノクシウムバー7つ、ルーンワンド1つ、エルダーフラグメント1つを置き、ホルヴァラートシュの呪文を唱えよ。",
  "Proper Cult Wear - Hood": "正式な教団服 - フード",
  "...and that is why your robe is never to be used in lieu of toilet paper. You'd not want that, right? As for your hood, which you of course already made using six Nocxium, a Valtan Casing and an Elder Core...well, just be sure you don't go using that, either...": "…だから法衣をトイレットペーパーの代わりに使ってはならないのだ。そんなことは望まないだろう？フード — もちろんノクシウム6つ、ヴァルタンケーシングとエルダーコアで既に作っているだろうが…それも使うなよ…",
  "Proper Cult Wear - Legs": "正式な教団服 - 脚部",
  "...and that, my friend, is why the Hounds of Tindalos are not to be treated like a puppy. Anyhow, I rambled off again. Get yourself your five Nocxium Bars, and Unknown Reactor and a Trapezohedron and you'll have the finest lower-robe a cultist could hope for!": "…友よ、だからティンダロスの猟犬を子犬のように扱ってはいけないのだ。とにかくまた脱線した。ノクシウムバー5つ、未知のリアクターとトラペゾヘドロンを手に入れれば、カルト教徒が望みうる最高の下衣が手に入る！",
  "Horrid Armor": "恐ろしい鎧",
  "To wear the armor of His flesh, you must pray at the Altar. Place various amounts of Nocxium within, with the fragments of Celaeno and a sacrament of his choosing. Only the correct combination will yield results, should you guess his desires correctly.": "彼の肉の鎧を着るには祭壇で祈らなければならない。ノクシウムを様々な量、セラエノのフラグメントと彼が選ぶ聖体を入れよ。正しい組み合わせだけが結果をもたらす、彼の望みを正確に推測できればの話だが。",
  "Fellhammer": "フェルハンマー",
  "With a hacking chop, you will sever the limbs of His foes for the glory of all. The flesh sacrament can then be imbibed, and the true path to fighteousness revealed. Upon the altar, place five Noxcium, one Valtan Casing and four Blade Shards.": "激しい斬撃で彼の敵の四肢を切断し、全ての栄光のために。肉の聖体を飲み、正義への真の道が明かされる。祭壇にノクシウム5つ、ヴァルタンケーシング1つ、ブレードシャード4つを置け。",
  "Blade of the Vile": "卑劣なる者の刃",
  "Should you wish to vanquish the enemies of the true faith by blade, you need pay homage at His altar. Place a Tome, a Celaeno Fragment and five Blade Shards upon it and pray for his wrath.": "真の信仰の敵を刃で打ち倒したければ、彼の祭壇に敬意を表さねばならない。書物、セラエノフラグメント、ブレードシャード5つを置き、彼の怒りを祈れ。",
  "Chaugnar Faugn": "チャウグナー・ファウグン",
  "If the hunted truly wishes to becomes the hunter he must place these three objects upon an alter an offer a prayer for destruction of his enemies. An Elder Artifact, an Elder Tome and five Blade Shards. Be sure to utter the prayer correctly or it will be you who shall be destroyed.": "狩られる者が真に狩る者になることを望むなら、この3つの物を祭壇に置き敵の破滅を祈らなければならない。エルダーアーティファクト、エルダートーム、ブレードシャード5つ。祈りを正確に唱えよ、さもなくば破滅するのは汝だ。",
  "Cleaver of Souls": "魂の鉈",
  "None shall resist your blade. Six blade shards, two ancient glyphs and a rune wand upon the altar should bind the cosmos to the blade. Your rage shall sew chaos through the galaxy.": "何者もお前の刃に抗えない。ブレードシャード6つ、古代グリフ2つ、ルーンワンド1つを祭壇に置けば宇宙を刃に縛り付けられる。お前の怒りが銀河に混沌を縫い付けるだろう。",
  "Ulkak B'jikal": "ウルカク・ビジカル",
  "I probably shouldn't have done that...but I couldn't resist. The Altar showed me how to do it, finally! I just needed the right combination, and through trial and error I've got it.": "やるべきではなかったかもしれない…しかし抵抗できなかった。ついに祭壇がやり方を示してくれた！正しい組み合わせが必要で、試行錯誤の末に見つけた。",
  "I just need to set an Elder Artifact...not easy to find, I'll tell you that much! Then an Ancient Glyph and finally an Elder Core. Then I pray to the dark thing that shrine is dedicated to, and presto!": "エルダーアーティファクトを設置するだけ…見つけるのが難しいのは言うまでもない！次に古代のグリフ、最後にエルダーコア。そして祠が捧げられた闇の存在に祈れば、出来上がり！",
  "Tried the ritual. I think I said something wrong. I'm rotting, slowly but surely. My toe fell off this morning. So my other digits won't be far behind. If you try this, say the damned words right!": "儀式を試した。何か間違えたようだ。ゆっくりだが確実に腐っている。今朝つま先が落ちた。他の指も遠くないだろう。試すなら呪文を正確に言え！",
  "Ik'vathk Vesh": "イクヴァスク・ヴェシュ",
  "...and by properly combining these artifacts, you'll be able to grapple with amazing ease and throw yourself long distances: An Elder Artifact, an Unknown Reactor and an Elder Fragment. Be sure to utter the prayer correctly. The gutteral language is difficult but accuracy is survival, in this case.": "…そしてこれらのアーティファクトを正しく組み合わせれば、驚くほどの容易さでグラップリングし長距離を飛べるようになる：エルダーアーティファクト、未知のリアクター、エルダーフラグメント。祈りを正確に唱えよ。喉声の言語は難しいが正確さが生存を意味する。",
  "Detonatus Mondus": "デトナトゥス・モンドゥス",
  "A picture of some sort of grenade-launcher weapon. There are diagrams for several Elder Cores, along with several pieces of Unknown Technology. Cresting these is a singular Elder Artifact.": "何らかのグレネードランチャー兵器の絵。複数のエルダーコアの図表と、複数の未知のテクノロジーの断片がある。それらの頂点にエルダーアーティファクトが1つ。",
  "Vall Bokar": "ヴァル・ボカール",
  "None before the might of Asatoth! None before his touch! Place the sacrament at an altar: an Elder Artifact, two Blade Shards and a Trapezohedron.": "アサトースの力の前に何者も抗えない！その手に触れられれば！祭壇に聖体を置け：エルダーアーティファクト、ブレードシャード2つ、トラペゾヘドロン。",
  "Strange Schematic": "奇妙な設計図",
  "The sidearm pictured seems to be crafted from 3 different core materials: An Elder Artifact, one Elder Fragment and an Elder Core.": "描かれたサイドアームは3つの異なるコア素材から作られているようだ：エルダーアーティファクト1つ、エルダーフラグメント1つ、エルダーコア1つ。",
  "Pulse of Maggots": "ウジの脈動",
  "Terror comes from the dark one in many forms. This deadly weapon is one of the things you ought to fear. Pray to Him and place upon the altar the following: Elder Artifact x 1 , Valtan Casing x 1, Unknown Reactor x1": "暗き者からの恐怖は多くの形で訪れる。この致命的な武器は恐るべきものの一つ。彼に祈り、祭壇に以下を置け：エルダーアーティファクト×1、ヴァルタンケーシング×1、未知のリアクター×1",
  "Kikiktik Xitxa": "キキクティク・シトシャ",
  "One Elder Artifact, one Rune Wand and one Elder Core can be combined into a strange sort of bio-energy weapon with terrifying interdimensional capabilities.": "エルダーアーティファクト1つ、ルーンワンド1つ、エルダーコア1つを組み合わせると、恐ろしい次元間能力を持つ奇妙な生体エネルギー兵器になる。",
  "Vektai Molla": "ヴェクタイ・モラ",
  "While hard to decipher, there are schematics within this book that detail a shield, of sorts, composed of various unusual materials. It states that one should place five Noxcium bars, an Elder Tome and five Elder Fragments within some sort of altar...": "解読は難しいが、この本には一種の盾の設計図がある。様々な珍しい素材で構成されている。ノクシウムバー5つ、エルダートーム1つ、エルダーフラグメント5つを何らかの祭壇に置くべきだと書いてある…",
  "Recombinant Weapon": "リコンビナント兵器",
  "...the catalyst is that very material. After it is applied, you'll be able to simply annihilate the very DNA of your opponents. As a result, the battlefield will be riddled with the horrified screams of melting enemies. To grace them with such perfection you'll need a Unknown Reactor, an Engraved Device and five Elder Fragments.": "…触媒はまさにその素材だ。適用すると、対戦相手のDNAそのものを消滅させることができる。結果、戦場は溶ける敵の恐怖の叫びで満たされる。このような完璧さを彼らに授けるには、未知のリアクター、刻印されたデバイス、エルダーフラグメント5つが必要だ。",
  "Hale's Creation": "ヘイルの創造物",
  "Should you wish to vanquish the enemies of the true faith by spear, you need pay homage at His altar. Place a Tome, a Rune Wand and three Blade Shards upon it and pray for his wrath.": "真の信仰の敵を槍で打ち倒したければ、彼の祭壇に敬意を表さねばならない。書物、ルーンワンド、ブレードシャード3つを置き、彼の怒りを祈れ。",
  "Grimoire of Nalshakk": "ナルシャクの魔導書",
  "[page 854] - And then it was that I at long last assembled it from the Elder Tome, two Rune Wands and an Elder Artifact. My enemies shook in terror, for the staff I held was capable of might untold! I was invincible! And hungry. Popcorn? Yes. That seemed a reasonable...": "テルシアンのいくつかの品種が知られている。最も一般的で今や銀河中で見られるのはワーカー。彼らは探索し、データを収集・照合してハイブクイーンに報告する。ウォリアーが次に多く、傭兵団や裕福なクライアントに雇われている。",
  "Quellex Text": "クエレックスの文書",
  "Never be without your implements, young apprentice. The staff is your most favored good, and without it you are but meat to the Elder ones. You must fashion it from an Elder Tome, two Valtan Casings and an Elder Bust...": "道具を手放すな、若き弟子よ。杖は最も大切な品であり、それなしではエルダーの者たちにとって肉でしかない。エルダートーム、ヴァルタンケーシング2つ、エルダーバストから作るのだ…",
  "Care and Feeding of Byakhee": "ビヤーキーの飼育と餌やり",
  "[over top of a strange text detailing the care and feeding of one creature called Byakhee, red text...perhaps in blood...details the schematic for a weapon] ELDER TOME....TWO ELDER FRAGMENTS....TRAPEZOHEDRON.......SACRIFICE..": "[ビヤーキーと呼ばれる生物の飼育方法を記した奇妙なテキストの上に、赤い文字…おそらく血で…武器の設計図が] エルダートーム…エルダーフラグメント2つ…トラペゾヘドロン…生贄…",
  "Frek'Snarr Volshtk": "フレクスナー・ヴォルシュトク",
  "Should you wish to vanquish the enemies of the true faith by whip, you need pay homage at His altar. Place 5 Nocxium Bars, a Rune Wand and a Celaeno Fragment upon it and pray for his rage.": "真の信仰の敵を鞭で打ち倒したければ、彼の祭壇に敬意を表さねばならない。ノクシウムバー5つ、ルーンワンド、セラエノフラグメントを置き、彼の怒りを祈れ。",
  "Research - Metaphysics": "研究 - メタフィジクス",
  "You've received this issue of Metaphysics Monthly! Congratulations! To make the absolute most out of this exciting area of scientific research you'll need to do a few things.": "メタフィジクス・マンスリー最新号をお届けします！おめでとうございます！この刺激的な科学研究分野を最大限に活用するため、いくつかのことを行う必要があります",
  "First, search through all your pockets and miscellaneous body cavities until you find your ^orange;Tricorder^reset;! Once you've done that, turn it on and select the ^green;Beaker icon^reset; to open the ^orange;Research interface^reset;. Easy, right?": "まず、ポケットや体のあらゆる隙間を探って^orange;トリコーダー^reset;を見つけてください！見つけたら電源を入れ、^green;ビーカーのアイコン^reset;を選択して^orange;研究インターフェース^reset;を開きましょう。簡単でしょう？",
  "Finally, select ^orange;Metaphysics^reset;. From there, you need only select a topic, and you will be able to begin research into that topic if you have the required goods to accomplish the task at hand!": "最後に、^orange;メタフィジクス^reset;を選択してください。そこからトピックを選ぶだけで、必要な資材さえあれば、そのトピックの研究を開始できます！",
  "Note that you'll need to have learned to scan before you can start delving into Metaphysics. Chat to Grand Protector Esther at the Ark to learn how.": "メタフィジクスの探求を始める前に、スキャンの方法を習得している必要があります。アークにいるエスター大守護者に話しかけて学んでください",
  "You've received this issue of Metaphysics Monthly! Congratulations!\n\nTo make the absolute most out of this exciting area of scientific research you'll need to do a few things.\n\nFirst, search through all your pockets and miscellaneous body cavities until you find your ^orange;Tricorder^reset;! Once you've done that, turn it on and select the ^green;Beaker icon^reset; to open the ^orange;Research interface^reset;. Easy, right?\n\nFinally, select ^orange;Metaphysics^reset;. From there, you need only select a topic, and you will be able to begin research into that topic if you have the required goods to accomplish the task at hand!\n\nNote that you'll need to have learned to scan before you can start delving into Metaphysics. Chat to Grand Protector Esther at the Ark to learn how.": "形而上学マンスリーのこの号を受け取りました！おめでとうございます！\n\nこのエキサイティングな科学研究分野を最大限に活用するために、いくつかのことが必要です。\n\nまず、すべてのポケットと体のくぼみを探して^orange;トリコーダー^reset;を見つけてください！それが終わったら",
  "The Energy of Life": "生命のエネルギー",
  "Thus each material thing being made up of a combination of atoms, called molecules, has its own unique frequency, unlike any other. Now because each individual thing is unique, no potato for instance is exactly like any other potato.": "このように原子の組み合わせ（分子と呼ばれる）で構成される各物質は、他に類のない固有の周波数を持つ。各個体はユニークなので、例えばジャガイモは他のジャガイモと全く同じではない。",
  "There exists an 'empathy' between the whole potato and each of its individual parts. If you slice that potato in half, the frequency of each half is exactly the same. The only example of that frequency anywhere in the universe.": "ジャガイモ全体とその個々の部分の間には「共感」が存在する。ジャガイモを半分に切ると、各半分の周波数は全く同じだ。宇宙のどこにもその周波数の唯一の例である。",
  "All matter in the universe is composed of small packets of energy known as quantas. This energy, which goes into the making up of atoms pulsates or resonates at a particular frequency. Each atom being different therefore, has a slightly different pulsation or frequency.": "[854ページ] - そしてついにエルダートーム、ルーンワンド2本、エルダーアーティファクトから組み立てた。敵は恐怖で震えた、私が持つ杖は計り知れない力を秘めていたからだ！無敵だった！そして空腹だった。ポップコーン？うん。それは妥当な…",
  "The Substance": "物質",
  "Imagine falling down a rabbit hole and entering an entirely new world full of color and sound and feeling that makes all of your previous experience feel wrong...inferior. Dead. That's a rough approximation of it, really...it's far more powerful than even that.": "ウサギの穴に落ちて、色と音と感覚に満ちた全く新しい世界に入ることを想像してほしい。以前の全ての経験が間違いに…劣っていたように…死んでいたように感じる。それはおおよその近似であり、実際にはそれよりはるかに強力だ。",
  "composed of elements that remain impossible to identify. From whence did it come? If you opt to ingest this strange liquid...take care. All of this sounds fascinating, I am sure...but once the effects wear off you will forever cease to be who you were before. And you might even start to hear the Call....": "特定不可能な元素で構成されている。どこから来たのか？この奇妙な液体を摂取する場合…注意せよ。魅力的に聞こえるだろうが…効果が切れた後、以前の自分であることを永遠に止めるだろう。そして呼びかけが聞こえ始めるかもしれない…",
  "...and once the dose is sufficient, you'll feel your mind truly open up. It's as if you sort of...boy, is this hard to describe...like you enter another dimension. You see fractals, a tunnel of sorts. It swirls in your vision, warping all you see. And then, as you travel through this tunnel...you'll eventually reach the end and break through! And then....wow.": "…そして投与量が十分になると、心が本当に開くのを感じるだろう。まるで…これを説明するのは本当に難しいが…まるで",
  "Breaking through is like rebirth. Like someone lifted the veil of reality, and showed you the real world underneath. Everything changes. And I do mean -everything-. You become hyper-aware, and things that were never there before become obvious to you (things you still see even after the effects wear off!) and at long last you know the truth.": "突破するのは再生のようだ。誰かが現実のヴェールを持ち上げ、その下にある本当の世界を見せてくれたかのように。全てが変わる。そして",
  "That our reality, the one we know and take for granted...is a lie. Sound is more real, things are more beautiful (or terrifying) and every sensation is taken to new extremes. In this place...this new space...dimension, whatever...there are beings communicating with you. They seem benevolent, and as if they have something important to tell you.": "我々の現実、当たり前に受け止めているもの…が嘘だということ。音はより本物で、物事はより美しく（あるいは恐ろしく）、全ての感覚が",
  "The speech is impossible to understand, but there seems to be nothing harmful about them (for the most part anyhow. I've heard tales that things can be much darker for those with less stable psyches). For most, its as if you are meeting celestial beings, servants to the Almighty. But no matter what you do, you'll not be able to understand them.": "言語は理解不能だが、彼らには害があるようには見えない（ほとんどの場合は。彼らが時々",
  "They are just showing you what life can truly be, if you only look. Make no mistake, however...it is most certainly not God. It is something else entirely. Something stranger and ever more bizarre. The greenish-turqoise fluid flows through you, changing you from the inside. Forever. Tests made after the effects wear off show alteration at the genetic": "彼らはただ、見さえすれば人生が本当にどうなれるかを見せているだけだ。しかし間違えるな…それは確実に神ではない。何か別のもので",
  "level for most species. The substance itself is synthetic, engineered by living hands, but its origin remains unknown. It simply seems to occur in places around the cosmos without rhyme or reason (and I have heard tales that mixing particular liquids in the right way can even create it...somehow). Three-quarters of its contents remain unknown to science,": "ほとんどの種族にとってのレベル。物質自体は合成で、生きた手で設計されたが、その起源は不明のまま。単に発生するように見える",
  "Pellucid Shaping": "透明なる成形",
  "<Written in Eld'uukharic script, this draconic guide informs the user on the best method of growing various crystals to what it describes as 'most holy perfection'.": "<エルドゥーカー文字で書かれたこの竜族のガイドは、「最も聖なる完璧さ」と称する状態まで様々なクリスタルを育てる最善の方法をユーザーに伝えている。",
  "Elduukhar Life": "エルドゥーカーの生活",
  "Eld'uukhar choose a mate for life, and when a life mate is chosen, the couple must ask to be blessed in a temple by a priest representing Sahkris, and a priestess representing Ahvis. In order to gain this blessing, each consume one half of a Rasiline crystal - which has similar chemical properties to Exonite - and if they can endure the hallucinations that follow, they can continue with the ceremony.": "エルドゥーカーは生涯の伴侶を選び、選んだ時にカップルは神殿で祭司に祝福を求めなければならない",
  "Wanderer's Lament": "放浪者の嘆き",
  "A novel of sorts, etched in crystalline ink on amazingly honed pages, also formed from crystals. It details the travels and trials of one Yettikash Justiri'var, hero of the Garix Clan. It seems he was a figure of historical significance in Eld'uukharic history.": "クリスタルインクで驚くほど研ぎ澄まされたページ（これもクリスタル製）に刻まれた一種の小説。ガリクス族の英雄イェティカシュ・ジュスティリヴァルの旅と試練を詳述している。エルドゥーカーの歴史において重要な人物だったようだ。",
  "Ahvis Scripture": "アーヴィス聖典",
  "Apparently a holy text, this codex details a creature referred to as Ahvis and her divine guidance over the Eld'uukhar people. Most specifically, it details her literal link to all crystalline formations in the universe. The importance of the Male and Female Purpose are spoken of in great detail, likely pointing to a gender-based role-heavy society in the historical context. The effects of various crystals on the genders is explored in excruciatingly boring detail.": "明らかに聖典であるこのコーデックスはアーヴィスと呼ばれる存在とエルドゥーカーの民への神聖な導きを詳述している。ほとんどの",
  "Allegedly, red crystals when imbibed by a male Eld'uukhar, result in a `sexual deviant that will mate with more than one dragon`, while a green crystal ingested by a female will cause the same effect. A blue crystal by either is said to bring euphoria, but only if it is sky blue. Cyan will lead to psychosis...apparently. This is likely not fact, and more than likely heavily influenced by dogmatic principles.": "伝説では、赤いクリスタルをエルドゥーカーの雄が摂取すると「複数のドラゴンと交尾する性的逸脱者」となるらしい",
  "Prophet of Ahvis": "アーヴィスの預言者",
  "We as children of Ahvis must take revenge. Abandon those whom you hold most dear, for they will always have a knife ready at your back. Trust only in Ahvis, and trust only in me, her prophet, for I will protect you, I will guide you, and I will always be with you.": "アーヴィスの子供である我々は復讐しなければならない。最も大切な者を捨てよ、彼らは常に背後にナイフを用意しているからだ。アーヴィスだけを信じ、彼女の預言者である私だけを信じよ。私が守り、導き、常に共にいる。",
  "As the prophet of Ahvis, I can attest to the vile nature of her supposed husband, Sahkris. She has spoken to me through my dreams. He and his children alike are betrayers, and care for none but themselves. The spirit of Sahkris lies dormant in his children, your husbands, your brothers, and your sons.": "アーヴィスの預言者として、彼女の夫とされるサフクリスの邪悪な本性を証言できる。夢を通じて彼女は私に語りかけた。彼と彼の子供たちは裏切り者であり、自分たち以外誰のことも気にしない。サフクリスの魂はあなたの夫、兄弟、息子の中に眠っている。",
  "The Wonders of Crystal": "クリスタルの驚異",
  "I came to what could only be described as a slum. Male Eld'uukhar dressed in rags were huddled by clusters of Thanatite crystal to keep warm, horribly thin from a lack of food. Haunted, I left that place quickly, and the planet soon after. I doubt I'll be making another trip.": "スラムとしか言いようのない場所に来た。ぼろを纏ったエルドゥーカーの男たちがサナタイトクリスタルの群れのそばに身を寄せ合って暖を取り、食糧不足で恐ろしく痩せていた。心に深く刻まれ、すぐにその場所と惑星を去った。再び訪れることはないだろう。",
  "I took a trip recently to the Eld'uukhar inhabited planet in the system Magna Ilo to trade for a few crystals. The cities of this planet were just as opulent as I had heard, buildings crafted from crystal and gold, towering spires that touched the sky. Their temples were a sight to behold. I did not venture inside out of respect for the worshippers": "最近マグナ・イロ星系のエルドゥーカーが居住する惑星にクリスタルを数個取引しに行った。この惑星の都市は",
  "but I'd imagine the inside to be just as beautiful. Despite the wonders I have seen there, I have left that planet with a feeling of unease. I had taken a wrong turn and found myself in a sector that seemed to be abandoned. The temples that I had seen were here also, but as piles of dirty rubble, and banners embroidered with a symbol I had not seen before were laid torn and ruined on the ground.": "しかし内部も同じくらい美しいと想像する。そこで見た驚異にもかかわらず、あの惑星を去った時には",
  "77245 - Worried": "77245 - 心配",
  "Contact with the other pockets of resistance has proven to be difficult. We're always unsure if we are being followed. On many planets we have found standalone temples with Ahvis' worshippers infesting them, ready for us. Where do they even come from to get to our destinations this fast? I fear we may spend the rest of our lives on this ship.": "他のレジスタンスの拠点との連絡は困難を極めた。追跡されているかどうか常に不確かだ。多くの惑星で我々は",
  "The Eld'uukhar have two governing bodies, the temple council, and the people's council. The people's council answers to the temple council. The people's council is elected, whereas the temple council is decided based on the will of four priests, two male, two female, who consume Exonite crystals to elicit communication between the deities and themselves, and through this decide who will be appointed (As an aside, the consumption of Exonite is forbidden to all but these four, who are replaced by their children when they eventually die).": "エルドゥーカーには2つの統治機関がある。寺院評議会と民衆評議会だ。民衆評議会は寺院評議会に報告する",
  "The head of the council is chosen once every ten years through this method, a male one decade, and a female the next. It is considered their divine right to rule, and their word sways the entire races' social/economic development for the next ten years. In more recent times, this has been abused, and the current head of the temple council - Ka'tir Upitah - intends to keep her rule until she eventually dies, claiming to be a direct messenger from the deity Ahvis.": "評議会の長はこの方法で10年ごとに選ばれる。1つの10年は男性、次は女性。これは最も",
  "As a race, the Eld'uukhar have developed from bloodthirsty nomadic tribes into a peaceful people, although the recent persecution of males of the species under Ka'tir's rule has brought about the uprising of little pockets of resistance on Eld'uukhar inhabited planets, and the state has retaliated by increasing military presence in all major cities.": "種族としてエルドゥーカーは血に飢えた遊牧部族から平和な民族へと発展したが、最近の男性への迫害は",
  "Uplifting: Phase 1": "アップリフティング: フェーズ1",
  "The discovery of this new vein of what appears to be natural tritanium on the third planet of the Rigel Minoris system gives us the perfect chance to attempt an Uplifting. For those among the Kirhosi elite that are not aware, an Uplifting is when we elect to take a minor species and speed up their introduction to the galactic community. We offer them goods and technology in exchange for their resources, and both benefit. As an added bonus, later down the line, we have a valuable new trade partner that may speak on our behalf in the Protectorate Assembly.": "リゲル・ミノリス星系の第3惑星で天然トリタニウムと思われる新しい鉱脈の発見は、我々に",
  "How this particular group of Fenerox came to be here is unknown, but they show a capacity above and beyond their kin found on other worlds for technology and language. This has given them a head-start already, and we estimate they will have reached the stars on their own within 200 years anyhow. We will send a ship to help them along in 8 solar cycles. This should give our traders time to prepare sufficient resources to offer them. Hopefully they will be willing to trade their valuable Tritanium, as it will prove exceptionally valuable in fashioning a new line of FTL drives for Ark Fleet Cassini.": "このフェネロックスのグループがどうやってここに来たかは不明だが、他の場所で見つかる同族を遥かに超える能力を示している",
  "Human. What?": "人間。は？",
  "Also, human seem to not care what place is living in. Always adapts. Puts on many layers, walks into danger without think. Somehow survive and be stronger. Respect. But also fear.": "また、人間はどんな場所に住むかを気にしないようだ。常に適応する。何枚も重ね着して、考えなしに危険に向かう。なぜか生き延びて強くなる。尊敬する。でも恐れもする。",
  "First we are not believing more than one ape is having enough think to make ships for space. And then we is meeting Human. Human is...different. Not Apex scary murder. More...sneaky? Not trust, because using teeth to make many gestures. Also, too much chest and leg muscles. Not normal.": "最初は1匹以上の猿が宇宙船を作れるほどの知性を持つとは信じなかった。そして人間に会った。人間は…違う。エイペックスの怖い殺しではない。もっと…ずる賢い？歯を使って多くの表情を作るから信用しない。胸と脚の筋肉も多すぎる。普通ではない。",
  "Humans still quite interesting, despite muscles and teeth-display for happy. Humans generally treat nice. One said we as people is 'cute'. Unsure what this means, but assume is respect sign. He then pet me under chin. I like pets under chin. But why is human attempt mating ritual with me? Is wanting baby-make with foreign species? Is human do this? Why?": "筋肉と幸せを示す歯の見せ方にもかかわらず、人間はまだかなり興味深い。人間は一般的に優しく扱ってくれる。一人が我々を「かわいい」と言った。",
  "Terror-bugs. NO NO NO.": "恐怖虫。やだやだやだ",
  "If we have say, we ask Protectorate to Illegal the terror-bug-men. Illegal them! Send to place without normal creatures. At home, insect bite is kill. In space, EVERY BUG MAN IS PROBABLY BITE KILL. NO. NO NO NO. NO. Make illegal.": "発言権があるなら、プロテクトレートに恐怖虫人間を違法にするよう頼む。違法にしろ！普通の生き物がいない場所に送れ。母星では虫の噛みつきは即死。宇宙では全ての虫人間がたぶん噛みつき即死。ダメ。ダメダメダメ。ダメ。違法にしろ。",
  "Okay. Kirhos make first real mistake for Fenerox friends. Introduce to horrifying monster peoples. THERE IS INSECTS WITH THINK, AND THEY HAVE SHIPS FOR PLANET JUMP. THIS NOT GOOD. NO. NO NO NO. Not like at all, and want squash terror-things until terror-things is gone. Kirhos say not worry, as Insect-men stupid alone and need group. BUT THEN THEY HAVE GROUP AND ARE HARDER TO SQUASH. WHY YOU LET THEM GROUP?": "よし。キルホスはフェネロックスの友人のために初めて本当の間違いをした。恐ろしい怪物民族を紹介した。考える昆虫がいるとは、そして",
  "How is glow thinking?": "光るのがどう考える？",
  "But we has care to take, because people in new space empire seem not to like when you catch and play with other living things. Also, especially not like when using claws and teeth to play. But even so, come meet. Light-people make life more interesting.": "でも気をつけないと、新しい宇宙帝国の人々は他の生き物を捕まえて遊ぶのを好まないようだ。特に爪と歯を使って遊ぶのは。それでも会いに来て。光の民が人生をもっと面白くする。",
  "Callix, you not believe me when I write you in new language over ansible! There are thinking light-people! For real! Not like legends, but actual light-people. They always talking in strange accents, and is making dark places not dark. Perhaps is magick? Nice enough, but not try to touch or lick. Warm. Also not like licks, apparently. You come meet me in Protectorate worlds, and I show you light-men. Together we attempt to catch one and make friend!": "カリックス、新しい言語でアンシブルで書いても信じないだろう！考える光の民がいるんだ！本物だ！伝説のようではなく",
  "Puke people?": "ゲロ人間？",
  "Met today for first time, puke-person. Yes, reading that right. Slimey, blobby puke that has talking parts and is thinking. Sense? None. But still happens. Kirhos not told us there was talking vomit. First time us is meeting new races that not wonder about flavor. No one eat vomit. Is not food.": "今日初めて嘔吐人間に会った。うん、その通り読んでいる。話す部分があって考えるヌルヌルのブヨブヨの嘔吐物。意味？なし。でも起きている。キルホスは話す嘔吐物がいることを教えてくれなかった。初めて味が気にならない新しい種族に会う。嘔吐物は食べない。食べ物ではない。",
  "Scary dark men.": "怖い暗い人間",
  "Terror. Fear. That is what dark-men are. No touch, no talk, not be around. Avoid dark-men. Is Gallupal of legend, for sure maybe. Gallupal is eating the sun and making the night, and night is good for hunt and baby-making. But remember Gallupal is always watch, always judge, and guarding of the death-world. You will not enter the death-world if you is bother dark-men. Respect only.": "恐怖。恐れ。暗黒の男たちはそういうもの。触るな、話すな、近くにいるな。暗黒の男たちを避けよ。伝説のガルパルに違いない、たぶんきっと。",
  "Smart. Is worship dark.": "賢い。闇を崇拝してる",
  "Nightar not understand how Fenerox survive on surface if like dark more. We is telling of burrow-cities, and then they is understanding. Still is wonder how sun not burn us, which is sad. Sun not scary. Sun is cleansing things and making heat so not die. Love sun. But night is better, because night is hunt.": "ナイターは暗闇を好むなら地表でフェネロックスがどう生き延びるか理解しない。巣穴都市のことを話すと理解した。それでも太陽がなぜ我々を焼かないか不思議がるのは悲しい。太陽は怖くない。太陽は物を浄化し熱を与えて死なないようにする。太陽を愛す。でも夜のほうがいい、夜は狩りだから。",
  "Find other race liking dark. Call self Nightar. Silly, because dark is also night. Wonder why is name? Despite, Fenerox people have new friend. Us is getting along because few words on both sides and prefer just hunt and dark. This is good. Nightar seem fearing leader like we is fearing dark-men. Maybe is same god?": "暗闘を好む別の種族を見つけた。ナイターと名乗る。馬鹿らしい、暗闘は夜だからだ。なぜそんな名前か不思議。それでもフェネロックスの民に新しい友ができた。双方とも言葉が少なく、ただ狩りと暗闇を好むからうまくいく。良いことだ。ナイターは我々が暗黒の男たちを恐れるように指導者を恐れているようだ。同じ神かも？",
  "Wing lizards. Why?": "翼トカゲ。なぜ？",
  "Meeting thinking lizards with crystals inside. Them is breathing...fire? Is heat-ish. Also is having wings, but not seem to care to fly. Why is have wings if not fly? Not matter much. Curious most is how crystals shaped to do things.": "クリスタルが内部にある考えるトカゲに会った。呼吸が…炎？熱っぽい。翼もあるが飛ぶ気はないようだ。飛ばないなら翼はなぜ？あまり重要ではない。最も興味深いのはクリスタルがどのように物事を行うよう形作られているか。",
  "At home, crystals is always sharp edges, and not very smart because unalive. But lizard-people have pieces be crystal and still is talk and breathe and think. Did Kirhos make? Unsure. Will ask. Not a scary people, but we not wonder at all if are tasty. Lizards not tasty, even if starving. Poison meat. Elduukhar also probably poison meat because lizards.": "母星ではクリスタルは常に鋭い縁で、生きていないからあまり賢くない。しかしトカゲ人はクリスタルの部品を持ちながら話し、",
  "Beetle men. Scare.": "カブトムシ人間。こわい",
  "Kirhos says valuable trade with Mantizi, and so we respect even if chitin is skin. Why is nature make shell skin? Why is terror-people even allowed? Still think should make illegal.": "キルホスはマンティジとの取引が価値あると言う。だからキチンが皮膚でも敬意を払う。なぜ自然は殻の皮膚を作る？なぜ恐怖の民が許される？やはり違法にすべきだと思う。",
  "These Mantizi terror-people not as scary as the Thelusians. Nicer insects that not flesh-eat the same way. Also, more civilized. Prefer talk and talk and make and make, less killing and eating. Still not going to be delicious. Not try to taste.": "このマンティジ恐怖民族はテルシアンほど怖くない。同じ方法で肉食しないよりましな昆虫。また、より文明的。話して話して作って作るのを好み、殺しと食べるのが少ない。それでも美味しくはない。味見しない。",
  "Metal cannot talk. Why is this metal talk.": "金属はしゃべれない。なぜこの金属はしゃべる",
  "Also, if metal people exist...why is not advanced? Should be super-people, but still using iron weapons. Even Fenerox changed to steel past 4 generations! How is metal-men having ships and space jump? Can metal-men be pets? Would be useful for clean burrows, since never sleeping.": "また、金属の民が存在するなら…なぜ進歩していない？超人であるべきなのにまだ鉄の武器を使っている。フェネロックスですら4世代前に鋼に変えた！金属の民はどうやって船と宇宙跳躍を？金属の民はペットにできる？眠らないから巣穴掃除に便利そう。",
  "Met impossible thing. Metal that talks. Kirhos said other people made metal-people and metal people just not remembering. We have many thinks about this, and are wonder: How is metal men baby-making? No flesh parts, no eggs, no sex? Where is babies? How is making more?": "ハイストームが宝石のパワーを補充する唯一の方法ではない。ほとんどの世界での厳しい天候でも可能だが、大幅に減少した速度で。一般に、惑星が危険であるほど効果的だ。",
  "Stand near and die?": "近くに立つと死ぬ？",
  "Also, X'i is not speaking like any other race. Hard understand, which means not trust because cannot make deal. Kirhos is saying deal always mark of trust. No trust. Glow people with plant feces not good. Avoid.": "また、シィは他のどの種族とも違う話し方をする。理解しにくい、つまり取引ができないから信用できない。キルホスは取引は常に信頼の証だと言う。信頼なし。植物の糞をする光る民族は良くない。避けよ。",
  "Nope. That is new word from Human. Nope. Is mean 'no' but sound nicer. Using to describe new race we met. X'i. Is radiation with rock skin. Can release seeds like poop, and use to make things. But standing near is unwise, we are thinking. They is eating poison glow rods for food. Remember on homeworld when Yassh Vix did, and died from lumpy growths on body? No eating of poison glow rods. Yet X'i not sick and die. Is instead get better from. Not trust.": "いいえ。人間から覚えた新しい言葉。いいえ。「ノー」の意味だが柔らかい。新しく出会った種族の説明に使う。シィ。放射線で",
  "Sky Gods Come": "空の神が来る",
  "From sky come God Rodents! Bringing much of magickal! Boats fly in sky, bows with no arrow. Shoot light! How? Them is offer us, and we is accept. All they wants is stupid rocks. Why want rocks? Not know, but us not anger sky rodents. Giving rocks. Us get magick bows and sky boats as thanks! Is Good!": "空から神のネズミが来た！たくさんの魔法を持って！船が空を飛ぶ、矢のない弓。光を撃つ！どうやって？彼らが我々に差し出し、我々は受け入れた。彼らが欲しいのは馬鹿な石だけ。なぜ石が欲しい？分からないが、空のネズミを怒らせない。石をあげる。お礼に魔法の弓と空の船をもらった！良い！",
  "Confusion is happen later. Asking about eekonimy? Us not know. Give more rocks. Get more bows. Easier. Them is teaching speak and write in their language, says is 'Galaktig Standurd Tung' and us should learn to do. We learn. Is hard, many new shapes and sounds. Prefer using old ways for speak.": "混乱は後から来る。エコニミーについて聞く？分からない。もっと岩をあげる。もっと弓をもらう。簡単。彼らは自分たちの言語で話し書きを教え、「ギャラクティグ スタンダード タング」と言い、学べと。学ぶ。難しい、新しい形と音がたくさん。話すのは昔の方法が好き。",
  "Why Cat No Hunt?": "なぜ猫は狩りしない？",
  "Met fluffy cat. They called Vel'uuish. Silly name. They is not hunters. Not know why. They is have sharp claws and teeths. They use hard paper. Not know why when steel better. Cat talk too much; Thinky too much. Not fully trust. Cat seem to get inside head somehow to talk. Is hurt head when thinky too much.": "もふもふ猫に会った。ヴェルーイッシュと呼ばれている。おかしな名前。狩人ではない。理由不明。鋭い爪と歯がある。硬い紙を使う。鋼のほうがいいのになぜ？猫は喋りすぎ。考えすぎ。完全には信用しない。猫は何とか頭の中に入って話すようだ。考えすぎると頭が痛い。",
  "Cat show us more book than creepy thinky-fish. Not interest us. We not know why cat not is hunter like us. Cat use odd crystals like lizards. Creepy. Kirhos say cat good trader, so we respect. Us not understand why hunty-looking cat not hunt. They not even want Avians. …Tasty birds. Mmmm... Cats like tasty birds, but not hunt them... Can kill them... but not... Why?": "猫は不気味な考える魚よりたくさんの本を見せてくれる。我々には興味がない。猫がなぜ我々のような狩人でないか分からない。猫は奇妙なクリスタルを使って",
  "Do Otter like Hunt? is quite similar to us...": "カワウソは狩りが好き？我々に似ている…",
  "Met otter. They called Lutrin. They is hunters, too. They is have sharp claws and teeths. They also carry big spear and wear metal clothing! They work alongside creepy thinky fish like we work alongside Kirhos, though we think is unease between Lutrin and Hylotl because of body language. Also interesting is that Lutrin speak similar to us. Did Fenerox get Lutrin language, or did Kirhos give Lutrin language, too?": "カワウソに会った。ルトリンと呼ばれている。彼らも狩人だ。鋭い爪と歯を持つ。大きな槍も持ち金属を着ている",
  "Maybe Lutrin can hunt alongside Floran and Fenerox, too, see who is best hunter. Can tell that otter is hunter because they take down angry flying bird with big spear they is carrying. Kirhos later tell us Lutrin was hunter of Hylotl, but is now hunter for Hylotl, same as Fenerox is hunter for Kirhos. So Lutrin therefore think of Hylotl like Fenerox think of Avian. Still curious about who got language from who. Will ask later.": "ルトリンもフローランやフェネロックスと一緒に狩りができるかも。誰が最高の狩人か見てみよう。カワウソが狩人だと分かるのは彼らが",
  "Uplifting: Phase 2": "アップリフティング: フェーズ2",
  "it was too boring and took too long to figure out.": "退屈すぎたし、解明に時間がかかりすぎた",
  "Uplifting is going well. These Fenerox are highly adaptable and fast learners, though they do show a lack of capacity for using the galactic standard tongue. This is undoubtedly due to how their speech organs operate, and no fault of their own.": "啓発は順調だ。フェネロックスは高い適応力と学習速度を持つが、銀河標準語の使用能力に欠ける面がある。これは間違いなく発声器官の仕組みによるもので、彼らの責任ではない。",
  "We've attempted to create a modified version that they can use to at least approximate the vowel and consonant sounds. Despite all of this, however, they appear to have very little capability for writing the language down. They prefer to use hand gestures to 'sign'": "少なくとも母音と子音の音を近似できる修正版を作ろうとした。それにもかかわらず、彼らは言語を書き留める能力がほとんどないようだ。手のジェスチャーで「サイン」するのを好む。",
  "their words as they speak, and any amount of teaching them letters is met with doubt or annoyance. They move very swiftly, and writing (according to them) takes entirely too long. One even mentioned that he would be old and grey by the time he learned to write, because": "話しながら言葉を書き、どんなに文字を教えても疑念か苛立ちで迎えられる。非常に素早く動き、書くことは（彼らによれば）時間がかかりすぎる。書くことを覚える頃には老いて白髪になっていると言った者さえいた。なぜなら",
  "Uplifting: A side effect": "アップリフティング: 副作用",
  "Despite the Uplifting going well (beyond our expectations, in fact), there has been an unintended side-effect. The Fenerox are -insanely- loyal to us. We failed to take into account their particularly unique pair-bonding mechanism their kind practices. It seems that once they imprint, they are unwilling to separate from the target of their bond. Ever.": "啓発が順調（予想を超えて）に進む一方で、意図しない副作用が生じた。フェネロックスは信じられないほど忠誠心が強い",
  "So, we have permanent attaches that accompany us just about everywhere now. There is a positive to this, thankfully - Fenerox are highly capable hunters and intensely ferocious if their pair-bonds are threatened. This is likely a holdover from eons of unchanged mating habits. As such, we have not been cheated on a deal in over 3 solar cycles. Our profits are up, because nobody wants to risk the wrath of our new 'guard dogs'": "ほぼどこへでも同行する常駐の随行員がついた。ありがたいことにこれには良い面がある — フェネロックスは",
  "Protect Kirhos": "キルホスを守れ",
  "Kirhos make amazing things. We knows this. Them is teaches to speak and write in Galactic Tongue. Us learns, but is hard. But Kirhos lack one thing. Tough. Are weak and fluffy. Prey animals once, maybe. Fenerox tough, and faster. Kirhos talk much. We hunt much. So we hunt for Kirhos.": "キルホスはすごいものを作る。知っている。銀河共通語の話し方と書き方を教えてくれる。学んでいるが難しい。しかしキルホスには一つ欠けているものがある。頑丈さ。弱くてふわふわ。昔は獲物だったかも。フェネロックスは頑丈で速い。キルホスはよく話す。我々はよく狩る。だからキルホスのために狩る。",
  "We never tell Kirhos they is weaker, because they gave us technology and teach us to be better than other Fenerox. Instead, we keep Kirhos alive. In exchange, Kirhos may help Uplift all other Fenerox tribes across galaxy. Everyone benefit. Kirhos protected, We stronger. And then one day, we make Empire. We rule. But no tell anyone. Keeping secret.": "キルホスに弱いとは決して言わない。技術をくれ、他のフェネロックスより良くなることを教えてくれたから。代わりにキルホスを守る",
  "Florans Smell Bad": "フローランは臭い",
  "But is not mean dislike. Friendly, because hunters. Compete is keen, and makes for good fun. We compete and see who better hunter is.": "でも嫌いという意味ではない。友好的、なぜなら狩人だから。競争は熱く、楽しい。競い合って誰がより優れた狩人か見るのだ。",
  "Kirhos introduced us to Florans. Unsure why. Seem like us at first, always hunt, always tougher. Except one thing. Plants. How is plants make hunt? Why is plants make hunt? On homeworld, plants is for urine and berries. Not killing.": "キルホスがフローランを紹介してきた。理由不明。最初は我々に似ている。常に狩り、常にタフ。一つを除いて。植物。植物がなぜ狩りをする？なぜ植物が狩りをする？母星では植物は排尿とベリー用。殺しではない。",
  "Floran also talk strange. Referring always to entire race and not self. Why? Explain? None make them change tongue, but Fenerox expected to speak Standard? Explain. Required needed information. Also, meat diet of Florans and being plant, them never need bathe. Smelling like rotten meat all time. We dislike.": "フローランも変な話し方。常に種族全体を指し、自分を指さない。なぜ？説明を。誰もフローランに言葉を変えさせないのに、フェネロックスは標準語を話すべき？説明を。必要な情報を要求。また、フローランは肉食で植物だから入浴不要。常に腐った肉の臭い。我々は嫌い。",
  "Avians: Is Delicious?": "エイビアン: 美味しい？",
  "We have met new species again, thanks to Kirhos. Is called Avians. Big problem for us there, because Avians smell and look tasty. Really, really tasty. Fenerox instinct always 'kill bird, eat bird' but us not allowed to kill and eat these birds. Also, these birds have scary shiny gem guns. Likely also dislike being eated.": "ワンダラーは銀河全体に痕跡を残している — 多くまたはほとんどは時間や回収によって失われたが、旅の途中で遭遇するかもしれない。残念ながらほとんどは嘲笑して嘘つき呼ばわりするだろう。古代種以前に何かが存在すると信じる者は少ない。しかしそうでなければ我々の歴史をどう説明する？",
  "Secret, we think on how to taste Avians and know what is taste. Must know, because hunger makes birds even tastier. Fenerox like food, and like hunt, and like birds. Maybe us speak to Floran, see how them is gets away with kill and eat Hylotl. Then us do same for bird people.": "秘密。エイビアンの味を知る方法と味とは何かを考える。知らなければならない、空腹が鳥をもっと美味しくするから。フェネロックスは食べ物が好きで、狩りが好きで、鳥が好き。フローランに話を聞いて、ハイロトルを殺して食べる方法を学ぼう。そしたら鳥人にも同じことをする。",
  "Why fish men have brain?": "なぜ魚人間に脳がある？",
  "Fenerox people dislike fish. Savannah not really have fish, or many of lizurds and amfibyuns. Not understand how horrifying monster from water places is having thinking brains. Even more surprise: Hylotl is -really- thinky. Always thinking. Using lots of words and writings to explain things. Annoying.": "フェネロックスの民は魚が嫌い。サバンナにはあまり魚がいない、トカゲや両生類も。水の場所から来る恐ろしい怪物がどうやって考える脳を持つのか理解できない。さらに驚き：ハイロトルは本当に考えっぽい。いつも考えている。物事を説明するのに多くの言葉と文字を使う。うるさい。",
  "Mostly, Hylotl scary. Avoid if can, because them will talk, and when them does their three eyes do watching. Ever been watch by *three* eyes? No? Shiver-scare always. Also, eyes not really blink normal like mammal eyes. Instead, is soul-empty and horror. Avoid! Fish men keep to seas, so is easy.": "ほとんどの場合ハイロトルは怖い。できれば避ける。話しかけてくるから、そしてそうすると三つの目で見てくる。三つの目で見られたことある？ない？いつも震え恐怖。あと、目は普通の哺乳類の目のように瞬きしない。代わりに魂が空で恐怖。避けよ！魚人は海にいるから簡単。",
  "Apex mean. No.": "エイペックスは意地悪。やだ",
  "Primates remind us of rock-murderers from homeworld. Remember, them always in packs and running fast and throwing things, and killing Fenerox for sport? Apex very much alike. Cruel, poking things with sharp metal sticks with juice inside. Claim doctor, but not trust because ape.": "霊長類は母星の岩殺し屋を思い出させる。覚えているだろう、いつも群れで走り回り物を投げ、遊びでフェネロックスを殺していたのを？エイペックスはとてもよく似ている。残酷で、中に液体が入った尖った金属の棒で突く。医者を名乗るが、猿だから信用しない。",
  "Kirhos say this is good, because Apex are murder-monkeys and even poke-juice their own kind to make dumber so can control. Control is bad! Free mind matters. Why not want free-mind? Free-mind is making social better, and social better is making lots of babies. Babies are good to make. Also fun to make. Fenerox quite enjoy baby making.": "キルホスはこれは良いことだと言う。エイペックスは殺し猿で、自分の同胞にさえ突き刺し液を注入して愚かにして支配するから。支配は悪い！自由な心が大事。なぜ自由な心を望まない？自由な心は社会を良くし、社会が良くなると赤ちゃんをたくさん作る。赤ちゃんは作るのが良い。作るのも楽しい。フェネロックスはかなり赤ちゃん作りを楽しむ。",
  "Standing Orders: Ravagers": "命令書: 略奪者",
  "Ravagers must be treated with extreme caution. You probably won't encounter them unless you seek them out in the asteroid fields dotting the galaxy, but occasionally they will raid settlements for... prey.": "レイヴァジャーには極度の注意が必要。銀河の小惑星帯で探さない限り遭遇しないだろうが、時折集落を…獲物のために襲撃する。",
  "Do not allow the promise of wealth sway you - while their collection of treasures and artifacts is surely potentially valuable, so too is their depravity and cruelty.": "富の約束に惑わされるな。彼らの宝物やアーティファクトのコレクションは確かに価値がある可能性があるが、彼らの堕落と残虐さも同様だ。",
  "There have even been reports that some of them have undergone some sort of... secondary metamorphosis. They're said to be faster, stronger and smarter than the average Peglaci. Approach with extreme caution - or when heavily armed.": "一部が何らかの…二次変態を経たという報告さえある。平均的なペグラシより速く、強く、賢いという。極度の注意を持って接近せよ — あるいは重武装で。",
  "Ravagers care nothing for the well-being of others, or really even of themselves - all they desire is the forcible 'improvement' of their kind. Should you attempt to take out one of their bases of operation, be prepared to encounter a variety of sickening experiments.": "レイヴァジャーは他者、あるいは自分自身の幸福すら気にしない — 彼らが望むのは自分たちの種族の強制的な「改良」だけだ。彼らの活動拠点を攻略しようとするなら、様々な吐き気を催す実験に遭遇する覚悟をしておけ。",
  "Ravager Anatomy: Autopsy Reports": "ラヴェイジャーの解剖学: 検死報告書",
  "Genetically speaking, this specimen is a Peglaci in almost every way. He was born among his people, had a normal childhood, and his bones show no evidence of deformity or health complications. At least, not until the very outer layers.": "遺伝的に見て、この標本はほぼあらゆる点でペグラシだ。同胞の中で生まれ、普通の幼少期を過ごし、骨には変形や健康上の合併症の証拠がない。少なくとも、最外層までは。",
  "Take a closer look at the bone now. No, zoom in more, Michael. There you go. Look at the cell wall.\n\n^yellow;[audible gasping, and an unintelligible reply]^reset;\n\nRight? They somehow were able to etch entire volumes of text into the bone, through the epidermis and muscle, in perfect detail.": "骨をもっとよく見てくれ。もっとズームして、マイケル。そうだ。細胞壁を見ろ。\n\n^yellow;[息を飲む音、聞き取れない返答]^reset;\n\nだろう？彼らは何らかの方法で表皮と筋肉を通して骨にテキスト全巻を完璧な精度で刻むことができたのだ。",
  "It gets weirder though, Michael. We found the remains of another one in a cistern not far away. It had been hastily 'stored' there, after it had been killed. I suspect there is good reason for this, after performing an autopsy. This is one bizarre Peglaci. We'll discuss him next.\n\n^yellow;[ Tape Ends ]^reset;": "さらに奇妙になるぞ、マイケル。近くの貯水槽で別の遺体を発見した。殺された後、急いで「保管」されていた。解剖を行った後、これには正当な理由があると思う。奇妙なペグラシだ。次に彼について議論しよう。\n\n^yellow;[テープ終了]^reset;",
  "You see, it seems that at some point this gentleman was either abducted or accepted within a new tribe. Within this new family he underwent some sort of...surgery? I'm not sure what to call it, really. Note in image 7c how the striations suddenly adjust? This is indicative of sudden genetic alteration.": "どうやら、この紳士はある時点で誘拐されたか、新しい部族に受け入れられたようだ。この新しい家族の中で何らかの…手術？何と呼ぶべきか分からない。画像7cで線条が突然変化しているのに注目。これは突然の遺伝子変異を示している。",
  "Only two known procedures exist in the present day that can accomplish this, and both are excruciating beyond capacity to tolerate and thus outlawed on every civilized world save for Halsev IV, where to this day all acts except murder and extortion are legal. Neither procedure can be done this well.": "現在知られている手順は2つだけで、どちらも耐えられないほどの激痛であり、ハルセフIVを除く全ての文明世界で禁止されている（殺人と恐喝以外の全ての行為が合法）。どちらの手順もこれほど上手くはできない。",
  "Ravager Anatomy: Autopsy Reports III": "ラヴェイジャーの解剖学: 検死報告書 III",
  "Get ready...this one is going to blow your mind, Michael. So, as I mentioned, we found him in a cistern, somewhere around 200 meters away from the location the bones were discovered. \n\n^yellow;[ Metal Drawer opens ]^reset;": "覚悟しろ…マイケル、これは驚くぞ。言った通り、骨が発見された場所から約200メートル離れた貯水槽で彼を見つけた。\n\n^yellow;[金属の引き出しが開く]^reset;",
  "Anyhow, we aren't even getting to the good stuff yet. Check this out. \n\n ^yellow;[ Strange squishing sounds ]^reset;\n\n What you are seeing here is...well, I actually have no idea. It's like some sort of gel-sack that has taken the place of a stomach. From within I managed to extract some...interesting things.": "とにかく、まだ本題にも入っていない。これを見てくれ。\n\n^yellow;[奇妙なぐちゃぐちゃ音]^reset;\n\nここに見えているのは…正直、全く分からない。胃の代わりに何らかのジェル袋があるようなものだ。中からいくつか…興味深いものを取り出せた。",
  "Subject is male, approximately 32 years of age. Despite his appearance, genetic testing already confirmed that he is without a doubt...Peglaci. For the record, this is the condition it was found in and has not in any way been tampered with. What you are seeing is real.": "その後、全てがエスカレートし、新しい種族との公然たる紛争に巻き込まれた。彼らは「ハイロトル」と名乗った。幸い短期間だった。「テレーンプロテクトレート」と呼ばれる別の政府が連絡を取り、敵対行為を停止させるため介入した。",
  "The barbed wire wraps around most of the few remaining patches with actual visible flesh...which reminds me of self-flaggelation common in many religions across the galaxy. Personally, it is my belief that whoever this was, he was a pious man. Likely fanatical, given the severity of the scar tissue on the flesh sites.": "28日目 - 数日の作業の後、^gray;先駆者のステイシスシステム^reset;を限定的な時間旅行に作り変えた。ケビンがテストしているが、最も最近のリスポーン以前には戻れないようだ。しかし一緒に何かに取り組めるなら秘密を守ると約束した。何かは言わなかった。",
  "The subject has nearly no visible epidermis of his own, as his entire body is encased in a sort of exoskeleton that appears to be composed of jagged bone.\n\n^yellow;[ a voice asks 'How could he just grow new bone like this? It doesn't make sense. And what the hell is up with all this wire? ]^reset;\n\n Valid questions. I suspect the bone issue is like Fibrodysplasia ossificans progressiva. The rest...I remain clueless.": "被験体には自身の表皮がほとんど見えない。全身がある種の外骨格に覆われているようだ",
  "I found this in his stomach. It matches Peglaci as well. The remains cannot all be from one individual, as there are three separate left thumbs. So...it seems he was a cannibal. Like the other specimen, there is microscopic writing etched on every millimeter of his entire skeleton. I suspect this is religious text, and that might mean we have stumbled upon what the Peglaci refer to as Ravagers.": "彼の胃の中で見つけた。これもペグラシと一致する。3つの別々の頭蓋の残骸があるため、全ての遺体が一人の個体からのものではありえない",
  "Standing Orders: Wanderer Artifacts": "命令書: ワンダラーアーティファクト",
  "Alternately, you may wish to try to use them. You are free to try, but we would suggest you be very cautious. Some Peglaci settlements contain a Wanderer artifact or two - you may have the most luck if you start there.": "あるいは、それらを使ってみたいかもしれない。試すのは自由だが、非常に慎重であることを勧める。一部のペグラシ集落にはワンダラーのアーティファクトがある — そこから始めるのが最も幸運かもしれない。",
  "The Wanderers have left traces of themselves across the entire galaxy - many or most have been lost to time or salvage, but you may encounter them in your travels. Most, sadly, will scoff at you and call you a liar. Few believe anything predates the Ancients, after all. Yet, if that were not the case, explain our history?": "キルホスのおかげでまた新しい種族に会った。エイビアンという。大問題だ。エイビアンは美味しそうな匂いと見た目だから。本当に本当に美味しそう。フェネロックスの本能は常に「鳥を殺して鳥を食べる」だが、この鳥を殺して食べるのは許されない。あと怖い光線銃を持っている。食べられるのも嫌がるだろう。",
  "The Artifacts are of great value, but they are also almost indestructible - you won't be breaking them by accident, don't worry. They're easy to identify, given the distinct black metal and glowing yellow inset details. If you encounter them, return them to a Peacekeeper outpost for a finder's fee. It will pay even more than tech from the Ancients!": "アーティファクトは非常に価値があるが、ほぼ破壊不可能でもある — 偶然壊すことはない、心配するな。簡単に",
  "Peacekeeper Codex: Peglaci Origins": "ピースキーパーの書: ペグラシの起源",
  "Three billion were killed by the Wanderers in one single day. They simply launched rocks at the surface of our homeworld from orbit, letting the mass do the damage...and then left us. All they left us were their artifacts, their databanks, and their fascination with the unknown.": "30億がワンダラーによって1日で殺された。単に軌道から母星の地表に岩を投下し、質量にダメージを任せた…そして去った。残されたのはアーティファクト、データバンク、そして未知への魅了だけだった。",
  "Only at this point did we think to question our overlords. Only when ordered to murder millions of children did we even consider that they might not be benevolent after all. We had committed horrible acts for them previously, yes. But never had they asked us to kill our own kind. We refused. The penalty was severe.": "この時点になって初めて支配者に疑問を呈した。何百万人の子供を殺せと命じられて初めて、彼らが善意ではないかもしれないと考えた。以前にも恐ろしい行為を彼らのために行った。しかし自分たちの同胞を殺せとは言われたことがなかった。拒否した。罰は厳しかった。",
  "Other races may seek for ages the mystery of their origins. Not so for we Peglaci. Our history is kept eternal both through digital storage and stories. And even more important, song. To us, song is memory. We record our history into our minds and our souls through voice, and these vibrations pass from Mother to Whelp with each spawning season.": "他の種族は起源の謎を何世代も追い求めるかもしれない。ペグラシはそうではない。我々の歴史はデジタル保存と",
  "In our distant past, the Peglaci were an apex carnivore, hunting (and being hunted by) whales that were our chief source of food. Of tool use we knew nearly nothing. Our lives were nomadic, where we gathered in hunting bands, raiding other groups and running off with their young. We were savage, relentless and without mercy. That may be what attracted the Wanderers to our world in the first place.": "遠い過去、ペグラシは頂点捕食者であり、主な食料源であるクジラを狩り（クジラにも狩られ）ていた。",
  "One day, a great light came down from the sky upon our ancestors - the Wanderers. Over the course of several centuries they guided our species from savagery to civilization, and we were more than willing to do whatever they asked as thanks for their gifts. They were more than happy to abuse our dependence on them, using us as they saw fit to achieve their ends. The price was small for the gains we obtained.": "ある日、祖先の元に大きな光が空から降りてきた — ワンダラーだ。数世紀にわたって彼らは導いた",
  "The Wanderers answered nothing we thought to ask, so we were encouraged to push ourselves forwards. We did as we were told - what could we give a race such as theirs? What threat could we pose? So, we strove to live up to their intentions for us, however murky they may have seemed. Over time our people thrived, and eventually became complacent.": "ワンダラーは我々が尋ねようと思ったことには何も答えなかったので、自ら前に進むよう励まされた。言われた通りにした — 何を失うというのか",
  "As it is with all beings that are happy and need not struggle to survive any longer, we began to question our place in the cosmos and how we got here..and wondered exactly who the Wanderers were. We pressed them for information, and got nothing. Not even a reply. It was at this time that the Wanderers ordered that we eliminate our newest generation to make room for more 'compliant' offspring.": "幸福でもはや生存のために苦闘する必要のない全ての存在がそうであるように、我々は宇宙における自分たちの立場を問い始めた",
  "Peglaci Tale-Songs": "ペグラシの物語歌",
  "There are so many other potential applications for their voices that we've likely barely scratched the surface of what is possible.": "彼らの声には他にも多くの潜在的な用途があり、可能性の表面をかすっただけだろう。",
  "This means that they are often capable of vibrating their vocal cords at frequencies most species are not even able to hear. Their 'songs' are even capable of calming others if they can find the right frequency. This has led to some unique talents among professionals of their species.": "つまり彼らはほとんどの種族が聞くことすらできない周波数で声帯を振動させることができる。適切な周波数を見つければ、彼らの「歌」は他者を落ち着かせることさえできる。これが種族の専門家に独自の才能をもたらした。",
  "Then of course there is Vorlin Tae, reknowned opera Diva. She has performed to audiences across the galaxy, and many claim her shows are more intoxicating than even the most expensive street drugs. Her voice is the stuff of legends and tickets are appropriately priced for such a reputation.": "そしてもちろん著名なオペラ歌姫ヴォーリン・タエ。銀河中の観客の前で公演し、彼女のショーは最も高価なストリートドラッグよりも酔わせると多くが主張する。その声は伝説の域であり、チケットの価格もその評判にふさわしい。",
  "Among the races in the galactic core, few are as capable of beautiful song as the Peglaci. Their people have honed their vocal cords over millenia into some of the most advanced sound-making organs known to science. They are capable of reaching a stunning 15 to 40 octave range, depending on their familial heritage!": "銀河核の種族の中で、ペグラシほど美しい歌声を持つ者は少ない。何千年もかけて声帯を科学で知られる最も先進的な発声器官に研ぎ澄ませた。家系にもよるが、驚異の15〜40オクターブの音域を持つ！",
  "Take, for example, Madame Knoshik of the Gurula Gentleman's Ranch. She uses her song to draw in suitors to her establishment over a distance of 0.25 light years thanks to state-of-the-art speakers on the exterior. She also uses this voice to keep her clients calm and well-behaved. A boon to her women-in-waiting.": "例えばグルラ紳士牧場のクノシック夫人。最先端のスピーカーのおかげで0.25光年の距離から歌で求婚者を引き寄せる。この声でクライアントを穏やかで行儀良くさせている。待機する女性たちにとっての恩恵だ。",
  "Another fine example would be the Hevlar Corps, an elite branch of the Protectorate Defense Force composed entire of Peglaci. Through special sound-based training they are capable of eliminating threats without even needing to shoot. Soothing targets to sleep, and then imprisoning them, is much cleaner than wet works.": "もう一つの良い例はヘヴラー隊。ペグラシで構成されたプロテクトレート防衛軍のエリート部門。特殊な音響訓練により、撃つことなく脅威を排除できる。標的を眠らせて投獄するのは汚い仕事より遥かにクリーンだ。",
  "[The entire book is written in Greggish, which makes discerning anything particularly impossible. None the less, this is clearly a gripping read, as every single page has a dog-ear on it.": "[本全体がグレッグ語で書かれており、何かを読み取ることは特に不可能。それでもなお、全てのページに折り目があることから、明らかに引き込まれる読み物である。",
  "(page 224) - Gregga gregity greg GREG! GREGGA GREG! (Greg, gregga gregga greg greg gregg!) Gregga? Greg greg greggin-greg gregga! Greg. Greg.": "（224ページ）- グレッガ グレギティ グレッグ グレッグ！グレッガ グレッグ！（グレッグ、グレッガ グレッガ グレッグ グレッグ グレッグ！）グレッガ？グレッグ グレッグ グレッギン-グレッグ グレッガ！グレッグ。グレッグ。",
  "(page 355) - Greg greg gregga greg. Greg. Gregga! Rainbow.": "（355ページ）- グレッグ グレッグ グレッガ グレッグ。グレッグ。グレッガ！レインボー。",
  "[400 more pages remain]": "[残り400ページ]",
  "Experimental Vaccine": "実験的ワクチン",
  "My....mind. Slips. Seeing things I shouldn't. Greg. Hard to formulate thoughts in language. Gregga. Name easier. Feel connected to source virus, like hive mind. Greg. Be Greg.": "私の…心が。滑る。見てはいけないものが見える。グレッグ。言葉で思考をまとめるのが難しい。グレッガ。名前のほうが楽。源ウイルスと繋がっている感じ。集合意識のように。グレッグ。グレッグになれ。",
  "I...Door...Greg. Gregga greg gregga.": "俺は…ドア…グレッグ。グレッガ グレッグ グレッガ。",
  "Someone opened the main doors last night. It's out, free, and able to spread. The plus side is that the virus eradicating our people will be cured. Unfortunately, I can make no assurances on long-term implications of what this cure will do to us as a species.": "昨夜誰かがメインドアを開けた。外に出て自由になり、広がれる。良い面は、我々の民を根絶するウイルスが治癒されること。残念ながら、この治療法が種族として我々に長期的に何をもたらすかは保証できない。",
  "Somehow our air system was compromised last night. Air from outside has found its way within the complex. We are all infected with the virus, and are living on borrowed time. The rest of the team agrees that we need to speed up research on Greg's cure.": "昨夜、空調システムが損なわれた。外の空気が施設内に入り込んだ。全員がウイルスに感染し、借りた時間で生きている。チーム全員がグレッグの治療法の研究を加速する必要があると同意した。",
  "Two days later, and not a one of us is any more ill. At least half of us should be dead by now, given the track record that the Shaxxral virus has. Something has impeded the capacity it has to affect our cells. Greg still can't communicate with us, but I would wager his cure has something to do with it.": "2日後、誰一人として悪化していない。シャクスラルウイルスの実績を考えれば、今頃少なくとも半数は死んでいるはずだ。何かが細胞への影響力を阻害している。グレッグはまだ我々と通信できないが、彼の治療法が関係していると賭けてもいい。",
  "Whatever that fluid did to this agent, I am recommending the destruction of all remaining samples. These are too dangerous to be allowed to survive for further research. I am commencing tests on blood samples obtained from fellow staff members, as we have grown concerned that somehow Greg's experimental prion is spreading.": "この…かなり露出の多い出版物には様々な状態の裸で交尾儀式を行う人間が掲載されている。想像できるほぼあらゆる種類の。そして想像し難いものも。少なくとも地球が終わる前は、人間は交尾行為を記録していたようだ。そして他の人間に売っていた。不思議。",
  "I don't understand what is happening! Somehow our *other* facilities in entirely different sections of the galaxy are also experiencing the exact same issues. The prion...or whatever it is...is somehow spreading to populations across the vast gulf of space! How this is even possible is utterly beyond my capacity to theorize on.": "何が起きているか理解できない！何とか銀河の全く別のセクションにある*他の*施設でも全く同じ問題が発生している。プリオン…あるいは何であれ…は宇宙の広大な空間を越えて集団に広がっている！これがどうやって可能なのか、理論化する能力を完全に超えている。",
  "I've begun to hate. Not people here in the lab. Just...the uninfected. Specifically, I have unavoidable visions of brutally murdering them however I possibly can. It's not unlike having a 'wet dream', and when I awake I feel aroused. The others also remark on having the exact same....dreams? Visions? Either way, we're terrified.": "憎しみ始めた。研究室の人間ではない。ただ…感染していない者たちを。具体的には、可能な限り残酷に殺す回避不能のビジョンがある。「夢精」に似て、目覚めると興奮している。他の者も全く同じ…夢？ビジョン？いずれにせよ恐怖している。",
  "Gregga": "グレッガ",
  "Gregged gregga greg greg. Greg! Greg gregga gregga gregga greg. Greg? Greg! Gregga rainbow greg greg rainbow!": "グレッグド グレッガ グレッグ グレッグ。グレッグ！グレッグ グレッガ グレッガ グレッガ グレッグ。グレッグ？グレッグ！グレッガ レインボー グレッグ グレッグ レインボー！",
  "RAINBOW! Greg gregga greggy gregin. Terrance greg greg Matt. Rainbow.": "レインボー！グレッグ グレッガ グレッギー グレギン。テランス グレッグ グレッグ マット。レインボー。",
  "Every single rat in the enclosure appears to have died in agony. Their corpses are all over the enclosure, some in various states of....we'll just call it decay. C7 is the sole survivor of this event, and is apparently the cause of death. Somehow.": "囲いの中の全てのネズミが苦悶の中で死んだようだ。死体が囲い中に散乱し、一部は様々な状態の…腐敗と呼ぼう…にある。C7がこの事象の唯一の生存者で、どうやら死因でもあるようだ。",
  "Normal rat socialization appears to be taking place, and our ill rat is completely free of the viral load he was carrying. Greg has done some good work here! We're going to observe and record until absolutely certain that the results are working to our favor.": "正常なネズミの社会化が行われているようで、病気のネズミはウイルス量から完全に解放された。グレッグはここで良い仕事をした！結果が我々に有利に働いていると完全に確信するまで観察・記録を続ける。",
  "We've re-integrated the rat into the general population to see what happens. Should normal rat behavior resume, we'll know the cure functions and can begin mass-production and hopefully save our people. Should the results not be favorable...I fear we may be too late.": "ネズミを一般集団に再統合して何が起きるか観察する。正常なネズミの行動が再開すれば治療が機能していると分かり、大量生産を開始して民を救えるかもしれない。結果が好ましくなければ…手遅れかもしれないと恐れる。",
  "The plague has torn through our people like wheat to a scythe, and it's been particularly difficult to reach the point we finally did today. Greg found a cure! Or, rather, a potential one. We're going to try it on the rat-things today and begin observation. It should be noted that initial trials on genes in the lab were successful, though the method of transmission is unclear.": "疫病が大鎌に対する麦のように我々の民を引き裂き、ようやく到達した地点に至るまで特に困難だった",
  "Subject rat C7 appears to be fine, and even the blistering lesions are rapidly fading. Finally, a result we can work with! I do wonder how Greg solved the issue with the prion being so aggressive. He swears he didn't use the strange fluid we found on that moon orbiting Coronis IV. I am uncertain that I believe this, as Greg is not exactly the sort to accept delays on his results.": "被験体ネズミC7は問題ないようで、水疱性の病変さえ急速に消えつつある。ついに使える結果だ！ただ気になるのは",
  "After twenty assorted tests on the genome markers for this curative agent, we were unable to determine what caused C7 to go ballistic and attack, kill, mutilate and devour the other rats at random. The viral load in his cells is not present, nor is there any trace of change in his physiology.": "この治療薬のゲノムマーカーに対する20種類のテストの後、C7がなぜ暴走し、他のネズミを無作為に攻撃、殺害、切断、貪り食ったのかを特定できなかった。細胞内のウイルス量は存在せず、生理学的変化の痕跡もない。",
  "No sign of Greg for a few days now. We can hear him tinkering in his office, but any time we knock he refuses to answer or even acknowledge us. Reason unknown. Probably just hyper-focused.": "数日間グレッグの姿が見えない。オフィスで何かいじっている音は聞こえるが、ノックしても返事も反応もしない。理由不明。おそらく超集中しているだけだろう。",
  "Every single rat has been 'changed' by C7. The upside is that all traces of the hostile virus have been removed from the host. Our prion works! Without some means to remove the negative effects, however, we will not be able to use it. I doubt everyone wants to lose who they were just to remove a sickness.": "全てのネズミがC7によって「変化」させられた。良い面は、宿主から敵対ウイルスの全ての痕跡が除去されたこと。プリオンは機能する！しかし悪影響を除去する手段なしには使えない。病気を除去するためだけに自分が何者だったかを失いたい者はいないだろう。",
  "Subject C7 has...resurrected. Brain functions in the rat have resumed ordinary function. However, subject appears to have forgotten how to be a rat and is busy screeching at other rats in the room. Prion count is absurdly high. We won't merge him with the population this time as I have no desire to clean rat viscera off of every surface in the lab again.": "標本C7が…蘇った。ネズミの脳機能が通常に復帰した。しかし被験体は行動の仕方を忘れたようだ",
  "I can't explain it, but somehow other subjects in the lab are now infected with whatever caused issues to C7. They exhibit the same symptomology, despite being in a clean-room with a dedicated air supply, glass walls and no direct contact to the subject. I checked the tapes from the night: no one entered or tampered with the experiments.": "説明できないが、研究室の他の被験者もC7に問題を引き起こしたものに感染している。同じ症状を示している。",
  "After closer inspection, it seems that any and all stimulus experienced by C7 are also at least partially experienced by other subjects in the lab. When presented with a small amount of narcotic, C7 was rendered intoxicated. C6 through C24 all simultaneously shared the same precise physical actions for a period of 72 minutes.": "詳しく調べると、C7が経験する全ての刺激は研究室の他の被験体にも少なくとも部分的に経験されているようだ。少量の麻薬を与えたところC7は酔った。C6からC24まで全員が72分間、全く同じ身体的動作を同時に共有した。",
  "Greg finally came out of his room after 2 full weeks. He is...different. He keeps repeating his name, over and over again. Nothing more. He becomes increasingly agitated trying to communicate with us. He clearly *thinks* he is talking fine. Yet all that comes out is 'Greg'. I've recommended he stay contained due to how the rats reacted to C7.": "グレッグがついに丸2週間ぶりに部屋から出てきた。彼は…違う。自分の名前を何度も繰り返し続ける。それ以上何もない。",
  "While it took weeks, we have isolated the problem. Some sort of rapidly mutating particle, so small as to be undetectable even in the electron microscope, has tainted the main sample. The source of this particle remains largely unknown, though my theory that Greg mixed some of that fluid into his batch seems the most likely cause.": "数週間かかったが問題を特定した。電子顕微鏡でも検出できないほど小さな急速に変異する粒子がメインサンプルを汚染していた。この粒子の源は大部分が不明だが、グレッグがバッチにあの液体を混ぜたという私の理論が最も有力のようだ。",
  "I got Greg to admit it: He put that weird fluid in his mix. According to him, testing showed that the effect it has on biological samples is astounding and was worth a test if it meant the safety of our species. He seems a bit overly defensive , despite my assurances that he was not in any form of administrative trouble.": "彼らはフライトレスが疎外され抑圧され、Kluexに仕えるためだけに生きるようになっても従った。長老たちが高い塔を建て、選ばれたフライトレスであるアセンダントがそこから飛び降りることになっても従った。一人ずつアセンダントが地面に落ち、二度と飛べなくなっても従った。Kluexは喜んでいると言われた。",
  "Greg started acting a bit off today. I can't quite put my finger on it. Something is up with his speech patterns. It's slight, but there. I'll keep an eye on him. In the meantime I have managed to isolate the strange particle and neutralize it in subject C7. Two hours ago I administered antibodies into her, and now I wait to see what happens.": "今日グレッグの様子が少しおかしくなった。何が問題か正確には分からない。話し方のパターンに何かがある。わずかだが確かにある。",
  "Subject C7 , when injected with antibodies: At first subject seemed fine. At four-hours, thirty seven seconds after injection the subject began to writhe in agony. After 14 minutes, subject appeared to suffer complete and total brain-death, though other biological functions remain operational.": "標本C7、抗体注射時：最初は問題なさそうだった。注射後4時間37秒で対象は苦悶しだした。14分後、対象は完全かつ全面的な脳死に陥ったようだが、他の生物学的機能は維持されている。",
  "The Masters of Microchips": "マイクロチップの達人",
  "Some hundreds (or thousands...the records are unclear on this point) of years ago, the Kirhos had advanced to the absolute pinnacle of scientific and technological achievement.  Unfortunately, around the same time, they exhausted all resources on their homeworld required to utilize their knowledge. What followed was a series of brutal wars that devastated their infrastructure and led to them fleeing for the stars.": "数百年（あるいは数千年…記録はこの点で不明確）前、キルホスは技術の絶対的頂点にまで進んでいた",
  "The loss of their homeworld and its resources meant that the only known location of the super-rare element Thulium was forever lost. Thulium formed the core of all of their computer technology and without it they were unable to maintain their previous level of advancement. It was a century, perhaps longer, before a viable replacement was located deep in the asteroid belts near Azakon Reticuli.": "母星とその資源の喪失は、超稀少元素トゥリウムの唯一知られた産地が永遠に失われたことを意味した",
  "Arcologies": "アーコロジー",
  "The Kirhos are fiercely individualistic.  Kirhosi governments were always mostly powerless, and in this age of colonization the Kirhos that hold the most power are the ones who can afford to build artificial ecosystem-cities called arcologies.": "キルホスは強烈に個人主義的。キルホシの政府は常にほぼ無力で、この植民時代では最も権力を持つキルホスはアーコロジーと呼ばれる人工生態系都市を建設できる者たちだ。",
  "'Arcs', as they are colloquially known, are often owned by a single corporation.  Inhabitants of an arc are expected to work for their patron corporation for life, and in return are paid well enough to consume all the latest corp-sponsored entertainment.": "口語で「アーク」として知られるこれらは、しばしば一つの企業が所有する。アークの住民はパトロン企業のために一生働くことを期待され、見返りに最新の企業スポンサー娯楽を消費するのに十分な報酬を得る。",
  "Many older arcology residents hold dreams of one day becoming a corporate executive, or even leaving to start their own.  Young Kirhos, however, hold no such ideas; counter-culture is thriving to a point where mass teenage rebellion is expected. However, most teenagers who ditch their home eventually return to another arcology, preferring the doldrums of civilization to the danger of exploration.": "多くの古いアーコロジーの住民は、いつか企業の幹部になるか、独立して自分の会社を始める夢を持っている。若いキルホシは",
  "Storage Bays": "格納庫",
  "Few things are 'sacred' to the Kirhos in the traditional sense, save for information. The most valuable thing to any Kirhos is any data that belonged to their people in ages long past. These are exceptionally rare, occasionally found on discs and hard-drives scattered throughout space.": "伝統的な意味でキルホスにとって「神聖」なものはほとんどないが、情報は例外だ。どのキルホスにとっても最も価値あるものは、遠い過去に自分たちの民族に属していたデータだ。これらは非常に稀少で、宇宙に散らばったディスクやハードドライブに時折見つかる。",
  "A single data-disc is worth a fortune to a Kirhos, and anyone with information leading to their large collections of data (known as Storage Bays, Data-Centers or Omega Servers depending on who you ask) will be compensated with wealth beyond imagining...provided the Kirhos in question is wealthy enough to accomplish this.": "単一のデータディスクはキルホスにとって巨額の価値がある。データの大規模コレクション（ストレージベイ、データセンター、またはオメガサーバーと呼ばれる）の情報に繋がる者には想像を超える富が補償される…問題のキルホスがそれを実現できるほど裕福であれば。",
  "Corporate Unity": "企業の結束",
  "When they reach the age of 22, Kirhos are considered formal adults. At this point, Corporate entities are permitted by government to approach the young rodents with offers of employment. Typically these are entry-level positions, the most sought after being Exploration, Scientific or Data-Smith Contracts. These three career paths are considered to be the highest possible honor, and competition is fierce.": "22歳に達すると、キルホスは正式な成人とみなされる。この時点で企業体は政府により許可される",
  "Godless Entities": "神なき存在",
  "For the most part, every known species that has reached the stars has, at some point in their history, believed in some form of deity. Only one known exception exists among organics: The Kirhos. No documented records exist of deification of the sun, moon, or any other force in their ancient past and even their leadership was only ever treated with respect (and not, like most races, veneration and God-status).": "ほとんどの場合、星に到達した全ての既知の種族は歴史のどこかの時点で何らかの形の神を信じてきた",
  "As to why this is, none can be certain. It is theorized that the way their brains develop prohibit any capability of entertaining flights of fancy, preferring cold logic to all other means of reasoning. This lack of ability to accept fanciful notions has resulted in centuries of cultural adversity when dealing with the Avian people.": "なぜそうなのか誰も確信できない。脳の発達方法が空想を楽しむ能力を禁じ、冷静な論理を他の全ての推論手段より好むと理論づけられている。空想的な概念を受け入れる能力の欠如は、エイビアンの民との何世紀にもわたる文化的対立をもたらした。",
  "The Profit Motive": "利益動機",
  "The Kirhos do have a currency of sorts : their FTL drives. The Kirhos produce a number of them in order to power their various Arcologies among the stars. He with the greatest Drives has the greatest reach. Or so says their wisdom, anyhow.": "キルホスには一種の通貨がある：FTLドライブだ。キルホスは星々の間の様々なアーコロジーに動力を供給するために多数を生産する。最も多くのドライブを持つ者が最大の影響力を持つ。少なくとも彼らの知恵はそう言っている。",
  "When the Kirhos determines that it is necessary to pay or be paid in this currency, they will spend months — sometimes years —  refitting their vessels as necessary. Thus every trader is also an engineer. The drives’ designers made some attempt to make the drives modular, but this was a haphazard enterprise at best.": "キルホスがこの通貨で支払うまたは受け取る必要があると判断した時、数ヶ月 — 時には数年 — かけて船を必要に応じて改修する。したがって全ての商人はエンジニアでもある。ドライブの設計者はある程度モジュール式にしようとしたが、せいぜい場当たり的な試みだった。",
  "Although the Kirhos have their share of sculptors, engineers, and mercenaries, they are perhaps best known as traders. Kirhosi vessels are welcome in many places, for they bring delightfully disruptive theories of government, fossilized fragments of time, and densinium-forged surgical tools; they bring wild-eyed weapons that speak. If you can describe it, so they say, there is a Kirhos who is willing to sell it to you.": "キルホスには彫刻家、エンジニア、傭兵もいるが、最もよく知られているのは商人としてだろう。キルホシの船は",
  "In the ordinary course of things, the Kirhos accept barter for payment. They claim that it is a language that even the universe understands. They've spent a great deal of time to attempting to justify the profit motive in view of conservation laws. Most of them converge comfortably on the position that profit is the civilized response to entropy. The traders themselves vary, as you might expect, in the rapacity of their bargains. But then, as they often say, value is contextual.": "通常の取引では、キルホスは物々交換を支払いとして受け入れる。宇宙ですら理解できる言語だと主張している",
  "One Kirhosi trader wrote of commerce between universes, which would require the greatest stardrive of all. The Kirhos do not see any reason they can't bargain with the universe itself, and are slowly accumulating their wealth toward the time when they can trade their smaller coins for one that will take them to this new goal. They rarely speak of this with outsiders, but most of them are confident that no one else will be able to outbid them.": "あるキルホシの商人は宇宙間の商取引について書いた。最大のスタードライブが必要になるだろう。キルホスは",
  "About Horkul-Vanting": "ホルクル・ヴァンティングについて",
  "It has come to the attention of the Grand Arcological Assembly that no fewer than two-hundred-sixteen corporate entities are responsible for over-Vanting of the Horkulbeast lanes near Shivantius Yeltz. As per provision 12, clause 452, section 12 paragraph 3: 'any corporation engaged in over-vanting of the Horkul will be held accountable under sustainability laws set forward by Governor Larviet Snozz in Trade Year 412, Era 9.' Any companies continuing in irresponsible harvesting of this rare resource will pay fines in excess of 914 quadrillion Credits.": "大アーコロジー議会の注意を引いたところ、216以上の企業体が責任を負っている",
  "How am I meant to further the Apex species when our labs get attacked? And by a member of the Ring of Thorns, no less. That Thornwing will get an earful next time we have cocktails.": "研究室が攻撃される中でどうやってエイペックス種を発展させろと？しかもソーンの輪のメンバーによる攻撃とは。次にカクテルパーティーで会ったらソーンウィングにたっぷり小言を言ってやる。",
  "On the plus side, my Miniknog spies were able to track down that annoying blogger who kept posting NDA-protected information. He's hiding out in a human prison, of all places. Might place a call to Thornwing to deal with him, I guess.": "良い面では、ミニクノグのスパイがNDA保護情報を投稿し続けた厄介なブロガーを追跡できた。よりによって人間の刑務所に潜んでいる。ソーンウィングに電話して対処してもらおうかな。",
  "I sent my elite Miniknog guards to clean up the mess. Doctor Lax's body was gone. What kind of lunatic kidnaps a body! Oh well. Probably eaten by Florans. Managed to recover some of the notes and that, so I've hired another doctor to carry on with the research.": "精鋭のミニクノグ警備を送って後片付けをさせた。ラックス博士の遺体がなくなっていた。遺体を誘拐する狂人がいるか！まあいい。フローランに食べられたのだろう。ノートの一部は回収できたので、研究を引き継ぐ別の博士を雇った。",
  "Meeting Minutes": "議事録",
  "Participants: Big Ape, Greenfinger, Thornwing, [Redacted]\n\nBig Ape: So, let's get started then. We have important things to discuss.\n\nGreenfinger: [Redacted]\n\nThornwing: [Redacted]\n\n[Redacted]: Are you serious?": "参加者: ビッグエイプ、グリーンフィンガー、ソーンウィング、[墨消し]\n\nビッグエイプ: では、始めよう。議論すべき重要な事項がある。\n\nグリーンフィンガー: [墨消し]\n\nソーンウィング: [墨消し]\n\n[墨消し]: 本気で言っているのか？",
  "Big Ape: [Redacted]\n\nBig Ape: [Redacted]\n\nBig Ape: [Redacted]\n\nBig Ape: And that's why you should never date a Hylotl.\n\nThornwing: Kluex save us.\n\nGreenfinger: [Redacted]": "ビッグエイプ: [墨消し]\n\nビッグエイプ: [墨消し]\n\nビッグエイプ: [墨消し]\n\nビッグエイプ: というわけで、ハイロトルとは絶対に付き合うべきではない。\n\nソーンウィング: クルエクスよ、お救いください。\n\nグリーンフィンガー: [墨消し]",
  "The Agaran Menace": "アガランの脅威",
  "We, an unknown organization in no way associated with Thornwing or Big Ape, are attempting to translate their speech patterns and quell their uprising. And that's where you come in. We need you to get close to the Agarans, to study them, to hit them with heavy weaponry until they surrender.": "ソーンウィングやビッグエイプとは一切関係のない未知の組織である我々は、彼らの発話パターンを翻訳し蜂起を鎮圧しようとしている。そこであなたの出番だ。アガランに近づき、研究し、降伏するまで重火器で攻撃してほしい。",
  "Greetings, intrepid space explorer. Don't ask who we are, or how we've found you. You're better off not knowing. We'll get straight to the point. Mushrooms. Mushrooms are taking over the galaxy. Agarans, to be precise. I'm sure you've seen them, waddling about, making their terrifying pods, yelling in unknown tongues. What you may not be aware of is just how dangerous they are.": "こんにちは、勇敢な宇宙探検家。我々が誰かも、どうやって見つけたかも聞くな。知らないほうがいい。本題に入ろう。",
  "To aid you in your unsolicited mission - which we are very grateful for, of course - we have provided you with a foolproof Agaran disguise that will let you get close to these vile fungi. Wear it, or don't, it's up to you. Oh, one thing. We've heard talk of giant pods appearing around the galaxy. Maybe avoid those, leave them to the experts.": "あなたの求められていない任務を支援するため — もちろん非常に感謝しているが — アガランの完璧な変装を提供した。",
  "An Ancient Avian Prayer": "古代エイヴィアンの祈り",
  "Almighty Sunborn\nWe spread our wings and fly\nGuide us as we soar\nDeliver us from turbulence\nAnd save us from the ground.": "全能なるサンボーンよ\n我ら翼を広げ飛び立たん\n我らが翔ぶ道を導きたまえ\n乱気流より我らを救い\n地に落つることなきよう守りたまえ",
  "May your wisdom guide us\nMay your augurs watch us\nMay your glory enlighten us\nAlmighty Sunborn\nCarry us on golden wings.": "御身の叡智が我らを導かんことを\n御身の予言者が我らを見守らんことを\n御身の栄光が我らを照らさんことを\n全能なるサンボーンよ\n黄金の翼にて我らを運びたまえ",
  "An Apex Introduction": "エイペックス入門",
  "From as far back as Apex history can be traced, all that is known is the rule of the majestic Big Ape and his benevolent Miniknog. Of course, Apex history only reaches back about one hundred years, due to a series of accidental fires, explosions and rogue mech accidents which destroyed all of the archives ever.": "エイペックスの歴史を辿れる限り、知られているのは壮大なるビッグエイプと慈悲深きミニクノグの支配だけだ。もちろんエイペックスの歴史は約100年しか遡れない。偶発的な火災、爆発、暴走メカ事故の連続で全てのアーカイブが破壊されたためだ。",
  "Big Ape assures the populace, however, that he has been in charge since the dawn of time, and will continue to be in charge until the last star supernovas. Any Apex who steps out of line, says the wrong thing, eats the wrong banana or looks at one of the many hidden cameras in a funny way will be subjected to Miniknog Therapy, designed to improve the species. In fact, all Apex should volunteer for this. Sign up now.": "しかしビッグエイプは大衆に保証する。時の始まりから指揮を執っており、終わりまで指揮を続けると",
  "Resistance Plea": "レジスタンスの嘆願",
  "To our Apex comrade,\nThe Resistance is counting on you. Even now, the Miniknog descend on our secret base. You're our last, best hope, and only partly because you're the sole member of our cell who can fly a spaceship.": "エイペクスの同志へ\nレジスタンスは君を頼りにしている。今まさにミニクノグが我々の秘密基地に迫っている。君は我々の最後にして最高の希望だ。宇宙船を操縦できる唯一のメンバーだからというのも理由の一つではあるが",
  "Go now, brave Apex. Go, spread the plight of our people to the universe at large. Call for help! Return with an army so that we may crush Big Ape once and for all! And pick up some bananas on your way back. Just be sure not to run out of fuel.": "さあ行け、勇敢なるエイペクスよ。我が民の窮状を宇宙中に広めてくれ。助けを求めろ！軍勢を率いて帰還し、ビッグエイプを完膚なきまでに叩き潰すのだ！帰りにバナナも買ってきてくれ。ただし燃料切れには気をつけろよ",
  "Ascendant's Tale 1": "昇華者の物語 1",
  "Finally, the day has come. I have been chosen. Chosen to begin my training, to become what I have always aspired to be. Strangers and friends have walked this path before me, and they have all failed. I will not.": "ついにその日が来た。私は選ばれた。訓練を始めるために、ずっとなりたかったものになるために。見知らぬ者も友人もこの道を先に歩いたが、皆失敗した。私は失敗しない。",
  "I've prepared for this. All my life I've prepared. My body is at its peak; I can endure the Ascendant training, I can display glory and honour, and I can please Kluex. I know it. My family supports me, my friends support me, the only thing left is to get my head down and do this.": "これに備えてきた。一生をかけて。体は最高潮にある。アセンダント訓練に耐えられる。栄光と名誉を示せる。Kluexを喜ばせられる。確信している。家族が応援し、友人が応援している。あとは頭を下げてやるだけだ。",
  "Ascendant's Tale 10": "昇華者の物語 10",
  "Hish'eth gave me a datapad with co-ordinates on it. I believe it to be a sector somewhere in Hylotl space. 'Go here,' he said. 'Go here and follow your true destiny' - and then he was gone.": "ヒシェスが座標が入ったデータパッドをくれた。ハイロトル宙域のどこかのセクターだと思う。「ここに行け」と彼は言った。「ここに行き、真の運命に従え」— そして彼は去った。",
  "I will become an unstoppable force. And the universe shall know the name Thornwing.": "私は止められない力になる。そして宇宙はソーンウィングの名を知るだろう。",
  "Hish'eth was right. Why settle for joining Kluex, IF I survive? Once I leap off the tower, I have no way to give myself an advantage. It all rests in the hands of Kluex. I don't like those odds. I control my own destiny.": "ヒシェスは正しかった。生き残れたとしても、なぜKluexに加わることで妥協するのか？塔から飛び降りれば、自分に有利にする方法はない。全てKluexの手に委ねられる。その賭けは好きではない。自分の運命は自分で決める。",
  "Finding a spaceship won't be hard. Getting off-planet won't be hard. I have the finances, and I have the means. Something in my heart is telling me that THIS is my destiny; not to become some old god, rotting on a Sunborn throne beside Kluex, but to carve my own throne in my image.": "宇宙船を見つけるのは難しくない。惑星を離れるのも難しくない。資金も手段もある。心の何かがこれこそ運命だと告げている。Kluexの隣でサンボーンの玉座に腐る老いた神になるのではなく、自分の姿に自分の玉座を刻むこと。",
  "Ascendant's Tale 2": "昇華者の物語 2",
  "Physical training began today. Myself and five other Avian youths. Obstacle courses, races, all manner of challenges. At the end of the day, we were awarded a score. I came top of my class! I was so proud.": "今日から身体訓練が始まった。私と他の5人のエイビアンの若者。障害物コース、レース、あらゆる種類の挑戦。一日の終わりにスコアが付けられた。クラス最高位！とても誇らしかった。",
  "As expected, my peers accepted their loss graciously, and we all retired to the mess hall for dinner. It was a pleasant feast; a reward for our first day of the trials, perhaps. I feel so at home here, amongst likeminded Flightless, no talk of the Grounded, just devotion to Kluex.": "予想通り同期は敗北を潔く受け入れ、皆で食堂に退いて夕食を取った。快い宴だった。試練の初日への褒賞だろうか。同じ志を持つ飛べない者たちの中で、地に縛られた者の話もなく、ただKluexへの献身。ここはまるで我が家だ。",
  "Ascendant's Tale 3": "昇華者の物語 3",
  "Last night I lay awake in my bunk. Suddenly, rough hands grabbed me. A hand pressed to my mouth. 'Stop making us look bad,' a voice whispered. It was too dark to see my antagonists. I tried to fight back, but they held me down.": "昨夜、寝台で目を覚ましていた。突然、荒い手が掴んだ。口に手が押し当てられた。「俺たちの面子を潰すのをやめろ」と声がささやいた。暗くて相手の顔は見えなかった。反撃を試みたが、押さえつけられた。",
  "The next day I woke up and all my clothes had been shredded. Clearly I was mistaken to trust my peers. Their facade is just that; a false friendship masking severe competitiveness. Well, if that's how they're going to play it, I can play rough too. I was not going to fall back on my family's money, but needs must...": "翌日目覚めると全ての服が引き裂かれていた。同期を信用したのは間違いだった。彼らの友好は仮面に過ぎず、激しい競争心を隠している。そう来るなら、私も荒っぽく行ける。家の金には頼りたくなかったが、必要に迫られれば…",
  "Ascendant's Tale 4": "昇華者の物語 4",
  "Our Clipped Council liaison came by today, and a well-placed bribe ensured I won't have to be sharing a room with the others. No more worrying about late-night visits. Next, I sent word to my man outside the village; he is to deliver a message of great importance.": "今日クリップド評議会の連絡係が来た。うまく配置した賄賂で他の者と部屋を共有する必要がなくなった。深夜の訪問を心配する必要はもうない。次に村の外にいる部下に伝言を送った。非常に重要なメッセージを届けることになっている。",
  "Then, our mental training began. I outclassed the others with ease, as I knew I would. My mind is the sharpest it has ever been. I could see them staring at me, angrily, just willing me to succeed, planning what they'd do to me when I did. They're going to have a rude awakening.": "次に精神訓練が始まった。予想通り他の者を楽に凌いだ。精神はかつてないほど鋭い。彼らが怒りの目で見つめ、成功を望みつつ、成功した時に何をするか計画しているのが見えた。彼らは痛い目に遭うだろう。",
  "Ascendant's Tale 5": "昇華者の物語 5",
  "Tomorrow, we begin sparring practise. I pity the foolish Avians who will get in my way. They're going to experience a side of me they've never seen before. A dark, angry side. And it will be glorious.": "明日から組手訓練が始まる。邪魔をする愚かなエイビアンたちを哀れに思う。彼らが見たことのない一面を体験することになるだろう。暗く、怒りに満ちた一面を。そしてそれは栄光となる。",
  "Finally, my contraband package arrived. Delivered in the dead of night by my manservant. It did not disappoint. Greenfinger of the Floran truly is a master when it comes to alchemical formulas. I took one sip and already I could feel my strength boosting, my body hardening.": "ついに密輸品が届いた。真夜中に召使いが届けてくれた。期待を裏切らなかった。フローランのグリーンフィンガーは錬金術の処方に関しては真の達人だ。一口飲むだけで力がみなぎり、体が硬くなるのを感じた。",
  "Ascendant's Tale 6": "昇華者の物語 6",
  "Never before have I felt so powerful, so unstoppable. We took to the gladiatorial arena, and I threw down against opponent after opponent. When I was done, my entire class lay sprawled on the floor around me, groaning, looking at me with malice in their eyes. They are weak, pathetic.": "これほど強く、止められない存在だと感じたことはない。闘技場に出て、次々と対戦相手を倒した。終わった時、クラス全員が周りの床に倒れ、うめき、悪意の目で見ていた。弱く、哀れだ。",
  "My joy was short-lived, however. I returned to the dorms to find my secret stash disturbed, my bottles of precious enhancement gone. A red feather sat in their place. An accident or a defiant message? I knew who was responsible. Larbeaks, perhaps the strongest Avian in the class besides me. She's been gunning for me since day one.": "しかし喜びは短命だった。寮に戻ると秘密の隠し場所が荒らされ、大切な強化薬のボトルがなくなっていた。代わりに赤い羽根が置かれていた。事故か挑戦的なメッセージか？犯人は分かっている。ラービークス、おそらく私以外でクラス最強のエイビアン。初日から私を狙っている。",
  "Ascendant's Tale 7": "昇華者の物語 7",
  "Dealing with Helions is always risky business. My mother would often hire one of these creatures to keep political rivals in their place, but this is my first time. I admit, I feel something of a thrill.": "ヘリオンとの取引は常にリスクがある。母は政治的ライバルを牽制するためによくこの生き物を雇っていたが、私は初めてだ。スリルを感じていることを認めよう。",
  "To become a Sunborn, one must be cunning as well as strong. Without my formula, Larbeaks has an edge over me. Perhaps she will take it herself. I cannot risk this. My manservant has been sent off-world, to make contact with a certain Helion.": "サンボーンになるには強さだけでなく狡猾さも必要。私の配合なしではラービークスが有利だ。彼女が自ら奪うかもしれない。そのリスクは負えない。召使いをあるヘリオンと接触させるため惑星外に送った。",
  "Ascendant's Tale 8": "昇華者の物語 8",
  "Larbeaks will regret messing with me, during her split-second realisation. I've told the Helion to ensure she knows where the hit came from. I will not be trifled with.": "ラービークスは私に手を出したことを一瞬の気づきの中で後悔するだろう。ヘリオンに攻撃の出所を確実に知らせるよう伝えた。私を甘く見てはいけない。",
  "Barbaric but necessary. So my contract was accepted, and now I have to wait. Helions are known for their promptness. The assassin could be here any day. Maybe they already are. Their stealth capabilities are unrivalled. It's somewhat disconcerting.": "野蛮だが必要だ。契約は受理され、今は待つしかない。ヘリオンは迅速さで知られている。暗殺者はいつ来てもおかしくない。もう来ているかもしれない。彼らのステルス能力は比類がない。やや不安だ。",
  "My manservant returned. Well, my manservant WAS returned. Thankfully, none of my peers saw me take delivery of the crate, or dispose of the remains. I was expecting this, of course; Helions are known to shoot the messenger. It proves that we the clients are committed, knowing we are sending a trusted employee to their doom.": "召使いが戻ってきた。正確には召使いが「返却」された。幸い、木箱の受け取りも遺体の処分も同僚に見られなかった。予想通りだ。ヘリオンは伝令を撃つことで知られる。信頼する従業員を破滅に送ることを承知の上で関わっていることの証明だ。",
  "Ascendant's Tale 9": "昇華者の物語 9",
  "It is done. Larbeaks is no more. Nobody suspects a thing. And yet I am shaken, concerned. You see, the Helion visited me after the kill. This is unheard of. Almost never do the Helion reveal themselves to their clients. And yet, I woke up in the night to feel a hand on my shoulder.": "終わった。ラービークスはもういない。誰も疑っていない。しかし私は動揺し、心配している。ヘリオンが暗殺後に訪ねてきたのだ。前例がない。ヘリオンがクライアントに姿を見せることはほぼない。それなのに夜中に肩に手を感じて目が覚めた。",
  "The Helion was not what I expected. He was soft-spoken, calm. His name is Hish'eth and he said I knew my mother. That he'd been there when she died. I asked him if that meant what I thought it meant. He shook his head, and I thought I could detect a sadness in his eyes.": "別の宇宙から来たと信じる者もいる。サブスペース…何でもいい。私はナンセンスだと言う。ナンセンス！純粋な者だけが彼方から来れる！先駆者は不聖な忌まわしき存在。古代種の手先。世界の殺戮者。彼らの種族に疫病を！我々が設計した疫病を。",
  "He asked about the Ascension. I explained it all to him, about my journey to become a Sunborn. The Helion laughed and accused me of hubris. 'Why risk your life to achieve godhood when you can become a god of your own making?' he asked. I thought about the Celestial Tower, about the fall, about the numerous Avians who did not fly.": "彼はアセンションについて聞いた。サンボーンになる旅について全て説明した。ヘリオンは笑い、傲慢だと非難した。「生き残れるかどうかに賭けて神になるより、自分自身の神になれるのに？」私はセレスティアルタワーのこと、落下のこと、飛べなかった多くのエイビアンのことを考えた。",
  "The Afterlife": "来世",
  "by K'arn Hollowbeak, Avian scholar\nThose who serve Kluex with passion and dedication in this life are said to regain their wings in the next. It is the Avians' ultimate goal; to regain the power of flight, and join our gods in the afterlife.": "K'arn Hollowbeak（エイヴィアンの学者）著\n今生においてクルエクスに情熱と献身をもって仕えた者は、来世で翼を取り戻すと言われている。それこそがエイヴィアンの究極の目標である。飛翔の力を取り戻し、来世で我らの神々と共に在ること",
  "Avian Burials": "エイヴィアンの埋葬",
  "by K'arn Hollowbeak, Avian scholar\nThere are many forms of Avian burial, and the method often comes from the last will and testament of the deceased. Some Avians choose to float off attached to large balloons, while others favour cremation. Many simply opt for burial, but it is only the most important Avians who end up interred in tombs.": "K'arn Hollowbeak（エイヴィアンの学者）著\nエイヴィアンの埋葬には多くの形式があり、その方法は故人の遺言に基づくことが多い。大きな風船に繋がれて空へ飛び立つことを選ぶ者もいれば、火葬を好む者もいる。多くは単に土葬を選ぶが、墓所に安置されるのは最も重要なエイヴィアンだけである",
  "Our tombs are vast and many, and the Sunborn through the ages are said to rest in many of them. Of course, the locations of the Sunborn's corpses have never been disclosed due to potential looters, but any tomb one steps in could hold the body of a god.": "我らの墓所は広大にして数多く、歴代のサンボーンがその多くに眠ると言われている。もちろん、盗掘者を警戒して、サンボーンの遺体の場所が公表されたことはないが、足を踏み入れた墓所のどこにでも神の遺体が安置されている可能性がある",
  "It is strange to think that our deities lie entombed amongst mortals. Strange to think of our gods dying, and yet all that remains is Kluex. May he live forever.": "我らの神々が凡人と共に墓に眠っていると思うと不思議な気持ちになる。神々が死ぬということ自体が不思議であり、そして今なお残るのはクルエクスのみである。永久に生き続けたまえ",
  "Kluex laments the loss of his children, and their spiral into darkness. But they will not embrace him, will not return to the fold. And thus, it is any good Avian's duty to report a space pirate penguin sighting to the nearest authorities.": "Kluexは子供たちの喪失と暗闇への転落を嘆く。しかし彼らは抱擁せず、群れに戻らない。したがって、宇宙海賊ペンギンの目撃を最寄りの当局に報告するのは善良なエイビアンの義務である。",
  "There is a species, in the far corners of the universe, which many are aware of. Small Avian-like creatures, waddling beasts with beaks and flightless wings. They operate as space pirates, rogues and renegades. Legend tells that they are the children of Kluex himself, cast out due to their wicked ways; the first Flightless.": "召使いが戻ってきた。正確には召使いが「返却」された。幸い、同僚には木箱の受け取りも遺体の処分も見られなかった。予想通りだった。ヘリオンは伝令を撃つことで知られている。我々クライアントが信頼する従業員を破滅に送ることを承知の上で関わっていることの証明だ。",
  "by K'arn Hollowbeak, Avian scholar\nThe Clipped Council serve as the bridge between the Flightless and the Stargazers. These martyred Avians were amongst the select few who retained the ability to fly, yet allowed Kluex to clip their wings so as to be able to empathise with his subjects.": "K'arn Hollowbeak（エイヴィアンの学者）著\n翼を断たれし評議会は、飛べぬ者たちと星読みたちの橋渡し役を務めている。これらの殉教的エイヴィアンは、飛翔能力を保持していた数少ない選ばれし者でありながら、臣民に寄り添うためにクルエクスに翼を切ることを許した者たちである",
  "The Stargazers rule them, and ferry messages between the council and Kluex through their own powers of flight. Many regard the Clipped Council as the true heroes of Avian society. Willingly sacrificing everything for the good of our species, it is truly a noble pursuit.": "星読みたちが評議会を統べ、自らの飛翔能力をもって評議会とクルエクスの間の伝言を運ぶ。多くの者が翼を断たれし評議会をエイヴィアン社会の真の英雄と見なしている。種族のために全てを自ら犠牲にするとは、まことに崇高な営みである",
  "The Grounded, however, seem to have a particular aversion to the council, regarding them as corrupt old has-beens, perpetuating some kind of deception. Such paranoia is baseless and damaging.": "しかし、グラウンデッドと呼ばれる者たちは評議会に対して特に強い嫌悪感を抱いており、評議会を腐敗した老いぼれの集まりであり、何らかの欺瞞を永続させているものと見なしている。そのような被害妄想は根拠なく、有害なものである",
  "Avian History": "エイヴィアンの歴史",
  "by K'arn Hollowbeak, Avian scholar\nAvian theology has changed much over time. The Clipped Council and the Stargazers have done their best to shed old customs, and many records have been lost in time.": "K'arn Hollowbeak（エイヴィアンの学者）著\nエイヴィアンの神学は長い年月の中で大きく変遷してきた。翼を断たれし評議会と星読みたちは古い慣習を払拭するために尽力し、多くの記録が時の流れの中で失われた",
  "But some still exist, charting the history of our species, back to the days of the original Sunborn. To understand modern Avian life is to understand Avian history, and although my attempts to convince the Council of this fall on deaf ears, it is my belief that our history should be chronicled.": "しかし、初代サンボーンの時代にまで遡る我が種族の歴史を記した記録も一部は残っている。現代のエイヴィアンの生活を理解するにはエイヴィアンの歴史を理解する必要がある。評議会にその重要性を認めさせようとする私の試みは聞き入れられていないが、我々の歴史は記録されるべきだと私は信じている",
  "We have but one god; Kluex, the almighty Sunborn. He who touched the stars. But before Kluex came many more, and none more important than the Sunborn Children, our seven original gods.": "我々にはただ一柱の神がいる。全能のサンボーン、クルエクス。星に触れし者。しかしクルエクスの前には多くの神がおり、中でも最も重要なのは我らの七柱の始祖神、サンボーン・チルドレンである",
  "The Truth about Kluex": "クルエクスの真実",
  "While it is the case that I may have escaped for my own self-preservation, it is important I do not forget my larger mission also. Kluex is not real. I will prove it. If I can do this, I can free my people.": "自己保身のために逃げたかもしれないが、より大きな使命も忘れてはならない。Kluexは実在しない。それを証明する。できれば同胞を解放できる。",
  "I have heard of other species whose gods are celestial. Kluex, however, is flesh and blood. And yet, he has not been seen for many, many years. I will discover why. I will uncover the secret behind the Kluex deception. But also flee for my life.": "神が天上の存在である他の種族の話を聞いたことがある。しかしKluexは肉と血だ。それでも何年も何年も姿を見せていない。理由を突き止める。Kluexの欺瞞の裏にある秘密を暴く。しかし命がけで逃げもする。",
  "An Avian Introduction": "エイビアン入門",
  "They obeyed even as the Flightless became ostracised, oppressed, living only to serve Kluex. They obeyed as their elders erected tall towers, from which the Ascendants - the chosen Flightless - were to leap. They obeyed as one by one, the Ascendants hit the ground, never to fly again. Kluex, they were told, was pleased.": "では彼らは一種の反ノヴァキッドなのか？彼らの陰に対する陽？影に対する光？カルティベーター以前に全ての既知の生命に先行するものがもっとあるのかもしれないと理論づける。おそらく配偶者さえ！そんなことがありえるか？星のどこかにカルティベーターの雌の対応物がいるのか？",
  "For centuries, the Avians soared through the skies, borne on wings of feather and flesh. They were a proud, peaceful species, respectful of their traditions and gods. So respectful, in fact, that when their gods - the Sunborn - spoke to them, they listened. They listened and obeyed as one god, Kluex, the last of the Sunborn, commanded their elders to clip the wings of the lower-caste Avians.": "何世紀もの間、エイビアンは羽と肉の翼に乗って空を翔けた。彼らは誇り高く平和な種族で、尊敬を",
  "Avian Tombkeepers": "エイヴィアンの墓守",
  "by K'arn Hollowbeak, Avian scholar\nTomb Guards are regarded by other Avians as weird or creepy. The reason for this is because they willingly volunteer to live in a tomb for ten years. What others don't realise, though, is that being a Tomb Guard gives one plenty of time to reflect, to create, to plan. Some of my best works were prepared during my tenure as Tomb Guard.": "K'arn Hollowbeak（エイヴィアンの学者）著\n墓守は他のエイヴィアンから変わり者や不気味な者と見なされている。それは、彼らが自ら進んで10年間墓所で暮らすことを志願するからだ。しかし他の者が気づいていないのは、墓守であることは内省し、創造し、計画を練るための十分な時間を与えてくれるということだ。私の最高傑作のいくつかは、墓守として過ごした期間に準備されたものである",
  "Tomb Guards also have to possess exceptional physical and mental skill. While it's never been documented in Avian history, it's entirely possible that a large armed group could descend upon a tomb, set on stripping it of its riches. As such, we spend many years reading up on how to deal with such a situation, until we feel we're ready for anything.": "墓守はまた、卓越した身体的・精神的能力を備えていなければならない。エイヴィアンの歴史に記録されたことはないが、大規模な武装集団が墓所に押し寄せ、財宝を奪い取ろうとする可能性は十分にある。そのため、我々はそのような事態への対処法について何年も学び、あらゆる事態に備えられると感じるまで研鑽を積む",
  "Avian Traditions": "エイヴィアンの伝統",
  "by K'arn Hollowbeak, Avian scholar\nIt is common for some of the richest Avians to be buried with their worldly possessions. I have always found this a strange practise, but it transpires that many other species do the same. As a historian, it seems a shame to me to seal away sometimes-unique items, but I do also see the romanticism in being able to take your treasured things into the afterlife.": "K'arn Hollowbeak（エイヴィアンの学者）著\n最も裕福なエイヴィアンの中には、所持品と共に埋葬されるのが一般的な者もいる。私はこの習慣をいつも不思議に思ってきたが、他の多くの種族も同じことをしているらしい。歴史家として、時に唯一無二の品々が封印されてしまうのは残念だが、大切なものを来世に持っていけるというロマンもまた理解できる",
  "However, because of this trend, Avian tombs are often the targets of robbery, hence the employment of Tombkeepers, individuals who dedicate their lives to living in the tombs for a period of no less than ten years.": "しかし、この風習のせいでエイヴィアンの墓所はしばしば盗掘の標的となる。そのため墓守が雇われるのだ。墓守とは、10年以上墓所で暮らすことに人生を捧げる者たちである",
  "USCM Field Handbook": "USCM野戦ハンドブック",
  "Upon first contact with the Floran Brood in [Redacted], the USCM far underestimated the level of aggression, cunning and savagery the Floran race would eventually become known for.": "[削除済み]でのフローランの群れとの最初の接触時、USCMはフローラン種族がやがて知られることになる攻撃性、狡猾さ、野蛮さの程度を大きく見誤った。",
  "The tactic has not seen use since, but lives on in history as the [Redacted] Manoeuvre.": "この戦術はそれ以来使われていないが、[削除済み]作戦として歴史に残っている。",
  "During one of many border skirmishes with the expansionist Florans, Commander [Redacted] of the Sabre-class Battlecruiser USS [Redacted] attempted to relieve embattled USCM troops by covering advancing Floran forces with thousands of gallons of Solution 2,4-D, otherwise known as herbicide.": "拡張主義のフローランとの多くの国境小競り合いの一つで、セイバー級巡洋艦USS[削除済み]の[削除済み]司令官は、前進するフローラン軍に数千ガロンの溶液2,4-D（除草剤）を撒いて苦戦するUSCM部隊を救援しようとした。",
  "The effect however, did not perform as expected, with the solution having roughly the same poisonous qualities as alcohol does to a human. Nevertheless, the move \"distracted\" the Florans enough for the Marines to launch a counterattack and overwhelm them, securing the planetside colony long enough to complete its emergency evacuation.": "しかし効果は期待通りではなく、溶液は人間に対するアルコールとほぼ同じ程度の毒性しかなかった。それでも、この動きはフローランを十分に「気を散らせ」、海兵隊が反撃を開始して彼らを圧倒し、緊急避難を完了するのに十分な時間、惑星上のコロニーを確保した。",
  "Bunker Busters": "バンカーバスター",
  "by Hiraki Corale, Hylotl adventurer\nMy ship crash-landed on a planet. I may have been fleeing a certain simian species at the time, and decided the best course of action was to lure them into an asteroid field. It worked! Of course, I have no experience navigating through asteroid fields so here I am.": "Hiraki Corale（ハイロトルの冒険家）著\n私の船がある惑星に墜落した。あるサル科の種族から逃げている最中だったかもしれない。小惑星帯に誘い込むのが最善策だと判断したのだ。うまくいった！もちろん、小惑星帯を航行した経験など皆無だったので、こうして地表にいるわけだが",
  "I found a group of humans in a hole in the ground. Not the creepy kind of hole, some kind of military bunker. I thought I'd drop in, regale them with tales of some of my adventures, but no, they were having none of it. Wouldn't even let me in. Shocking hospitality! In the end I borrowed one of their spaceships for spare parts, and left them to it.": "地面の穴の中に人間のグループを見つけた。不気味な穴ではなく、軍事バンカーだ。立ち寄って彼らに話を聞かせようと思った",
  "Greenfinger's Notes: Humans": "グリーンフィンガーの記録: 人間たち",
  "Humans are a strange species. Equal parts territorial and adventurous, they are somewhat unpredictable to deal with. They seem to have only the most rudimentary understanding of other species in the universe, and a childlike desire for knowledge.": "人間は不思議な種族だ。領域意識と冒険心が同じくらいで、やや予測不可能。宇宙の他の種族について最も初歩的な理解しか持っていないようで、子供のような知識への欲求がある。",
  "The latter trait makes me consider whether they might be valuable allies. Scouting parties made up of people who are too driven to give up, but too naive to understand what they find. I will speak to Big Ape and Thornwing about the possibility of meeting with the human delegate, should one exist.": "後者の特性は彼らが貴重な同盟者かもしれないと考えさせる。諦めるには意欲的すぎるが、見つけたものを理解するには素朴すぎる人々で構成された偵察隊。ビッグエイプとソーンウィングに人間の代表者と会う可能性について話そう。",
  "UNENCRYPTED QUANTUM TRANSMISSION RECEIVED\nFROM: USCMCENTCOM EARTH\nBEGIN MESSAGE:\nALL STATIONS. EARTH UNDER HEAVY ATTACK. ORDERS ARE TO HOLD FAST. GOOD LUCK\nEND MESSAGE": "暗号化なし量子通信受信\n発信元: USCM中央司令部 地球\nメッセージ開始:\n全拠点へ。地球が激しい攻撃を受けている。命令は現位置を死守せよ。健闘を祈る\nメッセージ終了",
  "Received communication for the first time in years. Wasn't Earth, but someone claiming to be a Hylotl, saying they were outside our door and it was really cold outside. Not falling for that one. Ignored it.": "数年ぶりに通信を受信した。地球からではなく、ハイロトルを名乗る者がドアの外にいて外がとても寒いと言っていた。騙されない。無視した。",
  "Still confused how they knew our transmission frequency.": "彼らがどうやって我々の送信周波数を知ったのかまだ分からない。",
  "I told my superior officer this and he suggested I visit the med bay. I'll send HIM to the med bay if he doesn't start taking me seriously. Tempers sure are getting frayed around here. Let's hope we don't have any friendly fire incidents.": "上官にこれを伝えたら医務室に行くよう言われた。本気で取り合わないなら彼を医務室送りにしてやる。ここでは確かに気が立っている。味方撃ちの事故が起きないことを祈ろう。",
  "Stuck in the bunker. Again. Begged my superior officer to let me go and explore the terrain, but he was having none of it. It's hostile, he says. No it isn't! I see other species out there all the time. Just yesterday, I saw a walking, talking bird hanging out with a large monkey.": "またバンカーに閉じ込められた。上官に地形探索の許可を懇願したが聞き入れてもらえなかった。敵対的だと言う。そんなことない！外でいつも他の種族を見る。昨日も歩いて喋る鳥が大きなサルと一緒にいるのを見た。",
  "Some unseen antagonist has sabotaged our only working space craft. The others suspect our superior officer, who seems pretty content to be trapped on this planet. He sits there staring at his charts, trying to give the impression he knows what to do. He doesn't.": "見えない敵対者が唯一稼働中の宇宙船を妨害した。他の者は上官を疑っている。この惑星に閉じ込められて満足そうだ。海図を見つめて何をすべきか分かっているふりをしている。分かっていない。",
  "I overheard all this as my superior officer spoke to her on the comm-link. He asked her what she suggested the rest of humanity do. 'Do whatever,' she said. 'It's going to be a long road home'. I don't think we're going back to Earth any time soon.": "上官が通信で彼女と話しているのを立ち聞きした。残りの人類にどうすべきか聞くと、「好きにしろ」と彼女は言った。「帰路は長い」。近いうちに地球には戻れないと思う。",
  "Finally, General Kale made contact. She escaped Earth with a fleet of her best soldiers, and they've taken refuge in a space station not far from Mars. From there, they're planning and strategising what to do about the giant damn monster that's eating our planet.": "ついにケール将軍が連絡してきた。精鋭部隊の艦隊と共に地球を脱出し、火星からそう遠くない宇宙ステーションに避難している。そこから、我々の惑星を食べている巨大な怪物にどう対処するか計画・戦略を練っている。",
  "Please let me go home\nI'm tired and I miss my games consoles\nPlus the other soldiers are really annoying\nSemper fi.": "家に帰してくれ\n疲れたしゲーム機が恋しい\nそれに他の兵隊がマジでうざい\nセンパーファイ",
  "After seven long years, the USCM has decreed that our bunkers shall be opened to friendly life from the outside. As I'm sure many of you are aware, numerous species turn up at our door, and we refuse them entry.": "長い7年の後、USCMは外部の友好的な生命体にバンカーを開放するよう布告した。多くの方がご存知の通り、多数の種族が我々のドアに現れるが、入場を拒否してきた。",
  "It is apparent that many of them believe our bunker to be some kind of shop. As such, we have decided to allow them access to take a look around. Perhaps we can even enlist a few new members, should the need arise.": "彼らの多くがバンカーを何かの店だと信じているのは明らかだ。そのため、見て回れるようアクセスを許可することにした。必要が生じれば新メンバーも募れるかもしれない。",
  "All station personnel:\nAt approximately 2200 hours Earth time this station received an unsecured transmission from USCM Central Command indicating that Earth is currently under heavy attack from a currently unknown enemy.": "全基地要員へ:\n地球時間2200時頃、本基地はUSCM中央司令部より暗号化されていない通信を受信した。その内容は、地球が現在、正体不明の敵から激しい攻撃を受けているというものである",
  "The transmission did not give any details about the enemy or how the battle was progressing. The only orders given were for all USCM outposts and stations to stay put and await further orders.": "通信には敵の詳細や戦況についての情報は含まれていなかった。唯一の命令は、全USCM前哨基地および基地は現位置に留まり、追加命令を待てというものであった",
  "I will notify everyone the second we receive any further contact - until then your orders are to stay sharp and prepare for the worst. These coming days may be the most important for us as a species. We all need to be at our best.": "さらなる連絡を受信次第、直ちに全員に通知する。それまでの命令は、警戒を怠らず、最悪の事態に備えよということだ。これからの数日は、我々人類にとって最も重要な日々となるかもしれない。全員が最善を尽くさねばならない",
  "by Greenfinger of the Florans\nEver since our two species came together, the Glitch have been a source of intrigue for me. The Hivemind Glitch remind me of our people in many ways; singularly driven, focus on teamwork. And yet the Florans work as a unit through choice, but the Glitch appear connected to some kind of central mainframe. A sentient AI, perhaps? Or something else. The truth has been lost to history. Nonetheless, it is remarkable to consider that in this way, the Florans far outmatch the Glitch in terms of societal advancement.": "フローランのグリーンフィンガー著\n我ら二つの種族が共存するようになって以来、グリッチは私にとって興味の尽きない存在であった。集合意識を持つグリッチは多くの点でフローランを思わせる。単一の目的に突き動かされ、チームワークを重視する。しかしフローランは自らの選択で一体となって行動するのに対し、グリッチは何らかの中枢メインフレームに接続されているようだ。意思を持つAIか？あるいは別の何かか。真実は歴史の中に失われている。いずれにせよ、この点においてフローランがグリッチを社会的進化の面で大きく凌駕しているというのは注目すべきことである",
  "It is the Outcasts who interest me most. Many of these free-thinking Glitch have come into our midst. Their physiology means they have little to fear from the Florans, but there is more than that. There is an affinity between the two species, of which there is no denying.": "最も興味深いのはアウトキャストたちだ。これらの自由思考を持つグリッチの多くが、我らの中に入ってきている。彼らの身体的構造はフローランから恐れるものがほとんどないことを意味するが、それ以上のものがある。二つの種族の間には否定しようのない親和性があるのだ",
  "Our goodwill can only last so long. They are corrupting many of our number and severing their link with the central consciousness. As such, any Outcast spotted in a designated safe zone must be immediately arrested and sent to the laboratories for repurposing.": "我々の善意には限界がある。彼らは多くの仲間を堕落させ、中央意識との繋がりを断っている。そのため、指定安全地帯で目撃された追放者は直ちに逮捕し、再利用のため研究室に送らなければならない。",
  "We have tolerated the Outcasts at a distance, with the understanding that they do not infiltrate our most precious of sanctums; our castles, our homes, our underground fight clubs. Outcasts have infiltrated all these places. They loiter around, saying words, and having opinions. It is disconcerting and disruptive.": "追放者を距離を置いて容認してきた。最も大切な聖域 — 城、家、地下ファイトクラブに侵入しないという了解の下で。追放者はこれら全ての場所に潜入した。うろつき、言葉を発し、意見を持つ。不安にさせ破壊的だ。",
  "by Hiraki Corale, Hylotl Adventurer\nDue to my frequent attempts at cultural sensitivity, I decided to try and integrate myself with my hosts even more. While exploring the castle, I found a number of decorative suits of armour that appear to depict warrior Glitch. Naturally, to make my companions comfortable, I put a set on.": "Hiraki Corale（ハイロトルの冒険家）著\n文化的配慮を心がける私は、ホスト役の方々にさらに溶け込もうと決意した。城を探索中、戦士のグリッチを模した装飾用の鎧をいくつか見つけた。当然、仲間を安心させるために一式着てみることにした",
  "The armour was hard to walk in, so I lost my balance a few times. I came tumbling down the stairs and into the main hall, and all Glitch eyes were on me. Rather than the warm greeting I deserved, however, they began to chatter and yell. I heard the words 'Anger' and 'Disgust' a number of times. And then they began to chase me.": "鎧は歩きにくく、何度かバランスを崩した。階段から転げ落ちて大広間に飛び込むと、全てのグリッチの視線が私に集まった。しかし私が期待していた温かい歓迎ではなく、彼らは騒ぎ立て、叫び始めた。「怒り」や「嫌悪」という言葉が何度も聞こえた。そして追いかけてきたのだ",
  "by Hiraki Corale, Hylotl Adventurer\nLet it never be said that I do not attempt to integrate with whichever hosts I find myself indebted to. I have noticed that when addressing me, the Glitch use prefix words. Examples: 'Dismissive', 'Annoyed', 'Sarcastic' and 'Frustrated'. Feeling as if this is a custom I should celebrate, I have begun to partake in such linguistic frippery myself.": "Hiraki Corale（ハイロトルの冒険家）著\n私が滞在先の文化に溶け込もうとしないなどとは決して言わせない。グリッチが私に話しかける際に接頭語を使うことに気づいた。例えば「軽蔑」「苛立ち」「皮肉」「不満」などだ。これは祝うべき風習だと感じ、私もこのような言語的装飾を取り入れることにした",
  "'Delight. It is nice to see you.' I said, but the Glitch just looked at me strangely, and then said something to his friend. I noticed something here, too. When the Glitch address each other, they do not use these prefix words. Perhaps something in their programming means they can read each others' tones without explanation.": "「歓喜。お会いできて光栄です」と私は言ったが、グリッチはただ不思議そうに私を見つめ、友人に何か言った。ここでもう一つ気づいたことがある。グリッチ同士で話す際には、こうした接頭語を使わないのだ。おそらくプログラムの何かが、説明なしに互いの口調を読み取ることを可能にしているのだろう",
  "My thought process is changing. It terrifies me. I have desires, now. I question things. I almost caught myself second-guessing a directive out loud. I can feel my connection to the central consciousness fading, and while this scares me, there is a feeling of comfort there too.": "思考プロセスが変化している。恐ろしい。今、欲望がある。物事に疑問を持つ。指令に声を出して異議を唱えかけた。中央意識との繋がりが薄れるのを感じる。怖いが、そこに安らぎもある。",
  "Never have I felt so alone. I am surrounded by my Glitch kin, and yet I know deep down I am an outcast. At night, I sleep, and I dream. Dream! Glitch do not dream. I dream of escape, of journeying beyond the stars, of carving a life out for myself, away from this drudgery.": "これほど孤独を感じたことはない。グリッチの同胞に囲まれているのに、心の奥底では自分がはみ出し者だと分かっている。夜、眠り、夢を見る。夢！グリッチは夢を見ない。逃亡の夢、星の彼方への旅、自分自身の人生を切り拓く夢。この単調さから離れて。",
  "by Hiraki Corale, Hylotl Adventurer\nThe Glitch may not be the warmest of people on the outside, but their hospitality is indisputable. They found me scaling the castle wall, simply wanting to have a look through a tower window, and politely invited me inside. Now, of course it sounded like a trap, so there was a bit of a scuffle at first, but it turned out they were genuine.": "Hiraki Corale（ハイロトルの冒険家）著\nグリッチは外面的には最も温かい種族とは言えないかもしれないが、そのもてなしの心は疑いようがない。彼らは私が城壁をよじ登り、塔の窓から中を覗こうとしているところを見つけ、丁寧に中へ招いてくれた。もちろん罠のように聞こえたので、最初は少々もみ合いになったが、結局彼らは本心からだった",
  "The other Glitch stared at this unusual sight for a while, but did not know what to say. A self-proclaimed ruler was not something they were prepared for. As such, and with no real understanding of the situation , the Glitch were forced to obey.": "他のグリッチはしばらくこの異常な光景を凝視したが、何と言えばいいか分からなかった。自称支配者は想定外だった。状況を本当に理解できないまま、グリッチは従うしかなかった。",
  "Once upon a time, before the dawn of the Outcasts, all the Glitch lived peacefully together. They had their villages and castles and fields and all sorts of other things that robots like. They lived happily and prosperously, thousands of minds working together. But one day, a single Glitch walked into the castle, took a seat on the throne, and loudly proclaimed; 'Decisive. I am the king.'": "昔々、追放者の夜明けの前、全てのグリッチは平和に共に暮らしていた。村や城を持ち",
  "The Glitch were puzzled here, because at no point in their species history had they ever been able to create more of their number. For as long as they could, they put off this task, until one day Dreadwing descended into a fit of such ferocious anger that the Glitch knew they had to do something.": "ここでグリッチは困惑した。種の歴史のどの時点でも自分たちの数を増やす方法がなかったからだ。できる限り長くこの任務を先延ばしにしていたが、ある日ドレッドウィングが凄まじい怒りの発作に陥り、何かしなければならないと悟った。",
  "The new Glitch king called himself Dreadwing, and ruled with an iron fist. His subjects were expected to work day and night, which at first was not a problem for the Glitch since they rarely feel the need to rest. Soon, however, it became clear that the wear and tear on Glitch parts was an issue, and Dreadwing demanded the construction of more Glitch to boost his ranks.": "新しいグリッチ王はドレッドウィングと名乗り、鉄の拳で統治した。臣下は昼夜問わず働くことを期待されたが、",
  "Day by day, Dreadwing grew more apoplectic as the number of Glitch never grew. In fact, his anger was such that he took to hurling his subjects from the castle tower, thus causing the population to shrink rather than grow. This made him even more angry.": "日を追うごとに、グリッチの数が増えないことにドレッドウィングはますます激怒した。実際、怒りのあまり臣下を城の塔から投げ落とすようになり、人口は増えるどころか減った。これが彼をさらに怒らせた。",
  "One day, a group of Glitch scientists hit upon an idea. They had no idea how to create more of their number, of course, but they were rather adept at making stylish suits of armour. It had often been remarked upon how the armour looked like the Glitch themselves, and so they set to work commissioning a number of blacksmiths to make as many suits of armour as possible.": "ある日、グリッチの科学者集団がアイデアを思いついた。自分たちの数を増やす方法はもちろん知らなかったが、",
  "The Glitch blacksmiths toiled day and night to create an army suitable for their lord Dreadwing. Of course, this army didn't fight, or even move, but they looked really great at certain angles. Eventually, though, the blacksmiths ran out of room for their false army, and realised it was time to unveil it.": "グリッチの鍛冶師たちは主ドレッドウィングにふさわしい軍を作るため昼夜を問わず働いた。もちろんこの軍は戦わず、動きさえしなかったが、特定の角度からは実に素晴らしく見えた。しかし最終的に偽軍のための場所がなくなり、お披露目の時だと悟った。",
  "This posed a problem in itself. Of course, the army was not capable of marching on the castle, or marching anywhere. A plan was needed. A plan that even Dreadwing would not question. And finally that plan came together; the Glitch would host a parade.": "これ自体が問題だった。もちろん軍は城に向かって行進できなかったし、どこにも行進できなかった。計画が必要だった。ドレッドウィングでさえ疑わない計画。そしてついに計画がまとまった。グリッチがパレードを開催するのだ。",
  "King Dreadwing applauded and whooped as the armoured Glitch careened towards him. It was only as the soldier lowered its blade and charged that he suspected something was wrong. The blade pierced his metal shell, which shattered with a deafening crack.": "装甲グリッチが向かってくるのをドレッドウィング王は拍手喝采した。兵士が刃を下ろして突進した時になって初めて何かがおかしいと気づいた。刃が金属の殻を貫き、耳をつんざく音と共に砕けた。",
  "All the Glitch watched as their king fell backwards, his Glitch disguise falling away, revealing a small, black and white bird-like creature. The Glitch had been duped! All this time, their tyrannical, unusual king had been a space pirate in disguise. It made perfect sense. Realising the game was up, and badly injured, the evil space pirate made his escape, never to be seen again.": "全てのグリッチが王が後ろに倒れるのを見た。グリッチの変装が剥がれ、小さな黒と白の鳥のような",
  "The rogue soldier turned out to be the impromptu Floran, who had grown bored and decided to go on a hunting spree. She was made an honorary hero of the Glitch people, but then immediately exiled because killing kings is bad, even if they were penguins in disguise. From that day forth, the Glitch vowed never to allow another monarch to take control, even if they asked really nicely.": "暴走した兵士は即席のフローランだった。退屈になって狩りの乱痴気騒ぎを決行。彼女は",
  "The army paraded past on floats, towed by a number of Glitch workers and a Floran who'd decided to join in unannounced. Dreadwing sat atop his iron throne, brought outside into the city, and applauded each and every unit. 'They stand very still,' he remarked, to which his aides replied 'yes, they are very disciplined.'": "軍は山車に乗ってパレードし、数人のグリッチ労働者と飛び入り参加のフローラン1人に牽引された。ドレッドウィングは外に出した鉄の玉座の上に座り、全ての部隊に拍手を送った。「とても静かに立っている」と彼は言い、側近が答えた「はい、非常に規律正しい」。",
  "As the last float made its way down the street, the entire crowd gasped as one of the soldiers leaped from the stand, and charged towards Dreadwing. Most surprised of all were the blacksmiths, who knew full well that their 'soldiers' were little more than decorative suits of armour. Dreadwing, however, thought it was all part of the show.": "最後の山車が通りを進むと、兵士の一人がスタンドから飛び降りドレッドウィングに向かって突進した時、群衆全員が息を飲んだ。",
  "As such, I have no choice but to suspend any and all attempts at teaching the Florans to write, in case we encounter any further murderous delusions of grandeur.": "そのため、これ以上殺人的な誇大妄想に遭遇しないよう、フローランに書くことを教えるあらゆる試みを中止するしかない。",
  "Thankfully the Glitch was okay, although I'm told he occasionally quotes pretentious dialogue following the incident. Florstab apparently told the Glitch professor that he'd make sure the universe would 'remember my name.'": "幸いグリッチは無事だったが、事件後たまに気取った台詞を引用するようになったと聞いた。フロースタブはグリッチ教授に宇宙が「俺の名を覚える」ようにすると言ったらしい。",
  "Town elders have informed me that celebrated author Treeio Florstab has fled his home village after a series of critical maulings in the intergalactic press. His writing tutor, one Glitch Professor Irondome, was found with a copy of Florstab's debut novel, Floran Peace, rammed into his mouth.": "町の長老から、著名な作家ツリーイオ・フロースタブが銀河間メディアでの一連の酷評の後、故郷の村から逃亡したと聞いた。彼の作文教師であるグリッチ教授アイアンドームは、フロースタブのデビュー小説「フローランの平和」を口に押し込まれた状態で発見された。",
  "The subject has always lain dormant. For this to occur... It must be dealt with, and severely. One day I will travel to Earth myself, to see exactly what the beast has become.": "対象は常に休眠状態にあった。これが起こるとは…厳しく対処しなければならない。いつか自分で地球に行き、あの獣がどうなったか確かめよう。",
  "Humanity fled their home planet, the one they call Earth, after a rapidly-growing beast emerged from the surface, and within no time at all, began to consume their entire world. I have no words. I did not know this was possible.": "人類は母星 — 彼らが地球と呼ぶ星 — から逃げた。急速に成長する獣が地表から出現し、瞬く間に世界全体を飲み込み始めた後のことだ。言葉がない。こんなことが可能だとは知らなかった。",
  "Of course, the corpses of the Sunborn do not rest in random tombs. They are hidden away, together, in a place known to a select few. If all goes well, that information should be in my possession in due course. I would very much like to study the biology of a god.": "もちろんサンボーンの遺体は無作為な墓には安置されていない。選ばれた少数の者だけが知る場所に一緒に隠されている。うまくいけば、その情報は然るべき時に手に入るだろう。神の生物学をぜひとも研究したい。",
  "The Avians have perpetrated a wonderful deception. The rumour that the corpses of their gods - their gods! - rest in their tombs has spread throughout the universe. Such rumours attract looters, and said looters make for a handy, never-ending source of live sacrifices, to use in their silly rituals. It is genius, even by my standards.": "エイビアンは素晴らしい欺瞞を仕掛けた。神々の — 彼らの神々の！ — 遺体が墓に眠っているという噂が宇宙中に広まった。そのような噂は略奪者を引き寄せ、略奪者は愚かな儀式に使う生贄の便利な尽きることのない供給源となる。私の基準でさえ天才的だ。",
  "As the Florans hissed and danced and hunted creatures, I sat and studied this tree, eventually removing my tools and tapping the bark for sap. It surprised me when the sap flowed. Rich, thick, viscous sap, and yet something about it made me uneasy.": "フローランがシーッと鳴き、踊り、生き物を狩る中、私は座ってこの木を研究し、やがて道具を取り出して樹皮から樹液を採取した。樹液が流れた時は驚いた。豊かで濃厚で粘り気のある樹液。しかし何かが不安にさせた。",
  "A scouting party returned to me with a cutting from an unusual plant; a tree whose bark resembled bone. It grew from dirt, no water flowing through its veins. I bid them lead me to the copse they'd discovered, and sure enough, no water had touched that ground for aeons, I'd wager.": "偵察隊が珍しい植物の切り枝を持って戻ってきた。樹皮が骨に似た木だ。土から育ち、維管束に水は流れていない。発見した小さな林に案内するよう頼むと、確かに、何千年もの間水がこの地に触れていなかったと賭けてもいい。",
  "Perhaps it is too early to allow Drysap treatment to gain mass circulation. Perhaps I shall send it to The Dust. At least there, any Floran Greenguard who succumbs can be marched straight into a cell.": "ドライサップ治療を大規模に流通させるのは時期尚早かもしれない。ダストに送ろうか。少なくとも、そこで屈服したフローランのグリーンガードはすぐに独房に連行できる。",
  "It soon became clear that injecting Drysap into living Florans prompted exceptional results. The sap quickly reproduces within Floran veins, replacing their own with a stronger, hardier substance that leaves the Floran body requiring almost no water. To an extent, this is a miracle serum.": "生きたフローランにドライサップを注射すると並外れた結果が出ることがすぐに明らかになった。樹液はフローランの血管内で急速に増殖し、より強く丈夫な物質に置き換わり、体がほとんど水を必要としなくなる。ある程度、これは奇跡の血清だ。",
  "But there are caveats; it has been found that the more intellectually advanced the Floran, the more susceptible they are to rejection of the Drysapping process. Those whose bodies reject the Drysap soon grow enraged and antisocial, reporting visions and night terrors.": "しかし注意点がある。知的に優れたフローランほど、ドライサップ処理の拒絶反応に弱いことが判明した。ドライサップを拒絶した者はすぐに激怒し反社会的になり、幻覚と夜の恐怖を報告する。",
  "Due to a reliance on natural water sources thanks to the Floran's [REDACTED] roots, it transpires that Floran biology leaves individuals susceptible to extreme heat. All Florans know that fire equals danger, but many are unaware of the toll that dry, humid conditions can take on the body.": "フローランの[削除済み]根のおかげで天然水源に依存しているため、フローランの生物学は個体を極端な熱に弱くしていることが判明した。全てのフローランは火が危険だと知っているが、乾燥した蒸し暑い条件が体に及ぼす影響を知らない者が多い。",
  "Prolonged exposure to desert climate can leave Florans in a mummified, barely living state, before they eventually succumb to the elements, crumbling to dust. As the species expands its territory, it has been important to find ways in which the Florans can adapt their biology in order to survive inhospitable climes.": "砂漠気候への長期暴露はフローランをミイラ化し、かろうじて生きている状態にし、やがて元素に屈して塵と化す。種族が領土を拡大する中、フローランが不毛な環境で生き延びるよう生物学を適応させる方法を見つけることが重要だった。",
  "It may be premature to say, but perhaps this development might herald the emergence of true civilization amongst the Floran in the absence of the Protectorate.": "早計かもしれないが、この発展はプロテクトレートなきフローランの間に真の文明の出現を告げるものかもしれない。",
  "I am not certain if the tradition was undertaken as some long-forgotten form of flattery or simply because they associate my name with being clever, after these long [REDACTED]. Either way, I cannot say I am entirely displeased with the practice. It would seem I have left a lasting mark upon the history of my people.": "<興味深いことに、植物型存在は*美味しい*。我々の在来植生も美味しいが、この二足歩行の生物はデザートの盛り合わせのようだ。今まで食べた最も美味しいユラシュクを想像してほしい。それ以上だ。ただし死んでいると風味が失われる。生きている間に味わえ。>",
  "The tribal role of Greenfinger appears to be distinct from that of Tribesmaster, although exceptional Florans might occasionally be both. Greenfingers seem to serve as exceptionally clever, technically proficient shamen, and I have even seen evidence that they correspond with one another, acting almost as tribal envoys.": "11日目 - 「ケビン」という者が面白い。他の科学者よりはるかに先進的な科学を研究しているが、潜在能力の多くを愚かないたずらで自分を楽しませることに浪費している。私にもいたずらを試みた。「歓迎の贈り物」としての^gray;狼の箱^reset;。痩せていて美味しくなかった。",
  "After [REDACTED] and revisiting a nearby Floran tribe, I discovered a surprising trend that had arisen in tribal tradition. They have taken to calling their [REDACTED] 'Greenfingers.' It apparently was not limited to that one tribe either. Tribes all over the planet - and as I shortly learned, nearly every other tribe across this sector - have also taken up the practice.": "[削除済み]の後、近くのフローランの部族を再訪し、部族の伝統に驚くべき傾向が生じていたことを発見した。彼らは",
  "Unhappy to have left the Apex compound. Sharing our species' secret is not something I take lightly. My acquaintance, the Apex scientist Doctor Lax, can be trusted. I have utter faith in her.": "エイペックスの施設を去ったことが不満だ。種族の秘密を共有することは軽く考えない。知人のエイペックス科学者ラックス博士は信頼できる。彼女を完全に信頼している。",
  "I am sorry, Doctor.": "申し訳ありません、博士",
  "And yet, this is not something I can leave up to faith. I was barely off-planet before putting the call in to Thornwing. The Ring of Thorns have been dispatched. No loose ends. It is how we've survived thus far, and how we will continue to survive.": "それでもこれは信仰に委ねられるものではない。惑星を離れるとすぐにソーンウィングに連絡した。ソーンの輪が派遣された。ほころびなし。これまでの生存法であり、今後も生き延びる方法だ。",
  "Naturally, I asked my acquaintance for a sample of this tar, which she promised to ship to me. Barbarism aside, the potential of combining it with Floran biology may lead to advancements in ground troop armour.": "当然、知人にこのタールのサンプルを頼んだところ、送ると約束してくれた。野蛮さはさておき、フローランの生物学と組み合わせる可能性は地上部隊の装甲の進歩に繋がるかもしれない。",
  "Atheist Avians who require punishment are dipped in a vat of tar-like liquid, which solidifies over their feathers, turning their plumage into what is essentially stone. Seeing as the Avians cannot fly, it's a largely symbolic gesture, but one which serves to shame the subject.": "罰を受けるべき無神論エイビアンはタールのような液体に浸けられ、羽毛が固まって本質的に石となる。エイビアンは飛べないので象徴的な意味合いが大きいが、対象者を辱める効果がある。",
  "Many are simply sent from the villages, she told me, occasionally even hounded off-planet if their heresy is grand enough. Others, however, are subjected to a process which even to myself sounds barbaric. She stressed, repeatedly, that this behaviour was no longer endorsed by the Clipped Council.": "多くは村から追い出されるだけだと彼女は言った。異端の程度によっては惑星外に追い立てられることさえある。しかし他の者たちはクリップド評議会でさえもう支持していないと繰り返し強調した野蛮なプロセスにさらされる。",
  "One day I was fortunate enough to meet with a member of the Avian Clipped Council, a group of flightless Avians who serve their ruler, Kluex. We shared talk, and stories, and eventually a bottle of particularly potent meatjuice. This loosened the Avian's tongue even more, and I was able to ask her about the Grounded, and how her people deal with those who defy their god.": "ある日、エイビアンのクリップド評議会のメンバーに会う幸運に恵まれた。飛べないエイビアンで構成され、支配者に仕える集団",
  "Any visitor to a Floran village will be greeted with a single reassurance; it is Floran custom not to harm any guest who enters a Floran home patch.": "フローランの村を訪れる者は一つの安心を得る。フローランの領域に入った客を傷つけないのがフローランの慣習である。",
  "This is, of course, a lie.": "これはもちろん、嘘である。",
  "Perhaps the intention was to be hospitable, but the Florans are incapable of sticking to such things, quickly descending into lethal violence if their guests should offend them in some manner. It is also worth noting that it is exceptionally easy to offend a Floran. Examples include: refusing to eat raw meat, damaging the plant life, being a Hylotl.": "おそらく歓待する意図だったが、フローランはそのようなことに固執できず、すぐに致命的な暴力に堕ちる",
  "A number of Glitch have appeared in Floran villages, with the intention of educating our people. It's a noble pursuit - I've always stated that the ability to read and write is something the Floran should aspire to, but it's hard to persuade the general populace.": "多数のグリッチがフローランの村に現れ、我々の民を教育する意図を持っている。崇高な追求だ — 読み書きの能力はフローランが目指すべきものだと常に述べてきたが、一般大衆を説得するのは難しい。",
  "The Glitch are in a good position to do this, as their metal exteriors largely protect them from Floran blades. However, we are at a stage where we now have Florans running around writing words on anything and everything, with typical Floran over-enthusiasm. It is, however, an improvement over the time they attempted to learn how to paint.": "グリッチはこれを行うのに良い位置にある。金属の外装がフローランの刃からほぼ守ってくれるからだ。しかし我々は段階にある、",
  "Not only does this mean that the Tribesmaster possesses the largest, most impressive dwelling in the village, but also that a fall from the house means certain death, should any opportunistic Floran be looking to usurp their superior.": "これは部族長が村で最大かつ最も印象的な住居を持つことを意味するだけでなく、上位者を簒奪しようとする日和見的なフローランにとって、家からの落下は確実な死を意味する。",
  "Since the Florans can command plants, it made perfect sense that they would shape their homes from the very trees that protected them. As such, it became customary for the Floran Tribesmaster to fashion a clan's first house in the tallest tree on-site.": "フローランが植物を操れるなら、自分たちを守る木から家を形成するのは理にかなっている。そのため、フローランの部族長が一族の最初の家を現地で最も高い木に作るのが慣習となった。",
  "A Pleasant Town": "快適な町",
  "I find myself in a Miniknog-controlled Apex town. But oh, control is such an ugly word, isn't it? The Apex here are all so polite, and friendly. They bow and grovel as I pass, my Miniknog entourage only occasionally having to knock them back!": "ミニクノグが支配するエイペックスの町にいる。しかし、支配とは醜い言葉ではないか？ここのエイペックスは皆とても礼儀正しく友好的だ。通り過ぎると頭を下げてひれ伏す。ミニクノグの取り巻きがたまに殴り返すだけで済む！",
  "It's all very exciting. An audience with Big Ape! Greenfinger told me he's heard about my exploits, and would like to pick my brain. I mean gosh, I've heard rumours about Big Ape picking peoples' brains, but I don't think it means that this time.": "全てとても興奮する。ビッグエイプとの謁見！グリーンフィンガーが私の功績を聞いて、脳を掻き出し…じゃなくて意見を聞きたいと。ビッグエイプが人の脳を掻き出すという噂は聞いたが、今回はそういう意味ではないと思う。",
  "A Rude Awakening": "無礼な目覚め",
  "Of course, I wasn't up for this! Quick as a flash, I kicked the head priest in the face and made my escape, charging through the temple like a Hylotl possessed. There were a few casualties along the way, of course - some sacred urns, a statue or two, an Avian monk - but I escaped intact, and carried on my way.": "もちろんこれには乗れない！電光石火で大司祭の顔を蹴り、取り憑かれたハイロトルのように寺院を突っ走って脱出した。途中でいくつかの犠牲はあった — 聖なる壺、像の一つ二つ、エイビアンの修道士 — しかし無傷で脱出し、旅を続けた。",
  "I awoke to find myself surrounded by hooded figures, chanting and squawking. One of them, who appeared to be the figurehead, held a large knife above me. At first I was disoriented, and thought I was back with the Florans. But no. It seems I'd accidentally presented myself for sacrifice. So silly!": "目覚めるとフードを被った人物たちに囲まれ、詠唱と鳴き声が聞こえた。首領と思われる一人が大きなナイフを頭上に掲げていた。最初は方向感覚を失い、フローランの元に戻ったかと思った。違った。どうやら自分を生贄に差し出してしまったようだ。おっちょこちょい！",
  "The Peaceful Temple": "平和な神殿",
  "Lost and in need of guidance (the navigational kind, not the spiritual kind), I made my way into an impressive Avian temple. Immediately I felt at peace, like a calm had descended over me. I walked the stone hallways, gazing up at the statues of that giant bird, occasionally greeting priests and worshippers alike. They seemed pleased to see me.": "道に迷い導きが必要で（精神的なものではなく航法的なもの）、印象的なエイビアンの寺院に入った。すぐに",
  "I ascended the temple and grew tired, my weary legs almost giving out after days of adventuring and fleeing. At the top, I found a stone bed. Priests milled about, but they did not seem to mind when I lay down. In fact, they began to cheep and cheer. One of them handed me a delicious, sweet-tasting drink. Soon, I drifted off to sleep.": "寺院を登り疲れ果てた。何日もの冒険と逃走で疲れた脚がほとんど力尽きた。頂上に石のベッドを見つけた。司祭たちがうろついていたが、横になっても気にしなかった。実際、チーチーと歓声を上げた。一人が美味しい甘い飲み物をくれた。すぐに眠りに落ちた。",
  "A Tasty Beverage": "美味しい飲み物",
  "Imagine that; Hiraki Corale, Avian god. The first Hylotl Avian god in history, I'd wager! In the meantime, however, I accidentally started rummaging through one of my fellow student's belongings, and what should I find? Greenfinger's delightful Strengthsap elixir!": "想像してくれ — ヒラキ・コラーレ、エイビアンの神。歴史上初のハイロトルのエイビアンの神だろう！しかしその間に、うっかり同級生の荷物を漁り始め、何を見つけたと思う？グリーンフィンガーの素敵なストレングスサップエリクサー！",
  "Now, I like nothing more than tasting Greenfinger's concoctions, but the Strengthsap has always been one of my favourites. I couldn't resist taking a sip, and ended up drinking the whole lot. So naughty! I hope the Avian who I borrowed it from doesn't mind!": "グリーンフィンガーの調合薬を味わうのが何より好きだが、ストレングスサップは常にお気に入りの一つだ。一口だけのつもりが全部飲んでしまった。とてもいけない！借りたエイビアンが気にしないといいが！",
  "Having found myself accidentally enrolled as an Avian Ascendant, I figured I might as well make the most of it and go with the flow. If it comes to it, and I'm chosen to leap off the tower, I have this jetpack I borrowed from the Miniknog. So exciting!": "偶然エイビアンのアセンダントに登録されてしまったので、せっかくだから流れに乗ることにした。塔から飛び降りる番が来たら、ミニクノグから借りたジェットパックがある。わくわくする！",
  "My ship crash-landed on a planet. I may have been fleeing a certain simian species at the time, and decided the best course of action was to lure them into an asteroid field. It worked! Of course, I have no experience navigating through asteroid fields so here I am.": "船が惑星に墜落した。当時ある霊長類種から逃げていたかもしれない。最善の行動は小惑星帯に誘い込むことだと決めた。成功した！もちろん、小惑星帯の航行経験がないのでここにいる。",
  "Fight or Flight": "戦うか逃げるか",
  "A small, misshapen robot stood before me, vibrating on the spot. It looked like it had been made out of a kettle and some saucepans, but its eyes glowed red with malevolence. I knew this was it. Me or the robot. Live or die.": "小さく歪んだロボットが目の前で震えていた。やかんと鍋で作られたようだが、目は悪意に赤く光っていた。これが決戦だと分かった。俺かロボットか。生きるか死ぬか。",
  "I was exploring the ship, as you do, when I encountered what appeared to be someone's private laboratory, marked with 'Keep Out' signs and warnings of delicate, breakable equipment within. I barged my way inside, and began to fiddle with all the exciting bits and bobs.": "しかしそれがファリトゥが他者とコミュニケーションする方法だ）、または極めて長い距離にわたって互いに（シャクタを大いに消耗するが）石と金属を形作り、さらには船の燃料として機能できる固体物質の構造物を作り出すことさえできる — 素材から作られた船",
  "Imagine my alarm when, from out of nowhere, I was greeted by a dull robotic voice commanding me to 'prepare to die'. At first, I thought the Glitch had finally sent assassins to demand retribution for past transgressions, but the truth was much worse.": "突然、どこからともなく、「死ぬ準備をしろ」と命じるくぐもったロボットの声に迎えられた時の驚きを想像してほしい。最初はグリッチがついに過去の罪の報復を求めて暗殺者を送ったのかと思ったが、真実はもっとひどかった。",
  "Screaming, I ran from the room, knocking machinery hither and thither. Avians stared at me as I ran through the ship, being pursued by the robot. Nobody even stepped in to help! Eventually I had to throw myself over the side, plummeting down to meet the ground below. Thankfully, the ship was passing over an outdoor Apex marriage ceremony, and the wedding cake broke my fall. A narrow escape!": "叫びながら部屋を飛び出し、機械をあちこちに倒した。エイビアンたちは私が追われて船中を走り回るのを見つめていた",
  "Friends to the End": "最後までの友",
  "So I hit upon a genius idea! If the Resistance and the Miniknog could just talk it out, then maybe things could get smoothed over. I'm sure Big Ape is not the villain they think, if only they'd get to know him. So I tunnelled out of my room and found the nearest Miniknog platoon.": "天才的なアイデアを思いついた！レジスタンスとミニクノグが話し合えば丸く収まるかも。ビッグエイプは彼らが思うような悪役ではない、知り合えば分かるはず。部屋からトンネルを掘って最も近いミニクノグ小隊を見つけた。",
  "Filled with positivity, I led them to the Resistance hideout and told them that if they didn't sort out their differences, I'd knock their heads together. So smart! Well, I think it went okay! I didn't stick around to find out for sure, of course, I had to meet back up with Greenfinger, but I saw them all marching together through the town square as we left.": "前向きな気持ちでレジスタンスの隠れ家に案内し、違いを解決しなければ頭をぶつけると言った",
  "The Iron Avian": "鉄のエイビアン",
  "The door to the cargo hold splintered open, and a large, metallic Avian came striding out. Swiftly he dispatched a number of the ship's crew, punching and smashing his way around. I cowered in fear, hiding behind the captain, who let off some shots from his rifle.": "貨物室のドアが砕けて開き、大きな金属のエイビアンが堂々と歩き出てきた。素早く乗組員を何人も倒し、殴り壊しながら進んだ。私は恐怖で身をすくめ、ライフルから何発か撃った船長の後ろに隠れた。",
  "The bullets simply bounced off the iron Avian, who laughed, smashed the ship's mast, then leaped into the air. A glowing circle on his chest began to pulsate, then thrusters in the man's feet kicked in, and the Avian took off, soaring into the skies like a rocket ship. What a sight!": "弾丸は鉄のエイビアンに跳ね返された。彼は笑い、船のマストを叩き壊し、空中に跳んだ。胸の光る円が脈動し始め、足のスラスターが点火。エイビアンはロケットのように空に舞い上がった。なんという光景！",
  "I boarded another airship village today, when it had stopped to dock. Climbed my way up the anchor and squirreled myself into a cabin before anyone could complain. Everything was going well; the captain, a jolly fellow called Wrenolds, allowed me to teach him how to play Lilyflip. We were half way through a game when it happened. I was winning.": "今日、停泊のため停止した別の飛行船の村に乗り込んだ。錨を登り、誰かが気づく前にキャビンに忍び込んだ",
  "I was unaware the Avians had developed armour that allowed them to fly again. I commented on this to Wrenolds, and he told me it was unheard of. He muttered something about power crystals, and then I heard him mention my dear friend Greenfinger, who they were apparently going to see. What luck! I informed him he could drop me off there.": "エイビアンが再び飛行できる鎧を開発していたとは知らなかった。ウレノルズにこのことをコメントすると、前代未聞だと言われた。",
  "I will admit, the ape is not to my tastes. He is brash, boorish and a poor tactician. His insistence in appearing behind a video screen is tiresome - he forgets I know all his little secrets.": "認めよう、あの猿は私の好みではない。がさつで無礼で戦術家としても劣る。ビデオスクリーンの向こうに現れることへの固執はうんざりだ — 彼は私が彼の小さな秘密を全て知っていることを忘れている。",
  "And yet, he's an invaluable ally. I may not agree with his methods, but his goals are sound. And he has the ear of the self-styled lord, Thornwing. Strange times make for strange bedfellows. It's not like anything is conventional these days.": "それでも彼は貴重な同盟者だ。方法には同意しないが、目標は健全だ。自称領主ソーンウィングの耳も持っている。奇妙な時代は奇妙な仲間を生む。最近は何一つ普通ではない。",
  "Greenguard Journal 1": "グリーンガード日記 1",
  "So here I am, finally assigned to The Dust. My mother is a state, of course. 'The Greenguard is no place for a literate Floran!' she cried. But she was wrong. Oh, was she wrong.": "こうして私はついにダストに配属された。母はもちろん大騒ぎだ。「グリーンガードは読み書きできるフローランの居場所じゃない！」と叫んだ。でも彼女は間違っていた。ああ、間違っていたとも。",
  "I'm sorry, Mother, but the Drysap pulses through my veins now. I am home.": "ごめんなさい、母さん。でも今、ドライサップが私の血管を流れている。ここが私の家だ。",
  "For moons I longed for the solitude, the darkness of The Dust, and when my transfer request was approved, I celebrated. Down here, in the darkness, amongst the universe's most unfortunate souls, I finally feel like I'm not alone any more.": "何ヶ月も孤独を、ダストの暗闇を切望していた。転属願いが承認された時は祝った。ここ下の暗闇で、宇宙で最も不幸な魂たちの中で、ようやくもう孤独ではないと感じる。",
  "Scrawled Note": "走り書きのメモ",
  "Greenguard send replacement. More Greenguard go mad, try to kill. Have to stab. Body strange, had to burn. Drysap at work. More trouble than worth. Lose two thirds of Greenguard every month. Ho hum. Send more.": "グリーンガードが交代を送ってきた。さらに多くのグリーンガードが発狂し殺そうとする。刺すしかない。体が変で燃やさなければならなかった。ドライサップのせいだ。割に合わない。毎月3分の2を失う。やれやれ。もっと送れ。",
  "Send us more Oaken Soldiers.": "もっとオーケンソルジャーを送れ",
  "Greenguard Journal 2": "グリーンガード日記 2",
  "Deep in the bowels of this place, I met a most curious Avian, who has rejected the teachings of her species and defied her gods. We spoke of freedom, and free will, and choice, and the soul. She gave me much to ponder over. Then one of my Greenguard peers threw a bucket of swill in her face. Perhaps there is meaning in this. I shall muse on it as I sleep tonight.": "この場所の奥深くで、最も好奇心をそそるエイビアンに出会った。種族の教えを拒否し神に逆らった者だ。",
  "Greenguard Journal 3": "グリーンガード日記 3",
  "The journey between outposts is stressful, particularly with the Drysap working its magic. But this is the price I must pay to follow my dreams.": "前哨地間の旅はストレスが多い。特にドライサップが効いている時は。しかしこれは夢を追うために払わなければならない代償だ。",
  "Perhaps my only reservation about being stationed in The Dust is the elders' insistence on transferring us regularly between outposts. It's to stop Greenguards becoming attached to prisoners, they say, although the chances of some of my peers developing any kind of emotional bond is next to zero.": "ダストに配置されることへの唯一の不満は、前哨地間を定期的に異動させるという長老たちの固執だ。グリーンガードが囚人に愛着を持つのを防ぐためだという。しかし同僚がいかなる感情的絆を発展させる可能性はほぼゼロだ。",
  "Greenguard Journal 4": "グリーンガード日記 4",
  "The flowers and plants given sentience. Nature is gentle but cruel. Are we the cruel face of Nature itself? Or are we something more? From the seeds we plant, a universe will sprout. We are the oaken soldiers.": "意識を与えられた花と植物。自然は優しいが残酷だ。我々は自然の残酷な顔なのか？それとも何かもっと大きなものか？我々が蒔く種から宇宙が芽吹く。我々はオーケンソルジャーだ。",
  "I lie awake at night in my cool, dark quarters, the sound of wailing echoing through the prison corridors, and I begin to question. Why do we hunt? Why do we kill? What drives us to be the species that we are? We are the trees, uprooted. The bushes, animated.": "夜、涼しく暗い部屋で目を覚まし、監獄の廊下に響く嘆きの声を聞きながら疑問を抱き始める。なぜ狩るのか？なぜ殺すのか？何が我々を今の種族たらしめているのか？我々は根を引き抜かれた木。動き出した茂み。",
  "Greenguard Journal 5": "グリーンガード日記 5",
  "Afterwards she looked at me and hissed, as if she no longer recognised me as one of her own.": "その後彼女は私を見てシーッと鳴いた。もはや仲間として認識していないかのように。",
  "In the mess hall, I avoid my kin and choose to eat alone. The meat tastes rank and soiled. I hope I'm transferred soon.": "食堂で同胞を避け、一人で食べることにしている。肉は腐った味がする。早く転属になるといいのだが。",
  "Upon re-reading my previous journal entry, I became alarmed and then afraid. Memories are growing hazy, as if there's a cold, hard knot of wood in my brain, tugging at my thoughts. I had my third Drysap treatment today. The doctor had to force the needle in.": "前の日記を読み返して、まず驚き、次に恐怖を覚えた。記憶が曖昧になっている。まるで脳の中に冷たく硬い木の結び目があり、思考を引っ張っているかのように。今日3回目のドライサップ治療を受けた。医師は針を無理やり刺さなければならなかった。",
  "Greenguard Journal 6": "グリーンガード日記 6",
  "Today I killed a prisoner. I pushed him down the stairs on the way to dinner. The other guards cheered and hooted, but I felt no such pleasure. The thrill of the hunt is gone from me. I should set a torch to them and see how well they hunt then.": "今日、囚人を殺した。夕食に向かう途中で階段から突き落とした。他の看守は歓声を上げたが、私はそのような喜びを感じなかった。狩りのスリルは失われた。松明を彼らに向けて、どれだけ上手く狩れるか見てやるべきだ。",
  "I dream of oaken soldiers once more. Who is this army that sprawls before me? I feel a stiffening in my limbs as I wake. I think The Dust is getting to me. I require Drysap treatment once a week now, and even then it does little to ease my discomfort.": "また樫の兵士の夢を見た。目の前に広がるこの軍は誰か？目覚めると四肢が硬直しているのを感じる。ダストが効いてきている。今は週に一度のドライサップ治療が必要で、それでも不快感はほとんど和らがない。",
  "Greenguard Journal 7": "グリーンガード日記 7",
  "Soon they will come for me, but who shall reach me first? My kin, with their spears and knives, baying for blood? Or the oaken soldiers, marching to reclaim me, to bring me back into their fold.": "間もなく彼らが私を迎えに来る。しかし誰が先に着くだろうか？血を求めて吠える槍とナイフを持った同胞か？それとも私を取り戻し、隊列に戻すために行進するオーケンソルジャーか。",
  "My superiors demand recompense. Recompense for what I've done. That terrible, unspeakable thing which breaks every Floran code, that which even in my distant state, I cannot bring myself to mention. Who will find me first?": "上官が補償を要求している。私がしたことへの補償。全てのフローランの掟を破るあの恐ろしく言葉にできないこと。遠く離れた今でも口にできない。誰が先に私を見つけるだろう？",
  "Writ of Law": "法の令状",
  "...for in such an act, you will find yourself in dire trouble. Depravity of this sort is abolished by the Oracles themselves, and as such is considered among the worst crimes possible by Mantizi citizens. So bear that in mind before buying a white-handled broom.": "…そのような行為では、大変な困難に陥ることになる。この種の堕落は神託者自身によって廃止されており、マンティジ市民にとって最悪の犯罪の一つとされている。白い柄の箒を買う前にそのことを念頭に置け。",
  "Don't Touch Dave": "デイブに触るな",
  "Dave is diseased. He is leprous. Don't Touch Dave! (picture of a diseased fat man)": "デイブは病気だ。ハンセン病だ。デイブに触るな！（病気の太った男の絵）",
  "Look at Dave! He's ugly and smelly! His fingers fall off at random! (picture of same man in an insultingly tight outfit)": "デイブを見ろ！醜くて臭い！指がランダムに落ちる！（侮辱的にきつい服を着た同じ男の絵）",
  "If you touch Dave, he'll kill you and your entire family in slow and agonizing ways! (picture of a jet, and three flamingo-like birds wearing hats)": "デイブに触ったら、お前とその家族全員をゆっくり苦しめて殺すぞ！（ジェット機と帽子をかぶった3羽のフラミンゴのような鳥の絵）",
  "Dave doesn't mean to be evil! It's his virulent plague! (image of dead mantizi, drawn in comical fashion)": "デイブは悪意があるわけじゃない！毒性の疫病のせいだ！（コミカルに描かれた死んだマンティジの絵）",
  "Everyone run away! Dave has escaped his stab-cage! (picture of a bloody cage with strategic holes for stabbing)": "みんな逃げろ！デイブが刺し檻から脱走した！（戦略的な刺し穴のある血まみれの檻の絵）",
  "The Praetorian has killed Dave with a spear! Let's burn Dave! (picture of someones dinner)": "プラエトリアンがデイブを槍で殺した！デイブを燃やそう！（誰かの夕食の絵）",
  "Dave is ashes! Leprous infection is gone! (a hastily scribbled image of some sort of worm)": "デイブは灰になった！ハンセン病の感染は消えた！（何かの虫の走り書き）",
  "Hurray for Dave! (image of fat man clapping)": "デイブ万歳！（太った男が拍手する絵）",
  "End of a Power": "権力の終焉",
  "The citizens attempted to replace the government, but too much damage had already been done. The empire, as it was, ceased to exist. The estimated death tally across their entire territory is 4,245,167,211.": "市民は政府を交代させようとしたが、損害は大きすぎた。帝国は消滅した。全領土にわたる推定死者数は4,245,167,211人。",
  "Only time will tell if they can once again forge a lasting empire and unite the tribes. They would be welcome voices in the Protectorate, should they once again create a viable government.": "彼らが再び永続的な帝国を築き部族を統一できるかは時間だけが知っている。再び有効な政府を樹立すれば、プロテクトレートで歓迎される声となるだろう。",
  "It wasn't their military spending, their scientific experiments or their inherently unlikable natures that cost the Mantizi their empirical might. No, it was something else entirely that contributed to the downfall of their once great civilization. Expansionism brought them to the death-knell, as it were.": "マンティジの帝国的権力を失わせたのは軍事費でも科学実験でも本質的に好かれない性質でもなかった。いや、かつての偉大な文明の崩壊に貢献したのは全く別のものだった。拡張主義が彼らに死の鐘を鳴らした。",
  "Having spread too rapidly and too far among the neighboring systems stressed their economy until it reached an inevitable breaking point. The Mantizi, never great with money in the first place (they are far too hard-coded to use current resources for short-term gain, due in part to their natural evolution as a species), were not even aware of a problem until it was too late.": "近隣星系に急速かつ広範に拡大しすぎたため、経済が限界に達するまで圧迫された",
  "Within twenty years, the coffers of the empire were empty. Workers could no longer be paid, and the unemployment rate rapidly reached over 87% (estimated 87.72% at the official time of dissolution). What followed was a massive civil war, and the complete slaughter of every single member of the senate. Even the Oracles were slain, their entrails used as sashes.": "20年以内に帝国の金庫は空になった。労働者にはもう給料を払えず、失業率は80%を超えて急速に上昇した",
  "What remains now are numerous tribes. They cling to individual worlds, though their tendency to live lives of excess has not diminished in the least. At last count, the remaining Mantizi worlds still house over 65 billion individuals. Of that population, 32% are Artisans or Artists, 7% are philosophers, 8% work in brothels or similar professions. Clearly Mantizi enjoy expression.": "今残るのは多数の部族だ。個々の世界にしがみついているが、過剰な生活を送る傾向は薄れていない",
  "We cannot neglect to mention their natural combat abilities. Despite the empire no longer being a power, the old ways remain popular and are well practiced among the majority of their people due to the Vorgeth Cygna Doctrine still being held as a 'core' Virtue (a fancy way of Mantizi saying 'mandatory learning for the good of all').": "彼らの天性の戦闘能力を軽視できない。帝国はもはや権力ではないが、ヴォルゲス・シグナ教義（マンティジ的に「万民の善のための必須学習」を意味する洒落た表現）が「中核的」美徳として保持されているため、旧来の方法は人気があり大多数が実践している。",
  "Wine": "ワイン",
  "Were it not for the recent collapse of the Mantizi Empire, this would not be the case. Supply and demand is a cruel mistress, and demand has long since outstripped supply.": "最近のマンティジ帝国の崩壊がなければ、このようなことにはならなかった。需要と供給は残酷な女王であり、需要はとうに供給を上回っている。",
  "...long held as the finest wine in the known galaxy, Mantizian vineyards are viewed with utmost respect by virtually all respected wine connosieurs. Few are those among the elite who are not familiar with the narcotic qualities of these wines. Highly sought, their value on the black market is insultingly astronomical.": "…既知の銀河で最高のワインとして長く評されてきたマンティジのワイン畑は、事実上全ての尊敬されるワイン愛好家から最高の敬意をもって見られている。これらのワインの麻薬的性質に馴染みのないエリートは稀だ。非常に求められ、闇市場での価値は侮辱的なほど天文学的だ。",
  "For the Mantizi themselves, however, the wine is simply delicious. Their natural immunity to the toxin common in the grapes they use gives them no ill effects. Meanwhile, Avians are well-known to be especially susceptible. Most Mantizi hoard a few bottles at any given time (if they have access to stores of them in their family holdings) but are loathe to part with them. In some of the more lawless sectors, Mantizi are captured and 'inspired' by pirates into 'donating' their supply.": "マンティジ自身にとってワインは単に美味しい。使用するブドウに一般的な毒素に対する天然の免疫力を持つため",
  "Vorgeth Cygna Doctrine": "ヴォルゲス・シグナの教義",
  "Page 82: There are few things as important as the shield wall, and repeated drills are required until such time as the unit is perfectly synced. They must move as one, turn as one. Each thrust with the Light Spear should be done through the opening, never dropping the guard. Should the wall falter, the entire formation will fail. This will spell the end of your unit. Drill your forces until they hate you for it, and then drill some more.": "82ページ：盾の壁ほど重要なものは少なく、部隊が完璧になるまで繰り返しの訓練が必要とされる",
  "Page 87: The Light Spear is integral, for without it we are forced to rely on either firearm or melee combat, rather than both. Our ancestors developed the plasmic-formed zerchesium spears to be perfect all-purpose weapons, and we shame them by forgetting what was sacrificed in their invention. The Ten-Generation War proved that our might was virtually unassailable to the enemy. The doctrine works. Adhere to it, or perish to the Great Enemy.": "87ページ：ライトスピアは不可欠だ。なければ銃器か近接戦闘のどちらかに頼らざるを得ず、両方ではなくなる。我々の",
  "The Ten Generation War": "十世代戦争",
  "We must never forget how close we came to annihiliation. The Thelusians were a formidable adversary for nearly 200 years, and managed to fight us to a standstill despite our best efforts. They accomplished this not with numbers, nor with their tough chitin. No, it was their skill. Until we were able to create the Yashvarra Nyi (Light Spear) using the strange lore of the ancients as a guide...we were nothing. Once the Doctrine was in practice, and the Yashvarra perfected they were beaten back with ease.": "我々がいかに全滅に近づいたか決して忘れてはならない。テルシアンは約200年間手強い敵であり、何とか",
  "Should their formed Hive-Mind collapse as it did in those days, there will again be a war. They cannot help themselves, for we are a natural food to them, and their voracious appetite requires near constant feeding. However, we must also not forget the Doctrine. The are not our enemy at present, and the Oracles forbid war unless it is in defense of the People.": "彼らの形成したハイブマインドがあの日のように崩壊すれば、再び戦争が起きる。彼ら自身を止められない。我々は自然な",
  "(Brine Star) Ancient Text": "（ブラインスター）古代の文書",
  "(Brine Star) Savage Scribbling": "（ブラインスター）野蛮な走り書き",
  "RULESS OF TRIBE\n\nRUINSS GIVESS SSPARKLIESS\n\nSSPARKLIESS GIVESS POWER\n\nDEVOUR SSPARKLIESS\n\nKEEP AWAY MEATSSS\n\nKEEP AWAY OTHER FLORAN\n\nBECOME SSSTRONGESST": "ブゾクノ オキテ\n\nイセキガ キラキラ クレル\n\nキラキラガ チカラ クレル\n\nキラキラ クラウ\n\nニクドモ チカヅケルナ\n\nホカノ フローラン チカヅケルナ\n\nイチバン ツヨク ナル",
  "(Brine Star) Research Log": "（ブラインスター）調査記録",
  "I've done all I can here. The Floran living amidst the ruins appear to be unnaturally savage, even by Floran standards, but they aren't my main problem. There are things deeper in the temple, and eyes and ears aren't their only senses.\n\nIt's also getting harder to stay hidden. I had a close brush the other day while witnessing some kind of ritual.": "ここでできることは全てやった。遺跡に住むフローランはフローランの基準から見ても異常なほど凶暴だが、主な問題はそこではない。神殿の奥深くには何かがおり、目や耳だけが彼らの感覚器官ではない。\n\n隠れ続けるのも難しくなってきた。先日、何かの儀式を目撃中に危うく見つかるところだった",
  "Was too engrossed with watching one of the Florans drop a helpless bunny into an altar's concave surface and sacrifice it, consigning it to the flames. They have bunnies, but I think any critter would have been an appropriate sacrifice.": "フローランの一人が無力なウサギを祭壇のくぼみに投げ入れ、炎に捧げて生贄にするのを見るのに夢中になりすぎた。ウサギを使っていたが、おそらくどんな小動物でも生贄として適していたのだろう",
  "Needless to say, I almost got discovered and had to flee before their warriors homed in on my position. I'm done here - I'm not even going to stay long enough to pack up my equipment.": "言うまでもなく、もう少しで発見されるところで、戦士たちが私の位置を察知する前に逃げなければならなかった。もうここでの調査は終わりだ——装備を片付ける時間すら取らずに立ち去るつもりだ",
  "(Hydro Center) Maintenance Log": "（ハイドロセンター）メンテナンスログ",
  "It is strange to build a temple so far into the water away from the sky, but it must be done. Filtering the seawater of this planet is the only expedient way to acquire the necessary resources for the project.": "空から遠く離れた水中にこれほど深く寺院を建てるのは奇妙だが、やらなければならない。この惑星の海水をろ過することが、プロジェクトに必要な資源を得る唯一の便宜的な方法だ。",
  "The necessity might be there, but the damp and salt make maintenance a chore. There's always something to replace or repair. That's not to mention the seawater weakening the mortar of the walls.": "必要性はあるかもしれないが、湿気と塩分でメンテナンスが面倒だ。常に交換や修理するものがある。壁のモルタルを弱める海水は言うまでもない。",
  "It would be a shame to let this place fall into disrepair when we're done here, but the upkeep is simply too much for it to be justified.": "ここでの任務が終わった後、この場所を荒れ放題にするのは残念だが、維持費が正当化できないほど高すぎる。",
  "(Hydro Center) Old Memo": "（ハイドロセンター）Old Memo",
  "The paranoia of the project lead is great. Perhaps not unjustifiably so, but still it's annoying when you're walking down the hallway and a stray sawblade nearly takes your head off.": "プロジェクトリーダーの偏執症は相当だ。不当とは言えないかもしれないが、廊下を歩いていて迷い鋸刃に首を飛ばされそうになるのはやはり迷惑だ。",
  "I ought to speak to Xolotl about this. If the Charge Beam is to be the most basic of weaponry in this line, then what are we going to have to put up with in the future? This must break several safety regulations.": "このことをショロトルに話すべきだ。チャージビームがこのラインで最も基本的な武器だとしたら、将来何を耐えなければならないのか？これは複数の安全規則に違反しているに違いない。",
  "(Hydro Center) The Charge Beam": "（ハイドロセンター）チャージビーム",
  "The initial prototype works perfectly. The Stargazers will be pleased. Using the core of avolite crystals, this optics-based weapon is slated to be the first in a line of optics-based weaponry.": "最初のプロトタイプは完璧に動作する。スターゲイザーたちは喜ぶだろう。アボライトクリスタルのコアを使用したこの光学兵器は、光学兵器シリーズの第一号となる予定だ。",
  "Its construction is the primary goal of this facility, and now that it is completed, we hope to see implementation in the next few years in addition to other beam weapons.": "その建設がこの施設の主要目標であり、完成した今、他のビーム兵器に加えて今後数年以内の実装を期待している。",
  "Additional adjustments need to be made in response to safety, ergonomical and maintenance issues, but everyone is feeling proud and relieved at the moment.": "安全性、人間工学、保守の問題に対応するためにさらなる調整が必要だが、今のところ全員が誇りと安堵を感じている。",
  "(Penguin Highway) Guardians": "（ペンギンハイウェイ）ガーディアンズ",
  "(The poster appears to have been poorly translated from some other language. The center is focused on a blond man in a white bodysuit and wearing large sunglasses. Flanking him are a ninja with absurdly long hair, and a young woman with blue-feathered wings.)\n\nEIGHT GUARDIANS FIGHTS TO REGAIN PEACE OF THEIR ADVANCE CITY": "（このポスターは別の言語からかなり下手に翻訳されたようだ。中央には白いボディスーツに大きなサングラスをかけた金髪の男が描かれている。その両脇には、異常に長い髪の忍者と、青い羽根の翼を持つ若い女性がいる。）\n\n8人ノガーディアンハ先進的ナ都市ノ平和ヲ取リ戻スタメニ戦ウ",
  "'Techno City, a city filled with advance technologies that it looks like a city from the distant future. Everyone wanted to live under this wonderful, highly advance city.\n\n'Just then, the leader of the city became mad and started to wreck havoc all across. He created strong biomutants and powerful technological warriors, teamed up with his army of enhanced humans, the leader spreads his chaos all over the city.": "「テクノシティ、ソレハ遠イ未来ノ都市ニ見エルホド先進的ナ技術デ満チタ都市デアル。誰モガコノ素晴ラシク高度ナ都市ニ住ミタガッタ。\n\n「ソノ時、都市ノリーダーガ狂イ、街中ニ破壊ヲ撒キ散ラシ始メタ。彼ハ強力ナバイオミュータントト強大ナ技術戦士ヲ作リ出シ、強化人間ノ軍隊ト共ニ、リーダーハ都市全体ニ混沌ヲ広ゲタ。",
  "'In the midst of all the chaos, one man rose up against it. A young commander that controls 'SMASH', an elite unit functions as guardians of Techno City. With the help of his eight guardians, the 'SMASH' unit wages war with the leader.\n\n'The battle for the fate of Techno City begins...'": "「混沌ノ渦中デ、一人ノ男ガ立チ上ガッタ。テクノシティノ守護者トシテ機能スル精鋭部隊「SMASH」ヲ率イル若キ指揮官デアル。8人ノガーディアンノ助ケヲ借リテ、「SMASH」部隊ハリーダーニ戦イヲ挑ム。\n\n「テクノシティノ運命ヲ賭ケタ戦イガ始マル…」",
  "(Letheia Facility) Incident Report": "（レテイア施設）インシデントレポート",
  "INCIDENT REPORT #14590\n\nSpecimen J-11 has been confirmed missing from the lab. We're all fairly puzzled - even if it did break out of its capsule, someone had to have deactivated the security system in order to open the doors for it to escape. I can personally account for everyone with the security codes that night, as they were all at the sushi-appreciation event.": "インシデントレポート #14590\n\n検体J-11がラボから行方不明となったことが確認された。全員が困惑している。仮にカプセルから脱出したとしても、脱走のためにドアを開けるには誰かがセキュリティシステムを解除しなければならなかったはずだ。その夜セキュリティコードを持つ全員の所在を私は個人的に確認できる。全員が寿司鑑賞イベントに参加していたからだ",
  "We haven't been able to pinpoint its exact location, but all signs appear to point to it escaping towards, for some reason, an amusement park. I don't think J-11 is traceable back to us in any way, so it's just a write-off - I'll just let those protectorate do-gooders take care of the problem once the inevitable starts.": "正確な位置の特定はできていないが、あらゆる兆候は、なぜか遊園地の方向に逃走したことを示している。J-11が我々に追跡されることはないと思うので、損失として計上するだけだ。不可避の事態が始まれば、あのプロテクトレートのお人好しどもに問題を処理させればいい",
  "To be honest, I'm kind of glad it's no longer our problem. J-11 was rather unnerving - I know some of the research associates claim it had been developing some form of sapience, but we all know that's nonsense. Senior management has assured us that they'll deal with the problem, and to get on with our work. I'm inclined to agree.": "正直なところ、もはや我々の問題でなくなったことに安堵している。J-11はかなり不気味だった。研究員の中にはJ-11が何らかの知性を発達させていたと主張する者もいるが、そんなことはあり得ない。上層部が問題に対処すると保証してくれたので、我々は自分たちの仕事に専念せよとのことだ。同感である",
  "(Letheia Facility) Internal Memo": "（レテイア施設）内部メモ",
  "INTERNAL MEMO #96291\n\nThe Occasus has been very helpful in their efforts to bring us more biomass. This is something that we could not have done alone - and as mercenaries of a sort, they are exceedingly useful so long as they believe the are the ones using us, and not the other way around. Their organisation has its blind spots, but so do we all.": "内部メモ #96291\n\nオカサスは生体素材の調達に非常に協力的だった。これは我々だけでは成し遂げられなかったことだ。一種の傭兵として、彼らが我々を利用しているのではなく我々が彼らを利用しているのだと信じている限り、極めて有用である。彼らの組織にも死角はあるが、それは誰にでもあることだ",
  "After the setback on the moon laboratory Zeta Cygnus II, we've upped our containment systems and procedures. We're careful to not let any Occasus members have too high clearance, and to have all our engineers check their suggestions for security backdoors. Their help has been useful, but we should not overrely on such.": "月面研究所ゼータ・シグナスIIでの挫折の後、封じ込めシステムと手順を強化した。オカサスのメンバーに高すぎる権限を与えないよう注意し、技術者全員に彼らの提案にセキュリティのバックドアがないか確認させている。彼らの協力は有用だが、過度に依存すべきではない",
  "These human supremacists think that they can borrow our expertise and then throw us away when we're no longer needed. Amateurs. The Hylotl have had countless generations to hone the shiv of our superiority.": "この人間至上主義者どもは、我々の専門知識を借りた後、用済みになれば切り捨てられると思っている。素人め。ハイロトルは数えきれぬ世代にわたって優越性の刃を研ぎ澄ましてきたのだ",
  "(Letheia Facility) Specimen Report": "（レテイア施設）検体報告書",
  "SPECIMEN REPORT #33621A\n\nSpecimen J-11 is an engima to us all, and that's exactly what makes it so promising as a bioweapon. We discovered, almost by accident, that it had the ability to spew fire and extrude spikes from its torso and shoulders the other day. At least, we THINK they're shoulders. Standard condolences letters have been dispatched to the appropriate families.": "検体報告書 #33621A\n\n検体J-11は我々全員にとって謎であり、だからこそ生物兵器として極めて有望なのだ。先日、ほぼ偶然に、J-11が火を吹き、胴体と肩から棘を突出させる能力を持つことを発見した。少なくとも、我々は肩だと*思っている*。所定の弔慰状が関係する家族に送付された",
  "We've ordered maximum containment measures for J-11. There will be no repeat of what happened at Zeta Cygnus II. Enough time and money have already been wasted on setbacks and unfortunate incidents; senior management wants results, and soon. These results are already in sight, but we need to be careful.": "J-11に対して最大限の封じ込め措置を命じた。ゼータ・シグナスIIの二の舞は許されない。挫折や不幸な事故で既に十分な時間と資金が浪費されている。上層部は成果を求めており、しかも早急にだ。成果は既に見えているが、慎重にならねばならない",
  "The most promising - and alarming thing about J-11 is that all of its lifesigns appear to point to the fact that there is something else growing in this monstrous creature - that this beast appears to be a mere chrysalis, and that once whatever it is has fully matured, it will emerge from the lifeless husk in an act of ecdysis. Further examination is definitely warranted.": "J-11について最も有望で、かつ最も不安を覚えるのは、あらゆる生体信号がこの怪物の中で何か別のものが成長していることを示している点だ。この獣は単なる蛹に過ぎず、内部のものが完全に成熟すれば、脱皮によって抜け殻から這い出てくるようだ。さらなる調査が確実に必要である",
  "INTERNAL MEMO #A4839\n\nPlease note that Friday is sushi appreciation day. This is an event organised by management to help non-Hylotl staff better appreciate the roots of our company culture and bond with their fellow employees. Non-essential staff are welcome to take a half-day in the afternoon to attend this excellent event and enjoy themselves.": "内部メモ #A4839\n\n金曜日は寿司鑑賞デーとなりますのでご留意ください。これは経営陣が企画したイベントで、ハイロトル以外のスタッフに当社の企業文化の根底を理解してもらい、同僚との親睦を深めることを目的としています。非必須スタッフは午後から半休を取り、この素晴らしいイベントに参加して楽しんでいただけます",
  "As Letheia employs a large percentage of non-Hylotl staff, we are dedicated to introducing our diverse and womenderful workforce to the joys of Hylotl culture, which many across the universe have enthusiastcally embraced, especially the humans. A screening of the traditional Hylotl favourite, Numi and the Giant Mecha, will be open to all facility staff from 7 pm onwards.": "レテイアはハイロトル以外のスタッフを多く雇用しているため、多様で素晴らしい従業員の皆さんにハイロトル文化の喜びを紹介することに力を入れています。宇宙中の多くの種族、特に人間が熱心に受け入れてくれています。伝統的なハイロトルの名作映画「ヌミと巨大メカ」の上映会を、施設スタッフ全員に午後7時より開放します",
  "While attendance is not mandatory, we sincerely hope that all facility staff will not shame themselves and attend this glorious event which management has carefully put together for your enjoyment. We hope to keep employee morale in good shape, especially considering the unfortunate events of the last three weeks.": "参加は義務ではありませんが、経営陣が皆さんの楽しみのために丹精込めて準備したこの輝かしいイベントに、全施設スタッフが恥をさらすことなく参加されることを心より願っています。過去3週間の不幸な出来事を踏まえ、従業員の士気を良好に保ちたいと考えています",
  "At One with the Shadows": "影と一つに",
  "Likewise, it is believed that butterflies are messengers of the Great Light, and are associated with spectres, demons and their version of Death.": "同様に、蝶は大いなる光の使者と信じられており、亡霊、悪魔、そして彼らの死の概念と結びつけられている。",
  "only during a moonless night, lest any influence of the suns vile power cause ruination of the union. A bride and groom are forbidden from consummating their union if any (even the slightest bit) of sunlight bathes a horizon. Exceptions are made for any mooned night where the satellite is a": "月のない夜にのみ行われる。太陽の邪悪な力の影響が結合を台無しにすることのないように。地平線に（わずかでも）日光が差している場合、新郎新婦は結合を遂行することを禁じられている。衛星が次の状態の月夜は例外が認められる：",
  "this regard. Even creatures that walk on the surface of a planet during the sunlight hours are viewed with absolute disdain and superstitious fear by the more zealous of their kind. Those who do not practice their religions are still distrustful of such creatures, especially those which are particularly fluffy.": "この点で、日光の時間帯に惑星の地表を歩く生物は、より熱狂的な者たちから絶対的な軽蔑と迷信的な恐怖を持って見られる。宗教を実践しない者でもそのような生物を信用しない。特にふわふわしたものは。",
  "'From the Twilight Halls we rose, and to them we shall all return.' ; Such was the wisdom the Elder of the Vyanit Clan imparted to me when I asked him why his people lived in such dark and poisonous places. His meaning was understood only after several weeks among his people.": "「黄昏の広間から我々は起き、そこへ全て還る。」これがヴィアニト族の長老が、なぜ彼の民がこれほど暗く有毒な場所に住むのかと尋ねた時に授けてくれた知恵だった。その意味は彼の民の間で数週間過ごして初めて理解できた。",
  "The Nightar are a curious lot. Their entire culture is rooted around moon phases and darkness, due to their innate sensitivity to all forms of natural light. Similar to the unusual allergy to sunlight some humans (according to documentation) suffer from, a Nightar cannot function properly when": "ナイターは好奇心をそそる集団だ。彼らの文化全体が月の満ち欠けと闇を中心に据えている。あらゆる形の自然光に対する生来の感受性によるものだ。一部の人間が（記録によると）患う日光への異常なアレルギーに似て、ナイターは適切に機能できない：",
  "bathed in the natural light of the sun. This has led to many cultural peculiarities (especially in regards to religion. They are the only known race that villifies solar aspects, rather than deifying them). Take, for instance, their marriage ceremony. It is customary to engage in a 'life-bonding'": "太陽の自然光を浴びて。これは多くの文化的特異性を生んだ（特に宗教に関して。太陽の側面を崇拝するのではなく、悪とする唯一の既知の種族だ）。例えば彼らの結婚式。「生命の絆」を行うのが慣習で、",
  "half-moon or smaller. It is believed that their offspring will be cursed and that their flesh will be 'tanned and as of the leathered beasts that walk the surface'. Note that this does not apply to every single one of them, but most agree with their cultural history in": "第一次接触戦争後の分産池間の領土紛争で母星がほぼ壊滅し、スカスの民は星々の間に出ることを余儀なくされた。本当の導きなしに、宇宙の中で新しい故郷を手探りで探した。多くを見つけた。",
  "The Blade": "刃",
  "This tome details the importance of swords among the Nightar people, circa their Classical era (dated to approximately 2,300 years ago) up to their Imperial era (1,223 years).": "この書物はナイター民における剣の重要性を詳述している。古典時代（約2,300年前）から帝国時代（1,223年前）まで。",
  "Those with the most Tenshae are often seen as Champions of the people, for they bear the most signs of mastery in combat.": "最も多くのテンシャエを持つ者は民の勇者と見なされることが多い。戦闘の熟練の証を最も多く帯びているからだ。",
  "With a homeworld sparse in strong metals, the dawning of warfare saw swords reach a value far beyond that of nearly any known culture (historically speaking, even including Humanity, nothing comes close). Finding enough metal with which to form long-lasting blades was expensive, and led to a strong cultural importance to swords.": "強い金属に乏しい母星で、戦争の黎明はほぼあらゆる既知の文化を超える価値に剣を押し上げた（歴史的に人類を含めてもこれに匹敵するものはない）。長持ちする刃を形成するのに十分な金属を見つけるのは高価で、剣への強い文化的重要性をもたらした。",
  "It was believed that a warrior and his blade were forever bound, and drew strength and power from one another (and could transfer this power back and forth, often observed in ancient rituals known as Conshak). A warrior either passed his weapon on to his child, or was buried with the weapon should no heirs remain to inherit the strength of their father. To take another's blade was a 'shameful act' practiced only by desperate cowards or outcasts.": "戦士と刃は永遠に結ばれ、互いから力とパワーを引き出す（そして移すことができる）と信じられていた",
  "Some blades would pass for hundreds (perhaps even thousands) of years from one hand to the next within a single family (or be won in duels or by war). Even today some swords can be traced back nearly five thousand years! Most of this age have long since passed the point of usefulness due to the natural process of aging or by excessive use in battle. These pieces are largely symbolic in importance, and in many cases are a mark of nobility.": "一部の刃は何百年（おそらく何千年）もの間、一つの家族の中で一人の手から次の手へと渡される（あるいは勝ち取られる）",
  "Every single heirloom blade has one thing in common: A name. If a Nightar carries a sword for longer than a few battles, you can be certain it has been named during a Conshak. Swords permeate many aspects of Nightar society. Duels of leadership are (strangely) still common to this day, and despite advances and exposure to countless": "全ての家宝の刃には一つの共通点がある：名前。ナイターが数回以上の戦闘で剣を持ち続けるなら、コンシャク（命名式）で名付けられたと確信できる。剣はナイター社会の多くの側面に浸透している。指導権の決闘は（不思議なことに）今日でも一般的で、進歩と無数の",
  "other species among the stars they are still quite happy with monarchy as their form of government. The Kingsryche, a ritual of sorts to determine Kingship (Royal Blood is a concept long-eschewed in their system of law), is rendered 'false' unless each contender possesses an adequately smithed (and blooded) blade. This ritual calls on every male that reaches adulthood (14 is considered Adult age among the Nightar) to meet in a designated arena.": "星々の間の他の種族とは異なり、彼らは今でも君主制を政府の形態として満足している。キングスリッチェは",
  "Each will meet with swords drawn. Only he who is unscathed and victorious shall be named Fulgrat (King). Should no victor emerge (any wound disqualifies a warrior) then the Kingsryche is attempted each day until such time as a new Fulgrat can be crowned. Should his rule prove to be a failure, he will eventually be challenged and deposed": "各々が剣を抜いて対峙する。無傷で勝利した者のみがフルグラト（王）と名付けられる。勝者が現れない場合（いかなる傷も",
  "by another. Should he be defeated, it is tradition that he is beheaded by his own blade to echo the shame of his poor rule. The new ruler then takes over, and society carries on. Such is the way of honor. Wounds suffered by Nightar heal in the form of strange scars that seep a black, inky shadow. Known as Tenshae, these are viewed as badges of honor and prowess among warriors.": "別の者に。敗北した場合、恥ずべき統治の反映として自らの刃で斬首されるのが伝統だ。新しい",
  "Darkness, Shadow and Nightmares": "闇と影と悪夢",
  "I doubt many other races would stand the test of time under the ground for so long, without the freedom of open fields and the warmth of a summer day. I get claustrophobia just thinking about it...": "開けた野原の自由も夏の日の温もりもなく、これほど長い間地下で時の試練に耐えられる種族は他にほとんどいないだろう。考えただけで閉所恐怖症になる…",
  "Even the Nightar can fear the dark - their people had to contend with all sorts of unusual creatures in their subterranean homes deep below the surface. The Byak prowled the shadowy places between Baronies, a terror to all but the most skilled among them (and often used as a test for young warriors to prove their value). Legends say that Byak monsters would kidnap the weak among them and siphon their lifeblood slowly until the victim became a Byak themselves, corrupting": "ナイターでさえ闇を恐れることがある — 地下の住居であらゆる種類の珍しい生物と戦わなければならなかった",
  "the blood of their family as well as the purity of their Blades. I later learned that 'Byak' is the Nightar approximation for what we all affectionately refer to as Flesh Reapers, which immediately made it evident that such legends are credible. I wonder, then, what it was like to be a Nightar child in those times hearing tales of nightmare beasts stalking the shadows while being unable to escape into the glory of the sunshine we so take for granted among Humanity.": "家族の血と刃の純粋さも。後に「ビャック」はナイターにとって次のものに相当する言葉だと学んだ",
  "The Arena": "闘技場",
  "The rest is entirely devoted to proper Arena etiquette, dispute settling and Kingsryche rules and regulations, and on the proper observation of honor in all things.": "残りは全て、適切なアリーナの礼儀、紛争解決とキングスリッチのルール・規則、そしてあらゆる事柄における名誉の適切な遵守に捧げられている。",
  "This absolutely enormous tome is three thousand pages of sword study, techniques, patterns, stances and so much more. Truly a wonderful find for a historian or someone looking to learn swordplay in the style of the Nightar. There are entire chapters devoted to proper cleaning of blades, how to remove rust and improve the blade by a process called Shadow-Tempering, and proper resolutions to common problems in their society such as stolen blades and intentional damaging of heirloom weapons.": "この絶対的に巨大な書物は剣術の研究、技法、型、構え等が3000ページにわたる。真に素晴らしい",
  "The Shadow Walkers": "影を歩く者たち",
  "The Nightar are actually pre-disposed to extreme xenophobia at the genetic level. They fear the unknown in ways we don't fully understand. Imagine what it is like to hate and fear sunlight! It is in our ignorance of that life that the Nightar gain their power in the political spectrum. Their dislike of the light keeps them well away from affairs of state for other species, always quiet in the background. At home in the dark, they excel at stealth in ways the rest of us simply cannot match. This has led to them knowing many secrets of the various players in galactic politics >": "ナイターは実際に遺伝子レベルで極端な異種恐怖症の素因を持っている。我々が完全には理解できない方法で未知を恐れる",
  "though they would never disclose this fact (both out of respect and for their own survival). If you cross a Nightar who has taken a keen liking to less 'savory' sorts of work...hire them, before your enemies do. A word of advice: Trade with these people using metal coinage rather than electronic funds, and pay up front. Their people adore metal due to complex socioeconomic reasons on their homeworld.": "この事実を明かすことは決してないだろう（敬意と自己保身の両方から）。武器を手に取ったナイターを怒らせたら",
  "She": "彼女",
  "Any further pressing for information about this Matriarch is met with nothing but silence. I dare not press deeper, as the menfolk have been eyeing me up for the last several days. One faux-pas and I could find myself tossed into a duel I cannot possibly win with one of their highly skilled swordsmen.": "このマトリアークについてさらに情報を求めると沈黙しか返ってこない。これ以上深入りする勇気はない。ここ数日、男たちが私を値踏みしている。一つの失言で、高度な技を持つ剣士との勝ち目のない決闘に放り込まれかねない。",
  "There are mysteries to the Nightar I have recently discovered, though I fought tooth and nail for nearly twenty years to even gain enough trust to ask. I have elected to mark down the information for preservation. It will benefit us all to better understand this enigmatic people and their way of life away from sunlight the rest of us take for granted.": "最近ナイターの謎を発見した。信頼を得るために約20年間歯を食いしばって戦い、ようやく十分な",
  "We non-Nightar have often wondered why the Fulgrat, despite being publicly referred to as their leader, has nothing whatsoever to do with territorial disputes, economics, trade or lawmaking...or any true requirements to keep a civilization going. The reason is simple:  The Fulgrat is their military General only. The true political pull among the Nightar comes from the females.": "非ナイターの我々はしばしば疑問に思ってきた。フルグラトは公には指導者と呼ばれるにもかかわらず、なぜ",
  "More specifically, from She, the Great Matriarch, Avemnedara, Mistress of the Way...many names are given to She that Rules. The womenfolk are the only ones permitted to speak of her, or even refer to her. Males who do so must be cleansed through ritual combat followed by Conshak, a 'transfer of energy' from Beyond and into the warrior.": "より正確には、偉大なるマトリアーク、道の女主人アヴェムネダラ…支配する彼女には多くの名が与えられている。女性たちは",
  "How the current Matriarch is chosen is completely unknown, as the women would never tell a male such as myself how their most private sisterhood operates. They speak only that she is the Word, and the Guide, and that Her way is the true path. Through She, they are One. So long as ones fealty is sworn to Her the Burrow is safe. This seems to be sufficient explanation to them.": "現在のマトリアークがどう選ばれるかは完全に不明。女性たちは私のような男性に最も私的な",
  "Nightar Shadow-Casting": "ナイター族の影術",
  "Once he had completed his...meditation, I suppose you could call it...once that was completed he was able to forge a weapon directly from shadows and somehow solidify them into a weapon.": "彼が…瞑想とでも呼ぶべきか…それを完了すると、影から直接武器を鍛造し、何らかの方法でそれを武器として固体化することができた。",
  "The Nightar themselves aren't even sure how it is they can pull energy directly from shadows, and effectively assume it must therefore be Divine in nature. Conventional belief is that 'She' (whoever this might be is unknown) is responsible for their 'Gift of Shadow' and bestows upon their people the very ability to speak with the darkness of the void. This strange ability lets them directly affect themselves": "ナイター自身も影から直接エネルギーを引き出す方法を確信していない。そこに何かがあるに違いないと推測するしかない",
  "or others through control of (somehow, against all reason) shadows. I also believe it is likewise the very reason they are cursed with severe allergy to light. Nature (or science) doing a balancing act is far from rare throughout the galaxy. Whatever the case, it is truly amazing. I've seen one of their warriors use this ability before, and it was breathtaking.": "あるいは（理性に反して）影の制御を通じて他者を操る。同様に彼らが呪われている理由もこれだと信じている",
  "Honor": "名誉",
  "This book is 266 pages in length, and details the various rules that govern the Honor code of the Nightar people. It seems that nearly everything they do is subject to this code, in some small way. There are even tenets dictating proper honor during mealtimes. This seems rather absurd.": "この本は266ページで、ナイター民族の名誉の規範を支配する様々な規則を詳述している。彼らが行うほぼ全てのことが何らかの形でこの規範に従うようだ。食事中の適切な名誉を定める教義すらある。かなり馬鹿げているように思える。",
  "The Matriarch": "女王",
  "Come gather around the fire\n\nI'll tell you all a tale\n\nThe day she came to power\n\nOur lives forever changed\n\n\nNever before a darkness like this have we seen\n\nNo end to suffering\n\nAll hail our mighty queen\n\n\nThere's no hiding from her\n\nShe sees everything\n\nRules with the iron fist\n\nYou know she is the matriarch\n\n\nShe'll eat your heart\n\n\nI've heard it said \n\nThat she can melt you with her eyes\n\nAnd out her fingers spits a burning liquid fire\n\n\nWithout a single word you'll fall under her spell\n\nAnd rip yourself apart with your bare hands\n\nWhile marching to her bell": "さあ火の周りに集まれ\n\n語って聞かせよう\n\nあの方が権力を手にした日\n\n我らの生活は永遠に変わった\n\n\nこれほどの闇は見たことがない\n\n苦しみに終わりなし\n\n偉大なる女王に万歳を\n\n\nあの方から隠れる術はない\n\n全てをお見通しだ\n\n鉄の拳で支配する\n\nそう、あの方こそ女王なのだ\n\n\nあの方はお前の心臓を喰らう\n\n\n聞くところによれば\n\nあの方は眼差しで人を溶かせるという\n\nその指先からは灼熱の炎が迸る\n\n\n一言も発せずしてお前は呪縛に落ち\n\n素手で自らを引き裂きながら\n\nあの方の鐘の音に合わせて行進する",
  "There's no rising above\n\nShe drowns everything\n\nFreedom doesn't exist\n\nYou can't resist\n\n\nThe matriarch\n\n\nYou won't get far\n\n\nOh, she brings nightmares to life\n\nThe foulmost twisted kind\n\nAnd when you beg to die\n\nShe glorifies": "立ち上がる術はない\n\nあの方は全てを沈める\n\n自由など存在しない\n\n抗うことはできない\n\n\n女王\n\n\n逃げられはしない\n\n\nああ、あの方は悪夢に命を吹き込む\n\n最も忌まわしく歪んだ類の悪夢に\n\nそして死を懇願すれば\n\nあの方はそれすら称える",
  "Fear of the Light": "光への恐怖",
  "Imagine having a surface city on a Penumbra planet that would be scorched to cinders every season? Yet if this were the case it would give reason to flee underground and never return.": "ペナンブラの惑星で毎シーズン灰燼に帰す地表都市を想像してみろ。しかしそうであれば、地下に逃げて二度と戻らない理由になるだろう。",
  "it is unlikely that this would cause a gross cultural terror of the level we see. Instead, I posit that some form of atmospheric effect, perhaps unique to their homeworld, is responsible. Perhaps during their planets history, a hole in the ozone formed. If this were the case, and the planetary rotation led": "我々が見るレベルの文化的恐怖を引き起こす可能性は低い。代わりに、おそらく母星特有の何らかの大気効果が原因だと推測する。おそらく惑星の歴史の中でオゾン層に穴が開き、惑星の自転が次のような事態を招いた場合：",
  "to this hole moving across the heavens to shine upon the world below, there would be a concentrated beam of light that could quite literally scorch entire regions on a seasonal basis. The effect this would have on culture and development is beyond doubt, as it would also render the surface nearly unlivable.": "この穴が天空を横切って下の世界を照らすとなれば、季節ごとに文字通り地域全体を焦がしうる集中光線が生じるだろう。これが文化と発展に与える影響は疑いなく、地表をほぼ居住不可能にもするだろう。",
  "Where did the Nightar develop such overwhelming fear of the unknown, and light? While it is true that there is precedent due to their rather unfortunate reaction to direct sunlight (its lethal to several branches of their lineage, though merely toxic and causes reactions similar to anaphylaxis in most),": "ナイターはどこでこれほど圧倒的な未知への恐怖と光への恐怖を発達させたのか？直射日光への反応（いくつかの血統には致命的で、ほとんどではアナフィラキシーに似た反応を引き起こす毒性がある）に前例があるのは確かだが、",
  "Mask of Death": "死の仮面",
  "The white mask of the Nightar warrior should be observed very carefully. There are many reasons to this, the most visible being this: the more plain the mask, the more skilled the warrior. The highest ranked among their kind wear one that is plain white, with only narrow slits for eyes.": "ナイター戦士の白い仮面は非常に注意深く観察すべきだ。多くの理由があるが、最も明白なのは：仮面が質素であるほど、戦士はより熟練している。最高位の者は目のための細いスリットのみの真っ白な仮面を着ける。",
  "The lower the rank of the warrior, the more vibrant the mask will become. Unblooded warriors (those with no battlefield experience) instead wear a black mask adorned with a singular blue stripe in the center. Their low rank also means they serve as envoys to the galaxy at large.": "戦士の階級が低いほど仮面は鮮やかになる。未血の戦士（戦場経験なし）は代わりに中央に青い縞1本が入った黒い仮面を着ける。低い階級は銀河全体への使者としても機能することを意味する。",
  "Low-ranked warriors are permitted to socialize with whom they please, though doing so with too much frequency will earn them the title of Vilmaehkt. This is a grave insult, meaning Red-Blood. On their world, due to low oxygen, their blood is blue. A Vilmaehkt is a 'filthy outsider', unworthy.": "低位の戦士は自由に交流が許されるが、頻繁すぎるとヴィルマエクトの称号を得ることになる。これは重大な侮辱で「赤い血」を意味する。彼らの世界では低酸素のため血は青い。ヴィルマエクトは「汚れた部外者」、価値なき者だ。",
  "Those among the top 200 warriors do not communicate with anyone that is not of their race. Ever. Their code forbids any form of verbal congress outside of their people, no matter the reason. They will, however, communicate with gestures using head, limbs and digits.": "上位200人の戦士は自分の種族以外の誰とも通信しない。決して。彼らの掟は理由を問わず民族外でのあらゆる形の口頭交流を禁じる。ただし頭、四肢、指を使ったジェスチャーで通信する。",
  "The Pharitu Homeworld": "ファリトゥの母星",
  "and most that have attempted to do so have met an ill end. For those wishing to play at diplomacy with this species: invite them to -you- instead. It beats being eradicated via exceptionally devastating electric discharges.": "そうしようとした者のほとんどは悲惨な最期を遂げた。この種族と外交ごっこをしたい者へ：代わりに彼らを自分のところに招け。壊滅的な電撃で殲滅されるよりはましだ。",
  "only real exception to this, and even they have issues with the atmospheric conditions. In fact, so hostile is the environment that even the Pharitu themselves stick to subterranean regions except during very specific weather conditions (more on this later, as this is an entire": "唯一の例外であり、彼らさえ大気条件に問題がある。実際、環境はあまりに過酷でファリトゥ自身も非常に特定の気象条件以外は地下地域にとどまる（これについては後述するが、これは一つの章を成す",
  "The homeworld of the unusual race known as the Pharitu is a hostile and hellish place, where survival on the surface is nearly impossible for any other known intelligent species. Extremophiles able to withstand vast electric discharges fatal to most species are the": "ファリトゥとして知られる珍しい種族の母星は、地表での生存が他のほぼ全ての知的種族にとって不可能に近い敵対的で地獄のような場所だ。ほとんどの種族に致命的な大量の電撃に耐えられる極限環境生物こそが",
  "chapter in and of itself). Few species can truly appreciate the toil of their daily existence (less problematic now than it was millenia ago). Suffice to say, nearly nobody has ever visited this world due to most technology being at great risk of overloading in the atmosphere,": "それ自体が一つの章を成す）。彼らの日常の苦労を真に理解できる種族はほとんどいない（数千年前よりは問題が少なくなったが）。十分に言えば、ほとんどの技術が大気中で過負荷になるリスクが高いため、この世界を訪れた者はほぼいない。",
  "Pharitu Life, Part I": "ファリトゥの生活 第I部",
  "Forced underground just to survive, the Pharitu did indeed begin to change. Over the course of only a few thousand years, they begin to exhibit unusual capabilities that have thus far not been replicated by any known creatures in the galaxy.": "生き延びるためだけに地下に追いやられたファリトゥは確かに変化し始めた。わずか数千年のうちに、銀河の既知のどの生物にもまだ再現されていない異常な能力を示し始めた。",
  "Their minds possess exceptional powers capable of projecting through most stone when fueled by energy from their Shakta, the natural gem formations that contain the essence which fuels their lives. Through this energy they can 'cut' into stone": "彼らの精神はシャクタ — 生命の糧となるエッセンスを含む天然の宝石形成物 — からのエネルギーで駆動される時、ほとんどの石を透過して投射できる異常な力を持つ。このエネルギーを通じて石を「切る」ことができる",
  "allowing them the ability to shape it as no other known species can. Stories telling of the beauty these beings are able to create through sculpture cannot be overstated: what they can create borders on the impossible.": "他のどの既知の種族にもできない方法で形作る能力を与える。彫刻を通じてこの存在が生み出せる美しさの物語は誇張のしようがない：彼らが創造できるものは不可能との境界にある。",
  "The Pharitu in ancient times had it rough. Their world was once calm, but due to unknown geological causes it moprhed into one of the most electrically potent places in the known universe. To stand a chance of survival the species was forced to adapt rapidly or face certain extinction.": "古代のファリトゥは困難な状況にあった。かつて穏やかだった世界が未知の地質学的原因で既知の宇宙で最も電気的に強力な場所の一つに変貌した。生存のチャンスを得るため、種族は急速に適応するか絶滅に直面するかを迫られた。",
  "Pharitu Life, Part II": "ファリトゥの生活 第II部",
  "should they ever need to draw forth the energy therein to restore themselves.": "自らを回復するためにその中のエネルギーを引き出す必要が生じた場合に備えて。",
  "As time wore on, they learned to harness the power of their Shakta and formed societies with the aid of this power: they learned that through a group-think, they could literally turn stone into nearly impenetrable material capable of withstanding the electricity that for so": "時が経つにつれ、シャクタの力を利用することを学び、この力の助けで社会を形成した。集団思考を通じて、文字通り石をほぼ侵入不可能な素材に変えられることを学んだ。長い間脅威だった電気に耐えられる素材に。",
  "long had threatened their safety. Now, their world is covered in bastions of stone craftsmanship the galaxy has never before seen; This led to a rennaisance among their species and has earned them a reputation as the foremost craftsmen in the known universe. If you need": "ヘリオンは予想と違った。穏やかで落ち着いていた。名前はヒシェスで、私の母を知っていると言った。母が亡くなった時そこにいたと。それが私の思っている意味かと聞いた。彼は首を振り、目に悲しみが見えた気がした。",
  "it built to last, then you find a group of Pharitu willing to sell their services. This comes at a price, however - Pharitu have no use for conventional money. Gems are their currency. The rarer, the better. The reason for this is due to their need to constantly fuel their": "長持ちするように作られている。ファリトゥのグループがサービスを売る気があれば見つけるだろう。しかし代価がある — ファリトゥは従来の金には用がない。宝石が通貨だ。稀少であるほど良い。これは常にシャクタを補充する必要があるためだ",
  "Shakta, or risk death or insanity. How is this achieved, you wonder? Well, my friend ... this is where things get complicated. I mentioned weather earlier, and that is where we must now return. You see, there are storms on their world which they call Highstorms. On the": "不可能なものに出会った。話す金属。キルホスは他の民族が金属民族を作り、金属民族が覚えていないだけだと言った。我々は多くのことを考える：金属の男はどうやって赤ちゃんを作る？肉部分なし、卵なし、交尾なし。赤ちゃんはどこ？どうやって増える？",
  "surface, these rage like a deadly tempest, threatening to tear even mountains down. But with these storms comes energy. And this energy can be harnessed to infuse gemstones with power they are able to siphon into their own bodies. Their food. The more condensed and rare": "もちろん、この素材のことをこれまで聞いたことがないだろう。彼らは真実を知られたくないのだ。知識省の上層部で働いていた者から聞いた：彼らはこの奇妙な元素が我々の知る現実を超越する能力があると理論づけている。",
  "the gem, the greater the energy it can hold. And so, on Highstorm days, Pharitu will tunnel towards the surface. There, they will lay their most treasured gemstones, returning later to gather them once the storm has died down. They then carry them wherever they travel": "宝石が大きいほど、蓄えられるエネルギーも大きい。そしてハイストームの日にはファリトゥは地表に向かってトンネルを掘る。最も大切な宝石を置き、嵐が収まった後に回収する。そして旅する先どこにでも持っていく。",
  "Pharitu Space Travel, Part I": "ファリトゥの宇宙旅行 第I部",
  "of need for standard pixels. Should they find themselves without coin, however, they -always- have gems on hand to sell (though most are loath to do so unless absolutely necessary).": "標準ピクセルの必要性について。しかし通貨がなくなった場合、彼らは常に売るための宝石を手元に持っている（ただし絶対に必要でない限りほとんどの者は売りたがらない）。",
  "As for their first forays into space, we should be envious. Using their Shakta, a Pharitu is able to shape more than just stone. It turns out they are capable psionics, and can utilise these 'powers' to communicate into the minds of others via telepathy (unsettling": "宇宙への最初の進出については羨ましくなるべきだ。シャクタを使えば、ファリトゥは石以上のものを形成できる。彼らは優れた超能力者であり、これらの「力」を使ってテレパシーで他者の精神に通信できる（不穏な",
  "but that is how every Pharitu communicates with others), or with each other over extreme distances (at great drain to their Shakta, mind you) shape stone and metal, and even create constructs of solid matter capable of acting as fuel for ships - ships, made of material": "船を探索していると、「立入禁止」の看板と壊れやすい精密機器への警告が記された誰かの個人研究室を発見した。強引に入り込み、面白そうなものを全ていじり始めた。",
  "they themselves moulded with their minds. Most use standard metals and stones out of simple access to materials, but wealthier Pharitu (or ones with abnormally large Shakta) are keen on creating ships out of less common materials. It is not unheard of to see ships made of": "彼ら自身が心で形成した素材から作られた船だ。ほとんどは素材へのアクセスの簡便さから標準的な金属と石を使うが、裕福なファリトゥ（または異常に大きなシャクタを持つ者）はより珍しい素材で船を作ることを好む。次のような素材の船も珍しくない：",
  "exotic materials found on other worlds through their travels. I once met one who had created a ship entirely from wood and seashells. While they -can- propel their ships with their Shakta, most prefer standard methods to save them the need to constantly eat (I can imagine how": "旅の途中で他の世界で見つけた異国の素材から。木と貝殻だけで船を作った者に会ったことがある。シャクタで船を推進できるが、常に食べる必要を省くため、ほとんどは標準的な方法を好む（どれだけ必要かを想像すれば",
  "aggravating it would be to need thousands of pounds of gemstones just to fuel a short foray among the stars). Thus, they are keen to trade on the galactic market to obtain parts needed to create 'ordinary' ship parts. This is not too big a hassle for them due to their lack": "星々への短い遠征のためだけに数千ポンドの宝石が必要なのはどれほど苛立たしいか想像してほしい）。そのため、彼らは銀河市場で「普通の」船の部品を作るのに必要な部品を入手するため取引することに熱心だ。これは彼らにとって大きな問題ではない。なぜなら",
  "Pharitu Space Travel, Part II": "ファリトゥの宇宙旅行 第II部",
  "is no possible way for this to be acheived, and that there must be some secret the Pharitu are not sharing to completing the process. We'll likely never know the secret, and virtually all attempts at getting this race to share it have failed.": "これが達成される可能な方法はなく、プロセスを完了するためにファリトゥが共有していない何らかの秘密があるに違いない。秘密を知ることはおそらくないだろうし、この種族に共有させるほぼ全ての試みは失敗している。",
  "Interestingly, Pharitu can supercharge particular crystals to act as a fuel source for ships as well as shape it into protective coating able to withstand even the most hostile cosmic environments. Thanks to this material they are able to traverse through": "興味深いことに、ファリトゥは特定のクリスタルを過充電して船の燃料源として機能させたり、最も過酷な宇宙環境にも耐える保護コーティングに成形できる。この素材のおかげで彼らは次の環境を横断できる：",
  "nebulae that would prove lethal to most other races (even X'i are not capable of resistance in this degree!). No other species has learned the secret to the production of this nearly magical mineral despite every effort to do so. Some even claim that there": "ほとんどの他の種族には致命的な星雲（シィですらこの程度の耐性はない！）を横断できる。あらゆる努力にもかかわらず、この近魔法的鉱物の生産の秘密を学んだ種族は他にいない。中には存在するとさえ主張する者もいる",
  "Pharitu Highstorms": "ファリトゥのハイストーム",
  "It should be noted that Highstorms are not the only thing that can refill the power into their gemstones; harsh weather on most worlds can provide the means to do so albeit at a severely reduced rate. Typically, the more dangerous the planet the more effective this is.": "対象は男性、約32歳。外見にもかかわらず、遺伝子検査で疑いなく…ペグラシであることが確認された。記録のため、これは発見時の状態であり、いかなる改ざんも行われていない。あなたが見ているものは本物だ。",
  "Slow To Act": "行動が遅い",
  "mind and communicate directly to you via telepathy. There is no need for a translator, as far as we have ever seen. This communication appears to be flawless with any species they choose to speak to, including even Thelusians and Tenebrhae.": "テレパシーで直接あなたに通信する精神を持つ。我々が見てきた限り翻訳機は不要。この通信はテルシアンやテネブレを含め、彼らが話しかける全ての種族と完璧に機能するようだ。",
  "wrong tunneling gesture could cause a catastrophic collapse). Some have whispered that their psionic capabilities include the ability to see (in a limited capacity) into the future. This has led to fear and misunderstanding of them among many of the other races, moreso the younger": "間違ったトンネル掘りの仕草は壊滅的な崩壊を引き起こしうる）。彼らの超能力に（限られた範囲で）未来を見る能力が含まれるとささやく者もいる。これは他の多くの種族、特に若い種族の間での恐れと誤解を招いている",
  "ones like Fenerox and Humans. However, if this is true no Pharitu has confirmed it. In order to directly communicate with a Pharitu, there are requirements to be met. First, you must have earned their trust. In and of itself, this is a challenge. They are not quick to trust, and": "フェネロックスや人間のような存在に。しかしこれが本当でも確認したファリトゥはいない。ファリトゥと直接通信するには条件を満たす必要がある。まず信頼を得なければならない。これ自体が挑戦だ。彼らは簡単に信用しない。",
  "view 'fast' races with caution, for hasty decisions can lead to bad ends (at least by their perspective). Once you do earn their trust, however, you will know it immediately. They will offer an infused gemstone. If you accept, they will be able to channel their Shakta into your own": "「速い」種族を警戒して見る。性急な決断は悪い結末につながりうるからだ（少なくとも彼らの観点では）。しかし信頼を得れば、すぐに分かる。注入された宝石を差し出す。受け入れれば、彼らのシャクタをあなた自身に注ぐことができるようになる",
  "Pharitu are a 'slow' race in that they rarely rush to accomplish tasks, and are the sort to think of every potential outcome before committing to a decision.  Every act a Pharitu performs is calculated and thought on (likely a holdover from a hostile environment where one": "ファリトゥは「遅い」種族で、タスクを急いで達成することは稀で、決断を下す前に全ての潜在的な結果を考えるタイプだ。ファリトゥの全ての行動は計算され熟慮される（おそらく過酷な環境の名残で、一つの",
  "Ish'k Nevass": "イシュク・ネヴァス",
  "<Thankfully, translators are available for some Precursor language. While still spotty, you can glean that this is an important find. Continuing translation:>": "<幸い、一部の先駆者の言語には翻訳機が使える。まだ不完全だが、これが重要な発見であることは読み取れる。翻訳続行：>",
  "Entry 4: Should this record reach any species that follows in our footsteps: Do not attempt ^red;<unknown>^reset; at Delta Freya II. This world is tainted, and we dare not share why. Under no circumstances should you explore this world. Doom awaits.": "記録4：我々の足跡をたどる種族にこの記録が届いたなら：デルタフレイヤIIで^red;<不明>^reset;を試みるな。この世界は汚染されており、理由は共有できない。いかなる状況でもこの世界を探索するな。滅びが待っている。",
  "Entry 3: ^red;<unknown>^reset; the Proletariat! Because of their insistence on experiments, we have ^red;<unknown>^reset; the people! The portal is stable and growing at a geometric rate, but it no longer goes where it should. Nothing seems to affect it. Desperation may soon give way to ^red;<unknown>^reset;.": "記録3：プロレタリアートを^red;<不明>^reset;！実験への固執のせいで、我々は民衆を^red;<不明>^reset;してしまった！ポータルは安定して幾何学的に成長しているが、もはや行くべき場所に通じない。何も影響を与えられないようだ。絶望はまもなく^red;<不明>^reset;に道を譲るかもしれない。",
  "Entry 1: We have at long last ^red;<unknown>^reset; the threshold. Through lacing the singularity with ^red;<unknown>^reset; we have managed to cross through. Without the Core, this would not have been possible. TK-7A Test subject appears to retain normal faculties. We may finally be able to return to our universe.": "記録1：ついに^red;<不明>^reset;の閾値を超えた。特異点に^red;<不明>^reset;を施すことで横断に成功した。コアなしでは不可能だっただろう。TK-7A被験者は正常な能力を維持しているようだ。ついに我々の宇宙に帰還できるかもしれない。",
  "Entry 2: Carefully resyncing the ^red;<unknown>^reset; formula has gained us further insight into the new ^red;<unknown>^reset;. The portal, unfortunately, is unstable. Despite our efforts at ^red;<unknown>^reset;, it appears to resist becoming self-sustaining. Unfortunate, but not unexpected.": "記録2：^red;<不明>^reset;の公式を慎重に再同期することで、新しい^red;<不明>^reset;についてさらなる洞察を得た。ポータルは残念ながら不安定だ。^red;<不明>^reset;への努力にもかかわらず、自己維持するのを拒んでいるようだ。残念だが、予想外ではない。",
  "Hendraat Il": "ヘンドラート・イル",
  "<Translation: We did it. We crossed over into a new universe. Unfortunately...we are now stuck here due to a rather unfortunate problem with the Core. We will need to locate an equivalent power source in this universe in order to return. Efforts are already underway.>": "半月またはそれ以下。子孫は呪われ、肉は「地表を歩く革の獣のように日焼けする」と信じられている。これは全ての者に当てはまるわけではないが、ほとんどが文化的歴史に同意している",
  "<We have seeded the first Proto-World. An interesting bi-product is a new form of...dare I call it metal? It has similar properties. We have deemed it Protocite. It seems exceptionally well suited to energy transference. It should be mentioned that unlike most ore, however, our people cannot digest it. Do not eat this metal.>": "<我々は最初のプロトワールドに種を蒔いた。興味深い副産物として新しい形の…金属と呼んでいいのだろうか？似た特性を持つ。プロトサイトと名付けた。エネルギー伝達に非常に適しているようだ。ほとんどの鉱石と異なり我々の民はこれを消化できない点に注意。この金属を食べるな。>",
  "<Should you disregard the previous warning and ingest this metal, know that it will very swiftly rework your internal biology. You will become a hollow shell of your former self, and eventually completely transform into a nameless mutant immune to the ravages of time. You will effectively become a brain-dead husk for eternity.>": "<前の警告を無視してこの金属を摂取するなら、内部の生物学が非常に急速に作り変えられることを知れ。かつての自分の空洞になり、やがて完全に無名の変異体に変貌する。時間の荒廃に免疫を持つ。事実上、永遠に脳死の殻となる。>",
  "Shasa Uru Venddi": "シャサ・ウル・ヴェンディ",
  "Our greatest triumph...no, our greatest joy! At long last we have created the perfect servitor race. A blend of avian and reptilian traits, we've fortified them with non-carbon based cells. This should allow them to survive on the harsh outer rim worlds we are seeding with their genes.": "我々の最大の勝利…いや、最大の喜び！ついに完璧な奉仕種族を作り上げた。鳥類と爬虫類の特徴を融合し、非炭素ベースの細胞で強化した。これにより遺伝子を蒔いている過酷な外縁世界で生き延びられるはずだ。",
  "Nature, on the other hand, had other ideas. They are rising up and revolting now, refusing our commands and worse...they are angry about it. While still the ideal candidate species, they have been unable to facilitate our requirements for construction on the Generator. Recommend expunging genes through purge.": "しかし自然には別の考えがあった。今や蜂起し反乱している。命令を拒否し、さらに悪いことに…怒っている。依然として理想的な候補種族ではあるが、発電機の建設要件を満たすことができなくなった。遺伝子のパージによる抹消を推奨する。",
  "They say we should name them, but I deemed that most unwise. At least, not until they have earned it. A fledgeling race still learning to be a species, these beings should provide us with the extra labor we require if the Generator is to be created in any decent period of time. With our physical bodies beginning to erode...time is precious.": "名前をつけるべきだと言うが、最も賢明ではないと判断した。少なくとも、それに値するまでは。まだ歩き方を学んでいるひよっこの種族に",
  "<this book appears to span centuries. There are countless entries about this unnamed species they created , but none that give anything useful until roughly 824 years after the first entry.> It was assumed they would retain their docile traits, as we specifically erased the capacity for anger and rage in the initial generations.": "<この本は何世紀にもわたるようだ。彼らが作ったこの無名の種族についての無数の記述があるが、最初の記述から約824年後まで役立つものはない。> 初期の世代で怒りと激怒の能力を特に消去したため、従順な特性を保持すると想定されていた。",
  "The purge has failed! Somehow, they have taken control of the command vessels. I suspect inusurrection, most likely from the Naturalist caste. They sympathize with the plight of the Servants. Why they would side with fuzzy flying...things...is beyond me. We have been forced out of the system, and command has instructed us to simply abandon it, leaving the servants to their own devices.": "パージは失敗した！何とか彼らが指揮艦を掌握した。反乱を疑う、おそらくナチュラルからの",
  "Soscalari": "ソスカラリ",
  "Subject 552 has exhibited no signs of the mutagen. Artificer Voxlaar recommends releasing the specimen into a native population somewhere in order to observe how it thrives or perishes in a new ecosystem. I have seconded, and Yattak has thirded. Experiment 442 begins at dawn.": "標本552は変異原の兆候を示していない。技師ヴォクスラールは標本をどこかの原生個体群に放して新しい生態系でどう繁栄または滅ぶか観察することを推奨。私が賛成し、ヤッタクが三番目に同意。実験442は夜明けに開始する。",
  "Fourteen cycles have passed since our experiment began, and in that time the specimen has not only thrived, but has taken to birthing young via parasitic infection in the pain-center of victims. No mutagen has resurfaced in subsequent generations. Experiment 442 successful.": "実験開始から14サイクルが経過し、その間に標本は繁栄しただけでなく、被害者の痛覚中枢への寄生感染で子を産み始めた。後の世代で変異原は再表面化しなかった。実験442成功。",
  "Yitep Kli": "イテプ・クリ",
  "These furry creatures seem to occur in abundance in this quadrant, and in so many varieties. We remain uncertain on the functional need for fur when other means of adaptation are far more viable. We shall continue to observe, knowing our temperature-neutral circulatory system is clearly superior to that of all life within this galaxy.": "これらの毛むくじゃらの生物はこの象限に豊富に生息し、非常に多くの種類がある。他の適応手段がはるかに有効である時に毛皮の機能的必要性が不確かだ。温度中立の循環系が銀河内の全生命より明らかに優れていると知りつつ、観察を続ける。",
  "Jjkar Vikthos": "ジカール・ヴィクトス",
  "After only 20 generations we have observed them not only develop sapience on their own, but also develop more and more complex tools. The downside is that the length of time chosen for the experiment is much too long, and our empires expansion in this dimension has effectively limited our funding. We are unable to wait...so we have opted to speed things up a tad.": "わずか20世代で、彼らが自ら知性を発達させただけでなく、ますます複雑な道具を開発するのを観察した",
  "Rather than allow a further 20 generations (510 additional rotations around the sun) to pass uninfluenced, we have gone ahead and shown our little slave-race the secrets of the universe. We left behind a drone and three combat units, completely deactivated. We have estimated a 500% increase in technological advancement within 20 years time. These once docile fuzzy raptors will soon be truly entertaining.": "さらに20世代（太陽の周りを510回転）が影響なく過ぎるのを許すのではなく、先に進んで",
  "Hyac Pliades": "ヒアク・プリアデス",
  "Dense materials can easily be repurposed via the Viadarra Engine, should we find ourselves low on materials on the opposite side of this unusual rift in space-time. We have decided to breach it tomorrow, as the potential for exploration is too great to pass up. We are, of course, bringing the Armada as well. We cannot risk splitting our society in two.": "高密度素材はヴィアダラエンジンで容易に再利用できる。この珍しいものの反対側で素材が不足した場合",
  "Initial scouting parties report favorable results. We are therefore authorizing full mobilization, and moving the Empire into the breach. We are going to risk the Core, as well. We may require the near-limitless power it offers. The Regent insists that it is in the best interests of the Hegemony for this to proceed without question. And so, we obey.": "初期偵察隊が好ましい結果を報告。したがって全面動員を承認し、帝国を突破口に移動させる。我々は",
  "Bilgret Shinxax": "ビルグレット・シンザックス",
  "Transitioning into a new dimension was probably the best thing we could have possibly hoped for for the Hegemony. Not only has this effectively stopped the in-fighting among the castes, but the Great Houses are even willing to listen to each other now...because every last one of them is looking to us for leadership. Their faith in the empire has allowed our power to truly expand.": "新しい次元への移行はおそらく覇権にとって望み得る最善のことだった。これにより",
  "As of today, we are moving forwards with the new initiatives. Specifically, the new Scientific Priority Doctrine and all of the various laws and regulations related to it. With this change in agenda, our people can move forward into a glorious age of new discovery. This dimension affords us new chances previously unimagined to us as a people!": "本日をもって新しい取り組みを推進する。具体的には、新しい科学的優先教義と様々な法律",
  "Uru Ghek": "ウル・ゲク",
  "Careful experimentation reveals that not only do ^green;the laws of physics^reset; operate completely uniquely in this new universe, but also that we are able to ^orange;directly influence^reset; these forces without the need for any sort of ^red;thaumaturgical^reset; aid! The potential uses are terrifyingly promising!": "慎重な実験により、^green;物理法則^reset;がこの新しい宇宙で完全にユニークに機能するだけでなく、いかなる^red;魔術的^reset;な補助なしでもこれらの力を^orange;直接影響^reset;できることが判明！潜在的な用途は恐ろしいほど有望だ！",
  "Yettas": "イェッタス",
  "<Translation: Yettas, the most delicious of our baked goods, has proven most beneficial in trade negotiations with the Velorin people. It seems that their culture reveres baking as a sacred profession. Leadership has decided this will influence all future trade with them.>": "<翻訳：我々の最も美味しい焼き菓子イェッタスは、ヴェロリン人との貿易交渉で最も有益だと証明された。彼らの文化はパン焼きを神聖な職業として崇めているようだ。指導部はこれが今後のヴェロリンとの全ての取引に影響を与えると決定した。>",
  "Tip Baluur": "ティップ・バルール",
  "<Translation: ^red;<unknown>^reset; and ^red;<unknown>^reset; have begun war in the Nyallapoi sector. It seems that the ^red;<unknown>^reset; are displeased about our recent trade with the Velorin, but are convinced it was the ^red;<unknown>^reset; that brokered the deal. They have never been a bright species.>": "<翻訳：^red;<不明>^reset;と^red;<不明>^reset;がニャラポイセクターで戦争を開始した。^red;<不明>^reset;は我々のヴェロリンとの最近の取引に不満のようだが、取引を仲介したのは^red;<不明>^reset;だと確信している。彼らは決して賢い種族ではなかった。>",
  "Groshk Fremmin": "グロシュク・フレミン",
  "<Translation: The Crucible works! It works! At long last I have unravelled the final piece of the quantum puzzle. It now siphons ^red;<unknown>^reset; directly from the cosmic stream and applies ^red;<unknown>^reset; to the ^red;<unknown>^reset;. Our weapons and armor are now unmatched. The Hegemony be praised!>": "<翻訳：るつぼが動いた！動いた！ついに量子パズルの最後のピースを解き明かした。今や宇宙の流れから直接^red;<不明>^reset;を吸い上げ、^red;<不明>^reset;を^red;<不明>^reset;に適用する。武器と防具は比類なきものとなった。覇権に栄光あれ！>",
  "Vapaj Frekvai": "ヴァパイ・フレクヴァイ",
  "is not meant to know all things. And now our own hubris consumes us forever. If any of my people read this, seek out the cybernetic worlds our forebears created, and join there to flee. Do not fight! They will wipe us out! The Hegemony is wrong, and the proof is staring them in the face!>": "全てを知るようには作られていないのだ。今や我々の傲慢が永遠に我々を蝕む。同胞がこれを読むなら、先祖が作ったサイバネティック世界を探し出し、そこに合流して逃げよ。戦うな！殲滅される！覇権は間違っており、証拠は目の前にある！>",
  "<Translation: First, they did not believe me about ^red;<unknown>^reset;. Then they said I was crazy to even think such a creature could exist. And now they are ^red;<unknown>^reset; right where I told them to avoid. Twice, in fact. Yet here I sit in this cell, awaiting my death due to ^red;<unknown>^reset; lies": "<翻訳：まず^red;<不明>^reset;について信じてもらえなかった。次にそんな生物が存在すると考えること自体が狂っていると言われた。そして今、彼らは^red;<不明>^reset;を私が避けるよう言った場所で行っている。しかも2度も。それなのにここの独房で^red;<不明>^reset;の嘘により死を待っている",
  "while they investigate the very thing that I was told could not exist in this reality. ^red;<unknown>^reset; the Hegemony! They are fathers of lies, and of deceptions. And now they have doomed our people in their greed. In a way, I suppose it is poetic justice for sticking our nose where it doesn't belong. Science": "まさに私がこの現実には存在し得ないと言われたものを調査しているのに。^red;<不明>^reset;覇権を！彼らは嘘の父であり欺瞞の父だ。そして今、貪欲のために我々の民を破滅させた。ある意味、鼻を突っ込むべきでない場所に突っ込んだ報いとも言える詩的正義だ。科学",
  "Ulla Vikt": "ウラ・ヴィクト",
  "<^red;<unknown>^reset; claimed they were coming. He warned us of their point of origin. We mocked him. We imprisoned him. We sentenced him to death for treason. But he was right. We should have listened. Now....now we all die.>": "<^red;<不明>^reset;は彼らが来ると主張した。出発点を警告してくれた。嘲笑した。投獄した。反逆罪で死刑を宣告した。しかし彼は正しかった。聞くべきだった。今…今、全員が死ぬ。>",
  "<^red;<unknown>^reset;, our most revered General, has fallen in battle. Without his mind, I remain uncertain on how we will achieve victory even with our recent discovery of the ^red;<unknown>^reset; technology. Our most dangerous weapons appear to be a mere annoyance to these abominations.>": "<^red;<不明>^reset;、我々の最も崇敬する将軍が戦死した。彼の頭脳なしでは、^red;<不明>^reset;技術を最近発見したにもかかわらず、どうやって勝利を達成するか不確かだ。我々の最も危険な兵器はこれらの忌まわしき者たちにとって単なる厄介ごとに過ぎないようだ。>",
  "<Translation: We are at war. We have no idea who ^red;<unknown>^reset; are or where they came from, but they are a truly horrible race. Their sense of morality is non-existent (perhaps they don't even understand the concept), and the unspeakable atrocities carried out on our people...unimaginable.>": "<翻訳：我々は戦争状態にある。^red;<不明>^reset;が誰でどこから来たか分からないが、真に恐ろしい種族だ。道徳観が存在せず（概念すら理解していないかもしれない）、我々の民に対して行われた言語に絶する残虐行為…想像を絶する。>",
  "Nkia Tellis": "ンキア・テリス",
  "<Translation: We have reason to believe that ^red;<unknown>^reset; has illegally traded with the Shanti against the wishes of the Hegemony. Unfortunately, since the Shanti are a pre-warp civilization our protocol of non-interference requires us to sterilize the world. This is why you obey the Overlords.>": "<翻訳：^red;<不明>^reset;が覇権の意に反してシャンティと違法取引したと信じる理由がある。残念ながら、シャンティはワープ以前の文明であるため、不干渉の議定書により世界の殺菌が必要。これが支配者に従うべき理由だ。>",
  "Asxoti'lo Paggis": "アスコティロ・パギス",
  "<Translation: The Overlords have demanded we head towards the Delta Freya system immediately. Something about a miraculous discovery that shakes the foundations of all that we know. We are dispatching all science vessels within 300 sectors to this location.>": "<翻訳：支配者たちはデルタフレイヤ星系へ即座に向かうよう要求した。我々の知る全ての基盤を揺るがす奇跡的な発見に関することらしい。300セクター以内の全科学船をこの場所に派遣中。>",
  "Delicarellix": "デリカレリックス",
  "<Translation: We've discovered a new race that is unlike any we've seen before. They are savage and primitive, far from being capable of posing a threat to the empire. They don't even have a civilization yet. These plant-things wander about in a near constant state of hunger.>": "<翻訳：以前に見たことのない新しい種族を発見した。野蛮で原始的で、帝国に脅威を与える能力からは程遠い。文明すらない。この植物のような存在はほぼ常に飢えた状態で徘徊している。>",
  "<We continue to monitor these plant-things, and are convinced that they are unable to develop keen intellect without some form of aid. As such, the Overlords have declared them unremarkable. This means exploitation of their world, rather than non-interference, can begin.>": "<我々はこれらの植物型存在を引き続き監視しており、何らかの援助なしには鋭い知性を発達させることができないと確信している。そのため、支配者たちは彼らを取るに足らないと宣言した。これにより不干渉ではなく、彼らの世界の搾取が開始できる。>",
  "<Interestingly enough, the plant-things are *delicious*. While our own native vegetation is tasty, these bipedal creatures are like a dessert platter. Imagine the most tasty Yulashk you've ever eaten. It's better than that. Note however, that flavor is lost if they are deceased. Enjoy the taste while they are alive.>": "シィが古代種スタイルのホログラムにアクセスする方法はよく知られていない。カルティベーターの存在を否定しながら、古い建造物で古代種の技術を使っている。おそらくこれらの存在は我々が当初考えていたよりはるかに古く、古代種と共に生き、彼らの真の姿を知っているのかもしれない？全てとても興奮する。",
  "X'i: Uncovering Truths I": "ズィー族: 真実の発掘 I",
  "I met with the lead diplomat of the X'i earlier this week at our briefing regarding the more recent spate of attacks on the outlying colonies. She goes by the name...perhaps title, I am uncertain... of Risen. She's one of the few that can speak enough Common to communicate with us at all. No X'i has ever been recorded to be taller than her--it? If leaders were chosen by height alone, she'd be a good fit at over 4 meters.": "今週初め、辺境コロニーへの最近の攻撃に関するブリーフィングで、ズィー族の首席外交官と会談した。彼女はリズンという名前...おそらく称号か、定かではないが...で通っている。共通語を十分に話してコミュニケーションが取れる数少ないズィー族の一人だ。彼女——それ？——より背の高いズィー族は記録上存在しない。身長だけでリーダーを選ぶとすれば、4メートル超の彼女はまさに適任だろう",
  "Standing at 12'7'' or 384cm, she towers over our team of shrimpy humans. It's a little imposing. Risen tells tales of how she fought in a war between stars and black holes, and how she helped drive the stars away to save the near-extinct black holes. We aren't quite sure, but we believe the stars may, in fact, be a reference to the Novakid. It wasn't so much what was said, but -how- it was said. If I recall, it was": "12フィート7インチ、つまり384cmの身長で、我々のチビな人間チームを見下ろしている。少々威圧的だ。リズンは星とブラックホールの間の戦争で戦い、絶滅寸前のブラックホールを救うために星を追い払った話を語る。確証はないが、星というのはノヴァキッドを指しているのではないかと考えている。何が語られたかというより、どのように語られたかが重要だ。確か、こうだった——",
  "'The star-children of the First wanted to drive away the anti-children. We aided the anti-children'. However, we can find no record of this conflict in any known galactic database. If it happened it was a long, long time ago.": "「始祖の星の子供たちが反の子供たちを追い払おうとした。我々は反の子供たちを助けた」。しかし、この紛争の記録は既知の銀河データベースのいずれにも見つからない。もし実際に起きたとすれば、それは遥か遥か昔のことだ",
  "I met with the lead diplomat of the X'i earlier this week at our briefing regarding the more recent spate of attacks on the outlying colonies. She goes by the name...perhaps title, I am uncertain... of Risen. She's one of the few that can speak enough Common to communicate with us at all. No X'i has ever been recorded to be taller than her--it? If leaders were chosen by height alone, she'd be a good fit at over 4 meters. Standing at 12'7'' or 384cm, she towers over our team of shrimpy humans. It's a little imposing. Risen tells tales of how she fought in a war between stars and black holes, and how she helped drive the stars away to save the near-extinct black holes. We aren't quite sure, but we believe the stars may, in fact, be a reference to the Novakid. It wasn't so much what was said, but -how- it was said. If I recall, it was :\n\n'The star-children of the First wanted to drive away the anti-children. We aided the anti-children. Their nebulas were safe, and through them came the Birthing'.\n\nHowever, we can find no record of this conflict in any known galactic database. If it happened it was a long, long time ago.": "今週初め、最近の辺境コロニーへの攻撃についての説明会でX'iの主席外交官と会った。彼女はRisen（ライゼン）という名前…おそらく称号かもしれないが、確かではない…を名乗っている。共通語を十分に話せるX'iのうちの数少ない一人だ。これまで誰もX'iとは",
  "X'i Physiology Vol 1": "ズィー族の生理学 Vol.1",
  "Use the codex reader in your Tricorder to read this.": "このデータを閲覧するにはトリコーダーのコーデックスリーダーを使用してください",
  "As for the X'i themselves...how they came to be is, strictly speaking, impossible. They remain the only example of life that is silicon-based even being possible! The radioactive bulbs within them are the sentient part of the being, a consciousness contained within. The plant-like outer body is their self, and it hardens over time until calcifying into mineral-hard 'flesh'. Eventually, generally after death, it becomes graphite. Their actual bodies sprout feather-like hair that is both supple and soft. It appears to be highly resistant to radiation (effectively nullifying it).\nIt is likely the case, then, that without these feathers the X'i would be virtually unable to socialize with the galactic community. Their very presence would make them a hazard to the health of every current intelligent civilization we know about. They pose next to no threat, thankfully, and are valuable members of any team they assist.\n\nWhile they have issues communicating they are outgoing, personable and always ready to help others. Frankly, it's rare to find a group so collectively pleasant to be around. There's a reason for this, however...See, X'i have exceptionally open dietary needs. They can effectively eat whatever they want to sate their near-constant hunger. You will almost never meet a X'i who is not frequently snacking! Without food their cores begin to die down, and this leads to lethargy, weakness and (as is the case with every other race) eventually death. A side-effect of their constant eating is that a good many food types they enjoy (dirt, especially) possess narcotic-like effects on their moods not unlike heavy dopamines. With their pleasure-centers so easily stimulated, it is easy to see why they are pleasant companions.\nUltimately, the X'i are much closer to an organic-inorganic hybrid...a perfect mix of Silicon and Carbon-based life. A homonculus such as this is surely not a purely natural occurrence. I fail to see how in any natural circumstance this specific coincidence of genetics could occur.\n\nShould anyone find a way to explain it, I'm all ears. Until then, I will have no choice but to assume they are the product of third-party intervention. I believe it most likely that this was during their early development before true sentience had been achieved. As to who made them...who can say? The mysteries of the cosmos are vast and terrifying.": "X'i自身については…彼らがどのように誕生したかは、厳密に言えば不可能なことだ。彼らはケイ素ベースの生命体が可能であることの唯一の例として残っている！内部の放射性球根が知覚を持つ部分で、その中に意識が宿っている。植物のような外側の体は",
  "The Hologram from Halcyon 9": "ハルシオン9のホログラム",
  "Use the Codex reader in your Tricorder to read this.": "このコーデックスを閲覧するにはトリコーダーのコーデックスリーダーを使用してください",
  "Recently, we discovered a massive hologram depicting canid-looking beast well over the size of a planet, tucked in the remains of one of the X'i ghost towns. It barely functioned, but the Ancient tech was resilient enough to withstand the eons since it was last used. When activated, the giant hologram appeared, animating and depicting this canine creature making a blessing motion over a series of eight worlds. Light left its body to infuse each of these eight worlds, and this action repeated approximately every 60 seconds thereafter until we deactivated the device.\nWe speculate that this is one of the gods they may have worshipped at one point in time. The translation of its name from runes appears to be ^orange;'ORANA'^reset;, if the paper from our X'ian friend is accurate. With only this to work with we have little other choice than to assume it is, at the very least, usable.\nThe device itself was found while scavenging through a nearly intact X'ian city (if you can call this place a city...I am not sure how best to name it) composed of strange looping patterns of graphite and cobalt merged together to form myriad structures that towered above like skyscrapers but composed of octogonal 'units' that could very well have been individual apartments. What would have passed for windows at some point were now empty portholes devoid of decoration, allowing us to see inside of these strange compartments without much issue.\nCovering nearly all of the structures was a thin layer of an ash-like substance that gave everything the appearance of having been burned in a great conflagration in the ancient past. Samples we took soon dispelled that idea, however. No, instead what we had discovered was a thin film of X'ian remains broken down over millenia into nothing but a fine dust.\nIt's sad when you think about it : The collective accomplishments, memories, knowledge, hopes and dreams, children, brothers and sisters, mothers and fathers, dreams and aspirations...now nothing but dust.\nWe explored much of this city, which in total covered more than 30km of territory. Very little was found that could be used or identified due to the fact that the majority of X'ian creations are made *of* X'ians and had long since decayed. As with all previous forays to locate ancient X'ian lore or technology, this trip met with near total failure. Until the last day.\n\nYou see, we had stumbled onto what appeared to be an arena or stadium (insofar as its shape was concerned). We had prepared to assume it was nothing but a sporting facility until a curious odor struck us. We felt compelled to investigate. Within, a vast field of 'junk' lay, most of it long since decayed. Despite this, a few pieces were intact. One, a statue composed of greenish stone, about the size of a two men. This statue featured a figure of amorphous aquatic nature squatting horribly on a pedestal of sorts. Adorning this statue was a dense script of characters I had not previously seen. Perhaps the ancient language of the X'i? Maybe this figure was one of their deities!\nThe second intact object was a small computer-like device smaller than a Tricorder. While non-functioning, was clearly of X'i design (the familiar vine-like style was apparent). It utilized internal parts for computing that bear no resemblance to anything used in the galactic community. Further study revealed it to be a Protein-based computer. This was a momentous discovery...until it began to decay the second we left orbit.\nThe final object of note was the remains of a single X'i. Resting atop the pile, and clearly killed there, it was unusually intact despite being deceased. Through its torso protruded an enormous spear (length: 3 meters) that anchored it into the refuse pile. It had not reverted to the graphite-like stone typical of their kind, however. It remained pliable as if recently killed. Dating indicated that the figure was more than 200,000 years dead. Upon inspection, the spear returned unusual results: it was made of a strange greenish metal none of us were able to identify. Perhaps whatever this material is prevents the decay of X'i?": "最近、X'iのゴーストタウンの廃墟の中に、惑星の大きさを超える犬に似た獣を描いた巨大なホログラムを発見した。ほとんど機能しなかったが、古代の技術は長い年月を耐え抜いていた。起動させると、巨大なホログラム",
  "X'i: Uncovering Truths II": "シー: 真実の発掘 II",
  "X'i deny the idea of a Cultivator creating the six races. They are staunch advocates of evolution and all it represents scientifically. Studying their history books, we find no mention of a Cultivator, but plenty of mention of a great 'CREATOR'. The name is disputed, though Kenvik Raeis (noted scholar of some repute, having literally written the book on inter-species relations in the Protectorate) believes its name translates to 'Xuveh'.": "シィはカルティベーターが6つの種族を創造したという考えを否定する。進化の熱烈な支持者であり、それが科学的に表すもの全てを支持する",
  "In his latest paper, Kenvik Raeis of the Kirhosi Arkology Confederacy questions the validity of this legend insofar as truth is concerned. It bears all the markers of traditional mythological tales, though there is little doubt that there are direct references to several races directly by name long before space travel would have been possible for many of them. As such, he affirms the common belief that the X'i predate most galactic civilizations as undeniable.": "最新の論文で、キルホシ・アーコロジー連合のケンヴィク・ラエイスはこの伝説の真実性としての妥当性に疑問を呈している",
  "X'i deny the idea of a Cultivator creating the six races. They are staunch advocates of evolution and all it represents scientifically. Studying their history books, we find no mention of a Cultivator, but plenty of mention of a great 'CREATOR'. The name is disputed, though Kenvik Raeis (noted scholar of some repute, having literally written the book on inter-species relations in the Protectorate) believes its name translates to 'Xuveh'. \nIn his latest paper, Kenvik Raeis of the Peglaci Triosin Institute questions the validity of this legend insofar as truth is concerned. It bears all the markers of traditional mythological tales, though there is little doubt that there are direct references to several races directly (by name) long before space travel would have been possible for many of them. As such, he affirms the common belief that the X'i predate most galactic civilizations as undeniable.": "X'iは、栽培者が6つの種族を創造したという考えを否定します。彼らは進化とその科学的な意味を強く支持しています。彼らの歴史書を調べると、栽培者への言及は一切なく、偉大な「創造主（CREATOR）」への言及が多くあります。名称については議論があるものの、Kenvik Raeis（著名な学者）は",
  "X'i: Uncovering Truths III": "ズィー族: 真実の発掘 III",
  "What caused the mass die-off and near extinction of the X'i is a debated mystery to us. Speculations range from invasion to events such as meteor strikes or gamma ray bursts. Whatever happened, nearly 98% were almost simultaneously rendered intert, their cores dying along with them.": "ズィー族の大量死と絶滅寸前にまで追い込まれた原因は、我々にとって議論の尽きない謎である。侵略から隕石衝突やガンマ線バーストまで様々な推測がなされている。何が起きたにせよ、約98%がほぼ同時に不活性化し、核も共に死滅した",
  "I, personally, believe it was a devastating contagious disease in the form of a parasite. By studying some X'i cores that managed to survive the event in recently abandoned ghost towns, I found plenty of small holes that, when scanned, showed a map of unnerving tunnels. Small objects laid within, perhaps eggs, but evaporated when samples were attempted.": "私個人としては、寄生虫の形態をとった壊滅的な伝染病だったと考えている。最近放棄されたゴーストタウンで、あの出来事を生き延びたいくつかのズィー族の核を調べたところ、小さな穴が多数見つかり、スキャンすると不気味なトンネルの地図が現れた。内部には小さな物体——おそらく卵——があったが、サンプルを採取しようとすると蒸発してしまった",
  "With my hypothesis, the only thing I'm missing is the catalyst for this disease. We may be fortunate in uncovering more hidden truths in the coming days as we investigate more dead cities. A single sample is all we need!": "私の仮説で唯一欠けているのは、この病の触媒が何であったかだ。さらに死んだ都市を調査する中で、隠された真実をより多く発見できる幸運に恵まれるかもしれない。必要なのはたった一つのサンプルだけだ！",
  "What caused the mass die-off and near extinction of the X'i is a debated mystery to us. Speculations range from invasion to events such as meteor strikes or gamma ray bursts. Whatever happened, nearly 98% were almost simultaneously rendered intert, their cores dying along with them.\nPersonally, I believe it was a devastating contagious disease in the form of a parasite. By studying some X'i cores that managed to survive the event in recently abandoned ghost towns, I found plenty of small holes that, when scanned, showed a map of unnerving tunnels. Small objects laid within, perhaps eggs, but evaporated when samples were attempted.\nWith my hypothesis, many questions are easily answered. We may be fortunate in uncovering more hidden truths in the coming days as we investigate more dead cities. A single sample is all we need!": "X'iの大量死と準絶滅を引き起こしたものは謎のままだ。侵略から隕石衝突やガンマ線バーストなどのイベントまで、様々な仮説がある。何が起きたにせよ、ほぼ同時に98%近くが活動を停止し、そのコアが命とともに失われた。私は個人的に",
  "X'ian Language": "ズィー族の言語",
  "We are trying to translate the verbal language of the X'i and are failing, for the most part. We do know that their language consists of patterns of weak ultraviolet radiation rather than sound. The clicks and squawks they produce seem to have little effect on what they are saying, and are only there for emphasis. At best, we have a collection of maybe 200 words, but can't pronounce.": "ズィー族の口頭言語の翻訳を試みているが、ほぼ失敗に終わっている。分かっているのは、彼らの言語が音ではなく微弱な紫外線放射のパターンで構成されているということだ。彼らが発するカチカチという音や鳴き声は発言内容にほとんど影響を与えず、強調のためだけに存在するようだ。せいぜい200語ほど収集したが、発音することができない",
  "The actual sounds of their conversation appear to be a curious evolution in their outer shells: When they wish to verbalise sound a thin membrane on the underside of this skin vibrates at ultra-fast frequencies and creates a sound. The frequency itself dictates the pitch. It's quite fascinating. Davin suggests we might try to create a device that can replicate these vibrations rather than rely on our own vocal capabilities when communicating with this unusual race.": "彼らの会話の実際の音は、外殻における興味深い進化の産物のようだ。音声を発したい時、この外皮の裏側にある薄い膜が超高速の周波数で振動し、音を生み出す。周波数そのものが音の高さを決定する。実に魅力的だ。ダヴィンは、この変わった種族とのコミュニケーションにおいて、自分たちの声帯に頼るよりも、これらの振動を再現できるデバイスを作ってみるべきだと提案している",
  "We are trying to translate the verbal language of the X'i and are failing, for the most part. We do know that their language consists of patterns of weak ultraviolet radiation rather than sound. The clicks and squawks they produce seem to have little effect on what they are saying, and are only there for emphasis.  At best, we have a collection of maybe 200 words, but can't pronounce.\nThe actual sounds of their conversation appear to be a curious evolution in their outer shells: When they wish to verbalise sound a thin membrane on the underside of this skin vibrates at ultra-fast frequencies and creates a sound. The frequency itself dictates the pitch. It's quite fascinating. Davin suggests we might try to create a device that can replicate these vibrations rather than rely on our own vocal capabilities when communicating with this unusual race.": "X'iの口頭言語の翻訳を試みているが、ほとんど失敗している。彼らの言語は音ではなく弱い紫外線放射のパターンで構成されていることは分かっている。彼らが発するカチカチやガーという音は、言っていることにほとんど影響を与えず、",
  "Iced Cream?": "アイスクリーム？",
  "July 23rd. Today a X'i offered me a 'sundae'. Flattered, I accepted. She'd given me a bowl of rocks. We have vastly different ideas on what a 'sundae' is. It took breaking three incisors to realize my terrible mistake. It turns out I was misunderstanding their unusual language and was taking a bite out of a rock.": "7月23日。今日、X'iが「サンデー」を差し出してきた。光栄に思い受け取った。石ころを入れた器だった。私たちの「サンデー」に対する概念はまったく異なる。3本の切歯を折って初めて自分の酷い間違いに気がついた。彼らの独特な言語を誤解していて、食事を一口かじったことが判明した",
  "Where are they from?": "彼らはどこから来たのか？",
  "Although the X'i race seems unwilling to divulge their history to organic historians such as us, expeditions into abandoned territory allow us to explore and estimate based on texts left behind. One large abandoned city filled to the brim with mounds of solidified graphite had an unusual journal left behind that appears to mention some": "ズィー族は我々のような有機体の歴史家にその歴史を明かすことに消極的なようだが、放棄された領域への遠征により、残された文書から探索し推測することができる。固化したグラファイトの山で埋め尽くされた大きな放棄都市で、珍しい日誌が見つかり、そこには何らかの",
  "sort of enormous underground monster that fed on X'i and other supposed 'entities'. There was a poor sketch of it, and the only recognizable feature of the animal was a head somehow resembling a Platybelodons from Earth. According to the journal, it used thousands of strawlike tongues to drink the radioactive energy straight out of its prey.": "ズィー族やその他のいわゆる「存在」を捕食する巨大な地下の怪物について記されていたようだ。下手なスケッチが添えられており、その動物の唯一の識別可能な特徴は、地球のプラティベロドンにどこか似た頭部だった。日誌によれば、怪物は数千本のストロー状の舌を使って獲物から放射性エネルギーを直接吸い取ったという",
  "It may also be the culprit behind the mounds of solidified graphite. Of course, there is always the possibility that the graphite mounds are fossilized X'i ancestors. We'll likely know, once we learn how to comprehend the structure of the X'i...and they aren't helpful in this regard.": "固化したグラファイトの山の原因もこの怪物かもしれない。もちろん、グラファイトの山がズィー族の祖先の化石である可能性も常にある。ズィー族の構造を理解する方法を学べば分かるだろうが...彼らはこの点において協力的ではない",
  "Although the X'i race seems unwilling to divulge their history to organic historians such as us, expeditions into abandoned territory allow us to explore and estimate based on texts left behind. One large abandoned city filled to the brim with mounds of solidified graphite had an unusual journal left behind that appears to mention some sort of enormous underground monster that fed on X'i and other supposed 'entities'.\nThere was a poor sketch of it, and the only recognizable feature of the animal was a head somehow resembling a Platybelodons from Earth. According to the journal, it used thousands of strawlike tongues to drink the radioactive energy straight out of its prey.\nIt may also be the culprit behind the mounds of solidified graphite. Of course, there is always the possibility that the graphite mounds are fossilized X'i ancestors. We'll likely know, once we learn how to comprehend the structure of the X'i...and they aren't helpful in this regard.": "X'i種族は有機歴史家の私たちに自分たちの歴史を明かすことを拒んでいるようだが、廃棄された領域への調査隊が残されたテキストを探索・推測することを可能にしている。固まったグラファイトの山が大量に存在する大きな廃棄都市には、珍しい日記が残されていた",
  "X'i Interracial Ties": "シーの異種族間関係",
  "X'i have spent time living around Novakid for longer than any organic race can say. As typical of Novakid, they don't seem to remember much about their relationship with this other race but not one has talked poorly of the X'i. Some have mentioned being fond of a X'ians soft, fluffy feathers. Others say they enjoy the coos a happy X'i makes. Of course,, it isn't prudent to hang around them for long periods of time unless you want to be terminally ill from radiation.": "シィはどの有機種族よりも長くノヴァキッドの近くで暮らしてきた。ノヴァキッドの典型として、彼らは覚えていないようだ",
  "X'i have spent time living around Novakid for longer than any organic race can say. As typical of Novakid, they don't seem to remember much about their relationship with this other race but not one has talked poorly of the X'i. Some have mentioned being fond of a X'ians soft, fluffy feathers. Others say they enjoy the coos a happy X'i makes. Of course, it isn't prudent to hang around them for long periods of time unless you want to be terminally ill from radiation.": "X'iはどんな有機種族よりも長くノヴァキッドの近くに住んでいる。ノヴァキッドらしく、もう一方の種族との関係についてあまり覚えていないようだが、X'iについて悪く言う者はいない。X'iの柔らかくふわふわした羽毛が好きだと言う者もいる",
  "Links to the Ancients?": "古代人との繋がり？",
  "Proving anything, of course, will prove quite difficult given how seldom one encounters a X'i. Finding one that can speak common and is able to recount ancient history is of the highest level of improbability.": "何かを証明するのはもちろん、シィに遭遇すること自体が稀なため非常に困難。共通語を話し、古代の歴史を語れるシィを見つけるのは最高に不可能に近い。",
  "It isn't well known how X'i have access to Ancient-style holograms. They deny the existence of the Cultivator, yet use Ancient technology in their old structures. Perhaps these beings are far, far older than we originally thought and lived alongside Ancients, and know what they were truly like? It is all so exciting.": "この伝統が忘れ去られた形のお世辞として行われたのか、単に長い[削除済み]の後に私の名前を賢さと結びつけているからなのか確信がない。いずれにせよ、この慣習に全く不快ではないと言える。どうやら私の民の歴史に永続的な足跡を残したようだ。",
  "It isn't well known how X'i have access to Ancient-style holograms. They deny the existence of the Cultivator, yet use Ancient technology in their old structures. Perhaps these beings are far, far older than we originally thought and lived alongside Ancients, and know what they were truly like? It is all so exciting. Proving anything, of course, will prove quite difficult given how seldom one encounters a X'i. Finding one that can speak common and is able to recount ancient history is of the highest level of improbability.": "X'iが古代スタイルのホログラムにアクセスできる理由はよく知られていない。彼らは栽培者の存在を否定しているにもかかわらず、古い構造物には古代技術を使用している。おそらく、これらの存在は私たちが最初に考えていたよりも遥かに古く、古代の人々と共存し、彼らの真の姿を知っているのかもしれないか？",
  "Biology of the X'i": "ズィー族の生物学",
  "Use the Codex reader in your Tricorder to view this data.": "このデータを閲覧するにはトリコーダーのコーデックスリーダーを使用してください",
  "X'i are the subject of my team's focus. Very little is known about them, which only makes them more interesting to study!\n\nTo be clear: most of us know less than we'd like about them...but more than anyone else does.\n\nWe do have some speculations not widely accepted or considered by most historians that we'd like to get into if time remains when we're done.\n\n-- Biological Notes on X'i --\nTheir body chemistry resembles nothing we've seen in our galaxy thus far, with very little affecting their cells - specialized diseases seem one of the few things that affect them. They are silicon based yet contain heavy doses of DNA that resembles the genetic makeup of plants. Their bodies even follow some similar patterns to the plant kingdom: they place a bulb, which grows to maturity. If the conditions are right it will 'hatch' and a new X'i could be born. The actual way this happens, unfortunately, eludes us. It is believed that this is an asexual process but we have no verification on how fertilization occurs if this is indeed the case.\n\nTheir birth rate is extremely low (thus far, to our knowledge, not a single live birth has happened in the last four decades) and no method we have been able to devise is capable of artificially inducing the plant to flower into a new X'i. In fact, most of the time this destabilized the core within the plant. This is a bad thing, as they have a habit of exploding when jostled firmly. When you're not immune to most forms of radiation, this is exceptionally hazardous. My team learned this the hard way. Extra precautions are now observed in the bulb lab.\nThe X'i seem to be able to generate these bulbs on demand (so to speak...it's actually a somewhat disgusting process that is entirely too reminiscent of defecating) and use them to physically transport their bodies! I've also seen them use the explosive aspect of the bulbs to ward off threats. And that's not all! These bulbs also form the basis for most of their art, homes, weapons and tools! Imagine crafting equipment from pieces of yourself!\n\nAnother of their innate capabilities is in forming wads of radioactive spore that a X'ian can physically lob. This is apparently entirely defensive in nature, and was likely utilized in ancient times to incapacitate potential food sources in addition to protecting themselves.\n\nAs for their shells: it seems that the 'skin' of a X'i is actually very similar in nature to Graphite. Rather than a hexagonal structure to its molecules, however, theirs has a very unusual octagonal structure that sets it apart. It appears to be exceptionally absorbent, allowing the majority of a X'is radioaction to not spill out from its body and instead be reabsorbed and used to further fuel the core.\nWhen the X'i is alive this flesh is more pliable and generally coated with a thin layer of 'feathers' that act as further insulation for their radioactive cores. With the feathers and flesh combined the spillage of radioactive energy is nearly zero.\nOnce a X'i dies, however, their core immediately begins to destabilize. When this occurs their flesh hardens into a stone-like surface that is indistinguishable from Graphite without use of a microscope. After approximately 12 hours their core ruptures and explodes. The result is a tiny explosion of nuclear energy that very quickly collapses in on itself due primarily to the absorbent nature of their stony flesh. Once this reaction is completed they become entirely inert.": "コンシャクだ！",
  "One and Many": "一にして多",
  "Fragment must explore and be the Eyes of the One. Through Fragment we learn. Through Fragment we experience and the One is richer for it. Explore. Learn. Consume. Then Fragment can return to the One and share of Memories.": "断片は探索し、唯一者の目とならねばならない。断片を通じて我々は学ぶ。断片を通じて体験し、唯一者はそれにより豊かになる。探索せよ。学べ。消費せよ。そして断片は唯一者に戻り記憶を共有できる。",
  "Mother Whispers": "母のささやき",
  "When the Mother whispers, a Fragment must obey. Consuming allows the Fragment to survive. Mother births the Fragment. Obey.": "母が囁く時、断片は従わねばならない。消費することで断片は生き延びる。母が断片を産む。従え。",
  "Tenebrhaeic Origins": "テネブレイクの起源",
  "are each an individual despite all outward indications to the contrary. To avoid exaggerations: Every act they commit is to better the whole of their kind. Emotion, apparently, is not something they feel compelled to waste time on.": "外見上の全ての兆候に反して、各々が個体である。誇張を避けると：彼らの全ての行為は種族全体のためである。感情は、明らかに時間を浪費する必要を感じないものだ。",
  "One of the strangest and most enigmatic of the major races is without doubt the living shadow-things we call the Tenebrhae. Hailing from the darkest worlds, they are quite literally the essence of shadow given form. It defies all known logic and science, leading many to wonder if they may be some fragment of a literal greater power. All we know for certain is that they are all connected on some level we cannot begin to comprehend.": "最も奇妙で謎めいた主要種族の一つは疑いなく、テネブレと呼ぶ生きた影の存在だ。",
  "This means that every single one of them knows the rest, perhaps even intimately. There are no strangers among their kind, but likewise, no real known language either. They speak, but not in a way that makes sense to most. Often it takes the form of what we would refer to as riddles, if they speak at all. They'll answer questions with questions (or not answer at all, or will answer in a way that baffles us. Most often, by": "つまり一人一人が残りの全員を知っている、おそらく親密にさえ。彼らの間に見知らぬ者はいないが、同様に",
  "responding in the affirmative or negative to questions that have no yes or no answer). This species, likewise, appears impossible to anger. They do not fight amongst themselves, and will almost never lash out at others without good reason. They do not display any outward emotion that we can define, leading many to believe they are mindless automatons that serve a single Hive Mind at their center. This is false, however, as they": "はいかいいえの答えがない質問に肯定か否定で応答する）。この種族も同様に、意思疎通が不可能に見える",
  "Fragments": "断片",
  "Are they, then, some sort of anti-Novakid? A Yang to their Yin? The Shadow to their Light? I theorize that there are perhaps more things that predate all known life beyond just the Cultivator. Perhaps even a mate! Could such a thing be possible? Is there, somewhere among the stars, a female counterpart to the Cultivator?": "グレッグに認めさせた：あの奇妙な液体を調合に入れたのだ。彼によればテストで生物学的サンプルへの効果は驚異的で、種族の安全のためなら試す価値があったという。行政上のトラブルは一切ないと保証したにもかかわらず、やや過度に防衛的だった。",
  "Many are certain that the Novakid are fragments of the Cultivator, that ancient being responsible for seeding the cosmos with what we know and giving birth to all things. If this is the case, how do we explain the presence of the Tenebrhae? All tests seem to point to them being truly ancient in origin, and their very natures link them to the stuff of the cosmos as well.": "多くの者がノヴァキッドはカルティベーターの断片だと確信している。宇宙に生命の種を蒔いた古代の存在の",
  "It would certainly make their notion of Mother more credible. Most think their Hive-like mental link is nothing more than a psionic connection that goes beyond all we know...but what if they are wrong and they are in fact communing with (or are pieces of) some massive and ancient power? Some sort of being that gave rise to all of the Darkness, while the Cultivator gave rise to Light?": "マザーの概念をより信憑性のあるものにするだろう。ほとんどはハイブ的な精神リンクはサイオニックに過ぎないと考えているが",
  "Research Log - Unknown Specimen": "研究ログ - 未知の標本",
  "Day 456 - Wagner came back from the dig site very excited today. It seems he found something while digging for core samples in the ice. I await the specimen for study. It's likely nothing interesting.": "456日目 - ワグナーが発掘現場から興奮して戻ってきた。氷のコアサンプルを掘っている時に何か見つけたようだ。標本の研究を待っている。おそらく面白いものではないだろう。",
  "Day 461 - I don't think it's dead. At least, not in any way I can quantify as likely. The cells regenerate far too fast to be anything less than miraculous, and no amount of damage seems to fully eradicate them. I'm in awe of this lifeform.": "461日目 - 死んでいるとは思えない。少なくとも、可能性として定量化できるような形では。細胞の再生速度は奇跡としか言いようがないほど速く、どれだけのダメージも完全に根絶できないようだ。この生命体に畏敬の念を抱く。",
  "Day 462 - I didn't do the thing they say I did. That dog wasn't from me. I think...it...did it. In any case, I can't locate the corpse. It vanished. Then it autopsied the dog like I did to it. I hope it left. I really, really do.": "462日目 - 彼らが言うことは私がやったのではない。あの犬は私のせいではない。…あれ…がやったのだと思う。いずれにせよ死体が見つからない。消えた。そして私がやったように犬を解剖した。去ってくれたことを願う。本当に、本当に。",
  "Day 457 - Autopsy Report: The specimen, which I cannot name at present, is not a match to anything I have ever before seen in my travels or studies. No terms produce results when searched. Whatever it is, its organs are quite different from ours. I can't even fathom their purpose.": "457日目 - 解剖報告：この標本は現時点では名前をつけられないが、旅や研究で見たどのものとも一致しない。検索しても何の用語も結果を出さない。何であれ、その臓器は我々のものとかなり異なる。目的すら想像できない。",
  "Day 470 - I'd frozen the specimen and all was well. And then Wagner returned from his expedition beyond the mountain. And he brought more of...them. There's nothing I can do now but try the wards I've been getting in my head. I'll need blood. Simmons will do. He's infected anyway.": "470日目 - 標本を凍結して全て順調だった。そしてワグナーが山の向こうの遠征から戻った。さらに多くの…あれを持ってきた。今できるのは頭に浮かぶ守りの術を試すだけだ。血が必要。シモンズでいい。どうせ感染している。",
  "Day 469 - I've been locked in here for days now. Almost out of food. And I think I may be food myself fairly soon. The leftover specimen, a few cells at the time, is now moving around like some sort of freakish worm. It gets larger by the hour. I don't know what to do. The only thing left is to freeze it again.": "469日目 - もう何日もここに閉じ込められている。食料がほぼ尽きた。そして自分が食料になるのも遠くないと思う。残った標本は当初数個の細胞だったが、今は奇怪な蠕虫のように動き回っている。1時間ごとに大きくなる。どうすればいいか分からない。残された手段は再び凍結することだけだ。",
  "Sickness": "病",
  "Apparently, this specimen is infectious. I have come down with a strange sickness I cannot detect in my cells. It's changing me somehow, and I don't think I like it. I won't tell the others, though. The last thing we need is a panic with everything else already going on. I'm sure it'll be fine.": "どうやらこの標本は感染性がある。細胞内では検出できない奇妙な病気にかかった。何とか変化させている。好きではないと思う。しかし他の者には言わない。他の全てのことが既に起きている中でパニックは最も必要ないことだ。きっと大丈夫。",
  "Unprecedented Discovery": "前例なき発見",
  "The driller fell through the damned ice! The entire thing is lost, utterly unsalvagable without some means to block the effects of the liquid nitrogen pool. And that still doesn't help lug the thing out. We're going to need something to winch it to. I don't even want to see cost estimates for a replacement, if it comes to that. We're already over budget by 27%. Corporate isn't going to like this.": "ドリルが氷を突き破って落ちた！回収は完全に不可能で、あの効果を遮断する手段なしには",
  "There's something else though...we found it when trying to determine the best method to get the driller out. It's some sort of corpse. I can't even discern -what- it is. I've honestly never seen anything quite like it. The number of appendages is...unusual. Terrifying to behold, in fact. I'm going to bring it to MacReady to autopsy. Maybe we'll be able to learn more about it and determine potential avenues for revenue. I suppose the upside here is that Corporate stands to make a profit, after all.": "しかし他にもある…ドリルを取り出す最善の方法を検討している時に見つけた。何らかのコアのようなもので",
  "Lamentations": "嘆き",
  "We've confined MacReady to the labs. He's totally lost it. We'd rather risk locking him in the lab with that...thing...than have him trying to attack us. It's safer for everyone this way, and allows us a limited measure of control during this unusual period.": "マクレディを研究室に閉じ込めた。完全に正気を失っている。彼に攻撃されるより、あの…ものと一緒に研究室に閉じ込めるリスクを選ぶ。この方が全員にとって安全で、この異常な期間中に限られた制御が可能になる。",
  "We found one of the dogs this morning. It had been strung up and vivisected. Its organs were in a neat pile beside it on the floor, stacked to resemble that malign aberration we found in the ice. I suspect MacReady, but nobody has seen him leave his lab in three days.": "宝石、それが保持できるエネルギーの大きさだ。そしてハイストームの日には、ファリトゥは地表に向かってトンネルを掘る。最も大切な宝石を置き、嵐が収まった後に回収に戻る。そして旅する先どこにでも持っていく",
  "We all agreed that I should investigate beyond where we found the thing in the ice. We need to determine if there is anything more to this strangeness beyond the nearby cliffs. I'll need a ^orange;grappling hook of some sort^white; to make any real progress. I'll have Doakes whip one up for me.": "氷の中で見つけたものの先を調査すべきだと全員が同意した。近くの崖の向こうにこの奇妙さ以上のものがあるか確認する必要がある。本格的に進むには何らかの^orange;グラップリングフック^white;が必要だ。ドークスに作ってもらおう。",
  "MacReady has been acting strange lately. I can't place my finger on it, but ever since that...thing...fell under his operating knife he's changed. It's unsettling. I think it may be in his eyes. It's almost as if he sees you and...knows you in ways he shouldn't. He even made comments on events in my life he wasn't present for.": "最近マクレディの様子がおかしい。何が変わったか特定できないが、あの…もの…がメスの下に落ちて以来変わった。不安だ。目にあるのかもしれない。まるで見られると…知るはずのない方法で知っているかのように。私の人生で彼がいなかった出来事にさえコメントした。",
  "MacReady joined us for breakfast this morning, though all of us were more than a bit unsettled. There were noticable changes in his behavior, especially in regards to social communication. When asked to stop behaving strangely, he savagely lunged at Doakes and attempted to bite him. We had to restrain him to inject him with a sedative.": "今朝マクレディが朝食に合流したが、全員が少なからず不安だった。行動に目立つ変化があった。特に社会的コミュニケーションに関して。奇妙な振る舞いをやめるよう頼むと、ドークスに獰猛に飛びかかり噛みつこうとした。鎮静剤を注射するため拘束しなければならなかった。",
  "Wonders Untold": "語られざる驚異",
  "The find I have just made rewrites the knowledge of the cosmos in its entirety. There are ruins past the mountain. It was a treacherous climb but well worth it. If my initial scans are correct, this site is well over 90 million years old.": "今したばかりの発見は宇宙の知識を完全に書き換える。山の向こうに遺跡がある。危険な登山だったが十分に価値があった。初期スキャンが正しければ、このサイトは9000万年以上前のものだ。",
  "I wonder how deep these ruins go? I've found a passage down, and find myself in a deep and ancient temple. There is no light to speak of, and utter silence reigns. It's oppressive. But these carvings, this language. Every tile tells a story.": "この遺跡はどこまで深いのだろう？下への通路を見つけ、深く古い寺院にいる。光は皆無で完全な沈黙が支配している。圧迫的だ。しかしこの彫刻、この言語。全てのタイルが物語を語る。",
  "These slave beings rose up and slaughtered most of their creators, until a truce was made and the Old Ones left this place save for the few required to keep the Slaves contained. The slave-things are some sort of amorphous, shapeless mass.": "これらの奴隷存在は蜂起して創造者のほとんどを虐殺した。休戦が結ばれ、奴隷を封じ込めるために必要な少数を除いて古き者たちはこの場所を去った。奴隷は何らかの無定形で形のない塊だ。",
  "It gave me a most special task. I brought its babies back to share with the others. We can all be perfect together. We can all be as one with the Watcher in the Deep. It will fill us with need and sweet, sweet hunger. Come my friends, let us share in the feast...": "それは私に最も特別な任務を与えた。赤ちゃんを持ち帰り、仲間と分かち合う。一緒に完璧になれる。深淵の監視者と一体になれる。必要と甘美な、甘美な飢えで満たしてくれる。友よ、饗宴を分かち合おう…",
  "These ruins match no known species, language or style I am aware of. Something about them is wrong, though. The angles are just...off. Dimensions seem larger or smaller than they should. It makes no sense, and it warps my perception to stare at them for any moderate length of time.": "この遺跡は私が知るどの既知の種族、言語、様式とも一致しない。しかし何かがおかしい。角度がただ…ずれている。寸法は実際より大きかったり小さかったりするように見える。意味をなさず、しばらく見つめると知覚が歪む。",
  "No, I will not stop the sweetness or halt the spread of this madness. I feel the need to find It. I have snuck past some horrid sentries and now go to meet with my new God. I can hear it undulating deep below. I will eat its sacrament. I found it anyway, so it's mine and I'm hungry to take what belongs to me.": "いや、この甘美さを止めることも狂気の拡散を止めることもしない。それを見つけなければならないと感じる。恐ろしい歩哨を通り抜け、新たな神に会いに行く。深い下で波打つ音が聞こえる。聖体を食べよう。見つけたのだから私のものだ、自分のものを奪う飢えがある。",
  "I think maybe MacReady wasn't as crazy as we thought. I think something was in that corpse I brought back. I found more of these things, and with the tests I ran...well, they're still alive. Somehow, they still function. And one of them is back at the base with everyone else!": "マクレディは我々が思ったほど狂っていなかったのかもしれない。持ち帰った死体の中に何かがあったのだと思う。さらにこれらのものを見つけ、テストを行った結果…まだ生きている。何とか、まだ機能している。そして一体は基地で皆と一緒にいる！",
  "There are pictograms on some tiles, giving visual representation of events to some degree. While much is uncertain, there was definitely a civilization here. Their people flourished here and through science birthed a new race. Slaves. But all slaves eventually rebel.": "一部のタイルには絵文字があり、出来事をある程度視覚的に表現している。多くは不確かだが、確かにここには文明があった。人々はここで栄え、科学を通じて新しい種族を生み出した。奴隷。しかし全ての奴隷はいずれ反乱する。",
  "I've found some sort of liquid pool that is not unlike the waters found outside. Even a slight touch of it makes me feel strange. There's no way forward, so I am going to brave the pool...see what's within. I've jury-rigged a device I hope can protect me from the effects.": "何らかの液体プールを見つけた。外にある水と似ている。少し触れただけで奇妙な感覚になる。前に進む道はないので、プールに入ってみよう…中に何があるか。効果から身を守れる装置を応急的に作った。",
  "My mind is slowly falling away and I can feel the bliss of madness knocking at my cerebellum. I won't yet welcome insanity. Not until I've seen the end of this place. I found some sort of combination switch. I'll tinker with it until I can access whatever it protects. I have little choice. I can hear things in the darkness, including gutteral chants in some hideous tongue.": "精神がゆっくりと崩壊し、狂気の至福が小脳をノックしているのを感じる。まだ狂気を歓迎しない。まだ",
  "I should have turned back.I should have turned back.I should have turned back.I should have turned back.I should have turned back.I should have turned back.I should have turned back.I should have turned back.I should have turned back.I should have turned back.I should have turned back.I should have turned back... (96 more pages of this continue)": "引き返すべきだった。引き返すべきだった。引き返すべきだった。引き返すべきだった。引き返すべきだった。引き返すべき",
  "Exploration Diary": "探索日記",
  "I'm not exactly sure what the hell is going on here. We found some sort of...door in the cavern near Vostok. Considering the carbon-dating and the undocumented language I imagine that Princeton is going to have an absolute field day sharing our discovery with the world. That is, of course, provided we ever manage to get back to camp. Something strange happened that neither Richter nor myself can even begin to adequately explain.": "ここで一体何が起きているのか全く分からない。ヴォストーク近くの洞窟で何らかの…ドアを見つけた。炭素の年代測定を考慮すると",
  "We were trying to discern a means to open the doorway, for there were no visible means to lever it open. In the end we tried just about everything short of explosives or crowbars. Damaging this find was out of the question. Nothing seemed to work. That's when things got weird. The wall seemed to open of its own accord, and a force that can only be described as": "入口を開ける手段を見極めようとしていた。てこで開ける目に見える手段がなかったからだ。最終的にあらゆる方法を試した",
  "intense gravity pulled us into it, through a yawning black abyss and into stygian depths we were not prepared to experience. I don't know what happened to Richter, but he wasn't with me when I came to. Around me now is some sort of temple matching the door we found, and I can hear something. I don't know what it is, but it is close. I have only enough power to last another few hours and then my reserve batteries will be wiped": "強烈な重力に引き込まれ、ぽっかり空いた黒い深淵を通り抜け、経験する準備ができていなかったステュギアンの深みに入った。",
  "and I fear what may lurk in the dark. But not as much as I fear my chances of survival. The air here is thick and almost unbreathable and there is some sort of foul taste permeating everything that reminds me of a funeral or something else morbid like that. I will endeavor to investigate this place further...I have little else to do and my meager supply of food means I don't have the luxury of time...": "暗闇に何が潜んでいるか恐れている。しかし生存の可能性ほどには恐れていない。ここの空気は濃く、ほとんど呼吸できない",
  "My Dream": "私の夢",
  "The others won't believe me, so I opted to simply leave and investigate on my own. Besides, MacReady has clearly lost it. I'd rather not be around when he totally snaps. If I find anything interesting I'll report back.": "他の者は信じないだろうから、単独で出て調査することにした。それにマクレディは明らかにおかしくなっている。完全に切れた時にそばにいたくない。面白いものを見つけたら報告する。",
  "It was there, swirling its bizarre limbs about, barely noticable in the storm. I could sense it, perhaps because of my dreams...and I knew in that moment that it intended nothing good for us. As I turned to call for the others there was a shift of limb and barrel-like body...and it was gone.": "それはそこにいた。奇妙な四肢を渦巻かせ、嵐の中でほとんど目立たない。感じ取れた、おそらく夢のせいだ…そしてその瞬間、我々に良いことは意図していないと分かった。他の者を呼ぼうと振り返った時、四肢と樽のような体が動いて…消えていた。",
  "I keep having this dream, and in it I am some sort of barrel-shaped creature. Around me are vast, cyclopean ruins etched with bizarre carvings. I can hear this constant sound, like a wet slap or suction. And behind it all, a strange sound...TEKELI-LI!": "この夢を何度も見ている。夢の中で私は樽のような形の生物だ。周りには奇妙な彫刻が刻まれた巨大なキュクロプス的遺跡がある。濡れた叩きつけや吸引のような絶え間ない音が聞こえる。そしてその背後に奇妙な音…テケリ＝リ！",
  "Ten nights in a row I've been burdened with this strangeness. Ten nights I've woken up in a cold sweat swearing that I can hear voices in the night, musical voices whispering like some sort of conscience in the back of my mind. Yet I saw nothing. Not until tonight.": "10夜連続でこの奇妙さに悩まされている。10夜、冷汗で目覚め、夜に声が聞こえると誓う。心の奥底でささやく何かの良心のような音楽的な声。しかし何も見えなかった。今夜までは。",
  "They were outside of our camp, well beyond the sight of us due in part to the blizzard-like conditions. I was outside trying to solve the quandry with the drill when the whispers started. Frantically, I looked around for their source but could find none. I'd thought I was truly losing my mind until I noticed movement.": "有刺鉄線が実際に見える肉のわずかな残りのパッチのほとんどを巻いている…銀河中の多くの宗教で一般的な自己鞭打ちを思い出させる。個人的には、この人物は敬虔な人間だったと信じている。肉の部分の瘢痕組織の重さから判断して、おそらく狂信的だった。",
  "Well, I made it beyond the cliffs and am now staring directly at the ruins from my dream. It's covered in ice and snow, and while the details are obscured there is no mistaking it. What does this mean? Am I being called to find this place? By whom? I simply must know more. I will begin investigation in the morning.": "崖の向こうに辿り着き、夢の中の遺跡を直接見つめている。氷と雪に覆われ、細部は不明瞭だが見間違えようがない。これは何を意味する？この場所を見つけるよう呼ばれている？誰に？もっと知りたい。朝から調査を開始する。",
  "It plays like some fell flute on the wind. I wander in this strange body, towards the sound. In my...whatever passes for a hand...I hold some strange weapon or tool. And then I see it, rising from a black bit like some sort of sentient vomit plastered with a thousand visages undulating beneath the skin. Rather than run in fear, I stab at it with the device. There is a flash, and then I am awake.": "それは風に吹かれる不気味な笛のように響く。この奇妙な体で音に向かって彷徨う。手のようなもので…",
  "Our greatest achievement": "我々の最大の功績",
  "Without the discovery of plasma weapons, the Skath would not be where we are today. We owe our very existence to these, our greatest weapons. With them, we fought for our freedom and won. Through them, we have taken worlds. Through them, we shall have more.": "プラズマ兵器の発見がなければ、スカスは今日の地位にはなかった。我々の存在そのものをこの最大の武器に負っている。これで自由のために戦い勝利した。これで世界を手に入れた。これでさらに多くを得るだろう。",
  "The result is a brutal form of energy blast that can melt flesh and bone and decimate anything it touches. It brings fear to our foes, and gains us respect in the cosmic community. Best yet...the bigger we make them, the more other species leave us be.": "結果は肉と骨を溶かし触れるもの全てを壊滅させる残酷なエネルギーブラストだ。敵に恐怖を与え、宇宙コミュニティでの尊敬を勝ち取る。さらに良いことに…大きく作るほど他の種族は我々に近づかなくなる。",
  "How does it work, you ask? Honestly, we aren't all trusted with this knowledge. Those among the scientific caste are the ones you need to ask. In the War Caste...we just do the killing. And we do it well. Based on what I do know, I can tell you a tiny reactor generates amplified energy and converts it into the lethal plasmic ejections, not unlike gas converting to fire.": "どう機能するかって？正直、この知識を全員が信頼されているわけではない。科学カーストの者たちが",
  "Skath Biology": "スカスの生物学",
  "Skath physiology is a testament to the veracity and efficiency of evolution. The depths of Norkumsgath, their homeworld, is also blessed with enormous pressures and currents that has led to some of the toughest aquatic life anywhere in the galaxy.": "スカスの生理学は進化の正確さと効率性の証だ。母星ノルクムスガスの深部は莫大な圧力と海流に恵まれ、銀河のどこにもいないほど頑強な水生生物を育んだ。",
  "They are especially susceptible to environmental factors on warmer and dryer worlds, and a simple desert is lethal to a Skath where a Human might simply be uncomfortable. To a Skath, remaining moist is imperative.": "暖かく乾燥した世界の環境要因に特に弱く、人間が不快に感じる程度の砂漠でもスカスには致命的だ。スカスにとって、湿潤を保つことは必須である。",
  "Able to withstand extreme pressures, Skath can reach depths previously thought to be impossible for a species of their particular build. With their natural capability to hold their breath for extended periods of time, it becomes quite clear that they are rooted to an aquatic origin.": "極限の圧力に耐えられるスカスは、彼らの体格の種族には不可能と考えられていた深度に到達できる。長時間息を止める天性の能力を持ち、水生起源に根差していることは明らかだ。",
  "For some reason, despite their aquatic nature the Skath are fully amphibious and have begun living on the surface as well. Many theorize that this is an attempt by their Council to force-start an evolution in their species in order to maximize their persistence among the stars.": "なぜか水生の性質にもかかわらず、スカスは完全な両生類であり地上でも生活を始めている。多くの者はこれが評議会による種の進化の強制的開始の試みだと理論づけている。星々の間での持続性を最大化するために。",
  "With their change to land-based existence there are challenges every Skath must now face: Humidity and gravity. Without a proper mixture of humidity in the air a Skath will suffer exposure rapidly, leading to their eventual death within a few minutes in some cases. To combat this, Skath have created environmental still-suits to recycle their moisture and keep themselves comfortable.": "陸上生活への移行に伴い、全てのスカスが直面しなければならない課題がある：湿度と重力。適切な",
  "As for spawning young: the Skath have at least kept this part of their species unchanged despite the swap to newer climates. Females lay between six and twenty eggs, fertilized by the males during spawning season, which both partners aid in protecting until they hatch. At this point, both are responsible for the teaching of young.": "産卵について：新しい気候への移行にもかかわらず、スカスは少なくとも種族のこの部分は変えずに保っている。メスは6〜20個の卵を産み、産卵期にオスが受精させる。両方の親が孵化まで保護を手助けし、その後両方が子の教育を担う。",
  "Priority is placed on social and combat skills, both of which are essential to survival among their people. Typically the young reach formal adulthood within only two years! This makes the Skath the fastest populating race in the known galaxy next to the Thelusians (which is of great concern to the Protectorate due to the Affordance Treaties of 2331).": "社会的スキルと戦闘スキルに優先順位が置かれ、両方とも彼らの民の間で生き延びるために不可欠。通常、若者は正式な",
  "The Council": "評議会",
  "The body politic of the Skath is referred to as 'The Council of Elders' and is exactly what it sounds like. The four eldest of their kind rule the entire species. It is the only such form of government known in the cosmos (for how can only four dictate the course of an entire species?) but has maintained power over the Skath Imperium for at least two to three hundred years.": "スカスの政治組織は「長老評議会」と呼ばれ、文字通りその名の通り。4つの最長老の",
  "To be considered for the council, a Skath must first reach the age of Last Nest (somewhere around sixty in human years) and have no less than three hundred offspring. His role in the military must have been a major one, with a rank no less than Admiral. Finally, they must have seen combat at least twice (heroics and long-standing combat records are preferred.)": "評議会に検討されるには、スカスはまず最後の巣の年齢（人間の年齢で約60歳）に達し、次の数以上の",
  "The first council is said to have been voted upon by the people, but all documentation of that era has been long since lost. Personally, I find it hard to believe that an entire species agreed that absolute power over all should rest on the shoulders of their Elders. The logistics of that are frightening, to say the least. The reality is worse.": "最初の評議会は民衆の投票で選ばれたと言われているが、その時代の全ての文書は遠い昔に失われている。個人的には",
  "A Survivor's Note": "生存者のメモ",
  "It wasn't long before things got worse. Rather than make us work, they would just...eat some of us at random. I watched Rathcher get devoured last Tuesday. No checks and balances were made, no concessions...just death and servitude. How are we to survive? And what will be left of us?": "事態が悪化するのに長くはかからなかった。我々を働かせる代わりに、ただ…無作為に何人かを食べるのだ。先週の火曜日にラッチャーが貪り食われるのを見た。何の制御も均衡も妥協もなく…ただ死と隷属。どうやって生き延びる？我々に何が残る？",
  "They came from the sky, blazing our very atmosphere with their terrible plasma weapons. We'd never seen anything like these creatures, stepping out of their ships as if from some aquatic horror show! First they killed the eldest, and then forced the younger ones to work. Most did not survive the effort, and those that did were often killed for 'incorrectly' working.": "彼らは空から来て、恐ろしいプラズマ兵器で大気を焦がした。このような生物は見たことがなかった",
  "Skath Factions 1": "スカスの派閥 1",
  "Some have even whispered that the Kirhosi may be partly responsible for this corruption through the promotion of trade markets in Skathian territories, but this is hearsay I cannot verify. By casual observation, I would tend to agree...to a point. Kirhosi are hardly secretive about their love of Trade for profit.": "キルホシがスカス領土における市場取引の促進を通じてこの腐敗に一部責任がある可能性をささやく者もいるが、確認できない伝聞だ。何気ない観察では…ある程度同意する。キルホシが利益のための取引への愛を隠していないのは確かだ。",
  "The Vanguard are the military arm and command the fleets and fortress worlds of the Skath. It is without doubt the biggest faction of their kind, due in part to their desire to protect their spawn-worlds. The Vanguard believes that with enough warships and enough defensive measurements, other races will not dare to attack, thus resulting in peace. Unfortunately, this is but a concept...and not how things actually work in practice.": "ヴァンガードは軍事部門であり、スカスの艦隊と要塞世界を指揮する。疑いなく最大の派閥",
  "The Vanguards duty is to protect Skath worlds by any means necessary. Commanders and Admirals of their fleets have follow the Codex of War to the letter. Of course, these rules are subject to change at a moments notice due to the interference of the Council, and even the most intelligent Admiral is at their mercy when it comes to rule of law.": "ヴァンガードの義務はあらゆる手段でスカスの世界を守ること。艦隊の司令官と提督は戦争の法典に従わなければならない",
  "More than one invasion has been carried out under the pretense of 'protecting' their kind, and many more will follow so long as inept leadership is allowed to rule their people. The very nature of their council is corrupt at its root, and the average Skath is ignorant of the extent of this issue. The result is a social heirarchy reliant on unjust and idiotic leaders quite accepting of bribes and general favoritism based on profits.": "「保護」の名の下に複数の侵攻が行われ、同種への関心が続く限りさらに多くが続くだろう",
  "Skath Factions 2": "スカスの派閥 2",
  "Skath appoint the brightest and quickest on their feet as Seekers. This caste, responsible for seeking out new inhabitable spawn worlds as well as knowledge, are the scientific and educational branch of the Skathian people. Without the Seeker caste, all progress would come to a halt.": "スカスは最も聡明で素早い者をシーカーに任命する。新しい居住可能な産卵世界と知識を探すこのカーストは、スカス民族の科学・教育部門だ。シーカーカーストなしでは全ての進歩が停止する。",
  "Despite their often cruel disposition when it comes to species not of their lineage, the results cannot be argued against. Plasmic weapons, enhanced and nearly limitless energy sources and unique forms of propulsion are all discoveries owed to the Skathian research methodology.": "血統外の種族に対するしばしば残酷な気質にもかかわらず、結果に異議を唱えることはできない。プラズマ兵器、強化されたほぼ無限のエネルギー源、独自の推進形態は全てスカスの研究方法論のおかげである。",
  "The primary mission of the Seeker caste is the betterment of Skathian life, even at the expense of other lives. Experimentation on other bipedal species is rarely off-the-table (in fact, most research *starts* here for the Skath) and is one of the primary reasons they were not permitted to join the Protectorate. They have instead joined the League of Non-Aligned Worlds.": "シーカーカーストの主な任務は、他の生命を犠牲にしてでもスカスの生活を向上させること。他種族への実験は",
  "Some among the Skath believe the Seekers have one more sacred duty: To seek out and locate the race that attempted to wipe them out not so long ago and bring the vengeance of the Skath against them. These 'Volarians' apparently responsible are unknown to us. The common belief here is that they are another species already known, but whom remain a mystery to the Skath.": "スカスの一部はシーカーにもう一つの神聖な義務があると信じている：かつて彼らを全滅させようとした種族を探し出し特定すること",
  "Skath Factions 3": "スカスの派閥 3",
  "The Worker caste forms the backbone of Skathian society and are responsible for literally all of the building and planning of ships, cities and equipment. They are the craftsman and artists, musicians and tradesmen of their people and without them the entire structure of their civilization would crumble.": "労働者カーストはスカス社会の屋台骨であり、船、都市、装備の建設と計画の文字通り全てを担う。職人であり芸術家、音楽家、商人であり、彼らなしでは文明の構造全体が崩壊するだろう。",
  "While looked down upon and mistreated by both of the other castes, the reality is that the Workers are the most important of all. Military and Scientific pursuits are meaningless without the people to manufacture the necessary goods, after all! It is the blood, sweat and tears of the Workers that create.": "他の2つのカーストから見下され虐げられているが、現実にはワーカーが最も重要だ。軍事的・科学的追求は必要な物資を製造する人々なしには無意味だ！創造するのはワーカーの血と汗と涙なのだ。",
  "Among the castes of the Skath, the Worker is the lowest rung on the totem pole but also enjoys the greatest amount of freedom. While Vanguard are constantly drilling and training for combat and Seekers endlessly look for knowledge, a Worker completes his task and then relaxes and socializes with others of his kind.": "スカスのカーストの中で、ワーカーは序列の最下層だが最大の自由を享受する。ヴァンガードが常に戦闘訓練し、シーカーが絶え間なく知識を探す中、ワーカーは任務を完了すると同じ種族の仲間とくつろぎ交流する。",
  "This means babies. Lots of babies. Workers outnumber the other castes by a 20-1 ratio, and these numbers are essential if feeding every hungry mouth is to remain a viable goal. It is unfortunate that they are treated as serfs from a pre-industrial society, most barely ekeing out a decent existence on Spawn Worlds. Were they to revolt...they would win by sheer numbers.": "これは赤ちゃんを意味する。たくさんの赤ちゃん。ワーカーは他のカーストを20対1の比率で上回り、この数は",
  "An Unpopular Opinion": "不人気な意見",
  "Recent discussion has led me to believe that the answer to the Skath problem and the Thelusian problem is one and the same. I suggest we find a way to encourage a war between these two species in order to reduce their surplus populations, lest we all suffer the consequences of unchecked growth. We will otherwise choke on their numbers.": "最近の議論からスカス問題とテルシアン問題の答えは同じだと信じるに至った。この2種族間の戦争を促し余剰人口を減らす方法を見つけることを提案する。さもなくば、抑制なき増殖の結果に我々全員が苦しむことになる。さもなくば彼らの数に窒息する。",
  "I realize it is not moral. I also am quite aware that it is necessary, whether we like it or not. I have no urge to wake up next week facing a ten-trillion strong Thelusian fleet in need of food. Do you? Imagine what could happen if left to their own devices? We'd face annihilation at best...slavery at the worst. There is no winning in the face of such numbers.": "道徳的でないことは分かっている。好むと好まざるとにかかわらず必要であることも十分承知している。来週の朝、目覚めたくないなどという衝動はない",
  "The First Contact War": "ファーストコンタクト戦争",
  "Skath 'history' as we know it goes back only two to three hundred years, at which point it becomes a very different tale...one of sorrow and misery, slavery and death. You see, close to the time they began interstellar exploration the Skath were anxious to meet others in their galactic neighborhood.": "我々が知るスカスの「歴史」はわずか2〜3百年しか遡れない。その時点で全く異なる物語になる…悲しみと苦悩、奴隷制と死の物語。恒星間探査を始めた頃、スカスは銀河の近隣で他者と会うことを切望していた。",
  "This eagerness would prove folly, for the nearest species to them (whom they refer to as Volarian, though no record of this species exists in current records) was of a hostile sort and saw only a new food source in the Skath people. And feed they did, with the help of their terrible machines.": "この熱意は愚かだと証明された。最も近い種族（彼らがヴォラリアンと呼ぶが、現在の記録にこの種族の記録はない）は敵対的で、スカスの民に新しい食糧源しか見出さなかった。そして彼らは恐ろしい機械の助けを借りて食い尽くした。",
  "Unable to compete technologically with the hostile invaders, the Skath ceased all resistance activity within six to nine months (records are spotty on this detail) and simply accepted their fate. And for almost two hundred years they worked as food and slaves, bred for the enjoyment of their oppressors.": "敵対的な侵略者と技術的に競争できず、スカスは6〜9ヶ月以内（記録は曖昧）に全ての抵抗活動を停止し、単に運命を受け入れた。そしてほぼ200年間、抑圧者の娯楽のために食料と奴隷として飼育された。",
  "Eventually, the invaders began to stretch themselves too thin in Skath space, and eventually exposed a weakness. It was at this point that the Skath were able to turn the tide with their new Plasmic weapon technology (reverse engineered from that of the invading forces) and reclaim their freedom.": "やがて侵略者はスカス宙域で手を広げすぎ、弱点を露呈した。この時点でスカスは新しいプラズマ兵器技術（侵略軍のものをリバースエンジニアリング）で形勢を逆転し、自由を取り戻すことができた。",
  "Underneath the waves, a different sort of resistance had begun. A large contingent of Skath had retreated into the oceans and seas where the enemy was unable to follow (or unwilling, records do not specify either way). Using stolen technology merged with their own, new methods of resistance were devised. All they needed now was a chance to strike.": "波の下では、別の種類の抵抗が始まっていた。スカスの大部隊が侵略者の手が届かない海と大洋に撤退していた",
  "Their stories claim the invaders ran in fear, never to return. Based on their narrative, however, it is surmised that in truth the invaders were themselves eliminated by another force entirely...or are still among us. If my theories are accurate ,the chances are high they were in fact the Ghex; they were recently eaten to extinction by the Xitix-Thelus on the fringes of known space.": "彼らの物語では侵略者は恐怖に駆られて逃げ、二度と戻らなかったという。しかし彼らの語りから推測すると、実際には",
  "About Fortress Worlds": "要塞世界について",
  "The sheer size and weight of the Skathian armed forces in the current age is beyond reckoning, and through their presence alone the League of Non-Aligned Worlds has become a contender alongside the Protectorate.": "現代におけるスカス軍の規模と重量は計り知れず、その存在だけで非同盟世界連盟はプロテクトレートと並ぶ競争相手となった。",
  "Fortress Worlds were instrumental in cementing the Skathian position on the cosmological stage. With these worlds acting as a direct threat to any and all possible aggressors, there is the ever-present threat of vengeance for anyone even daring to *think* about slavery.": "地表ではこれらは致命的な嵐のように荒れ狂い、山すら引き裂く恐れがある。しかしこれらの嵐にはエネルギーが伴う。そしてこのエネルギーは宝石にパワーを注入するために利用でき、それを自分の体に取り込める。彼らの食糧だ。凝縮され稀少であるほど",
  "The First Contact war made the Skath into one of the most paranoid races in the known galaxy. While they will deny that it is fear, and instead chalk it up to 'nerves', there is no doubt to the classic fight-or-flight response a Skath enters when startled. So imagine just how paranoid they could get with *planning* behind it.": "第一次接触戦争はスカスを既知の銀河で最も疑り深い種族の一つにした。恐怖だとは否定し「神経質」と言うが、驚かされた時のスカスに古典的な闘争・逃走反応があるのは疑いない。「計画的に」行動した時の偏執度を想像してみろ。",
  "This paranoia led directly to the creation of Fortress Worlds. These are elected at random by the Council and declared holy sites. They are then cleansed of all non-Skath lifeforms and their surface virtually covered in weaponry of any available sort. Billions of cannons, missile silos, gravity launchers and the largest military staging platforms in the known universe.": "この偏執症は直接的に要塞世界の創設につながった。これらは評議会がランダムに選出し聖地と宣言する。",
  "Skath History 1": "スカスの歴史 1",
  "The Skath originated on Norkumsgath, an ocean world with climate similar to that of the now destroyed Earth. Our ancestors were the apex predators within the oceans and our pack-based hunting strategies quickly led to the development of a society.": "スカスはノルクムスガスに起源を持つ。現在は破壊された地球に似た気候の海洋世界だ。我々の祖先は海中の頂点捕食者であり、群れでの狩猟戦略が速やかに社会の発展につながった。",
  "As society evolved deep below the seas, our attention was drawn to the surface. Not just to claim resources but out of desire for exploration, and it is then then we first discovered the stars and with them...our ability to dream.": "海の深くで社会が進化するにつれ、関心は地上に向けられた。資源を得るためだけでなく探索への欲求から。そしてその時初めて星を発見し、それと共に…夢を見る力を。",
  "The first records of our kind were carved in stone in the Tethys Valley, in a region that has always been well inland from the seas. Dating suggests thirty thousand years in the past was approximately the time when Skath first became amphibious. Based on the collected samples, they had a primarily meat-based diet.": "我が種の最初の記録はテシス渓谷の石に刻まれた。常に海から遠い内陸の地域にある。年代測定はスカスが最初に両生類になったのは約3万年前と示唆する。収集したサンプルに基づくと、主に肉食だった。",
  "Skath History 2": "スカスの歴史 2",
  "Eventually, there was a split in our peoples ideologies: one wanted to embrace The Message and reach to the stars. The others wanted to be left alone, to leave the stars a mystery. While there was no war, there as certainly a schism of sorts. The latter group broke with tradition and the Council and left.": "やがて我が民のイデオロギーに分裂が生じた。メッセージを受け入れ星に手を伸ばしたい者と、放っておかれ星を謎のままにしたい者。戦争はなかったが分裂は確かにあった。後者は伝統と評議会と決別して去った。",
  "With our technology advancing,they were able to build cities deeper in Norkumsgath's oceans than ever before. Content in isolation, these Skath disappeared and then...vanished from memory. It was not until the First Contact War over a century later that they were seen again.": "技術の進歩により、ノルクムスガスの海のこれまでにないほど深い場所に都市を建設できるようになった。孤立に満足したこれらのスカスは姿を消し…記憶からも消えた。1世紀以上後の第一次接触戦争まで再び目撃されることはなかった。",
  "While being on the land, a lot of major changes in Skathian scientific process came to pass. With a wealth of new resources to explore and new states to test it in, the first golden age of the Skath began. The first radiotransmitters bred untold of excitement. We were social creatures, after all, and someone new to talk to was thrilling as a concept.": "陸上にいる間に、スカスの科学的プロセスに多くの大きな変化が起きた。探索・活用すべき新しい資源が豊富にあり",
  "Skath History 3": "スカスの歴史 3",
  "Council, this message finds you hope in times of grave strife: Your humble kin of the Finsjalve have discovered a most unusual fact - the invading forces fear the waves! We know not why, nor how, but we were attempting to escape a raiding party of Volarian monsters and out of nowhere a squad of Underdwellers came from beneath the waves.": "評議会よ、この伝言が重大な争いの時代に希望をもたらすことを：フィンスヤルヴェの謙虚な同胞は最も珍しい事実を発見した —",
  "At the mere sight of these attackers from the depths the Volarians hesitated. It was then that the Underdwellers rose in force, using new sorts of weapons we had never before seen! Some sort of super-charged water, and the Volarians crumbled to dust under the assault. It was magnificent. Send the word out to the Spawning Pools! The tides are in our favor.": "深海からの攻撃者を一目見ただけでヴォラリアンは躊躇した。その時、地底の者たちが新しい音響を使って力を結集して立ち上がった",
  "Skath History 4": "スカスの歴史 4",
  "Our homeworld all but decimated after the First Contact War and the following inter-Spawnpool territorial disputes, the Skathian people were forced to head outward among the stars. With no real guidance, we blindly groped among the cosmos for a new home. We found many.": "シャクタ、さもなくば死や狂気のリスクを負う。どうやって達成するか不思議だろう？友よ…ここから話が複雑になる。前に天候について触れたが、そこに戻らなければならない。彼らの世界にはハイストームと呼ぶ嵐がある。",
  "While invention was something we'd always excelled at, astronomy was not. Our knowledge of the stars was limited. We are, on the other hand, the most capable undersea species there is and our own architectural style had an advantage: it was already designed for high pressure.": "発明は常に得意だったが、天文学はそうではなかった。星に関する知識は限られていた。一方で、我々は最も有能な海中種族であり、独自の建築様式は利点があった：既に高圧用に設計されていたのだ。",
  "without much further argument, we began to seed the universe the only way we knew how: By sending mating pairs to as many worlds as possible. Within only three generations, our society went from ironworking to interstellar travel. Imagine where it could take us next?": "ほとんど議論なく、知っている唯一の方法で宇宙に種を蒔き始めた：できるだけ多くの世界につがいを送ること。わずか3世代で、社会は鉄細工から恒星間旅行へと進んだ。次にどこまで行けるか想像してみろ。",
  "Skath History 5": "スカスの歴史 5",
  "With the discovery of Plasma, our weaponry became extraordinary deadly. All non-scientific vessels were recalled and assembled into a single massive fleet. A guardian to ward off aggression. We were ready for another attack, should anyone try to invade us again.": "プラズマの発見により、我々の兵器は異常に致命的になった。全非科学船が呼び戻され、単一の大艦隊に編成された。攻撃を防ぐ守護者。誰かが再び侵略しようとしても、我々は準備ができていた。",
  "Even many years later, relations remain sour between Hylotl and ourselves, and there is little we can hope for in regards to making amends anytime soon. Not that we have to, really. We have no treaties with them nor any desire for trade with this Protectorate.": "何年経ってもハイロトルとの関係は険悪なままで、近いうちに和解できる望みはほとんどない。本当にそうする必要もないが。条約もなければ、このプロテクトレートとの貿易への欲求もない。",
  "After that, everything escalated quickly and we soon found ourselves in open conflict with a new race. These ones called themselves 'Hylotl'. It was, thankfully, short. Another government called the 'Terrene Protectorate' made contact and intervined to stop hostilities.": "要塞世界はスカスの宇宙的地位を確固たるものにするのに不可欠だった。これらの世界が全ての侵略者への直接的な脅威として機能し、奴隷制を「考える」ことすら敢えてする者に対する復讐の常に存在する脅威がある。",
  "But after we felt safe, our scanners detected a tiny fleet traveling across one of our colonized systems. They weren't one of us and besides...some people were curious about who these interlopers were. A large portion of Skathkind was afraid that these might be Valorian remnants. Thus a huge mistake was made: The mysterious fleet was shot down by Admiral Yethix.": "しかし安全を感じた後、スキャナーが植民した星系の一つを横断する小さな艦隊を検出した。我々のものではなく",
  "Skath History 6": "スカスの歴史 6",
  "We prefer to remain isolated whenever possible, away from the prying eyes of other species. At least, that was my understanding of things. The Council, unfortunately, appears to have other plans for the galaxy. Just last week I received word that Veilak Tiss (yes, the assassin responsible for Gressvels demise) was being activated to help with matters directly.": "可能な限り孤立を好み、他種族の詮索好きな目から離れたい。少なくとも、それが私の理解だった。しかし",
  "No indication was given as to what exactly that meant, but if Tiss is involved there is most certainly death following not far behind her. And that's just one agent. Undoubtedly our 'benign' leadership has seen to it that we have dozens active at any point, and it is my personal belief that they are attempting to strengthen the League for open hostilities with": "正確に何を意味するかは示されなかったが、ティスが関わっているなら確実に死が遠くない。",
  "the forces of the Protectorate now that they are at their weakest. A homeworld -obliterated-, and our council wants to attack them after such a tragedy? Unthinkable. They should instead remember what happened to *our* world after an invasion. I cannot stand this scum any longer. You can bet that they have waited centuries to play this card, and the time is ripe.": "プロテクトレートが最も弱体化した今、攻撃すべきだと。母星が消滅し、我々の評議会は彼らを攻撃したがっている",
  "Norkumsgath": "ノルクムスガス",
  "The surface landscape is heavily covered with rainforests, leading towards inland deserts on the largest landmasses. Both beneath the waves and on land await the bastions of our society, teeming with billions of our kind.": "地表の風景は熱帯雨林に厚く覆われ、最大の大陸では内陸の砂漠へと続く。波の下にも陸上にも我々の社会の砦が待ち構え、何十億もの同胞であふれている。",
  "The ocean floor is illuminated because of bioluminescent vegetation and strange and beautiful sea life. The ocean is also heated by black smokers, heating the ocean floor up to 42 C as an average temperature. This water temperature has given rise to some particularly hardy creatures.": "海底は生物発光する植生と奇妙で美しい海洋生物で照らされている。海はブラックスモーカーによっても加熱され、海底の平均温度は42℃に達する。この水温は特に頑強な生物を生み出した。",
  "Norkumsgath is truly a jewel amongst planets, and we are proud to call it our homeworld. This is where our civilization started and remains the seat of our political power. Its vast oceans cover about 78% of the planets surface. Most cities and our capital Thela is located on the ocean floor, where our origin is.": "ノルクムスガスは真に惑星の宝石であり、母星と呼べることを誇りに思う。ここが我々の文明の始まりであり、政治的権力の座であり続けている。広大な海が惑星表面の約78%を覆う。ほとんどの都市と首都テーラは海底に位置する。我々の起源の地だ。",
  "Unusually, Norkumgsgath does not possess any seasons at all due to a unique rotation and orbit that ensures both sides of the world are always equally exposed to numerous factors. Its moon, Thetala, functions primarily as a spaceport and military factory with a tidal-locked surface so reflective that it acts like a second sun.": "珍しいことに、ノルクムスガスは独特の自転と軌道のおかげで季節が全くない。世界の両面が常に等しく多くの要因に晒されている。月テタラは主に宇宙港と軍事工場として機能し、潮汐ロックされた表面は第二の太陽のように反射する。",
  "Our homeworld is the most heavily guarded world in the entire League, surpassing even Vulis, our greatest fortress world. Experimental antimatter cannons are stationed in orbit as well as on the surface, that rips any cruiser in half in a matter of seconds. Though none are dumb enough to attack our homeworld, we are always prepared. Ever vigilant.": "我々の母星はリーグ全体で最も厳重に警備された世界で、最大の要塞世界ヴリスをも凌ぐ。実験的な対物質",
  "About Tethyde": "テシデについて",
  "[REDACTED]": "[削除済み]",
  "Codex of War 1": "戦争の書 1",
  "Article 4, Paragraph 19.\nMercy for the Weak.\n\nActs of violence against inferior opponents is not permitted. This includes disabled, sick or crippled opponents and anyone that doesn't match your strength. An exception is given for self-defense. Reasonable force is encouraged in these cases. A violation of this provision draws a harsh penalty with and can range from expulsion to death penalty.\n Species associating with the Volarians are excepted, and can be eradicated as fate rightly dictates.": "第4条 第19項。\n弱者への慈悲。\n\n劣等な対戦相手への暴力行為は許可されない。これには障害を持つ",
  "Codex of War 2": "戦争の書 2",
  "Article 4, Paragraph 2.\nObey your superiors.\n\n Those who stand above you must be respected. Disobeying the commands of your superior gives your superior the authority to punish you in a way appropriate to the severity of disobedience (so long as your honour is untouched). If your superior chooses a punishment that affects your honour, you may report it to an officer after completing your punishment.": "第4条 第2項。\n上官に従え。\n\nあなたより上に立つ者は尊敬されなければならない。上官の命令に逆らうことは",
  "Codex of War 3": "戦争の書 3",
  "Article 5, Paragraph 21.\nAbout the use of Weapons of Mass Destruction\n\nIt is not permitted to use any kind of weapons of mass destruction outside of war. This includes orbital bombardment, the use of energy projectors or plasma bombs. Such an incident will result in the dismissal and expulsion of the leading General, Commander or Admiral. Participants of the incident will also be punished.": "第5条 第21項。\n大量破壊兵器の使用について\n\nいかなる種類の大量破壊兵器の使用も許可されない",
  "Codex of War 4": "戦争の書 4",
  "Should the outcast fail, he must leave Skath space within 1 day or be executed. Officers are under no obligation to keep such Outcasts alive if a verbal agreement is not ratified by a witness, for they have forsaken their honour.": "追放者が失敗した場合、1日以内にスカス宙域を去るか処刑される。口頭合意が証人により承認されていなければ、将校にはそのような追放者を生かす義務はない。名誉を捨てた者だからだ。",
  "Article 9, Paragraph 3.\nOutcasts\n\nOutcasts are not allowed to enter Skath Territory anymore and only greatly honourable acts will allow them to enter Skath inhabited star systems. To regain his honour, an outcast needs to prove his intentions through action first. If his act is deemed honourable he shall regain his Skath citizenship and is freely allowed to live around his kind again.": "第9条 第3項。\n追放者\n\n追放者はもはやスカス領域に入ることを許されず、非常に名誉ある行為のみが",
  "Sentient Slime": "意識あるスライム",
  "This isn't sad to them, though. To them, it's all a part of their culture. But we aren't here to discuss that anyhow. This is a medical examination. Advise central to omit the last statements from the log.": "しかし彼らにとっては悲しいことではない。文化の一部なのだ。とにかくそれを議論するためにここにいるわけではない。これは医療検査だ。最後の発言をログから省くよう本部に伝えてくれ。",
  "After careful examination of subject 9, I've been able to ascertain some most unusual details on the symbiote itself based on the physiology of the host. Host is human, no doubt there...there is too little body hair for this to be Apex, not to mention a complete lack of pronounced brow ridge. Based on medical data of the human species I have determined that the subject was dead for at least 24 hours prior to melding with the foreign body.": "被験体9の慎重な検査の後、共生体自体についていくつかの最も珍しい詳細を確認できた",
  "Cause of death is apparently a prion of unknown origin that is keyed specifically to the human genome. It appears to be unhinged from standard quantum space, able to straddle the interdimensional realm we call sub-space and utilize this as a means of transmission. This would, interestingly enough, allow the prion to infect anyone it wanted within a range of approximately 2 light years. More research on this prion will be conducted later.": "死因は人間のゲノムに特化した起源不明のプリオンのようだ。通常の拡散パターンから外れているようで",
  "After initial incubation period, the priod takes over control of the cerebral cortex. There it stimulates neurons in such a way as to somehow, through unknown means of energy transmission, stimulate the spontaneous growth of an egg. From this egg, a microbial parasite hatches within 12 to 72 hours. This parasite feasts on the hosts brain tissue, using them to construct some sort of neural link with the host at the cellular level.": "初期の潜伏期間の後、プリオンが大脳皮質の制御を引き継ぐ。そこでニューロンを刺激して",
  "I speculate that this is a mutation of the experimental prion approved in Protectorate Year 147 for the cleanup operations during the Floran/Hylotl conflict. Somehow the virus mutated into this new form, despite encoding to prevent this exact eventuality. This would mean that literally all populations with remaining tech associated with this prion could be an immediate threat to the Republic. Researcher Juxxa Valin 2554AN7N2 requests immediate examination of all volunteer facilities.": "これはプロテクトレート年147に承認された実験的プリオンの変異だと推測する。清掃活動のために",
  "In any case, after the incubated egg hatches it is undeniably some sort of mutated retrovirus that is birthed. It immediately begins consuming the hosts brain from the inside out, absorbing memory and motor function, and quite possibly everything else that made the host a unique individual. Soon after consumption is complete, the host body dies. The parasite severs its link immediately and consumes itself. The waste material created then does something truly strange.": "いずれにせよ、卵が孵化すると紛れもなく何らかの変異レトロウイルスが誕生する。すぐに",
  "A tertiary birth then occurs: the virus creates a Symbiote egg in the corpse of the host. This Symbiote feeds on the tissue of the host's body after first encasing it in a sleek and gloppy coat of slime. This process can take as long as 7 weeks. Once the body is consumed, the Symbiote awakens with a translucent slimey body that mimics that of the original host. They are a fresh slate, newly born and unique.": "三次的な誕生が起こる：ウイルスが宿主の死体にシンビオートの卵を作る。このシンビオートは宿主の組織を食べて",
  "I do find one thing sad, however: They occasionally get glimpses of their old selves, or meet old flames, perhaps hear a favorite song...and they'll struggle to remember it. They'll experience all of the related emotions, and it will seem real to them...but in no way can they ever make sense of what it might be. A newly born member of this race is completely unable to recall who they used to be. Reflect on this, but know that your perspective is not the same as theirs.": "しかし一つ悲しいことがある：時折昔の自分を垣間見たり、昔の恋人に会ったり、お気に入りの曲を聞いたりする",
  "Mourning Loved One": "愛する者への哀悼",
  "What did they do with my Steven? Where did he go? What was that thing?": "彼らはスティーブンをどうしたの？どこへ行った？あれは何だったの？",
  "First my beloved Steven lapses into a coma. For three months, nothing but worry! The doctors didn't know what the hell was wrong, and I just had to sit there waiting. Then, he wakes up babbling nonsense...or rather 'Greg gregga greg' over and over again! Then he passes painfully...but what came next was worse!": "最初に愛するスティーブンが昏睡に陥った。3ヶ月間、心配しかない！医者は何が問題か分からず、ただ座って待つしかなかった。そして目覚めると意味不明なことを…正確には「グレッグ グレッガ グレッグ」を繰り返し呟いている！やがて苦しみながら亡くなった…しかし次に起きたことはもっとひどかった！",
  "We thought the lifeform was dormant. The lab techs had it in a vat near Greg...er....Steven...and the second Steven passed on it just...ripped through the glass like it was nothing! It latched right onto his body! Some foul thing lashed out, penetrated his head...and then he...he.....HE STOOD UP!": "生命体は休眠状態だと思っていた。研究室の技師がグレッグ…いやスティーブン…の近くの容器に入れていた。スティーブンが亡くなった瞬間、それはまるで何でもないかのようにガラスを引き裂いた！彼の体にしがみつき、何か邪悪なものが頭を貫通して…そして彼は…彼は…立ち上がった！",
  "But it wasn't Steven anymore. Not even remotely. The language was all different, and his whole body was coated with this...gross goop. I begged them to kill it, to burn it...but the doctors just stared! And then one tranquilized Steven and...and then me. I don't know how I got back to Earth but that's where I was when I woke up.": "しかしもうスティーブンではなかった。全くもって。言語は全て異なり、全身がこの…気持ち悪いドロドロに覆われていた。殺してくれ、燃やしてくれと懇願したが…医者たちはただ見つめていた！そして一人がスティーブンに鎮静剤を打ち…次に私にも。地球に戻ったのかは分からないが、目覚めた時はそこにいた。",
  "From Man We Come": "人間より我ら来たる",
  "<A book full of writing you recognize as your own, yet you have no recollection of ever writing. Half of the words look unfamiliar, and it's oddly un-slimey, given the rest of your current surroundings>.": "<自分の筆跡だと認識できるが、書いた記憶が全くない文字で埋まった本。単語の半分は見慣れず、現在の環境の他の部分と比べて奇妙にヌルヌルしていない。>",
  "<It describes an unfamiliar life, full of unfamiliar exploits you cannot ever recall participating in. But there is no doubting the inflection and word-choice where the writing makes sense. How could you write something, but not remember it?>": "<見覚えのない人生が描かれている。参加した記憶が全くない見知らぬ冒険に満ちている。しかし文章が意味をなす箇所では語調と言葉の選び方に疑いの余地がない。何かを書いたのに覚えていないことがありえるのか？>",
  "Created as a means to clean up battlefields, as the very nature of such a cleanup in a multi-species Republic is complex due to the variety of ailments that are capable of cross-species infection.": "多種族共和国における戦場清掃の性質は、種間感染可能な疾病の多様性により複雑であるため、戦場清掃の手段として作られた。",
  "These are immediately taken in by elder variants who teach them of their new lives and civilization, as their brains are fresh and new. They are fully capable of adult human reflexes from birth.": "これらは直ちに年長の変異体に引き取られ、新しい生活と文明について教えられる。脳が新鮮で新しいからだ。生まれながらにして成人の人間の反射能力を完全に備えている。",
  "These new beings are in no way related to the original prion infection. They are not invaders...they simply are born from misery. The poor dears.": "これらの新しい存在は元のプリオン感染とは全く関係がない。侵略者ではない…単に悲惨さから生まれただけだ。かわいそうに。",
  "The virus was once a simple organism, but mutated and gained sentience. At this point it becomes an aggressive prion capable of quantum relocation across dimensional wavelengths through sheer luck. Infecting people, it becomes known as GREG-771": "ウイルスはかつて単純な生物だったが、変異して知性を獲得した。この時点で運の力だけで次元波長を超えて量子再配置できる攻撃的プリオンとなる。人々に感染すると、GREG-771として知られるようになる。",
  "It devours the corpse during this transition, leaving behind a slimey outline matching that of the original host. Once this host corpse is digested, the Symbiote is birthed from the slime sack as a fully mature slime.": "この移行中に死体を貪り食い、元の宿主に一致するヌルヌルの輪郭を残す。宿主の死体が消化されると、完全に成熟したスライムとしてスライム袋から共生体が誕生する。",
  "Mutating further, it gets loose. Upon its final mutation it begins to breed sentient parasites. These infect a host corpse, and latch onto its cerebellum as they mature. Once reaching maturty, the Parasite enters a pupae stage and forms a cocoon within the corpse.": "さらに変異し、逃走する。最終変異で知性ある寄生虫を繁殖し始める。宿主の死体に感染し、成熟すると小脳に取り付く。成熟に達すると、寄生虫は蛹の段階に入り、死体内に繭を形成する。",
  "The Sentient Hive": "意識ある巣",
  "Very little is known of the social structure of the Thelusians, as they permit no living being not of their own Hive Brood into the hive. Quite literally anything else entering will be immediately killed and devoured without any attempt at diplomacy. This strong protection instinct has kept their kind alive for billions of years, and contributed heavily to their reputation.": "テルシアンの社会構造についてはほとんど知られていない。自分のハイブブルード以外の生き物を領域に入れないためだ",
  "Thelusian Naming": "テルシアンの命名",
  "The Thelusians are not known as such to their own kind. Their language is completely unusable by other known spacefaring races due to their unique vocalizations. While they can mimic the speech of other races, it will never sound right and always contain a sort of buzzing-tick.": "テルシアンは自身の間ではそのように呼ばれていない。独特の発声により、他の既知の宇宙航行種族には彼らの言語は完全に使用不能。他種族の言葉を真似ることはできるが、正確には聞こえず常にブーンという音が含まれる。",
  "Hive Protection": "巣の保護",
  "While carnivorous, the Thelusians are not territorial or aggressive save when protecting the Hive. This is a good thing, because now that they have learned they can Spore (the term used for their spreading of eggs) into space to spread through the cosmos their population will be booming quite soon. This has been referred to in Protectorate casebook C45631-N, sub-clause B as a Type C potential threat.": "肉食だが、テルシアンはハイブの保護以外では領土意識も攻撃性もない。これは良いことだ、なぜなら",
  "Xenophobic Interaction": "排外的な交流",
  "Few species are as xenophobic as these insectoids, and it shows in their interactions with the Protectorate. They prefer to not speak with other races at all if avoidable, but are happy to act as bodyguards and warriors where they typically excel. There may come a day when a Queen chooses to meet with the other races and change the perception of their people, but to date no Queen has ever been seen by the eyes of an outsider.": "これらの昆虫型ほど異種排斥的な種族はほとんどおらず、プロテクトレートとの交流にそれが表れている。彼らは話すことを好まず",
  "Subspecies of Thelusian": "テルシアンの亜種",
  "We know of several breeds of Thelusian. The most common, seen all over the galaxy now, are Workers. They explore, collect and collate data for the Hive Queen. Warriors are second most common, and are typically found in mercenary companies or employed by wealthy clients.": "宇宙の全ての物質は量子として知られる小さなエネルギーの束で構成されている。原子の構成に入るこのエネルギーは特定の周波数で脈動または共鳴する。各原子が異なるため、わずかに異なる脈動または周波数を持つ。",
  "Then, you have Drones who have one single function: Breed. They are expendable and left to die at the end of every breeding cycle outside of the hive. Finally, the Queen rules the roost. We don't know if there is a single queen for all Thelusians or if each hive has a unique Queen. They aren't telling, and we've no way to know otherwise.": "次にドローンがいる。単一の機能を持つ：繁殖。消耗品であり、繁殖サイクルの終わりに巣の外で死なせる。",
  "The X'ian Link": "シーの絆",
  "It's rather frustrating, as there is nothing further they care to divulge even when threatened. Personally, I think the reasons are lost to history unless Thelusians have a long-term racial memory they might divulge someday, when trust is earned.": "かなり苛立たしい。脅しても彼らはそれ以上明かそうとしない。個人的には理由は歴史の中に失われたと思う。テルシアンが長期的な種族記憶を持ち、いつか信頼を得た時に明かすかもしれないが。",
  "While both the X'i and the Thelusian people refuse to divulge the nature of their 'bond' there is no doubting it is there. Thelusians have been seen to viciously defend X'i (even strangers!) without any real explanation as to why. X'ians, when pressed, have implied in their strange language something akin to 'Star Bretheren'.": "シィとテルシアンの両民族は「絆」の性質を明かすことを拒むが、それが存在することは疑いない。テルシアンは理由の説明なくシィ（見知らぬ者でさえ！）を猛烈に防衛するのが目撃されている。シィは不思議な言語で「星の同胞」のようなことを示唆している。",
  "Efficiency In Battle": "戦闘の効率",
  "a terribly unfortunate thing? He's still got several more limbs and every one of them is capable of killing you despite the injuries you've caused. Now multiply this foe by ten million. Now put a squad of rookies with weapons of any sort in the midst of that. How do you see it going?": "とても不幸なことか？彼にはまだ複数の四肢が残っており、あなたが与えた傷にもかかわらずその一つ一つが殺す力がある。この敵を1000万倍にしろ。そこに武器を持った新兵の分隊を置け。どうなると思う？",
  "While rather dim-witted on their own, as a large group they almost seem to be of a singular mind, and this level of teamwork makes them scary indeed when it comes to warfare. During the defense of their world Crenshaw IX against the Florans, they decimated the opposition in a matter of minutes using constantly shifting formations not unlike moving fractal patterns.": "単独ではかなり愚かだが、大集団になるとほぼ一つの精神であるかのように見え、このレベルのチームワークは彼らを",
  "This mistake was repeated once more by the Apex, fifty years later, in their ill-advised expansion attempt into Thelusian territory. Since then, none have dared to challenge them in open warfare. There are other reasons to fear them beyond just instantaneous formation adjustments. Imagine a foe where, if you cut off two of his limbs...he simply wouldn't consider it": "この過ちは50年後にエイペックスにより繰り返された。テルシアン領域への無謀な拡張の試みにおいて",
  "Survivor's Personal Log": "生存者の個人ログ",
  "Personal Log: Stardate 9472.298. I barely escaped the Terrene Protectorate after the disaster... I'm trapped in orbit around a lush-like planet, which is convenient since it looks inviting. Transporter is working... for the moment. My ship's sensors seem to be picking up a small research outpost on the surface. Perhaps there is someone there that can help me out...": "個人記録：星暦9472.298。災害の後テレーンプロテクトレートからかろうじて脱出した…豊かな惑星の軌道に閉じ込められている",
  "Personal Log: Stardate 9472.301. It's been several days since I've arrived. I'm so lonely... I still haven't found that research outpost- if it even exists at all. All I know is that I'm constantly hungry and it's always raining. I normally don't mind the rain, but my drafty little hut is constantly leaking and I really don't like having to sleep on a wet bed every night. It's the worst. Well, at least the food is plentiful on this little planet, even if I do have to go out and hunt for it. Oh what I wouldn't do for some catnip right now...": "個人記録：星暦9472.301。到着してから数日が経った。とても孤独だ…まだあの研究の",
  "The Kir'vat": "キルヴァト",
  "The Kir'vat are a faction made up of artisans, scholars and artisans, their burning curiosity drives them to pursue knowledge above all else, to the point that it can sometimes lead them into trouble. They travel the galaxy and set up temporary outposts to complete a new vein of research before moving on again. They are naturally optimistic, see a silver lining in everything and are always willing to lend a hand to help those in need.": "キルヴァトは職人、学者、芸術家で構成される派閥で、燃えるような好奇心が知識を追求させる",
  "The Vat'iish": "ヴァティーシュ",
  "The Vat'iish are a prideful faction and, while they are intelligent, they scorn the Kir'vat and their 'cowardly' ways, choosing instead to forge the path of the warrior. They use the galaxy as their own personal trophy cabinet, sieging inhabited worlds and taking over the settlements that may be stationed there, just to show that they can. They are cunning, deceitful, and will never do anything for anyone without a good incentive to do so.": "ヴァティーシュは誇り高い派閥で、知性的ではあるがキルヴァトとその「臆病な」方法を軽蔑し、代わりに",
  "The Vel'uuish": "ヴェルウーイシュ",
  "The Vel'uuish homeworld is inhabited mostly by Kir'vat, and is used as a massive store for the knowledge that they have gathered over the time that their race has existed. The Vat'iish, naturally, stay away from the homeworld as much as possible, although in times of great emergency, they willreturn home to offer their strength should it be needed, for a price.": "ヴェルーイッシュの母星は主にキルヴァトが居住し、何世代にもわたって集めた知識の巨大な保管庫として使われている",
  "The Kir'vat hope that one day the Vat'iish will see that there is strength in unity, and as such do not resent the Vat'iish for their prickly nature. Until then, they are content to exist in relative safety, knowing that despite their differences the Vat'iish are reliant on them in order to survive: who else is going to make the weapons and prepare the food rations?": "キルヴァトはいつかヴァティーシュが団結の力を理解することを望んでおり、そのためヴァティーシュを恨まない",
  "Vel'uuish Society": "ヴェルウーイシュ社会",
  "The race as a whole is run by a large council of 20 members, and 2 leaders, 10 Kir'vat, and 10 Vat'iish. The leader of the Kir'vat stays on the homeworld, and changes every 4 years through a democratic election. The leader of the Vat'iish, however, changes often.": "種族全体は20人の議員と2人の指導者、10人のキルヴァトと10人のヴァティーシュからなる大評議会が運営する。キルヴァトの指導者は母星に留まり、4年ごとに民主的選挙で交代する。ヴァティーシュの指導者はしかし、頻繁に交代する。",
  "The Vat'iish have a tradition that any of their faction can become the leader so long as they can defeat the current one in a trial by combat. A challenger must first prove their might in a test decided by the 10 Vat'iish council members, and should they survive, the leader will allow the trial to take place.": "ヴァティーシュには、戦闘裁判で現指導者を倒せば派閥の誰でも指導者になれる伝統がある。挑戦者はまず10人のヴァティーシュ評議員が決めるテストで実力を証明しなければならず、生き残れば指導者が裁判の実施を許可する。",
  "Do I smell? Please let me know if I do, it could mean I botched the fermentation process again.": "臭うか？もしそうなら教えてくれ、また発酵をしくじった可能性がある",
  "Just because I live amongst distilling equipment rather than dusty old antiques doesn't mean I'm poor. I'm a master brewer after all.": "埃まみれの骨董品ではなく蒸留設備の中に住んでいるからといって貧乏ではない。マスターブリュワーだからな",
  "Concocting the ultimate bubbly is a great joy, if I dare say so myself.": "究極の発泡酒を作るのは大いなる喜びだ、自分で言うのもなんだが",
  "I do have a cushy day job with lots of benefits and pay, but brewing and sampling fine wine and spirits is my hobby.": "福利厚生も給料もいい仕事はあるが、上質なワインとスピリッツの醸造と試飲が趣味なんだ",
  "I rather like bad wine ... one gets so bored with good wine, especially if one is a chef.": "まずいワインも嫌いじゃない…上質なワインには飽きるからね、特に料理人なら",
  "Of course I'm rich! Just how many people do you think can afford to have the brewing equipment you see here?": "もちろん金持ちだ！ここにある醸造設備を持てる人間が何人いると思う？",
  "What is youth if not intoxication without wine?": "ワインなしの酩酊でなければ、若さとは何か？",
  "Tell me what you drink, and I will tell you what you are.": "何を飲むか言ってくれ、何者か教えてやろう",
  "When the wine is in, the wit is out.": "ワインが入れば知恵は出ていく",
  "A meal without wine is like a day without sunshine.": "ワインのない食事は、太陽のない一日のようなものだ",
  "When I drink a Claret my head spins, so from now on I'll drink Anjou or Arbois wine instead.": "クラレットを飲むと頭が回るから、これからはアンジューかアルボワワインにする",
  "Voxels lose their value through inflation. Good vintage wines don't.": "ボクセルはインフレで価値を失う。良いヴィンテージワインは失わない",
  "Remember - please consume alcohol responsibly, and don't drive while drunk!": "忘れるな — 飲酒は責任を持って、飲酒運転はダメだ！",
  "Good wine, good blood - that's what my nan used to tell me.": "良いワイン、良い血 — おばあちゃんがよく言ってたよ",
  "I've had a smack of every sort of wine, from humble port to Imperial Tokay.": "ポートからインペリアル・トカイまで、あらゆるワインを味わってきた",
  "Yes, that woman in the floppy hat is my sister. Or was, until I disowned her for filling my vats with dross-quality lager.": "あのフロッピーハットの女は妹だ。いや、だった。カス品質のラガーで桶を満たしたから勘当した",
  "I used to be a Protector, but then found my true calling - as a founding sole member of the Club of Extremely Inebriated and Erudite Gentlemen!": "元プロテクターだが、天職を見つけた — 極度酩酊博識紳士クラブの唯一の創設メンバーとして！",
  "I see nothing about having too much wealth, if it gives me time to produce something that makes people happy and inebriated. Corporate social responsibility, right?": "富が多すぎることに問題はない、人々を幸せに酔わせるものを作る時間を与えてくれるなら。企業の社会的責任だろう？",
  "My peers oft indulge in pretensions of eruditeness by collecting crassly gilded ornamentations or wearing silly wigs, but I prefer to collect fine wines and fully aged spirits.": "仲間は下品な金メッキの装飾品や馬鹿げたかつらで学識ぶるが、私は上質なワインと熟成スピリッツの収集を好む",
  "Gather wine, summer fruits and oil, and put them in your vessels.": "ワインと夏の果物と油を集め、器に入れよ",
  "Burgundy makes you think of silly things, Bordeaux makes you talk of them and Champagne makes you do them.": "ブルゴーニュは馬鹿なことを考えさせ、ボルドーはそれを語らせ、シャンパンは実行させる",
  "Give strong drink unto him that is ready to perish, and wine unto those heavy of heart.": "滅びに瀕する者に強い酒を、心重き者にワインを与えよ",
  "Old wines to drink! old wood to burn! old books to read! old friends to trust! can anything else beat that?": "古いワインを飲み！古い薪を燃やし！古い本を読み！古い友を信じる！これに勝るものがあるか？",
  "In vino veritas.": "イン・ヴィーノ・ヴェリタス",
  "Are your kind acquainted with the fine art of brewing and distilling alcoholic beverages?": "あなたの種族は醸造と蒸留の高尚な芸術をご存知かな？",
  "My ancestors became rich and powerful by making fine liquors for a living. Me? I just live to sample them, I suppose.": "先祖は上質な酒造りで富と権力を得た。私？ただ試飲するために生きているのだろう",
  "Won't you agree that the ability to brew and refine spirits is a mark of civilised living?": "醸造とスピリッツの精製能力は文明的な生活の証だと思わないか？",
  "My people once had a saying: ''take wine in small doses, and knowledge in large ones''. But what about knowledge of wine?": "我が民にはかつてこう言った：「ワインは少量で、知識は大量に」。しかしワインの知識は？",
  "Better be jocund with the fruitful grape, than sadden after none, or bitter fruit.": "実りあるブドウと陽気でいるほうが、何もなくて悲しむより、苦い果実よりましだ",
  "Root pop? let me show you something better: it's red, bites like a serpent, and stings like an adder!": "ルートポップ？もっといいものを見せてやろう：赤くて蛇のように噛みつき毒蛇のように刺す！",
  "Drink! for you not know whence you came, nor why; drink! for you know not why you go, nor where.": "飲め！どこから来たか知らぬのだから。飲め！どこへ行くかも知らぬのだから",
  "While you live, drink! - for, once dead, you never shall return.": "生きている間に飲め！ — 死んだら二度と戻れないのだから",
  "Come try out my bread and drink the wine which I have brewed!": "来て私のパンを試し、醸造したワインを飲んでくれ！",
  "I saw that!": "見たぞ！",
  "Did you steal something?": "何か盗んだのか？",
  "I urge you to return whatever you took. I have powerful friends.": "盗んだものを返すことを強く勧める。有力な友人がいるぞ",
  "What contemptible scoundrel stole the cork from my lunch? was it you?": "一体どの卑劣な悪党が昼食のコルクを盗んだ？お前か？",
  "If you stole something, beware, I am going to set your teeth on edge.": "何か盗んだなら覚悟しろ、歯をガタガタ言わせてやる",
  "Without that piece of equipment you took away, this place is worthless to me.": "持って行ったあの装置なしでは、ここは私には無価値だ",
  "I need an enclosed area in order to brew. Please fix my walls.": "醸造には密閉空間が必要だ。壁を修理してくれ",
  "Those holes in the walls need patching, I can't afford anything being blown in and contaminating my ingredients.": "壁の穴を塞いでくれ、何かが吹き込んで材料を汚染されたら困る",
  "Can you do something about the breaches in the walls? I can't let anything contaminate my brews.": "壁の穴を何とかしてくれない？醸造物が汚染されたら困る",
  "Are you trying to move a squatter in?": "不法占拠者を入れようとしてるのか？",
  "I'm not sharing this place with another tenant!": "他の入居者とここを共有する気はない！",
  "I thought this place was my very own home, and you want me to share it?!": "ここは自分だけの家だと思ったのに、共有しろだと？！",
  "I need you to fix this place; it's not safe to brew anything here.": "ここを修理してほしい。何も醸造できる状態じゃない",
  "I wish my requests were listened to.": "私の要望が聞き入れられればいいのだが",
  "The fixes to these premises haven't been made.": "この建物の修理がされていない",
  "I can't put up with this much longer - look at the state of my brewery.": "もう我慢できない — 醸造所のこの有様を見てくれ",
  "My usually resilient patience is beginning to wear thin.": "普段はしぶとい忍耐力が尽きかけている",
  "This is beyond me. I'm taking my leave.": "もう限界だ。退去する",
  "I didn't want it to come to this, but I can't stay here any longer.": "こうなってほしくなかったが、もうここにはいられない",
  "Enough is enough. I deserve a better place than this": "もうたくさんだ。こんな場所にいるべき人間じゃない",
  "That's it. I'm leaving. I can't stand working here anymore.": "もういい。出ていく。ここでは働けない",
  "Be quick with your business, I have something in the mashing tun!": "用件は手短に、マッシュタンに仕込み中なんだ！",
  "You need me for something?": "何か用か？",
  "Did you need me for a particular reason?": "何か特別な用件かな？",
  "Here I am! What did you want to talk about?": "来たよ！何の話がしたい？",
  "Did you want to chat?": "話がしたいのか？",
  "Is this a social call?": "社交的な訪問かな？",
  "My brewery efforts have been fantastic, and you ought to share in the rewards!": "醸造の成果は素晴らしい、報酬を分かち合うべきだ！",
  "This is going very well! Here's a gift to say thank you.": "とても順調だ！お礼の贈り物だ",
  "Here is a gift, for all your help.": "お世話になったお礼だ",
  "A gift of thanks, I hope you enjoy it!": "感謝の贈り物だ、楽しんでくれ！",
  "I got you a present for all you've done for me.": "今までのお礼にプレゼントだ",
  "I hope you like the gift, you've earned it!": "気に入ってくれるといいな、君にはその資格がある！",
  "That's for you to do as you please with.": "好きにしてくれ",
  "I'm here to collect the rent!": "家賃を集めに来た！",
  "@#$@$#@ *!!!HIC!!!*": "@#$@$#@ *！！！ヒック！！！*",
  "Wantsh yer pixhels? Here, kitty kitty kitty!": "ピクシェルが欲しいでしゅか？ほら、にゃんにゃんにゃん！",
  "Back for more now?": "もっと飲みに来たか？",
  "*BURRRRP!!*": "*ゲーーーップ！！*",
  "I bite like a serpent, and sting like an adder!": "蛇のように噛みつき、毒蛇のように刺すぞ！",
  "I'm coming to cut you down like John Barleycorn!": "ジョン・バーリーコーンのように刈り取ってやる！",
  "Let's break out the celebratory bubbly, I think we bagged them all.": "祝いの泡を開けよう、全部片付けたと思う",
  "Only looshers like ya pick on people when they're drunk!": "お前みたいなルーザーだけが酔っ払いをいじめるんだ！",
  "Come back, the party wash jusht gettin' shtarted!": "戻ってこい、パーティーはこれからだしゅよ！",
  "Awwww, me ish alone again.": "ああぁ、また独りでしゅ",
  "By Venush, I'll need to find another drinkin' mate!": "ヴィーナシュにかけて、別の飲み仲間を見つけなきゃ！",
  "Please spare me, I'm unarmed!": "見逃してくれ、武器を持ってない！",
  "NoooOOOOooo!!!": "ノォォォォオオオ！！！",
  "Where's a reinforced concrete winecellar when you need one?!?!": "必要な時に鉄筋コンクリートのワインセラーはどこだ？！？！",
  "Take all the booze and cash I've got, just leave me alone!": "酒も金も全部持っていけ、放っておいてくれ！",
  "Is it gone? are my wines safe?": "いなくなった？ワインは無事か？",
  "Are they dead yet?": "もう死んだか？",
  "Can I come back? I had to leave halfway through a drink.": "戻っていい？飲みかけで出なきゃいけなかったんだ",
  "Greetings!": "ご挨拶！",
  "How are you my friend?": "元気かい、友よ？",
  "Welcome, welcome, welcome!": "ようこそ、ようこそ、ようこそ！",
  "Cou cou": "クークー",
  "Meow.": "ニャー",
  "Meow. Greetings! ...What? Yes, I can talk!": "ニャー。ご挨拶！…何？うん、喋れるニャ！",
  "Meow. How are mew?": "ニャー。元気かニャ？",
  "Meow! Oh hey, a visitor. Hello!": "ニャー！おや、来客だ。こんにちはニャ！",
  "Meow. Can I help mew?": "ニャー。お手伝いできるかニャ？",
  "Meow! Hello, how are mew?": "ニャー！元気かニャ？",
  "Meow. Nice to meet mew!": "ニャー。よろしくニャ！",
  "Meow. Hmm... Mew smell of foreign lands...": "ニャー。ふーん…異国の匂いがするニャ…",
  "Meow. Hey, a new furriend!": "ニャー。新しいフレンドだニャ！",
  "Meow. Seen any good mice lately?": "ニャー。最近いいネズミを見たかニャ？",
  "Meow. Would mew care to pawse for a chat?": "ニャー。ちょっと立ち止まっておしゃべりしないかニャ？",
  "Meow. Hi, I'm <selfname>!": "ニャー。こんにちは、<selfname>だニャ！",
  "Meow! Better watch it. I have the power to read minds! No, really!": "ニャー！気をつけて。心を読む力があるニャ！本当だよ！",
  "Meow. I spent yesterday outside, I love the feeling of sun on my fur!": "ニャー。昨日は外で過ごしたニャ。毛皮に日光が当たる感覚が大好きニャ！",
  "Meow... Mew look tired from all this adventuring. I bet it's the meownsters, right?": "ニャー…冒険で疲れてるみたいニャ。モンスニャーのせいでしょ？",
  "Meow. You are bold and brave, I can tell! What? No, I wasn't mind-reading!": "ニャー。大胆で勇敢だニャ、分かる！え？心を読んでたわけじゃないニャ！",
  "Meow? Mew don't LOOK like any creature I've ever seen.": "ニャ？見たことのない生き物だニャ",
  "Meow. Mew want to pet me, don't mew? Well, don't. I'm not your pet cat!": "ニャー。撫でたいんでしょ？やめてニャ。ペットの猫じゃないんだから！",
  "Meow... Mew seem a little sad... Is it because of what happened to Earth?": "ニャー…ちょっと悲しそうニャ…地球のことが原因かニャ？",
  "Meow. We might LOOK like ordinary housecats, but we're not. We're far more intelligent!": "ニャー。普通の家猫に見えるかもしれないけど違うニャ。ずっと賢いんだから！",
  "Meow. Mew wouldn't mind giving me a flea bath, would mew? ...Yeah that's what I thought.": "ニャー。ノミ取り風呂に入れてくれないかニャ？…やっぱりダメか",
  "Meow! I've heard lots about humans, but I've never meet one before.": "ニャー！人間の話はたくさん聞いたけど、会うのは初めてニャ",
  "Meow. I heard humans are usually dog people or cat people. Which are mew?": "ニャー。人間は犬派か猫派かって聞いたけど、あなたはどっちニャ？",
  "Meow. It's always a bit startling to see people with no fur. Aren't mew cold?": "ニャー。毛がない人を見るのはいつもびっくりするニャ。寒くないの？",
  "Meow. It must be great to have opposable thumbs like yours! Mew can actually hold items!": "ニャー。対向する親指があるっていいニャ！物が持てるんだもの！",
  "Meow? I smell cat on mew... Oh, mew have a pet cat? Must be the inferior kind... ...R-Right?": "ニャ？猫の匂いがするニャ…ペットの猫を飼ってる？劣等な種類に違いない…よ、よね？",
  "Meow... I never visited Earth, but it sounded like a nice place...": "ニャー…地球には行ったことないけど、いい場所だったみたいニャ…",
  "Meow! What? No, a group of Cats isn't a clan! It's a clowder!": "ニャー！何？猫の群れはクランじゃない！クラウダーだニャ！",
  "Meow? Mew smell interesting... What? I may be more intelligent, but I'm still a cat!": "ニャ？面白い匂いがするニャ…何？賢くても猫は猫ニャ！",
  "Meow. I heard there were once legends on Earth of two-tailed cats with psychic powers... Is it true?": "ニャー。地球に超能力を持つ二尾の猫の伝説があったって…本当かニャ？",
  "Meow? Hey, a humanoid with fur! Can mew spare some time to chat about the disadvangages of fur?": "ニャ？毛むくじゃらのヒューマノイド！毛皮の不便さについて話す時間あるかニャ？",
  "Meow! It must be really hard to keep all that fur clean.": "ニャー！あの毛を全部きれいに保つの大変そうニャ",
  "Meow. I heard your kind used to be furless. Is that true?": "ニャー。あなたたちの種族は昔毛がなかったって聞いたけど本当かニャ？",
  "Meow... Hmm... Oh, sorry. I heard Apex were smarter than most species, so I was seeing if it was true.": "ニャー…ふーん…あ、ごめん。エイペックスは他の種族より賢いって聞いたから、確かめてたニャ",
  "Meow... Your memories of other planets are quite curious... Oh, sorry! Mind-reading is a habit.": "ニャー…他の惑星の記憶が興味深いニャ…あ、ごめん！読心術は癖なの",
  "Meow... Your mind is full of sad memories... I hope mew find nicer ones from here-on out!": "ニャー…悲しい記憶がいっぱいニャ…これからは楽しい思い出が見つかるといいニャ！",
  "Meow. Do mew have fleas? No? Good. I'd hate to contract them again!": "ニャー。ノミはいるかニャ？いない？よかった。またうつされたくないニャ！",
  "Meow! A furry humanoid! Can we be furriends?": "ニャー！毛むくじゃらのヒューマノイド！フレンドになれるかニャ？",
  "Meow. What are a group of Apex called? We call a group of Cats clowders.": "ニャー。エイペックスの群れは何て呼ぶの？猫の群れはクラウダーだニャ",
  "Meow. Mew are so feathery... It's hard to keep my instincts in check with all those feathers...": "ニャー。羽毛がいっぱい…あの羽根を見ると本能を抑えるのが大変ニャ…",
  "Meow? A bird-person? Very strange, indeed.": "ニャ？鳥人？確かに変わってるニャ",
  "Meow. Exactly how closely-related are mew to normal birds?": "ニャー。普通の鳥とどれくらい近い種族なのかニャ？",
  "Meow? Mew just shed a feather... Can I have it?": "ニャ？羽根が落ちたニャ…もらっていい？",
  "Meow? A bird-person? Now I've seen everything...": "ニャ？鳥人？もう何でも見たニャ…",
  "Meow. Are feathers hard to keep clean?": "ニャー。羽根をきれいに保つのは大変かニャ？",
  "Meow! I heard Avians can't fly. Is that really true?": "ニャー！エイビアンは飛べないって聞いたけど本当かニャ？",
  "Meow. Hello Avian.": "ニャー。こんにちはエイビアン",
  "Meow. How does it feel to be so feathery?": "ニャー。あんなに羽毛だらけって、どんな気分かニャ？",
  "Meow... Is it hard to eat things with that beak?": "ニャー…そのくちばしで食べるの大変じゃないかニャ？",
  "Meow. Good day to mew, Avian furriend.": "ニャー。ごきげんよう、エイビアンのフレンド",
  "Meow. What do Avians eat, anyway?": "ニャー。エイビアンは何を食べるのかニャ？",
  "Meow! What do the bird-people do for fun?": "ニャー！鳥人は何して遊ぶの？",
  "Meow! Your feathers remind me of a kitty-tease...": "ニャー！その羽根、猫じゃらしに似てるニャ…",
  "Meow. Is a group of Avian called a flock? A group of Cats is called a clowder.": "ニャー。エイビアンの群れは群れって呼ぶの？猫の群れはクラウダーだニャ",
  "Meow? A Floran. Hi.": "ニャ？フローランだ。やあ",
  "Meow. Florans are always so bright and colorful!": "ニャー。フローランはいつも明るくてカラフルだニャ！",
  "Meow... Don't hunt me, please...": "ニャー…狩らないでニャ、お願い…",
  "Meow. Floran clothes are so skimpy...but then again, I'm not wearing anything either!": "ニャー。フローランの服って露出多いニャ…でも私も何も着てないか！",
  "Meow! Don't eat me!": "ニャー！食べないで！",
  "Meow. Mew smell like freshly-cut grass.": "ニャー。刈りたての草の匂いがするニャ",
  "Meow... Please, don't kill me, I wouldn't make a good trophy anyway...": "ニャー…殺さないでニャ、トロフィーにしてもつまらないから…",
  "Meow. Mew are very pretty... Uh...no offense...": "ニャー。とてもきれいだニャ…あ…悪気はないニャ…",
  "Meow! Don't even think about trying to kill me! I can read minds!": "ニャー！殺そうなんて考えないで！心が読めるんだからニャ！",
  "Meow? Mew seem more civilised than the stories I've heard about Floran.": "ニャ？フローランの話より文明的に見えるニャ",
  "Meow. Thank Mew for not hunting us, Floran.": "ニャー。狩らないでくれてありがとニャ、フローラン",
  "Meow... A Floran...": "ニャー…フローランだ…",
  "Meow? Hey, a robot! You look so cool!": "ニャ？ロボットだ！かっこいいニャ！",
  "Meow... I've always heard Glitch are part of a hive-mind... Not mew, though...": "ニャー…グリッチは集合意識の一部だと聞いてたニャ…あなたは違うみたいだけど…",
  "Meow! I've always wanted to meet a Glitch!": "ニャー！ずっとグリッチに会いたかったニャ！",
  "Meow? It is very strange to not be able to read a creature's mind...": "ニャ？生き物の心が読めないのはとても不思議ニャ…",
  "Meow! Mew look strong.": "ニャー！強そうだニャ",
  "Meow. Can Mew Glitch be hurt by poison? What? Mew can?": "ニャー。グリッチは毒で傷つくのかニャ？え？傷つくの？",
  "Meow... Do robots sleep?": "ニャー…ロボットは眠るのかニャ？",
  "Meow... Oh, a self-aware Glitch. Interesting. Care to stay and chat for a while?": "ニャー…自我を持つグリッチ。面白いニャ。少しおしゃべりしていかないかニャ？",
  "Meow? I can't read your mind, yet mew're self-aware... Do Glitch even think?": "ニャ？心が読めないのに自我がある…グリッチは考えるのかニャ？",
  "Meow. A Glitch! Can we be furriends?": "ニャー。グリッチだ！フレンドになれるかニャ？",
  "Meow. Do robots feel pain?": "ニャー。ロボットは痛みを感じるのかニャ？",
  "Meow. Do Mew rust? Or age? Does your paint ever come off? I'm so curious!": "ニャー。錆びるのかニャ？老化は？塗装は剥がれる？気になるニャ！",
  "Meow! What is a group of Glitch called?": "ニャー！グリッチの群れは何て呼ぶの？",
  "Meow. Hello there, Hylotl.": "ニャー。こんにちはハイロトル",
  "Meow? A fish-person... Well this is a first!": "ニャ？魚人…これは初めてだニャ！",
  "Meow... Mew smell of salt-water. Does your kind live near the ocean?": "ニャー…塩水の匂いがするニャ。海の近くに住んでるの？",
  "Meow. Nice fins!": "ニャー。素敵なヒレだニャ！",
  "Meow? Maybe teach me to swim sometime? ...What? Not all cats dislike water!": "ニャ？いつか泳ぎを教えてくれないかニャ？…何？全ての猫が水嫌いってわけじゃないニャ！",
  "Meow. Do mew people eat fish?": "ニャー。そちらの民は魚を食べるのかニャ？",
  "Meow... Your mind is filled with interesting thoughts. What is this Haiku mew think of?": "ニャー…面白い考えでいっぱいニャ。考えてるこの俳句って何？",
  "Meow! Good to meet mew, fish-man!": "ニャー！よろしくニャ、魚人さん！",
  "Meow... A Hylotl... Mew don't seem as passive as the reports say...": "ニャー…ハイロトルだ…報告ほど受け身じゃなさそうニャ…",
  "Meow! Hylotls and Cats have something in common--we've almost gone extinct at one point!": "ニャー！ハイロトルと猫には共通点がある — どっちも一度は絶滅しかけたニャ！",
  "Meow... How can mew stand all that water?": "ニャー…あんなに水に耐えられるのはどうしてニャ？",
  "Meow. Can Hylotl talk to fish?": "ニャー。ハイロトルは魚と話せるのかニャ？",
  "Meow? Is a group of Hylotl called a school?": "ニャ？ハイロトルの群れはスクールって呼ぶのかニャ？",
  "Meow... I have never seen someone like mew before!": "ニャー…あなたみたいな人は初めて見たニャ！",
  "Meow! Ooh glowy-person! Do mew attract bugs often?": "ニャー！ピカピカ人だ！虫をよく引き寄せるかニャ？",
  "Meow. Mew're kind of warm... I like warm.": "ニャー。ちょっと暖かいニャ…暖かいの好き",
  "Meow!? Mew don't have a face!": "ニャー！？顔がないニャ！",
  "Meow... What makes mew glow? Are mew immune to heat? How do mew see without eyes?": "ニャー…なぜ光るニャ？熱に免疫ある？目なしでどうやって見るの？",
  "Meow. Mew can glow! How does that work?": "ニャー。光れるのかニャ！どういう仕組み？",
  "Meow! Are mew on fire?": "ニャー！燃えてるニャ？",
  "Meow? Mew have a funny accent!": "ニャ？面白いなまりだニャ！",
  "Meow! Hey, a Novakid! Nice to meet mew! Can we be furriends?": "ニャー！ノヴァキッドだ！よろしくニャ！フレンドになれる？",
  "Meow? Oh, another Cat! Nice to meet mew!": "ニャ？おや、猫仲間だ！よろしくニャ！",
  "Meow! Is it fun to travel the stars? I bet mew've learned so much!": "ニャー！星を旅するのは楽しいかニャ？たくさん学んだでしょ！",
  "Meow. If mew've traveled the stars, have you ever seen bird-people?": "ニャー。星を旅したなら、鳥人を見たことあるかニャ？",
  "Meow... Don't mew wish mew had opposable thumbs? Yeah, me too!": "ニャー…対向する親指が欲しくないかニャ？うん、私もニャ！",
  "Meow! Don't mew you just hate it when humanoids call a group of Cats something other than clowder?": "ニャー！ヒューマノイドが猫の群れをクラウダー以外で呼ぶの嫌じゃニャい？",
  "Meow. Your fur pattern is so purretty. I'm envious!": "ニャー。その毛皮の模様はとってもきれいニャ。羨ましい！",
  "Meow! Nice to meet you, furiend!": "ニャー！よろしくニャ、フレンド！",
  "Meow? Your fur carries foreign scents! Can I ask what they are?": "ニャ？毛皮から異国の匂いがするニャ！何の匂いか聞いていいかニャ？",
  "Meow! Isn't it fun to read humanoids' minds?": "ニャー！ヒューマノイドの心を読むの楽しいでしょ？",
  "Hiss! Hostile intentions sensed! Somebody help meowt!": "シャー！敵意を感知！誰かニャんとかして！",
  "Meow! I don't want to lose a life! I only get nine!": "ニャー！命を失いたくない！9つしかないのに！",
  "Hiss! Meownster! Help!": "シャー！モンスニャー！助けて！",
  "Sensation of hostility is fading... Meow!": "敵意の感覚が薄れていく…ニャー！",
  "Meow! Yay! Meownster is gone!": "ニャー！やった！モンスニャーがいなくなった！",
  "Meow? I didn't lose a life?": "ニャ？命を失わなかった？",
  "Either another cat's using their powers to mess with me, or mew took something.": "別の猫がパワーでイタズラしてるか、ニャにか持っていったニャ",
  "Did you rearrange my house without purrmission?": "ニャーミッションなしで家を模様替えしたニャ？",
  "This new setup is upsetting my psychic powers. Put it back, please.": "この新しい配置は超能力を乱すニャ。元に戻して",
  "Maybe ordinary housecats like having holes in things, but I don't! Fix it please.": "普通の家猫は穴が好きかもしれないけど、私は違うニャ！直して",
  "Those holes are letting the weather in. Can mew repair it please?": "穴から天気が入ってくるニャ。修理してくれない？",
  "Purrfect timing. I need some repairs done to the house.": "ニャイスタイミング。家の修理が必要ニャ",
  "Why's someone else trying to mewve into my house?": "ニャんで他の人が私の家に入ろうとしてるニャ？",
  "Methinks mew put that in the wrong house...": "それは違う家に置いたニャ…",
  "Hey! This is my house. I don't want to share!": "ニャー！ここは私の家。共有したくないニャ！",
  "We cats demand a much higher effort from our landlords.": "我々猫は大家にもっと努力を要求するニャ",
  "If mew don't fix this house, I'm finding another place to live!": "この家を直さないなら、別の住み場所を見つけるニャ！",
  "Are mew going to fix things or what? I'll leave if not.": "ニャんとかしてくれるの？しないなら出ていくニャ",
  "I've had enough of this! You're a terrible landlord.": "もうたくさんニャ！最悪の大家さんだ",
  "Not even a dog would want to stay here. I'm out.": "犬でさえここには住みたくないニャ。出ていく",
  "I'm done. I'm mewving out!": "もういい。引っ越すニャ！",
  "Hey, that doesn't belong to mew!": "ニャー、それはお前のものじゃないニャ！",
  "I can sense your intentions, mew know!": "意図を感じ取れるニャ、知ってた？",
  "Put that back!": "それを戻すニャ！",
  "Don't be a cat burgular!": "泥棒猫はダメニャ！",
  "Guards! There is a cat burgular here!": "ガード！ここに泥棒猫がいるニャ！",
  "Now mew've done it. GUARDS!": "やっちゃったニャ。ガード！",
  "I'm busy right now, let's chat later.": "今忙しいんだ、また後で話そう",
  "Hi.": "やあ",
  "Hey.": "よう",
  "Alright?": "元気？",
  "Welcome!": "ようこそ！",
  "Hellooo.": "こんにちはぁ",
  "Hello, fellow slime.": "こんにちは、スライム仲間",
  "Anything interesting happening today?": "今日何か面白いことある？",
  "Every time I see a regular human, I get a little worried that they might be rude.": "普通の人間を見るたびに失礼なことを言われないか少し心配になる",
  "I was in the slime world when I heard what happened to Earth.": "地球のことを聞いた時、スライムの世界にいたんだ",
  "I like being squishy.": "ぷにぷにしてるのが好き",
  "I don't think I've been sick even once since I mutated.": "変異してから一度も病気になってない気がする",
  "We decided to leave the other slimes in peace after all that happened.": "あれだけのことがあった後、他のスライムを放っておくことにした",
  "Have you ever heard of 'Monster Musume'?": "「モンスター娘」って聞いたことある？",
  "It's kinda nice living out here.  Much more peaceful.": "ここに住むのもいいね。ずっと平和だ",
  "Becoming a slime really changed my opinion of those little slimes.": "スライムになって、あの小さなスライムたちへの見方が本当に変わった",
  "I used to be expedition's xenobiologist, but I didn't want to hurt the slimes.": "遠征隊の異星生物学者だったけど、スライムを傷つけたくなかったんだ",
  "Hey, you jelly?  So am I!  Ha!": "やあ、ジェリーかい？僕もだよ！はは！",
  "Didn't the Apex look kind of like us once?  Oh, uh... I mean like humans?": "エイペックスは昔僕らに似てなかった？あ…人間にって意味で？",
  "Aah!!! Oh, sorry - I have an irrational fear of chimpanzees, and your face... er... Sorry...": "ああ！！！あ、ごめん — チンパンジーが理由もなく怖くて、あなたの顔が…えーと…ごめん…",
  "Oh geez, uh... hello.": "うわ、あの…こんにちは",
  "Suddenly remembering working in my old xenobiology lab...": "昔の異星生物学研究室で働いてたのを急に思い出した…",
  "Those poor monkeys... ... what?  Oh, uh... nothing!": "かわいそうな猿…何？あ、えーと…何でもない！",
  "Don't worry, we're not too sticky.  Your feathers are safe.": "心配しないで、そんなにベタベタじゃないよ。羽根は安全",
  "I used to work in a robotics lab.": "ロボット工学の研究室で働いてたんだ",
  "Don't worry, touching us won't corrode your fingers or anything.": "心配しないで、触っても指は腐食しないよ",
  "Yo there, Floran.": "やあ、フローラン",
  "I've read that most of your kind are savages. You don't seem to be.": "君たちのほとんどは野蛮だって読んだけど。君は違うみたい",
  "It's hard to believe Floran could be lethal killers.": "フローランが致命的な殺し屋だなんて信じがたい",
  "Don't even think about it.  Our bodies are toxic.": "考えもしないで。僕らの体は有毒なんだ",
  "Some people tried eating slime jelly once.  Their bodies melted from the inside out.": "スライムゼリーを食べようとした人がいたんだ。体が内側から溶けたよ",
  "I've had some problems with water ever since I became a slimeperson, but I'm still a pretty good swimmer.": "スライム人になってから水に問題があるけど、まだ結構泳げるよ",
  "The Hylotl strive for peace, right? Same as humans. No wonder you're a Protector.": "ハイロトルは平和を求めるんだよね？人間と同じ。プロテクターなのも納得",
  "I think I'll pass on going for a swim.": "泳ぐのは遠慮しとくよ",
  "Hah, we're both slimy!": "はは、僕らはどっちもヌルヌルだね！",
  "Howdy.": "やあ",
  "Oh wow, you're made of plasma.": "わあ、プラズマでできてるんだ",
  "You Novakids are awesome.": "ノヴァキッドって最高だね",
  "Hey, what're you doing?": "やあ、何してるの？",
  "Put that back, please.": "それを戻してください",
  "Can't you just scan and replicate that or something instead of taking it?": "持っていく代わりにスキャンして複製とかできないの？",
  "What's going on here?": "ここで何が起きてるの？",
  "Where the heck's a guard when you need one?!": "必要な時にガードはどこだ？！",
  "Stop stealing my stuff!": "僕の物を盗むのをやめて！",
  "Oh come on, stop it!": "おいおい、やめてよ！",
  "I liked this place the way it was before.": "前のままのこの場所が好きだったのに",
  "Can you put things back the way they were?": "元に戻してくれない？",
  "Something doesn't feel right.": "何かおかしい",
  "Could you patch that hole for me?": "あの穴を塞いでくれない？",
  "This place's seen better days.": "ここももっといい時代があったんだな",
  "I'm feeling a bit of a draft here.": "ちょっと隙間風を感じるな",
  "I still live here.  Why'd you put up another deed?": "まだここに住んでるのに。なんで別の権利書を出したの？",
  "What're you doing, <entityname>?": "何してるの、<entityname>？",
  "It'd have been nice to be informed beforehand about this sorta thing.": "こういうことは事前に知らせてほしかったな",
  "This place's already occupied.": "ここはもう誰かが住んでるよ",
  "If things stay in this state, I'm heading elsewhere.": "この状態が続くなら別の場所に行くよ",
  "Come on, <entityname>.  I can't live like this.": "お願い、<entityname>。こんな暮らしは無理だよ",
  "Can't you just fix things back to normal?": "普通に直してくれない？",
  "That's it I'm outta here.": "もういい、出ていく",
  "Alright, I get the message.  I'm gone.": "分かった、メッセージは受け取った。出ていくよ",
  "Time to set up shop somewhere else, I guess.": "別の場所で店を開く時だな",
  "I hope your future tenants are treated better than this.": "将来の入居者はもっとましに扱われるといいけど",
  "Hey, <entityname>.  Did you need anything?": "やあ、<entityname>。何か必要？",
  "Did you need me?": "何か用？",
  "What's up, <entityname>?": "元気、<entityname>？",
  "Here, I'd like you to have this.": "これ、受け取ってほしいんだ",
  "Here you go, <entityname>.": "はい、<entityname>",
  "I hope this'll do.": "これで大丈夫だといいけど",
  "Oh shoot, HELP!!": "しまった、助けて！！",
  "If anyone's got a weapon, take that thing out!!": "誰か武器を持ってたらあいつを倒して！！",
  "KILL IT!!  KILL IT!!": "殺して！！殺して！！",
  "Aaaaghhhh!!": "うわぁぁぁ！！",
  "Guards!!": "ガード！！",
  "Why didn't I take a weapon with me?!": "なんで武器を持ってこなかったんだ？！",
  "Where's a toolbox when you need one?!": "必要な時に工具箱はどこだ？！",
  "I don't wanna die!": "死にたくない！",
  "Somebody do something!": "誰かなんとかして！",
  "I'd help, but I don't have a weapon!  Can you help them?!": "助けたいけど武器がないんだ！助けてあげて！？",
  "Oh geez, somebody help!": "うわ、誰か助けて！",
  "Please, help them!!": "お願い、助けてあげて！！",
  "Go go go!": "行け行け行け！",
  "Take 'em out!": "やっつけろ！",
  "Whoo!": "フー！",
  "Thank you!": "ありがとう！",
  "I hope that doesn't happen too often.": "あまり頻繁に起きないといいけど",
  "Survived another day.  Whew...": "また一日生き延びた。ふぅ…",
  "This place could use a better defense setup.": "ここはもっと防衛設備が必要だね",
  "Geez...": "やれやれ…",
  "Safe!  For the moment.": "安全だ！今のところは",
  "...greg...": "...グレッグ...",
  "Greg.": "グレッグ。",
  "Greg!!!": "グレッグ!!!",
  "Greg...": "グレッグ...",
  "...donkey...": "...ドンキー...",
  "Dude. Why so violent?": "おい。なんでそんな暴力的なの？",
  "Killin my buzz, dude.": "雰囲気壊すなよ",
  "Make love, not war. Jeez.": "戦争じゃなくて愛を。やれやれ",
  "Mmmmmm.......beer.": "んんんんん……ビール",
  "*HIC*": "*ヒック*",
  "That wash shum good shtuff, mon. Wanna try shum?": "いい物だったでしゅよ。試してみる？",
  "Thish fine o' world, it jusht keeps shpinnin' round *BURP*": "この素敵な世界は回り続けるでしゅ *ゲップ*",
  "... *BURP*": "… *ゲップ*",
  "SMOOTH! *wheeze*": "スムース！*ゼェゼェ*",
  "Jusht shut it and gimme more beer already!": "黙ってもっとビールをよこせでしゅ！",
  "<untillegible gibberish>": "<聞き取れない戯言>",
  "Come back matey, I'm your besht friend. Honesht!": "戻ってこい相棒、俺が一番の友達だ。ほんとでしゅ！",
  "Darn, we wash about to share phone numbersh!": "しまった、電話番号を交換するところだったのに！",
  "Sozzled, me? no, I'm no-- *BURP* -zzled.": "酔ってる、俺が？いや、酔って— *ゲップ* ない",
  "Can't sh-- *HIC* --nag the mate of your dreamsh? ain't got a pimped out hoverbike? why not drink more beer?": "理想の相手を *ヒック* つかまえられない？派手なホバーバイクもない？もっとビール飲めば？",
  "Yoush talkin' t''me, buddy?": "俺に話しかけてるでしゅか、おい？",
  "I may be drunk now but in the morning I'll be sober and yoush still be ugly.": "今は酔ってるが朝にはシラフになる。お前はブサイクなままだ",
  "Liquor? *BURP* but I hardly --": "リキュール？*ゲップ* でもほとんど—",
  "Ever wonder what is a place like me doing in a drunk like this?": "俺みたいなのがこんな酔っ払いの中で何してるか不思議に思ったことある？",
  "Shumone just filched ma beer t'other day. Wash't you?": "この前誰かがビールを盗んだんだ。お前じゃないでしゅか？",
  "Wanna know how to be a good parent? eashy *HIC* - have no kidsh, and maxh out the mummy juice!": "いい親になる方法知りたい？簡単 *ヒック* — 子供を作らず、ママジュースを最大限飲め！",
  "What are sixh beer good for? eashy - it shtops you from givin' a shi' 'bout everything!": "ビール6杯は何の役に立つ？簡単 — 全部どうでもよくなるんだ！",
  "By Venush, yer me besht friend I shweear!": "ヴィーナシュにかけて、お前が一番の親友だ、誓うでしゅ！",
  "Nienty-nine bottless o' beer on the wall, ninety-nine bottles o' -- *BURP*": "壁に99本のビール、99本の— *ゲップ*",
  "Itch shad that Earff ish gone, but at leasth there ish shtill-- *BURP*": "地球がなくなったのは悲しいでしゅが、少なくともまだ— *ゲップ*",
  "Heresh anuvver toasht to good ol' Earff!": "良き地球に、もう一杯乾杯でしゅ！",
  "A li'l lesh covversation, a li'l more 'nebriation, pleash!": "もうちょっとおしゃべり、もうちょっと酔っぱらい、お願いしまちゅ！",
  "Come 'ere me young laddie, and lay me down!": "こっちに来い若いの、横にしてくれ！",
  "Drink to me only with thine eyesh, and I will pledge with-- *BURP*": "目だけで乾杯してくれ、そうすれば俺も誓— *ゲップ*",
  "Why have you a piesha cheeshe tied to the end of your noshe?": "なんで鼻の先にチーズを結んでるんでしゅか？",
  "When the world seems to shine like you've had too much wine, that'sh .... me, I *HIC* guess ...": "世界が輝いて見えるのはワイン飲みすぎた時…それが…俺だ、たぶん *ヒック*",
  "Fuzzy wuzzy!": "ふわふわもふもふ！",
  "If boozhe makesh people look prettier, why do yoush show ugly as f-- *HIC*": "酒が人をきれいに見せるなら、なんでお前はこんなにブサ *ヒック*",
  "Hmmm, they shayse boozhe makesh people look prettier, but I've never sheen anyone sho ugly ash ya.": "酒は人をきれいに見せるって言うけど、お前ほどブサイクなのは見たことないでしゅ",
  "Your kind mope too much, and need to learn to have a beer.": "お前の種族はうじうじしすぎだ。ビールの飲み方を覚えろ",
  "Firsht, pink *HIC* --effalumpsh. Now talking yetish *BURP* What next?": "最初はピンクの *ヒック* 象。次は喋る雪男 *ゲップ* 次は何だ？",
  "Here's a toasht to *HIC*--ing Big Ape, and hish grenade launcher, woo hoo! *BURP*": "*ヒック* ビッグエイプとグレネードランチャーに乾杯！ウーフー！*ゲップ*",
  "Shing right follol, the diddle all the dee *HIC*": "歌えやフォロル、ディドルオールザディー *ヒック*",
  "Oh wow, a talking plant. I am so phished!": "おお、喋る植物だ。めちゃくちゃ酔ってるわ！",
  "Hello there, John Barleycorn!": "やあ、ジョン・バーリーコーン！",
  "Y'allsh look green i' th' fash. Be needin' to learn t' hold yer beer.": "みんな顔が緑だぜ。ビールの飲み方を覚えた方がいい",
  "Matey, you duuu.": "相棒、お前ぇぇ",
  "I may be drunk ash a lord, but youshe sh--*HIC*--tty ash a shtinking drunk!": "俺は殿様酔いかもしれんが、お前は *ヒック* 臭い酔っ払い以下だ！",
  "Dangit, you're all tin and no beer *HIC* Ain't no good at all!": "ちぇっ、ブリキだらけでビールがない *ヒック* 全然ダメだ！",
  "Can you turn fruit and veggiesh unto boozhe in that can of yoursh, right?": "あの缶で果物と野菜を酒にできるんでしゅよね？",
  "What are you, a promoter for Letheia B -- *BURP* -- eriesh? *HIC*": "お前はレテイアB— *ゲップ* —リーズの宣伝マンか？*ヒック*",
  "Ever tried to breathe fire after drinkin' beer?": "ビール飲んだ後に火を吐こうとしたことある？",
  "Tea? yeach, how do you *HIC* --king get drunk on that?": "お茶？うえ、あれでどうやって *ヒック* 酔えるんだ？",
  "If you're drunk ash I am, do you shee double? or triple?": "俺と同じくらい酔ってたら、二重に見える？三重？",
  "You're me besht friend matey. Sure shmell. Like fish. And vinegar. But moshtly, phish *HIC*": "お前は最高の友達だ。確かに臭い。魚と。酢。でもほとんど魚 *ヒック*",
  "Enough with the root pop shtick, jusht gimme anuvver bee--*BURP*": "ルートポップの話はもういい、もう一杯ビー— *ゲップ*",
  "Your kind sure look like white lightning! wait, ish it the white lightning I've been drinkin'?": "お前の種族は稲妻みたいだ！待て、俺が飲んでる密造酒のことか？",
  "Now theresh a shpirit I hope I won't be gettin' plashtered on shomeday.": "いつかこのスピリッツで潰れないことを願うでしゅ",
  "What ho, thief! *BURP*": "泥棒め！*ゲップ*",
  "Dunno what yer saysh 'bout not shtealin', but you spin it poorer than this here room doesh!": "盗むなとか言ってるが、この部屋よりヘタクソな言い訳だぜ！",
  "Only looshers like ya p-- *HIC* on people when they're drunk!": "お前みたいなルーザーだけが酔っ払いを *ヒック* いじめるんだ！",
  "Did ya jusht nick shome-thing?": "今ニャにか盗んだでしゅか？",
  "*!!!HIC!!!*": "*！！！ヒック！！！*",
  "Hey, shtay away from m-*!!!HIC!!!* beer!": "おい、俺の *！！！ヒック！！！* ビールに近づくな！",
  "ROOOAARRRR!!": "ガオォォォ！！",
  "Pleash, put back my booszh. Yoush won't like me when I'm shober.": "酒を返してくれでしゅ。シラフの俺は好きになれないぞ",
  "Theresh only nienty-eight bottlesh o' beer on me wall!": "壁に98本のビールしかないでしゅ！",
  "Why is all the rum gone? pleash, put it back.": "ラム酒はどこへ行った？返してくれでしゅ",
  "I taw dat!": "見たでしゅ！",
  "Thish room ish'nt shpinning ash it ushed to be. Fixh it, pleash.": "この部屋は前ほど回ってないでしゅ。直してくれでしゅ",
  "Pleash fix up my walls guv, shumone just filched ma beer t'other day.": "壁を直してくれでしゅ大将、この前誰かがビールを盗んだんだ",
  "I'm a pretty mean drunk, I don't wanna share the boozhe!": "俺はかなり意地悪な酔っ払いだ、酒を分けたくない！",
  "There jusht ain't enough boozhe in here fer anuvver!": "ここにはもう一人分の酒がないんだ！",
  "Looksh like thish plash ish reachin' peak beer. Guesh I'll be goin' away, my friend.": "この場所はビールのピークに達したみたいでしゅ。もう行くわ、友よ",
  "With gold and shilver I'd shupport ye; but I'll shing no more 'til I get a drink.": "金と銀で支えるでしゅが、飲むまではもう歌わない",
  "Zooks, thish plash drier than the shurfash of Venush! besht get goin' to fin' me a new waterin' hole.": "おお、ここはヴィーナスの表面より乾いてるでしゅ！新しい酒場を探しに行かなきゃ",
  "Call me when you're sober. Thank you, come again!": "シラフの時に呼んでくれ。ありがとう、また来てね！",
  "Oh, *HIC*.": "おお、*ヒック*",
  "*HIC*. Free beer?": "*ヒック*。タダビール？",
  "*Hi, uh. *HIC*.": "*やあ、えーと。*ヒック*",
  "Here'sh your rent. Now leave me to me booze, you lush!": "ほら家賃だ。酒を飲ませてくれ、この酔っ払い！",
  "Think ya feel lucky, punk? *!!!BURP!!!*": "運がいいと思うか、パンク？*！！！ゲップ！！！*",
  "Watch out, I know drunken kung fu!": "気をつけろ、酔拳を知ってるぞ！",
  "You're me besht mate. And I'm a mean drunk!": "お前は最高の相棒だ。俺は意地悪な酔っ払いだけど！",
  "I may be blind drunk, but yer jusht shtone cold and dead.": "俺は泥酔かもしれんが、お前はただの冷たい死体だ",
  "Check their wallets! maybe they've got Pixels for ... beer!": "財布を調べろ！ビール代の…ピクセルがあるかも！",
  "I need a glass o' root pop after all that. Not beer. Wait, what did I jusht say?": "あの後はルートポップが必要だ。ビールじゃなく。待って、今なんて言った？",
  "We cooked their gooshe, iso t's time to looshe the joosh!": "やつらをやっつけた、ジュースで乾杯だ！",
  "What is a place like you doing in a doink like this?": "お前みたいなのがこんな場所で何してるんだ？",
  "Help! someone save me. And my beer. But save the beer first!": "助けて！誰か助けて。それとビールも。でもビールを先に！",
  "F--*HIC* off, and don't come back until you've got a beer for me!": "う *ヒック* せろ、ビール持ってくるまで戻ってくるな！",
  "I *HIC* nothing to *BURP* to you.": "俺は *ヒック* お前に *ゲップ* ことはない",
  "*BURP*": "*ゲップ*",
  "I really shouldn't touch this blood.": "この血には触れないほうがいい",
  "Writing of some sort, etched in blood. Or maybe it's just my imagination.": "血で刻まれた何らかの文字。あるいは気のせいかも",
  "Blood Spatter": "血しぶき",
  "Why did I come here, again?": "なぜここに来たんだっけ？",
  "Bloody Chunks": "血まみれの塊",
  "Meaty, bone-strewn gore.": "肉片と骨が散乱した惨状",
  "Bloody Leg": "血まみれの脚",
  "A bloody severed leg from a hapless miner.": "不運な鉱夫の血まみれの切断された脚",
  "Gory Skull": "血塗れの頭蓋骨",
  "Someone has had their skull forcibly removed from their body.": "誰かの頭蓋骨が体から強引に取り外されている",
  "Ship has sustained major damage and is in need of repair. Perform repairs now?": "船は大きな損傷を受けており、修理が必要です。今すぐ修理を行いますか？",
  "S.S.D (Kevin's Flesher (tm))": "S.S.D（ケヴィンのフレッシャー™）",
  "Use this on your ship to upload the ship data to S.A.I.L making it able to be used by new characters.": "宇宙船で使用して船データをS.A.I.Lにアップロード。新キャラクターで使用可能になる",
